    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539931/ops-dental-hygienist": {
      "title": "OPS Dental Hygienist",
      "description": "OPS Dental Hygienist Apply now Job no: 539931 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Dentistry Department: 34130103 - DN-PERIODONTICS RESIDENT Classification Title: OPS Dental Hygienist Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma, licensed as a dental hygienist in accordance with Chapter 466, Florida Statutes, and Basic Life Support (BLS) Certification. Job Description: Perform Treatments on patients consistent with the training of a licensed dental hygienist and as prescribed by faculty/residents, including but not limited to: periodontal charting, oral hygiene instructions, root planning and scaling procedures, and prophylaxis. Additional duties will include cleaning of dental treatment rooms and facilitating sterilization of instruments, assisting in maintaining inventories of materials for the resident graduate clinic, providing dental assisting services for faculty during periodontal surgery as required, and other additional duties as needed for the benefit of the Department of Periodontics. Expected Salary: $36.00 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma, licensed as a dental hygienist in accordance with Chapter 466, Florida Statutes, and Basic Life Support (BLS) Certification. Preferred: Experience handling general office equipment (fax machine, computer, copier and calculator). Information technology skills operating a computer, and experience with Windows, and Microsoft Office (Word, Access and Excel). Strong organizational skills Proven ability in critical thinking, problem-solving, and process evaluation/improvement Ability to deal with the public in a tactful and courteous manner Ability to communicate effectively with multiple persons during high volume periods Ability to coordinate work assignments effectively Poise and confidence when interacting with faculty and students in the clinic setting, with the ability to professionally maintain established industry standards Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Position is 20 hours per week. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541318/fiscal-team-lead-uf-emergency-medicine": {
      "title": "Fiscal Team Lead – UF Emergency Medicine",
      "description": "Fiscal Team Lead – UF Emergency Medicine Apply now Job no: 541318 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 29290100 - MD-EMERGENCY MED-AED Classification Title: Fiscal Assistant III Classification Minimum Requirements High school diploma or equivalent and five years of general accounts transaction experience. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: The University of Florida, College of Medicine, Department of Emergency Medicine (DEM), actively seeks a motivated and experienced individual to join us as the Finance Team Lead . Reporting to the Finance Manager, the Finance Team Lead will support departmental financial activities, including budgeting, financial reporting, and account reconciliation, while providing oversight of departmental fiscal operations and transaction processing. Additionally, this role will provide guidance to staff on fiscal processes, helping ensure compliance with university and department policies and procedures. The UF Department of Emergency Medicine proudly maintains an affiliation with UF Health Shands Hospital, a distinguished 1,162-bed teaching facility renowned for its Level 1 trauma center and cutting-edge burn center. As the primary referral center for North Central Florida, our institution stands as a beacon of excellence in healthcare. This affiliation underscores our commitment to top-tier medical care and innovation. Key Responsibilities: Finance Duties Generate and review monthly expense reports, identify variances to budget and propose necessary corrections. Assist the Finance Manager with the annual department budget. Oversee ADU personnel and payment administration, including ePAF processing, maintenance of ADU and CCM tracking logs, funding distribution updates, payee communications, resident moonlighting reporting through Qualtrics, and coordination of OPS shift payments with clinical scheduling. Fiscal Duties Oversee daily processing of requisitions, travel, PCard, and payables. Guide staff on department finance and fiscal procedures. Review vouchers and purchase orders for compliance with university, state, and federal regulations. Process and oversee travel authorizations and expense reports. Support account reconciliation and resolve discrepancies. Review transactions for accuracy, allowability, and proper documentation. Monitor expenditures, encumbrances, and balances to catch errors or follow-up items. Coordinate with faculty and university offices to obtain or verify reconciliation data. Oversee journal entries to ensure accurate fund allocation across chartfields. Identify and resolve transaction errors or missing information. Reconcile departmental and assigned fiscal accounts to maintain accurate records. Oversee Professional Development and CME funds. Attend meetings and training to stay current on procedures. Contract and Commitment Contract invoicing, reconciliations and accruals. Commitment funds invoicing, payment reconciliation, and monthly reporting. Team support Coach unit staff on how to initiate, route, complete, and correct fiscal transactions within university systems and established workflows. Provide guidance to faculty, staff, and administrators on transaction requirements, documentation standards, and procedural expectations. Assist with coverage for other team members during absences, peak periods, or shifting workload demands. Collaborate with colleagues to balance workload and maintain service standards. Schedule: Monday-Friday, 8:00 am-5:00 pm The City of Gainesville: Gainesville, home to the University of Florida, is ranked #1 best city to move to in Florida by USA Today. Centrally located in North Florida, it offers a blend of small-town charm and big-city amenities, with close proximity to major airports, family entertainment, and some of the best beaches in the world. Known for its beautiful landscapes and urban forest, Gainesville is a hidden gem that provides year-round outdoor activities, award-winning college sports, and a rich cultural scene. The University of Florida and UF Health are the leading employers in the area, making Gainesville an excellent place to work and raise a family. Learn more about Florida’s premiere health system, UF Health, and the advantages of living in Gainesville at UF Health Destination . Expected Salary: The hourly rate ranges between $23.94 - $25.86 and is commensurate with education and experience. At the University of Florida, we are committed to the well-being and professional growth of our employees. Our benefits package is designed to support your health, work-life balance, and financial security: Generous Paid Leave: Enjoy 22 days of paid vacation, 13 days of paid sick leave, 11 paid Holidays, and 8 weeks of paid parental leave. Individual and Family Health Insurance Benefits State of Florida Retirement Plan Options State of Florida Basic Life Insurance Public Service Loan Forgiveness Eligible Employer Professional Development Opportunities Wellness Programs available to employees For more details on our comprehensive benefits, visit UF Benefits . Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and five years of general accounts transaction experience. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred Demonstrated ability to serve in a team lead capacity and to lead through influence, facilitate problem solving, and promote a high level of customer service and accountability. Experience in financial, fiscal, accounting, or administrative business functions. Experience with travel processing and salary distribution management. Experience working with enterprise financial systems such as PeopleSoft, myUFL, UF GO, MyUFMarket. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications. Demonstrated ability to analyze financial information, identify discrepancies, and resolve issues. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to understand, interpret, and apply applicable rules, regulations, policies, and procedures. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Strong verbal and written communication skills and the ability to work effectively with diverse stakeholders. Experience in a higher-education, academic medicine, healthcare or similarly complex environment. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, candidates must submit the following documents: A cover letter detailing relevant experience and qualifications. A current resume/CV. For questions, please reach out to EM-Careers@ufl.edu This position is eligible for veterans' preference. To claim veterans' preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Form or equivalent certification with your application for consideration. See UF’s Veterans' Preference Page for more details. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541394/veterinary-diagnostic-lab-microbiology-technician-ii-care": {
      "title": "Veterinary Diagnostic Lab Microbiology Technician II (CARE)",
      "description": "Veterinary Diagnostic Lab Microbiology Technician II (CARE) Apply now Job no: 541394 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28334100 - VM-CLINICAL-MICRO-PARASITOLOGY Classification Title: Veterinary Diagnostic Lab Microbiology Technician II (CARE) Classification Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree in clinical microbiology or other biology related field and three years of relevant laboratory experience. Job Description: Perform a variety of diagnostic techniques and assays in the areas of bacteriology, mycology, mycobacteriology, mycoplasma, serology, virology and parasitology to identify pathogens of veterinary importance. Examples of techniques and assays include, but are not limited to, culture set-up, delineation, identification and susceptibility testing of pathogens of veterinary importance, biochemical tests, ELISAs, PCR’s, fecal flotations, sedimentations and direct smears. Incumbent proactively triages and processes specimens appropriately for the test requested and in a timely manner. Also, enters lab results and/or charges in the correct account or medical record promptly, sends test results to outside clients; prepares specimens for shipments to referral labs as needed. May be required to obtain certification in testing for Equine Infectious Anemia and provide monthly processing reports to the USDA. Performs preventive maintenance and quality control on laboratory equipment and analytical procedures at required intervals. Documents maintenance, QC, and repairs to equipment in the indicated by out-of-range quality control results, and verifies patient results that may have been affected. Maintains the cleanliness and orderliness of laboratories. Maintain inventory of hazardous waste and schedule pick-up of waste by Environmental Health and Safety. Properly process and dispose of hazardous, biohazardous and biomedical waste. Maintain laboratory supplies inventory and perform weekly ordering of supplies with approval of Laboratory Manager. Assist in development of work instructions with approval of Laboratory Manager. Perform various clerical duties including, results reporting into the hospital information system, faxing and e-mailing results to outside clinics and prepare request forms for shipment to referring laboratories. Assist and train other personnel as needed and dictated by expertise. Other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $19.00-$23.00 per hour Preferred Advanced degree in microbiology, biology, molecular biology or related field. Experience working in a diagnostic microbiology laboratory. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a CARE position offering limited benefits, including health insurance and paid time off. When appropriate certifications are achieved, promotional opportunities to a level II title may be available. This position will also become eligible for transition into a TEAMS (staff) salary plan. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541445/application-programmer-i": {
      "title": "Application Programmer I",
      "description": "Application Programmer I Apply now Job no: 541445 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering Department: 19070000 - EG-ENG SCH SUSTAIN INFRST ENV Classification Title: Application Programmer I Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and one year of appropriate experience. Appropriate college coursework may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: Assist with developing timely responses (generally same business day) to technical support questions for design-oriented bridge finite element analysis software and deep foundation analysis software maintained by the Bridge Software Institute (BSI). Populate technical engineering responses to end-user questions, coordinate responses with licensing personnel, hold screenshare sessions to help end-users navigate the interface and/or resolve technical challenges, and ensure that any feature requests or potential software bugs are reported to senior programmers/engineers. Assist with formulating, executing, and documenting verification cases for bridge finite element analysis software and deep foundation analysis software. Utilize one or more of manual calculation methods, design-oriented analysis software, and/or general-purpose finite element analysis software for a given verification case. Identify and document comparisons of pertinent analysis output to substantiate each verification case. Coordinate with senior engineers to populate and maintain internal and published verification reports. Enhance and maintain internal software applications that performs verification tasks on a BSI software packages for bridge finite element analysis as part of continuous integration, including just prior to official software releases. Coordinate with BSI engineers to prioritize which verification models are to be added to the verification model repository of the application. Integrate model files supplied by end-users and BSI engineers into the verification suite. Add/modify the feature set of the internal verification tool based on input from BSI engineers. Ensure that verification tasks are organized in the BSI queuing system and completed in a timely manner. Participate in research and development activities within BSI related to nonlinear finite element analysis (FEA), soil-structure interaction, and other topics within the scope of the institute. Assist with numerical studies using software such as LPILE, APILE, GROUP, ADINA, and LS-DYNA. Contribute to technical reports, conference papers, journal publications, and sponsored research projects. Coordinate with faculty, research staff, industry partners, and graduate students as needed to support research objectives. Assist with enhancing and maintaining C# and XSL-based application that renders results obtained from bridge finite element analysis into formatted HTML reports. Participate in implementation of XML-to-XSL string processing and rendered-HTML report formatting when new entries are added to the XML schema. Coordinate with engineers to document tasks that relate to enhancement of the report-generator user interface (UI). Perform coding tasks assigned by senior programmers and managed through the BSI queuing system. Perform other duties as assigned in support of BSI operations, including coordination of newsletters and technical publications, creation and testing of software installation packages, maintenance of user documentation in web and PDF formats through FLARE, website support, and software quality assurance activities. Expected Salary: $60,000-$70,000 annually; commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and one year of appropriate experience. Appropriate college coursework may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred: Master’s degree with specialization in structural engineering, or closely related field and one year of relevant experience. Experience developing software using programming languages such as Python, Fortran, MATLAB, C#, C++. HTML, and CSS. Experience in workflows utilizing Azure DevOps Server. Demonstrated ability to formulate, execute, and document analytical and numerical studies using software such as LPILE, APILE, GROUP, ADINA, and LS-DYNA. Demonstrated ability to apply numerical techniques from calculus, statistics, and linear algebra to engineering analysis and software development. Experience with finite element analysis, soil-structure interaction modeling, bridge engineering applications, or related structural and geotechnical engineering software is highly desirable. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to prepare technical documentation, verification reports, and research publications, are preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered for this position, you must upload a cover letter and resume with application. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Position is re-posted, current applicants do not need to re-apply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541551/nuclear-medicine-radiologist": {
      "title": "NUCLEAR MEDICINE RADIOLOGIST",
      "description": "NUCLEAR MEDICINE RADIOLOGIST Apply now Job no: 541551 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29130500 - MD-RADIOLOGY-NUCLEAR MEDICINE Classification Title: Nuclear Medicine Radiologist Classification Minimum Requirements: At the time of application, candidates much: Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology Completion of a Nuclear Medicine fellowship Be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida prior to employment Job Description: The Department of Radiology at the University of Florida is recruiting a nuclear medicine radiologist at the rank of Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Professor for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position. Primary clinical responsibilities will be based at UF Health Shands Hospital in Gainesville, Florida. This position will provide comprehensive coverage in nuclear medicine within a high-volume academic and tertiary care environment at UF Health Shands, featuring nationally ranked subspecialty programs, a comprehensive children’s hospital, and a Level 1 Trauma Center. UF Health is a premier National Medical Center for Team USA and the only NCI-designed cancer center at a public university in the state of Florida. This role offers the opportunity to practice high-quality, patient-centered radiology in a collaborative academic setting while benefiting from flexible scheduling and strong institutional support for teaching, research, and professional development. Faculty enjoy working with a strong residency program and an excellent referral base. Responsibilities include: Interpret a broad range of nuclear medicine and molecular imaging studies, including PET/CT, SPECT/CT, and general nuclear medicine examinations Supervise and perform diagnostic and therapeutic nuclear medicine procedures, including radiopharmaceutical therapies Collaborate with oncology, cardiology, neurology, and other clinical services to support multidisciplinary patient care Participate in protocol development, quality assurance, and radiation safety initiatives within the nuclear medicine division Teach and mentor radiology residents, fellows, and medical students through case readouts, conferences, and formal educational activities Engagement in scholarly and academic activities Gainesville is a vibrant, affordable community that offers an exceptional quality of life, combining the energy of a major academic center with the charm of a college town. Residents enjoy year-round warm weather, reasonable housing costs, minimal traffic congestion, and a dynamic university atmosphere. Located in North Central Florida, Gainesville provides convenient access to both the Atlantic and Gulf coasts, multiple international airports, world-renowned beaches and major metropolitan areas including Orlando, Tampa and Jacksonville. With a metropolitan population of approximately 350,000, the region is anchored by the University of Florida - one of the nation’s leading public universities - and a prominent Division 1 athletic program. The area offers excellent schools, a growing technology sector, and abundant outdoor recreational opportunities. As a leading academic institution and health system in the Southeast, the University of Florida fosters a strong and supportive environment for clinical care, education, and research. Benefits: Faculty receive a comprehensive benefits package through the University of Florida, including: Health, disability, and life insurance Malpractice coverage (including tail) and sovereign immunity under Florida law Paid continuing medical education (CME) and faculty development funding Reimbursement for licensure and Maintenance of Certification (MOC) expenses Access to leadership development and advanced training through the College of Medicine Expected Salary: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience, academic rank, and clinical expertise. The University of Florida offers a comprehensive benefits package. Required Qualifications: At the time of application, candidates much: Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology Completion of a Nuclear Medicine fellowship Be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida prior to employment Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: Qualified applicants should submit a CV and cover letter for consideration. Final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an institution outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a credentialing service approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES): http://naces.org/ . The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541619/assistant-scientist": {
      "title": "Assistant Scientist",
      "description": "Assistant Scientist Apply now Job no: 541619 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians, Biology/Life Science Department: 29030000 - MD-BIOCHEM - MOLECULAR BIOL Classification Title: Assistant Scientist Classification Minimum Requirements: Highest degree possible in field or equivalent professional experience; Evidence of pertinent experience for the position and qualities for the academic unit. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Medicine's Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology is recruiting a highly motivated Assistant Scientist to join a collaborative research program focused on glycogen metabolism and glycogen storage diseases. This is a full-time, 1.0 FTE, non-tenure-accruing faculty position. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty investigators, research staff, and trainees to design and conduct experiments, analyze complex biological data, lead research initiatives, and contribute to scientific publications and grant development. Key Responsibilities: Design, conduct, and oversee research studies related to glycogen metabolism and glycogen storage diseases. Develop, optimize, and implement laboratory methods and experimental protocols. Analyze and interpret research data, including metabolomics and other large biological datasets. Collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams to advance ongoing scientific projects. Prepare scientific manuscripts, abstracts, presentations, and reports for publication and dissemination. Present research findings at laboratory meetings, conferences, and scientific symposia. Assist in the development and submission of grant proposals and research funding applications. Mentor and provide scientific guidance to research staff, students, and trainees. Maintain accurate research records and ensure compliance with laboratory, university, and funding agency requirements. Stay current with emerging scientific literature and advancements in the field. Grant submission for external funding is expected. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Terminal doctoral degree in Biochemistry, Molecular Biology, or closely related field; demonstrated research experience in a laboratory setting. Preferred: Experience in glycogen metabolism, metabolic diseases, or related biomedical research areas. Knowledge of metabolomics, mass spectrometry, biochemical assays, or molecular biology techniques. Experience analyzing complex biological datasets. Demonstrated record of scientific productivity through publications and presentations. Experience contributing to grant preparation and research funding efforts. Strong organizational, communication, and project management skills. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a collaborative team. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload a cover letter, CV/resume, and contact information for at least two professional references. Publications are welcome under \"other document\" but not required. Final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an institution outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a credentialing service approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES): http://naces.org/ . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541644/clinical-research-coord-ii-department-of-obgyn": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coord II- Department of OBGYN",
      "description": "Clinical Research Coord II- Department of OBGYN Apply now Job no: 541644 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Grant or Research Administration Department: 30070000 - JX-OB-GYN-JACKSONVILLE Classification Title: Clinical Research Coord II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Reporting to the Manager, Clinical Research (CRM) within the UFCOM-J Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, and funded partially from existing research grants, the Clinical Research Coordinator II (CRC) will be the primary contact for coordination of clinical research activities within the department. CRC is expected to work proactively requiring minimal supervision. CRC is expected to perform all Core responsibilities as well as prepare and maintain biosketches for faculty and develop a list of areas of interest for faculty and resident physicians to help identify scholarly activity opportunities. Essential Functions: Faculty Support and Development: Develop and maintain a list of areas of interest for faculty. Assist resident physicians with navigating the IRB process and developing their presentations to ensure compliance with university, state, and federal policies. Project Coordination and Compliance: Monitor and ensure deadlines are met for research-related projects. Serve as a liaison among various stakeholders, ensuring compliance by documenting investigational product accountability and developing informed consent documents . Financial Management and Invoicing: Collaborate with the CRM and Business Manager on financial invoicing for vendors and study sponsors, including preparation of sponsor invoicing and resolving billing issues for study subjects. Oversee study material preparation and assist faculty and resident physicians with the development and submission of pre-award materials while monitoring post-award costs and effort. Event Coordination and Communication: Assist the CRM with the coordination of the quarterly Scholarly Activity Forum. Serve as the primary point of contact from the division of research within the OB/GYN department for the GME Administrative team regarding Resident Thesis Day. RFP Identification and Communication: Identify RFPs based on the interests of current faculty and resident physicians, and communicate RFP requests Expected Salary: Negotiable base on experience and academic appointment Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Certified Clinical Research Coordinator and/or other professional registration or certification, or medical credentials. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your resume, and 3 references Normal work hours will include a mix of 8 hour shifts Monday through Sunday during the time period of 8:00am to 9:00pm based on study schedules with a mix of day and evening shifts and 2-3 weekend shifts per month. There will be occasional on call duties, and travel for professional presentations and activities. The Search Committee will begin to review applications as soon as an applicant pool is identified. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541677/opspkyelementary-behavior-coach": {
      "title": "OPS-PKY-Elementary Behavior Coach",
      "description": "OPS-PKY-Elementary Behavior Coach Apply now Job no: 541677 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 18180600 - ED-ELEMENTARY SCHOOL Classification Title: OPS-Elementary Behavior Coach Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The primary objective of this position is to support student behavior to enhance overall academic achievement. Support students in developing self-regulation, social-emotional, and positive behavior skills. Coach and support teachers in implementing proactive classroom management strategies, behavior interventions, and practices that promote positive student engagement and self-regulation. Collaborate with teachers, counselors, administrators, and support staff to develop consistent and effective approaches to student behavior. Facilitate restorative conversations following conflicts or behavioral incidents to help students repair relationships, reflect on their choices, and develop problem-solving skills. Build strong partnerships with families and caregivers through proactive communication, collaboration, and shared problem-solving to support student success Observe classrooms and learning environments to identify behavior patterns, contributing factors, and opportunities for prevention and intervention. Complete required data entry and reporting related to student behavior and school safety, including discipline and SESIR reports, to support accurate documentation and monitor behavioral trends. Maintain appropriate documentation of interventions, observations, student progress, and communication with families and staff. Provide proactive student support across classrooms, common areas, arrival and dismissal, and other campus activities to promote a safe, respectful, and positive learning environment. Collaborate with the School Safety Officer, School Resource Officer (SRO), and school administration to support school safety initiatives, implement emergency procedures, and promote student well-being. Expected Salary: $21-$24 / Commensurate with experience & education Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Experience with PreK-5 supervision that includes strategizing as appropriate in maintaining a safe and respectful campus. Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in written communication. Special Instructions to Applicants: This is a 10-month, OPS appointment. In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541687/ops-instructional-technologist": {
      "title": "OPS Instructional Technologist",
      "description": "OPS Instructional Technologist Apply now Job no: 541687 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 02090000 - PV-UNIV CTR-EXCELLC IN TEACH Classification Title: OPS HOURLY NON-SECRETARY/CLERICAL Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree Job Description: The Center for Teaching Excellence (CTE) at the University of Florida is seeking a part‑time OPS Instructional Technologist to support the Center in the effective use of instructional technologies that enhance teaching and learning. This position provides hands‑on assistance with educational technology tools, learning management systems, and faculty development activities. The Instructional Technologist will assist with course and material development, program evaluation, workshop support, and the creation of guides and resources to help instructors. This position also serves as point of contact for office inquiries by email, phone, mail, and in person, providing information about services and resolving routine questions. The position assists with operations, workshop and event planning, program registration and participant tracking, communications for initiatives and campus partnerships, and program evaluation and data collection. This role is well‑suited for graduate students, early‑career instructional technologists, or individuals exploring careers in instructional design, learning technologies, or faculty development. This position is on‑site, located in Gainesville, Florida and is up to 15 hours per week, depending on unit needs. Responsibilities Provide instructional technology expertise and support for CTE materials and programs Assist with the use of Canvas tools, digital learning tools, multimedia platforms, and collaboration technologies used for instruction Support CTE workshops, events, and training sessions, including setup, facilitation assistance, and resource preparation Contribute to the development of documentation, quick‑guides, tutorials, and training materials Participate in exploratory work with emerging instructional technologies, including AI‑supported tools Collaborate with CTE staff and campus partners on teaching‑ and learning‑related initiatives Maintain accurate records of support interactions and project activities Drafting correspondence, reports, and spreadsheets; maintaining files, records, databases, and mailing lists; and updating website content and online resources Expected Salary: $15.00 per hour; commensurate with experience. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree Preferred: Graduate coursework or current enrollment in programs related to instructional technology, education, educational psychology, or related fields Experience supporting instructors, students, or staff in an educational or training environment Familiarity with learning management systems (Canvas preferred) Basic knowledge of teaching and learning principles or interest in developing such knowledge Experience using educational technologies such as video tools, collaboration platforms, or AI‑supported instructional tools Strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff Interest in higher education teaching support and faculty development Special Instructions to Applicants: Work visa sponsorship is not available for this position A criminal background check will be required This position is located in Gainesville, FL, and is not eligible for remote work Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered: Cover letter Resume List of three (3) professional references, including at least one previous or current supervisor This position is up to 15 hours per week, depending on unit needs. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541688/ops-administrative-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Administrative Assistant Apply now Job no: 541688 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 29080100 - MD-PATHOLOGY-GENERAL Classification Title: OPS Administrative Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Job Description: The Department of Pathology, Immunology, and Laboratory Medicine is recruiting for an OPS Administrative Assistant to assist faculty and staff with administrative, research, and teaching correspondence/materials (composition and editing of letters, memos, slides, tables, copying, FedEx etc.). Maintain files as necessary. Assists faculty and Pathology HR with hiring/volunteer paperwork. Sends initial paperwork and contact information to Pathology HR. Inform Pathology HR of changes/update to distributions lists. Assists faculty and staff with appointment scheduling (administrative, EP, conference room). Assist with time approval for supervisors as necessary. Update faculty and lab websites when necessary. Answers and directs incoming phone calls and messages. Fill out Faculty Leave Forms when appropriate. Assist faculty, staff, postdocs, graduate students, etc. with travel (domestic and foreign) arrangements (registration, airline, lodging, etc.). Submit Travel Authorizations prior to travel and make sure expense reports are processed accurately and in a timely manner using the proper funding. Fill out Faculty Leave Forms and inform supervisors of travel plans when appropriate. Assists faculty / lab personnel with ordering of lab supplies and equipment for nine labs, using PO’s and PCard purchases. Reconcile PCard charges weekly. Make sure invoices are processed in a timely manner and fiscal information is sent to Pathology Fiscal for accurate processing. Review (monthly) PCard Reporting. Work with faculty to efficiently and accurately expend budgeted funds. Inform faculty of fund balances when necessary. Assist with maintenance/repair and location of equipment when necessary. Assist with miscellaneous secretarial duties (letters, copying, mail, FedEx, follow-up on projects, etc.). Serve as back-up to the other Team Members as necessary. Assist other Team Members to standardize training and fiscal procedures (PCard, travel, etc.) and to strength our Team. Back-up for package retrieval and distribution as necessary. Assist with special projects and other duties as assigned and follow-up on status/completion. Expected Salary: Starting salary is between $18.00 - $19.00 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Preferred: Certification in UF Fiscal Management and Academic Department Support Knowledge of: Business and accounting procedures including certification in business communication, University/College of Medicine rules and regulations particularly related to subcontracting pre- and post-awards for grants Skills: Effective use of PC, internet and e-mail. Abilities: Problem solving and making decisions under stressful conditions, handling multiple tasks, and determining work priorities, working independently. Experience in: Microsoft Office including word processing and database and spreadsheet applications. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 12 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541678/federal-work-study-advising-assistant": {
      "title": "Federal Work Study Advising Assistant",
      "description": "Federal Work Study Advising Assistant Apply now Job no: 541678 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Student Services, Academic Advising/Support Department: 60320000 - AG-FAM YOUTH - COMM SCI Classification Title: FWS- STU AST-CLERICAL & ADMIN Classification Minimum Requirements: Be a current University of Florida full-time student in good standing with the University Qualify for the Federal Work-Study (FWS) Program in Fall and Spring Ability to dedicate 10-15 hours per week Job Description: The student assistant position in FYCS is for a Part-Time (10-20 hours based on work permit) Federal Work Study Student to work in the advising office. Family, Youth and Community Sciences (FYCS) is an applied social science department that provides education and experience for careers in human services, community development, cooperative extension, and youth professions. Description of possible duties: Assisting with departmental events Answer phone calls, take messages, and return phone calls Assist with administrative tasks Receive visitors and answers basic questions from students Maintain confidentiality of student and/or employee records Office duties such as scanning, copying, and mailing Run clerical errands on campus Word processing, editing, transcribing, proofreading, data entry, etc. Document preparation Assist in creating documents or presentations for internal or external department needs Other duties as assigned Expected Salary: $15.00/hour Required Qualifications: Be a current University of Florida full-time student in good standing with the University Qualify for the Federal Work-Study (FWS) Program in Fall and Spring Ability to dedicate 10-15 hours per week Preferred: Fine attention to detail, professionalism, dependability and effective communication skills Ability to work as a team member Prior customer service skills are preferred Demonstrated communication, organizational and leadership skills Effective interpersonal communication skills Self-starter; self-motivated; timely Experience using Microsoft Office, Excel, & Outlook Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. ALL students applying to this position must submit current UF Federal Work Study Award stating proof of Federal Work Study. Students seeking FWS employment should print/screenshot a copy of their Financial Aid Award Page, which contains the Federal Work Study award as proof of FWS eligibility. To locate your Financial Aid Award Page, go to https://one.uf.edu/financialaid/aidyear . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 09 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539095/clinical-asstasofull-professor-539095": {
      "title": "Clinical ASST/ASO/FULL Professor -  (539095)",
      "description": "Clinical ASST/ASO/FULL Professor - (539095) Apply now Job no: 539095 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Alachua Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29160406 - MD-FAMILY MEDICINE-JONESVILLE Classification Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: M.D. or D.O. degree or equivalent. Board Certification or eligibility in Family Medicine, and current Florida medical license or eligibility is required. Job Description: The University of Florida Department of Community Health and Family Medicine (CHFM) is seeking a Family Medicine physician (MD/DO) to join the UF Health Family Medicine Clinic in Gainesville. This is a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position at the rank of Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor, with rank commensurate with qualifications and experience. The selected candidate will provide direct patient care in an ambulatory setting while contributing to the department's educational mission. Teaching responsibilities include working with University of Florida College of Medicine medical students and Family Medicine residents during clinical rotations, when applicable. Faculty are expected to participate in educational conferences, seminars, and lectures as part of the department's academic activities. Clinical Responsibilities The physician will provide comprehensive primary care services at the UF Health Family Medicine Clinic serving patients across the lifespan. The clinic supports a collaborative, team-based care model that includes physicians, advanced practice providers, nurses, a registered nurse health coach, and pharmacist support. Key responsibilities include: Delivering high-quality patient care in the primary care clinic Participating in clinic and/or inpatient call rotations, depending on departmental needs and candidate interest Collaborating with and supervising Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioners (ARNPs) and Physician Assistants (PAs) as part of a team-based care model Contributing to departmental service and other faculty responsibilities as assigned Educational Responsibilities Faculty are expected to contribute to the educational mission of the department by: Teaching medical students and Family Medicine residents during patient care activities Participating in inpatient teaching rounds when applicable Engaging in departmental educational conferences, seminars, and lectures The department encourages scholarly activity and professional development. Faculty have access to experienced mentors and departmental support for developing scholarly work, presenting at professional meetings, publishing, and pursuing career advancement opportunities. Expected Salary: Salary commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: An M.D. or D.O. degree (or equivalent), board certification or eligible in Family Medicine Eligible or have a have a Florida medical license Proven experience in providing comprehensive primary care services to patients of all ages Strong diagnostic and clinical skills, with the ability to manage a wide range of acute and chronic conditions Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a patient-centered approach Ability to work collaboratively in a multidisciplinary team environment Experience with Electronic Health Record (E.H.R.) systems is essential Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue to receive applications until the position is closed. All applications must be submitted at: https://jobs.ufl.edu? Inquiries and nominations can be sent to CHFM-HR at careers@chfm.ufl.edu Complete applications must include the following files in PDF format: (1) cover letter (letter of interest) addressed to: Dr. Danielle Nelson, Search Committee Chair ; (2) a curriculum vitae; The final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Applications must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540423/ufhealth-family-physician-ocala-heath-brook-chfm540423": {
      "title": "UFHealth Family Physician - Ocala Heath Brook (CHFM)(#540423)",
      "description": "UFHealth Family Physician - Ocala Heath Brook (CHFM)(#540423) Apply now Job no: 540423 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Marion Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29169101 - MD-CHFM HEATH BROOK Classification Title: UF Health Physician Classification Minimum Requirements: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Job Description: UF Health Regional Physician Network is seeking a Family Medicine Physician to join UF Health Family Medicine – Ocala Heath Brook. This is an outstanding opportunity to join a patient-centered, collegial team committed to delivering high-quality clinical care. We welcome applicants interested in either full-time or part-time employment. The anticipated FTE may be flexible based on the selected candidate’s interests and the needs of the department. The selected candidate will receive a market-based, competitive salary, with benefits eligibility and available benefit options varying based on the FTE of the appointment. UF Health – The Power of Together! At UF Health, together, we strive to create unstoppable momentum toward the goal of improving individual and community health through discovery, clinical and translational science and technology, exceptional education and patient-centered, innovative, high-quality health care. At the heart of our mission is to provide high-quality clinical care and to promise every patient their best experience possible. Ready to join us? About UF Health: UF Health represents the shared vision and commitment to patient care excellence of more than 22,000 employees of the University of Florida Health Science Center and UF Health Shands health care system. With campuses in Gainesville and Jacksonville, UF Health includes six health colleges, nine research institutes and centers, two teaching hospitals, two specialty hospitals, and a host of physician medical practices and outpatient services throughout north central and northeast Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care; innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences; and high-impact research across the spectrum of basic, translational, and clinical investigation. The UF Health Regional Physicians Network represents the extension of our spectrum of patient-care services to regional community under the University of Florida’s College of Medicine. If you require an accommodation due to a disability to apply for this position, please contact the ADA Office at (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). For more information, visit the UF ADA Compliance website: https://ada.ufl.edu/ . Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Expected Salary: Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Benefits: The University of Florida provides comprehensive benefits programs, including the following: Florida has no State Income Tax Professional Liability is covered at no cost to members through Florida’s Self-Insurance Program. Tail coverage is not necessarily due to occurrence-based coverage Florida Birth-Related Neurological Injury Compensation Association (NICA) paid or reimbursed Professional Development and Continuing Medical Education (CME) time is allotted each fiscal year, memberships, dues, etc. Exemption available for D.E.A. license fee Paid Florida Medical License renewals for active faculty Low-Cost Health Insurance: UF participates in state and university-sponsored benefits programs for individuals, families, and domestic partners. Retirement Options: UF offers attractive retirement options through the Florida Retirement System to secure your future. Personal Time Off: UF employees have access to a generous paid leave plan (approximately 22 vacation days, 13 sick days, and 11 paid holidays annually, plus four additional days during the holidays!), a sick leave pool, paid maternity/paternity leave, paid medical leave, and leave payouts. GatorPerks: discount significant savings for various businesses and retailers For more information on the benefits, please click here: https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits/ Also, as a state organization, you might be eligible for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) program. See https://studentaid.gov/manage-loans/forgiveness-cancellation/public-service for more information. Required Qualifications: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Preferred: Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida Federal DEA Certification. Medical Degree – M.D., D.O., or foreign equivalent. Board certified in Family Medicine. Completion of an accredited residency program. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload cover letter, resume/CV, and three letters of recommendation. This requisition has been reposted and extended. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes. Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540877/administrative-assistant-i": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant I",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant I Apply now Job no: 540877 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29130100 - MD-RADIOLOGY-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Administrative Assistant I Classification Minimum Requirements High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Administrative Assistant I provides essential administrative, clerical, academic, and fiscal support to the department and assigned faculty. This position plays an important role in supporting efficient day-to-day operations and advancing the department’s clinical, academic, research, and educational activities. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, and service-focused, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and communicate effectively with faculty, staff, trainees, visitors, vendors, and external partners. Administrative Support Provides comprehensive administrative support to the department and assigned faculty. Receives, screens, sorts, and distributes incoming mail and correspondence. Answers departmental telephone lines, responds to routine inquiries, and directs calls appropriately. Maintains office supply inventories and coordinates the purchase of supplies, furniture, and equipment. Coordinates conference room schedules, meetings, seminars, and special events, including preparing meeting materials, agendas, and room arrangements. Prepares, edits, and distributes correspondence, reports, presentations, and other professional documents on behalf of faculty and departmental leadership. Manages calendars, schedules appointments, and coordinates divisional meetings, including preparing and distributing agendas and meeting minutes. Serves as a primary point of contact for faculty, staff, trainees, visitors, vendors, and external organizations, providing excellent customer service and facilitating effective communication. Provides backup support to the Chair’s Executive Assistant, including assisting with the preparation and tracking of documentation, deadlines, and other time-sensitive activities to ensure continuity of operations. Faculty, Academic, and Research Support Provides administrative support for faculty scholarly, academic, research, and educational activities. Assists with manuscript preparation, formatting, editing, and proofreading. Organizes references, tables, figures, appendices, and supporting materials for publication. Ensures documents comply with applicable journal submission requirements. Serves as a liaison with journals, publishers, departmental offices, and external organizations regarding manuscript submissions, revisions, and publication activities. Assists faculty with educational materials, presentations, and other academic projects that support the department’s teaching and research missions. Fiscal Support Supports the daily operations of the department’s fiscal office while ensuring compliance with university and departmental financial policies and procedures. Coordinates the timely processing of purchase orders, payments, grant expenditures, travel transactions, expense reimbursements, and income deposits through the HRIS and other university systems for both the University of Florida and the Florida Clinical Practice Association (FCPA). Processes checks, invoices, journal entries, requisitions, vouchers, and procurement transactions for departmental PCard holders. Reviews financial documentation for completeness and accuracy and maintains organized fiscal records. Serves as a liaison among vendors, faculty, staff, and central administrative offices to support efficient and timely financial operations. Travel Coordination and Institutional Reporting Coordinates travel through UFGO for faculty, staff, students, and guests attending meetings, seminars, presentations, and conferences. Arranges transportation, lodging, conference registration, and other travel accommodations. Processes travel authorizations and encumbrances in PeopleSoft. Prepares and submits post-travel expense reports in accordance with university policies. Compiles and submits data for annual surveys and institutional reporting requirements, including reports for MGMA, AAARAD, University Tax Services, UWO, Auxiliary Service Centers, Unrelated Business Income Tax, and Incidental Trust Funds. Additional Responsibilities Performs other related administrative, clerical, and operational duties and assists with special projects as assigned by the supervisor or departmental leadership. Expected Salary: $19.00 - $22.00, commensurate with experience. Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Experience supporting faculty, physicians, or executive leadership in a fast-paced, complex organization. Working knowledge of University of Florida administrative and financial systems, including PeopleSoft, UFGO, myUFL, or similar enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems. Experience processing travel authorizations, expense reimbursements, procurement transactions, and purchasing in accordance with university or government policies. Demonstrated experience coordinating meetings, conferences, seminars, and special events. Experience preparing professional correspondence, reports, presentations, meeting agendas, and meeting minutes. Familiarity with manuscript preparation, journal submission processes, or supporting academic and research activities. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, particularly Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Adobe Acrobat, with the ability to create and edit complex documents and spreadsheets. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and work independently while meeting competing deadlines. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail and a commitment to providing outstanding customer service. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Please list three (3) professional references. This position is eligible for veterans' preference. If you are claiming veterans' preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See UF’s Veterans' Preference Page for more details. This position is being reposted. All previous applicants are still under review and need not reapply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment No Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541633/clinical-assistantassociate-professor-family-medicine": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine Apply now Job no: 541633 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Health Care Administration/Support, Medicine/Physicians Department: 30160000 - JX-COMMUNITY MEDICINE-JAX Classification Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine Classification Minimum Requirements: Candidates must be MD/DO and have a Florida Medical License Job Description: The Department of Community Health and Family Medicine at the University of Florida College of Medicine-Jacksonville seeks a family medicine/internal medicine physician, MD/DO, to join us. The position is for Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor level on a clinical non-tenure accruing track at our outpatient care office - UF Health Family Medicine. This position is up to fulltime and will report to the medical director and chair of the department at the University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville. Base salary is based on experience and guaranteed with significant additional productivity incentives and benefits package. UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/ . Expected Salary: Negotiable upon Education and Experience Preferred: Board certified or board eligible Special Instructions to Applicants: This position is open until filled. The Search Committee will begin to review applications on January 19, 2025. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541643/manager-clinical-research-department-of-obgyn": {
      "title": "Manager, Clinical Research- Department of OBGYN",
      "description": "Manager, Clinical Research- Department of OBGYN Apply now Job no: 541643 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 30070000 - JX-OB-GYN-JACKSONVILLE Classification Title: MGR, Clinical Research Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in appropriate areas of specialization and two years of experience. Job Description: Funded partially from existing research grants, the Clinical Research Managers (CRM) work at the departmental level under the supervision of the Director, Healthcare Administration, to support department Principal Investigators, Co-Investigators, resident physicians, and central administration personnel by providing guidance on compliance with federal, state and university policies, financial, personnel, and other aspects of Clinical Research. This position will assist faculty in developing high-quality proposals, manage grant compliance reviews, and supervise a Clinical Research Coordinator II as well as other support staff as appropriate to ensure all submissions meet sponsor and university guidelines, while acting as a liaison between investigators and campus administrators . Essential Functions: Project Management and Oversight: Organize, direct, and manage all OB/GYN department sponsored projects, including award management, compliance, contract negotiation, budgeting, invoicing sponsors, and monitoring study progress to ensure alignment with institutional policies and regulations.. Grant and Contract Review: Manage the review process for grant and contract awards, ensuring compliance with sponsor and University regulations while supervisingnegotiations with grant and contracting officers to advocate for appropriate budget requests and terms. Faculty Documentation Maintenance: Update and maintain faculty Curriculum Vitae monthly to reflect all studies and publications accurately, ensuring that faculty and UFCOM research FTE reporting is conducted in a timely manner ahead of effort period deadlines . Scholarly Activity Coordination: Coordinate and facilitate a quarterly Scholarly Activity Forum, collaborating with the CRM and administrative team members to support the design and execution of the forum while documenting costs associated with scholarly activities with the business manager and CRC II for accurate and timely entry. Financial Oversight and Budget Preparation: Collaborate with the business manager and CRC II to document declared and miscellaneous costs associated with scholarly activities, resolve discrepancies with Payroll, conduct final reviews before submission to the Department Administrator, and assist in the preparation of the annual department budget related to research and scholarly activities . Expected Salary: Negotiable base on experience and academic appointment Required Qualifications: Master's degree in appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor's degree in appropriate areas of specialization and two years of experience. Preferred: RN, BSN, Certified Clinical Research Coordinator (CCRC) Experience within UF College of Medicine Research Special Instructions to Applicants: Normal work hours will include a mix of 8 hour shifts Monday through Sunday during the time period of 8:00am to 9:00pm based on study schedules with a mix of day and evening shifts and 2-3 weekend shifts per month. There will be occasional on call duties, and travel for professional presentations and activities. The Search Committee will begin to review applications as soon as an applicant pool is identified. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541646/regulatory-affairs-manager": {
      "title": "Regulatory Affairs Manager",
      "description": "Regulatory Affairs Manager Apply now Job no: 541646 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Grant or Research Administration, Health Care Administration/Support, Legal/Audit Services/Compliance Department: 27320503 - HA-UFHCI CRO REGULATORY Classification Title: MGR, Clinical Research Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor’s degree in appropriate areas of specialization and two years of experience. Job Description: The UF Health Cancer Institute is the 72nd NCI designated cancer center and the only one at a public university in the State of Florida. As a matrix cancer center, we span all of the University of Florida's 16 colleges, pulling together a world-class, multi-disciplinary membership of over 350 faculty and 150 staff to address the challenges of the cancer burden faced by the population we serve as we work together to find a cure. As a Regulatory Affairs Manager at the UF Health Cancer Institute (UFHCI), you will be responsible for leading regulatory compliance operations within the Clinical Research Office, overseeing Institutional Review Board (IRB) regulatory processes, and supervising a team supporting cancer clinical trials. Strong leadership, regulatory expertise, and the ability to collaborate across multidisciplinary clinical research teams are necessary for success in this role. In your new role you will be responsible for the following: Overseeing regulatory operations for clinical trial protocols, including IRB submissions, approvals, renewals, amendments, and regulatory documentation tracking. Leading, mentoring, and managing regulatory staff, including IRB Specialists and Assistants, while supporting staff development, training, and performance management. Providing regulatory guidance to investigators, research teams, and institutional partners to ensure compliance with federal regulations, sponsor requirements, and institutional policies. Directing portfolio oversight and quality assurance activities, including audit readiness, regulatory reporting, and clinical trial management system (CTMS) compliance. Developing and implementing standard operating procedures, workflow improvements, and compliance monitoring strategies to support research excellence and operational efficiency. This is a management level position, ideal for candidates with experience in clinical research regulatory affairs, human subjects research compliance, and team leadership within an academic or healthcare research environment. Employees in these roles operate as part of our collaborative research enterprise and are fundamental to the progress of cancer research being conducted at the University of Florida. A complete job description will be provided to candidates selected for interview. Expected Salary: $87,500 - $95,000 This is a TEAMS position, and is eligible for a suite of excellent benefits, retirement options, and paid leave . About the City of Gainesville Home to the University of Florida, one of the nation's top public universities, Gainesville offers vibrant academic and healthcare communities alongside an affordable cost of living, no state income tax, and mild winters. Enjoy the outdoors with over 30 miles of bike trails, freshwater springs, and numerous water activities, plus easy access to beaches and world-class theme parks. Gainesville combines historic charm with modern amenities, including a great school system, a lively downtown, and farmers' markets and craft breweries. Discover professional growth and quality of life in Gainesville—where community, innovation, and work-life balance meet! For more information, check out: The Guide to Greater Gainesville and Explore Gainesville in 60 seconds . Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in appropriate area of specialization; or a bachelor’s degree in appropriate areas of specialization and two years of experience. Professional clinical research and/or oncology certification (through SOCRA, ACRP, etc.) are required at the earliest of 12 months from hire or eligibility. Preferred: Knowledge/Experience: Master’s Degree in Regulatory Affairs, Health Care, Public Health, or a related field. Ten or more years of research experience and/or training in an Academic Medical Center. Prior experience as a supervisor or team lead and/or completion of leadership/management training program (eg. Managing at UF – The Supervisory Challenge). Qualities: Exceptional customer service with a professional, trustworthy, approachable demeanor and strong interpersonal skills, as well as the ability and desire to work with a broad range of people and appreciate a culturally diverse organization. Highly resourceful team-player with the ability to independently and with limited supervision work toward common goals as part of an administrative team. Demonstrated integrity, dependability, sound judgment, teamwork and resourcefulness to establish and maintain collaborative, positive and effective working relationships with internal and external partners. Proven sense of professional ethics and conduct, understanding and effective use of Emotional Intelligence strategies and skills. Forward-thinking mentality, actively seeking opportunities to learn, seek out, and apply new knowledge, methods, and information and proposing creative solutions with strong decision-making capability. Collaborative, uplifting, and positive personality. Ability to work with multigenerational teams. Skills/Abilities: Expertise in NCTN/ECTCN Cooperative group trials. Proficient time management skills and ability to successfully manage multiple priorities. Demonstrated ability to achieve high performance goals and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficient time management skills and ability to successfully manage multiple priorities seamlessly with excellent attention to detail. Excellent meeting coordination skills, delegation, and attention to detail. Exceptional interpersonal skills – in person, online and by phone, always maintaining a high level of professionalism and commitment to confidentiality. Demonstrated proficiency in project management, clinical research/trials experience is highly desirable. Special Instructions to Applicants: The University of Florida is a member of the State University System of Florida and an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment based on merit. Applicants must upload a copy of the following documents to be considered for this position: Cover Letter or Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae or Resume List of Three Professional References This is not a remote work position, and is located on the University of Florida's Main Campus in Gainesville, FL. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 27 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541648/clinical-assistantassociate-professor-family-medicine": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine Apply now Job no: 541648 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Medicine/Physicians Department: 30160000 - JX-COMMUNITY MEDICINE-JAX Classification Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor- Family Medicine Classification Minimum Requirements: Candidates must be MD/DO and have a Florida Medical License Job Description: The Department of Community Health and Family Medicine at the University of Florida College of Medicine-Jacksonville seeks a family medicine/internal medicine physician, MD/DO, to join us. The position is for Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor level on a clinical non-tenure accruing track at our outpatient care office - UF Health Family Medicine. This position is up to fulltime and will report to the medical director and chair of the department at the University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville. Base salary is based on experience and guaranteed with significant additional productivity incentives and benefits package. UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/ . Expected Salary: Negotiable Required Qualifications Candidates must be MD/DO and have a Florida Medical License Preferred: Board certified or board eligible Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will begin to review applications on January 19, 2025. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541651/associate-or-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Associate or Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Associate or Assistant Professor Apply now Job no: 541651 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Social/Behavioral Science, Counseling/Community Outreach/Social Work Department: 33070000 - HP-CLINICAL - HLTH PSYCHOLOGY Classification Title: Associate or Assistant Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology with a pre-doctoral internship from an APA-accredited program; candidates must be licensed or license-eligible in the State of Florida. Job Description: The Department of Clinical and Health Psychology (CHP) within the College of Public Health and Health Professions at the University of Florida is recruiting for three faculty positions in clinical health psychology at the Assistant or Associate Professor level. These are full-time (1.0 FTE), 12-month tenure-track positions; preference is at the Associate Professor rank, but applicants at the Assistant Professor rank are welcome. We are seeking psychologists with research and clinical interests in health psychology. We welcome all subspecialties; however, established collaborations with UF Health include solid organ transplant, psycho-oncology, pain and chronic illness, weight management, and/or sleep. The ideal candidates for these positions are expected to display a strong career record of scientific and scholarly achievements relative to other professionals at their current professional rank; have active interest and skills in building a collaborative research program within a dynamic, interprofessional, academic health center environment; add depth and/or breadth to existing areas of specialization represented by existing faculty in the Medical/Health Psychology area; and possess competency and willingness to engage in (i) mentorship of research and (ii) supervision of behavioral health service delivery within a Scientist-Practitioner graduate training program emphasizing evidence-based practice. The Candidates will work closely with colleagues within the department, physicians, and other healthcare providers in a dynamic healthcare environment. If applicable, day-to-day clinical service delivery responsibilities may take place across a variety of settings within the UF Health Science Center, including our outpatient UF Psychology Specialties Clinic, other UF Health Outpatient Clinics, or the inpatient units at UF Health/Shands Hospital. Taking into account interest and departmental needs, the faculty members will be expected to participate in clinical coverage for other departments' faculty as needed. In addition, classroom teaching may be assigned as part of the faculty member’s responsibilities. The Department ( http://chp.phhp.ufl.edu ): CHP manages a unique, freestanding academic clinical psychology program with 38 core faculty, more than 60 doctoral students, over 10 Interns, and multiple Postdoctoral Fellows. CHP has APA-accredited clinical psychology PhD and Internship programs. The Department has a 50-year history of providing APA-accredited training in clinical psychology and advanced specialty-specific training in three concentration areas: Clinical Health Psychology, Clinical Child/Pediatric Psychology, and Neuropsychology. The doctoral program has been ranked in the 93rd percentile by the National Research Council’s data-based ranking system. The Institution ( www.ufl.edu ): UF is ranked among the top five U.S. public universities and is a comprehensive Research I institution with a wide range of academic departments and programs. The College of Public Health and Health Professions ( www.phhp.ufl.edu ) is part of the University’s Health Science Center. The UF Health Science Center ( https://ufhealth.org/about-us ) is the country’s only academic health center with six health-related colleges located on a single, contiguous campus. They include the colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine. The Health Science Center generates more than half of UF’s total research awards. The UF Health Science Center is closely affiliated with UF Health, part of the University of Florida Health System. Within the healthcare system are an 850-bed teaching hospital, an 81-bed psychiatric hospital, a 60-bed inpatient rehabilitation facility, and numerous outpatient and specialty clinics, including the Psychology Specialties Clinic run by the Department of Clinical and Health Psychology. The Academic Health Center also partners with the adjacent Malcom Randall VA Medical Center and the UF Academic Health Center Regional campus located in Jacksonville, FL. Additional major institutes and centers at the University of Florida include the UF Health Cancer Center, the UF Genetics Institute, the Clinical and Translational Science Institute, and the McKnight Brain Institute, all of which provide state-of-the-art environments and access to patient samples and large data sets for faculty collaboration. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with experience. The University of Florida (UF) offers an exceptional benefits package, including health, dental and vision insurance; state retirement plans; a generous leave program; and tuition assistance. UF is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) eligible employer. For more information on benefits, please visit UF HR Benefits and Rewards at https://benefits.hr.ufl.edu/. Required Qualifications: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology with a pre-doctoral internship from an APA-accredited program; candidates must be licensed or license-eligible in the State of Florida. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidates for the position will have prior postdoctoral work in clinical or health psychology, experience at an academic health center, and an interest in student education and training. For hires at the associate professor level, a strong record of extramural funding and publishing in health psychology is essential. Hires at the assistant professor level should demonstrate potential to develop such a record. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please submit your application online at https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/ and attach your CV, letter of interest, and contact information for three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until a suitable applicant pool has been established. For questions, please contact Dr. Stephen Anton ( santon@ufl.edu ), Chair, Search Committee. Final candidates will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. Final candidates will also be required to provide three letters of recommendation upon hire. If an accommodation is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the U.S. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida’s Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541652/associate-or-assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Associate or Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Associate or Assistant Professor Apply now Job no: 541652 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Social/Behavioral Science, Counseling/Community Outreach/Social Work Department: 33070000 - HP-CLINICAL - HLTH PSYCHOLOGY Classification Title: Associate or Assistant Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology with a pre-doctoral internship from an APA-accredited program; candidates must be licensed or license-eligible in the State of Florida. Job Description: The Department of Clinical and Health Psychology (CHP) within the College of Public Health and Health Professions at the University of Florida is recruiting for three faculty positions in clinical child/pediatric psychology. These are full-time (1.0 FTE), 12-month tenure-track positions; preference is at the Associate Professor rank, but applicants at the Assistant Professor rank are welcome. While broad areas of research will be considered , there is particular interest in psychologists with research and clinical specialization in 1) trauma care and suicide prevention, 2) pediatric psychology (i.e., diabetes, sleep medicine, asthma/pulmonology), and 3) autism spectrum disorders. The ideal candidates for these positions are expected to display a strong career record of scientific and scholarly achievements relative to other professionals at their current professional rank; have active interest and skills in building a collaborative research program within a dynamic, interprofessional, academic health center environment; add depth and/or breadth to existing areas of specialization represented by existing faculty in the Child/Pedaitric Psychology area; and possess competency and willingness to engage in (i) mentorship of research and (ii) supervision of behavioral health service delivery within a Scientist-Practitioner graduate training program emphasizing evidence-based practice. The Candidates will work closely with colleagues within the department, physicians, and other healthcare providers in a dynamic healthcare environment. If applicable, day-to-day clinical service delivery responsibilities may take place across a variety of settings within the UF Health Science Center, including our outpatient UF Psychology Specialties Clinic, other UF Health Outpatient Clinics, or the inpatient units at UF Health/Shands Hospital. Taking into account interest and departmental needs, the faculty members will be expected to participate in clinical coverage for other departments' faculty as needed. In addition, classroom teaching may be assigned as part of the faculty member’s responsibilities. The Department ( http://chp.phhp.ufl.edu ): CHP manages a unique, freestanding academic clinical psychology program with 38 core faculty, more than 60 doctoral students, over 10 Interns, and multiple Postdoctoral Fellows. CHP has APA-accredited clinical psychology PhD and Internship programs. The Department has a 50-year history of providing APA-accredited training in clinical psychology and advanced specialty-specific training in three concentration areas: Clinical Child/Pediatric Psychology, Clinical Health Psychology, and Neuropsychology. The doctoral program has been ranked in the 93rd percentile by the National Research Council’s data-based ranking system. The Institution ( www.ufl.edu ): UF is ranked among the top five U.S. public universities and is a comprehensive Research I institution with a wide range of academic departments and programs. The College of Public Health and Health Professions ( www.phhp.ufl.edu ) is part of the University’s Health Science Center. The UF Health Science Center ( https://ufhealth.org/about-us ) is the country’s only academic health center with six health-related colleges located on a single, contiguous campus. They include the colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine. The Health Science Center generates more than half of UF’s total research awards. The UF Health Science Center is closely affiliated with UF Health, part of the University of Florida Health System. Within the healthcare system are an 850-bed teaching hospital, an 81-bed psychiatric hospital, a 60-bed inpatient rehabilitation facility, and numerous outpatient and specialty clinics, including the Psychology Specialties Clinic run by the Department of Clinical and Health Psychology. The Academic Health Center also partners with the adjacent Malcom Randall VA Medical Center and the UF Academic Health Center Regional campus located in Jacksonville, FL. Additional major institutes and centers at the University of Florida include the Center for Autism and Related Disabilities, the Clinical and Translational Science Institute, and the McKnight Brain Institute, all of which provide state-of-the-art environments and access to patient samples and large data sets for faculty collaboration. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with experience. The University of Florida (UF) offers an exceptional benefits package, including health, dental and vision insurance; state retirement plans; a generous leave program; and tuition assistance. UF is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) eligible employer. For more information on benefits, please visit UF HR Benefits and Rewards at https://benefits.hr.ufl.edu/. Required Qualifications: Applicants must have a doctoral degree in Clinical Psychology with a pre-doctoral internship from an APA-accredited program; candidates must be licensed or license-eligible in the State of Florida. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidates for the position will have prior postdoctoral work in clinical or health psychology, experience at an academic health center, and an interest in student education and training. For hires at the associate professor level, a strong record of extramural funding and publishing in health psychology is essential. Hires at the assistant professor level should demonstrate potential to develop such a record. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please submit your application online at https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/ and attach your CV, letter of interest, and contact information for three references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until a suitable applicant pool has been established. For questions, please contact Dr. David Janicke ( djanicke@phhp.ufl.edu ), Chair, Search Committee. Final candidates will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. Final candidates will also be required to provide three letters of recommendation upon hire. If an accommodation is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the U.S. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida’s Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
