    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541657/lecturer-in-ai-ethics-and-the-ethics-of-technology": {
      "title": "LECTURER in AI Ethics and the Ethics of Technology",
      "description": "LECTURER in AI Ethics and the Ethics of Technology Apply now Job no: 541657 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 16340000 - LS-PHILOSOPHY Classification Title: LECTURER in AI Ethics and the Ethics of Technology Minimum Requirements: Applicants will have a Ph.D. in Philosophy or complete the Ph.D. by date of hire and will provide evidence of effective teaching Job Description: The Department of Philosophy at the University of Florida, College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, invites applications for a nine-month, full-time, non-tenure-accruing position at the rank of Lecturer beginning August 16, 2027, where the applicant must have the ability to teach courses in AI Ethics and Ethics of Technology. The position will be renewed yearly, contingent on funding and successful performance of assigned job duties. Lecturer positions at the University of Florida come with a full benefits package and have their own promotion track, parallel to that for tenure-track faculty, from Lecturer, to Senior Lecture, and finally to Master Lecturer. Full-time lecturers are typically assigned 6 courses per academic year along with some service commitments for the department. Teaching assignments may include both undergraduate and graduate courses at all levels, and lecturers may (if they so desire) serve on dissertation committees. In addition to teaching courses in AI Ethics and Ethics of Technology, the successful candidate will have opportunities to teach advanced courses in their areas of specialization and are encouraged to develop such. Lecturers have regular voting rights in departmental governance and the opportunity to participate in governance across the university as well. In addition, they can apply for additional summer teaching jobs to help meet significant demand for the department’s courses The department has grown substantially in recent years through a series of new hires. While it remains committed to robust coverage of all the core areas of philosophy, it has developed particular strengths in the ethics of technology and the philosophy of artificial intelligence. The successful candidate will join a department with a critical mass of colleagues working on these questions, within a university that has made artificial intelligence a defining institutional priority. The University of Florida is home to the HiPerGator AI supercomputer and was recently ranked first in the nation in an assessment of institutional AI readiness. The position therefore offers an unusually broad audience for teaching in AI ethics and rich opportunities for collaboration with colleagues in engineering, data science, law, medicine, business, and the social sciences. To learn more about the Department of Philosophy, applicants are encouraged to visit the departmental website ( Department of Philosophy ). Expected Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. UF offers a strong benefits package for eligible faculty appointments, including health insurance, paid leave (as applicable), and retirement options. Learn more here . Required Qualifications: Applicants will have a Ph.D. in Philosophy or complete the Ph.D. by date of hire and will provide evidence of effective teaching. Preferred: An ideal applicant will have interest in research in AI Ethics or Ethics of Technology as a supplement to their teaching in such courses. Interest in other areas of applied ethics or adjacent areas of philosophy of mind, philosophy of cognitive science or philosophy of science would also be a plus. Evidence of successful work with undergraduates in independent studies or honors theses would also be welcome. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applications must be submitted online. Click on Apply Now at the top of this posting. A complete application includes: Letter of application summarizing the applicant's qualifications, interests, and suitability for the position A complete curriculum vitae A teaching portfolio, including a statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of teaching effectiveness (which can include syllabi, peer teaching evaluations, and/or student teaching evaluations) A writing sample of moderate length Names and contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin on January 1, 2027 and will continue until a successful applicant is selected. Only applications submitted by January 1, 2027 will be guaranteed review. All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States require evaluation by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541659/assistantin-student-success-advisor": {
      "title": "Assistant-In / Student Success Advisor",
      "description": "Assistant-In / Student Success Advisor Apply now Job no: 541659 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Academic Advising/Support, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 02080000 - PV-UF STUDENT SUCCESS ADMIN Classification Title: AST IN Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience in academic advising, student success, student development, or related student support services within a higher education setting. Strong understanding of student success principles, academic planning, and the factors that contribute to student retention and persistence. Demonstrated ability to develop and deliver workshops, presentations, and engagement initiatives for diverse student audiences. Experience collaborating with faculty, staff, and campus partners across multiple colleges or departments. Excellent written and verbal communication, and organizational skills. Job Description: The Student Success Advisor serves as a key member of the Office of Undergraduate Education and Student Success (UESS), supporting students as they explore academic pathways, transition into degree-granting majors, and develop strategies for academic success. This position provides centralized advising for exploratory students, coordinates student success initiatives, and collaborates with campus partners to enhance retention, persistence, and engagement. The Student Success Advisor also supports UF Preview operations and develops programs that help students make informed academic and career decisions. Responsibilities include: Provide holistic academic advising and support for exploratory students, helping them evaluate academic options, establish goals, and develop plans for successful transition into degree-granting majors. Monitor student progress and implement proactive outreach strategies to support retention, persistence, and timely graduation. Guide students through academic exploration and major-selection processes using advising best practices and data-informed interventions. Develop and facilitate courses, workshops, presentations, and other educational programming focused on academic exploration, student success, and transition support. Coordinate initiatives that connect students with academic resources, campus services, and experiential learning opportunities. Support the planning and delivery of the academic component of UF Preview Orientation. Collaborate with UF colleges, advising units, and campus partners to enhance student support services and promote awareness of academic pathways. Coordinate and support university-wide exploratory learning and engagement initiatives, including events that encourage exploration of majors, minors, and career options. Maintain accurate student records and utilize university systems and technologies to document advising interactions and monitor student outcomes. Participate in departmental, divisional, and university committees, trainings, and initiatives that advance the mission of UESS and student success at the University of Florida. Expected Salary: $60,000 - $65,000 annually; commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Master’s degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience in academic advising, student success, student development, or related student support services within a higher education setting. Strong understanding of student success principles, academic planning, and the factors that contribute to student retention and persistence. Demonstrated ability to develop and deliver workshops, presentations, and engagement initiatives for diverse student audiences. Experience collaborating with faculty, staff, and campus partners across multiple colleges or departments. Excellent written and verbal communication, and organizational skills. Preferred: · Experience advising exploratory, undecided, or undergraduate students during academic program transitions. · Experience developing and facilitating student success, academic exploration, or first-year programming. · Knowledge of academic planning, retention, and student success best practices. · Experience supporting orientation advising. · Experience using advising technologies, student information systems, and data to inform student support strategies. · Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with academic and student affairs partners across a decentralized environment. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, applicants must upload a cover letter, a curriculum vitae/resume, and three professional references. After initial review, confidential letters of recommendation will be requested on behalf of those applicants who are chosen to receive further consideration. Applicants are required to provide official transcripts to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. If an accommodation due to disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). If you have any questions, contact the search committee chairperson, Nigel Richardson, at Nigelrayrich@ufl.edu. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541667/uf-health-physician-orthopaedic-sports-medicine-surgeon-st-johns": {
      "title": "UF Health Physician- Orthopaedic Sports Medicine Surgeon - St. Johns",
      "description": "UF Health Physician- Orthopaedic Sports Medicine Surgeon - St. Johns Apply now Job no: 541667 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: St. Johns Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 30010100 - JX-DEAN-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Orthopaedic Sports Medicine Surgeon Classification Minimum Requirements: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Federal DEA Certification Job Description: UF Health St. Johns is seeking a Orthopaedic Sports Medicine Surgeon to join our established and highly respected team in one of the fastest-growing counties in Florida. UF Health St. Johns Orthopaedics has a strong reputation for clinical excellence, collaborative care, and innovation in orthopaedic procedures, with a focus on improving patient mobility and quality of life. As part of the UF Health system that’s recognized regionally and nationally for excellence you will practice in a collaborative environment designed to support high-quality care, strong patient outcomes, and long-term professional satisfaction. Position Highlights: Multidisciplinary environment in state-of-the-art facility. Join experienced team of orthopaedic surgeons and advanced practice providers. Robust patient referral base Competitive Compensation Commencement Bonus & Relocation Available CME Allowance Malpractice Coverage (Sovereign Immunity) Retirement Benefits EPIC EMR About St. Johns County St. Johns County is one of the fastest-growing and most desirable counties in Florida, consistently ranked for its exceptional quality of life, strong public schools (#1 in the state of Florida), family-friendly communities, and easy access to the Jacksonville metro area. About UF Health Flagler: UF Health St. Johns is a total health care enterprise aimed at advancing the physical, social and economic health of Northeast Florida communities. From serving as the lead agency for St. Johns County’s Continuum of Care with an aim to end homelessness, to bringing a new concept in health villages throughout the region, UF Health St. Johns is your caring partner throughout the journey of life. UF Health St. Johns is an extension of UF Health Flagler Hospital, which has a 130-year legacy of caring for the community. The 335-bed hospital has been named among America’s 50 Best hospitals out of nearly 4,500 nationwide. About UF Health Durbin: UF Health Durbin is a 42.5 acre health and wellness campus that will advance health care services as part of UF’s regional expansion plan for Jacksonville and St. Johns County. Located in northeast St. Johns County, UF Health Durbin Park will include a full -service 99-bed hospital with a focus on acute, intensive, emergency care, orthopaedics, neurosurgery, general surgery, cardiovascular medicine, and women’s services as well as a multidisciplinary medical office building. Future potential site development include the ability to expand hospital beds as well as an ambulatory surgical center, outpatient imagining and additional medial office building. We Offer Exceptional Benefits: Explore your benefit options at https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits/eligibility/staff-teams/ Low-cost State Health Plans: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life and Disability Insurance Florida Retirement System Retirement Plans Paid Time Off including for vacations, holidays, paid family leave, and sick leave Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer Sovereign immunity malpractice status No state taxes Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: MD/DO Degree Board certified Florida Medical License DEA License Preferred: Specialty License or Certification; Board certified or Board Eligible in Specified Area of Medical Specialty; Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida and Federal DEA Certification Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please submit an application at Careers at UF with the following documents attached: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and consideration will continue until the positions are filled. The University of Florida is an equal opportunity employer. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at https://naces.org/members/ The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes (Patient Contact and Bloodborne Pathogens) Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541669/uf-health-physician-primary-care-physician-st-johns": {
      "title": "UF Health Physician- Primary Care Physician - St. Johns",
      "description": "UF Health Physician- Primary Care Physician - St. Johns Apply now Job no: 541669 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: St. Johns Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 30010100 - JX-DEAN-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Primary Care Physician Classification Minimum Requirements: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Job Description: UF Health St. Johns is actively recruiting a board-certified/board-eligible primary care physician to join our expanding primary care network in one of the fastest-growing counties in Florida. As part of the UF Health system we are recognized regionally and nationally for excellence. As a primary care physician you will practice in a collaborative, patient-centered environment designed for high-quality care and long-term professional satisfaction. Position Highlights 100 % Clinical Outpatient (Full Time) Competitive Compensation Commencement Bonus & Relocation Available CME Allowance Malpractice Coverage (Sovereign Immunity) Retirement Benefits EPIC EMR About St. Johns County St. Johns County is one of the fastest-growing and most desirable counties in Florida, consistently ranked for its exceptional quality of life, strong public schools (#1 in the state of Florida), family-friendly communities, and easy access to the Jacksonville metro area. About UF Health Flagler: UF Health St. Johns is a total health care enterprise aimed at advancing the physical, social and economic health of Northeast Florida communities. From serving as the lead agency for St. Johns County’s Continuum of Care with an aim to end homelessness, to bringing a new concept in health villages throughout the region, UF Health St. Johns is your caring partner throughout the journey of life. UF Health St. Johns is an extension of UF Health Flagler Hospital, which has a 130-year legacy of caring for the community. The 335-bed hospital has been named among America’s 50 Best hospitals out of nearly 4,500 nationwide. About UF Health Durbin: UF Health Durbin is a 42.5 acre health and wellness campus that will advance health care services as part of UF’s regional expansion plan for Jacksonville and St. Johns County. Located in northeast St. Johns County, UF Health Durbin Park will include a full -service 99-bed hospital with a focus on acute, intensive, emergency care, orthopaedics, neurosurgery, general surgery, cardiovascular medicine, and women’s services as well as a multidisciplinary medical office building. Future potential site development include the ability to expand hospital beds as well as an ambulatory surgical center, outpatient imagining and additional medial office building. We Offer Exceptional Benefits: Explore your benefit options at https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits/eligibility/staff-teams/ Low-cost State Health Plans: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life and Disability Insurance Florida Retirement System Retirement Plans Paid Time Off including for vacations, holidays, paid family leave, and sick leave Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer Sovereign immunity malpractice status No state taxes Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Position Requirements Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. MD/DO Degree Board certified or board eligible Florida Medical License DEA license Preferred: Specialty License or Certification; Board certified or Board Eligible in Specified Area of Medical Specialty; Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida and Federal DEA Certification Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please submit an application at Careers at UF with the following documents attached: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Applications will be reviewed as they are received, and consideration will continue until the positions are filled. The University of Florida is committed to non-discrimination with respect to race, creed, color, religion, age, disability, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, national origin, political opinions or affiliations, genetic information and veteran status in all aspects of employment including recruitment, hiring, promotions, transfers, discipline, terminations, wage and salary administration, benefits, and training. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at https://naces.org/members/ The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes (Patient Contact and Bloodborne Pathogens) Advertised: 08 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
