    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541441/orthopedic-surgery-veterinary-technician-iii-care": {
      "title": "Orthopedic Surgery Veterinary Technician I/II (Care)",
      "description": "Orthopedic Surgery Veterinary Technician I/II (Care) Apply now Job no: 541441 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28311100 - VM-SURGERY Classification Title: Orthopedic Surgery Veterinary Technician Classification Minimum Requirements: Veterinary Technician I - High school diploma or equivalent and one year relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Veterinary Technician II - Credentialed veterinary technician Job Description: Are you a skilled veterinary technician who loves both learning and sharing your knowledge and is ready to join a busy team seeing cats and dogs with a wide variety of issues requiring orthopedic intervention? We are looking for our next team members in Small Animal Surgery and currently are recruiting for an Orthopedic Surgery position! Nursing staff in our service assist with appointments, small procedures under sedation and anesthesia in both sterile and aseptic conditions, diagnostic workups including digital radiography and CT, and a host of other surgical nursing skills in addition to client communication. Members of our team work closely with boarded veterinary surgeons, residents/interns, and veterinary students in a fast paced teaching and learning environment. We offer competitive wages, benefits including health insurance and paid leave and holidays, and a team-oriented approach to each day. This is a full time position, working Monday-Friday. Expected Salary: Non-Credentialed $18.00-22.00 Credentialed $20.00-25.00 Required Qualifications Veterinary Technician I - High school diploma or equivalent and one year relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Veterinary Technician II - Credentialed veterinary technician Preferred: Credentialed Veterinary Technician Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a CARE position offering limited benefits, including health insurance and paid time off. When appropriate certifications are achieved, promotional opportunities to a level II title may be available. This position will also become eligible for transition into a TEAMS (staff) salary plan. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541585/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II Apply now Job no: 541585 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29040100 - MD-ANESTHESIOLOGY-GENERAL Classification Title: Administrative Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of appropriate experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Department of Anesthesiology at the University of Florida is seeking an Administrative Assistant II to join our Faculty Support Services team. This position provides administrative and operational support to faculty within an assigned division, helping coordinate daily activities, manage competing priorities, and ensure things stay on track. We are looking for someone who is organized, proactive, and comfortable working independently in a fast-paced environment. The ideal candidate takes initiative, anticipates needs, and enjoys being part of a collaborative team where strong administrative support makes a difference. Faculty and Administrative Support Provide primary administrative support to faculty within an assigned division, serving as a reliable point of contact for day-to-day administrative needs. Maintain faculty calendars and schedules, proactively coordinating meetings, recurring commitments, and other departmental activities. Coordinate divisional meetings, including scheduling participants, preparing agendas, recording minutes, and arranging audiovisual support. Maintain faculty dashboards, prepare correspondence, and assist with routine administrative communications. Prepare, update, and maintain faculty curriculum vitae (CVs), and enter or transmit information into online systems supporting mid-cycle reviews, promotion, and tenure processes. Assist with the development and distribution of clinical call schedules by collecting availability and scheduling requests from faculty, fellows, and residents. Process continuing medical education (CME) documentation and maintain records of outstanding requirements to support faculty licensure. Collaborate with departmental communications staff to assist faculty with manuscript submissions. Support faculty in meeting required training and compliance deadlines. Provide backup logistical support for transporting faculty and fellow applicants, as needed. Fiscal and Financial Administration Coordinate faculty travel arrangements, including itineraries, travel authorizations, and reimbursements through PeopleSoft. Provide guidance to faculty regarding University of Florida travel policies, procedures, and requirements. Facilitate purchasing card transactions and reconciliations, prepare requisitions and purchase orders, and process payments for encumbered and unencumbered vouchers, travel, and Earn-to-Learn (E2E) transactions. Reconcile monthly purchasing card financial reports and maintain accurate records of expenditures. Monitor and update individual faculty Professional Development Account (PDA) balances. Assist with divisional purchasing and supply orders, including coordinating catering and refreshments for meetings. Work within assigned budget targets while ensuring transactions are processed accurately and in accordance with applicable University policies and procedures. Communication and Departmental Operations Serve as a professional and welcoming point of contact for internal and external constituents, exercising discretion and independent judgment when responding to calls, visitors, and inquiries. Answer calls to the Department of Anesthesiology switchboard, assess caller needs, and direct inquiries to the appropriate individual or department. Welcome visitors and guests and assist with directing them to appropriate locations. Receive and review faculty mail, independently respond to routine correspondence, and complete scheduling and informational questionnaires. Coordinate maintenance and repair requests for office equipment and support facilities. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes and operational efficiency. Contribute to shared Faculty Support Services responsibilities, providing backup coverage when team members are unavailable. Handle confidential information and daily correspondence with professionalism, discretion, and appropriate attention to privacy. Independently address routine administrative challenges and resolve conflicts as appropriate. Perform other related duties as assigned to support departmental operations. Expected Salary: $20 - $23, commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of appropriate experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Experience with PeopleSoft. Knowledge of standard office practices, including professional telephone etiquette, business correspondence, and common administrative forms. Familiarity with medical terminology. Strong customer service orientation and commitment to providing responsive administrative support. Experience coordinating complex calendars, scheduling meetings, and preparing travel itineraries. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications. Strong organizational skills and the ability to prioritize and coordinate multiple assignments. Demonstrated problem-solving skills and the ability to work independently. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including effective grammar, proofreading, and attention to detail. Ability to establish and maintain productive working relationships with colleagues, faculty, and external contacts. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This position is eligible for veterans' preference. If you are claiming veterans' preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See UF’s Veterans' Preference Page for more details. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541591/veterinary-clinical-education-specialist-emergency-critical-care": {
      "title": "Veterinary Clinical Education Specialist - Emergency & Critical Care",
      "description": "Veterinary Clinical Education Specialist - Emergency & Critical Care Apply now Job no: 541591 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28311001 - VM-ICU AND PCW SERVICES Classification Title: Education/Training Specialist II Classification Minimum Requirements Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and four years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Are you an experienced Veterinary ECC Technician ready to revolutionize the way we transform career pathways from day-one Assistants to elite Specialist Technicians, empowering our team from within? The University of Florida Emergency & Critical Care team is hiring an innovative ECC Clinical Education Specialist (ECC-CES) to help define how emergency medicine is taught across our ER, ICU, and Progressive Care Ward (PCW). What You’ll Do: • Drive Educational Innovation: Manage our ECC Trainee Technician’s, training of new ECC hires, Nursing Internships, and volunteer coordination. • Modernize Learning: Utilize cutting-edge digital tracking tools to set top-tier clinical standards. • Mentor & Lead: Provide hands-on coaching, lead technician continuing education, guide staff toward VTS certification, and support seasoned VTS technicians with ongoing career advancement. Why Join the University of Florida? As a full-time TEAMS employee at UF, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive compensation and perks package designed to support your total well-being: • Generous Time Away: Paid state holidays plus extensive paid leave accruals. • Comprehensive Health & Retirement Benefits: Excellent health insurance options, dental, vision, wellness programs and retirement plans including generous employer contributions. • In-house social worker: Orchestrates staff wellness initiatives within the hospital. • Educational Growth: Employee tuition assistance programs and continuous professional development opportunities. Ready to elevate your passion for ECC into a career-defining leadership role? Candidates selected for in-person interviews will participate in a structured assessment process designed to evaluate communication skills, clinical expertise, teaching ability, and alignment with the educational mission of the role. The interview process will consist of: • Panel interview and behavioral-based questions • A brief teaching demonstration (approximately 5-10 minutes) on either an ECC-related topic or a unrelated topic of your choice. • A communication-based practical exercise designed to assess coaching and instructional skills Candidates will receive additional details and preparation instructions prior to the interview. Expected Salary: Salary dependent on credentialing and experience, plus up to 30% differentials Preferred Credentialed Veterinary Technician (CVT/LVT/RVT) Veterinary Technician Specialist in Emergency & Critical Care (VTS-ECC) Experience developing educational programs, onboarding frameworks, competency-based learning pathways, or staff development initiatives. Experience applying adult learning principles within a clinical, academic, or healthcare environment. Experience developing and maintaining competency tracking systems, skills matrices, educational documentation, or training metrics. Experience presenting continuing education programs, facilitating workshops, or speaking at professional conferences. Demonstrated leadership experience within a veterinary teaching hospital, specialty practice, emergency hospital, or academic setting. Demonstrated commitment to continued professional growth, credentialing, specialization, and advancement of veterinary nursing. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541597/veterinary-client-services-supervisor": {
      "title": "Veterinary Client Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Veterinary Client Services Supervisor Apply now Job no: 541597 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Marion Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28360000 - VM-WORLD EQUESTRIAN CENTER Classification Title: Vet Client Services Supervisor Classification Minimum Requirements Associates degree and two years of relevant experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: The University of Florida Veterinary Hospital at the World Equestrian Center provides Small Animal Primary Care and Emergency services, as well as Equine Sports Medicine, Rehabilitation, and Diagnostic Imaging services. This role offers a unique opportunity to support both equine and small animal clients while helping shape the client experience in a growing and collaborative veterinary environment. The ideal candidate is an experienced leader with a passion for customer service, team development, and operational excellence. This position requires a professional and composed individual who can effectively manage a variety of situations, provide coaching and guidance to team members, address escalated client concerns, and work collaboratively with hospital leadership to continuously improve service delivery. The successful candidate must possess excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills while maintaining a positive attitude and professional demeanor. Why work for UF? We know you care about your own pets as much as we do our patients, so we offer discounts for all our employees’ pets. We encourage you to join our team and grow with us to make a difference. Benefits: The University of Florida offers competitive benefit including but not limited to; Paid Leave and Holidays Extensive Medical Benefits (including health, dental and vision) Professional Development Assistance Employee Discount This position requires a post-offer health assessment and background check. Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree and two years of relevant experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute an equivalent rate for the required experience. Expected Salary: $20 - 26 /hour Preferred • Knowledge of medical terminology, anatomy, and terminology • Knowledge of the equipment and materials used and their availability and applications. Ability to operate a computer and utilize office suite software such as excel • Experience with staff scheduling • Demonstrate consistent professional conduct and meticulous attention to detail • Excellent verbal and written communication skills as well as interpersonal skills with patients, staff, and other members of the patient care team • Critical thinking skills and a positive attitude • Excellent verbal and written communication skills as well as interpersonal skills with patients, staff, and other members of the patient care team. Ability to effectively communicate with employees of various levels and responsibilities • Able to work in a team environment and collaborate with a variety of personnel in a positive manner • Ability to effectively maintain a working environment while in stressful situations • Critical thinking skills and a positive attitude; Able to think independently and demonstrate good problem solving skills Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541613/student-financial-aid-coordinator-ii-state-programs": {
      "title": "Student Financial Aid Coordinator II (State Programs)",
      "description": "Student Financial Aid Coordinator II (State Programs) Apply now Job no: 541613 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 03060000 - EM-STUDENT FINANCIAL AID ADMIN Classification Title: Student Financial Aid CRD II Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: The University of Florida is hiring a Student Financial Aid Coordinator II to oversee state-funded scholarships and grants such as Florida Bright Futures. This role involves managing disbursements, ensuring accurate reporting, and staying compliant with state rules. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: State Program Oversight Lead all processes for Florida-funded scholarships and grants, including eligibility, selection, and fiscal management. Interpret and apply state aid policies and regulations. Develop and share procedures to ensure program compliance and efficiency. Awarding & Disbursement Coordinate the awarding and timely disbursement of state financial aid. Use professional judgment in eligibility decisions. Act as the university’s main contact for the Florida Office of Student Financial Assistance. Reporting & Compliance Handle all reporting and reconciliation tasks for state aid programs. Ensure accurate data submission and monitor fund disbursement and returns to stay compliant. Additional Duties Support the Manger with additional aid programs. Participate in financial aid presentations and professional development. Perform other tasks as assigned. Expected Salary: $47,500 annually In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Preferred: Student Financial Aid experience Demonstrated ability to work accurately with attention to detail Excellent organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills Microsoft Office proficiency, including Excel Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 06 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
