    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541497/recsports-student-assistant-intramural-sports-officialscorekeeper": {
      "title": "RecSports Student Assistant - Intramural Sports Official/Scorekeeper",
      "description": "RecSports Student Assistant - Intramural Sports Official/Scorekeeper Apply now Job no: 541497 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Recreation/Event Services, Student Services Department: 04020100 - SL-RECSPTS ADMIN Classification Title: STU-AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Job Description: The Department of Recreational Sports is currently looking for Officials & Scorekeepers to join our energetic team and move Gators toward lifelong wellbeing. Officials & Scorekeepers serve the department by officiating Intramural Sports contests across one or multiple sports, enforcing RecSports policies and procedures to promote participant safety and satisfaction, and developing professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Successful candidates will begin work at the start of the Spring 2027. For questions or additional information, please contact Danny Kandell ( dkandell@ufl.edu ). For more information about the role and onboarding process, visit RecSports Student Employment Webpage . RecSports Team Member Responsibilities Develop professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Uphold and exceed the expectations of the Cornerstones of RecSports Service: accountability, anticipating needs, attitude, and atmosphere. Demonstrate a desire to learn and apply knowledge as a RecSports ambassador. Take ownership of RecSports facilities and programs by exhibiting a responsible work ethic. Promote and maintain cleanliness and appearance within and surrounding RecSports facilities. Enforce RecSports policies and procedures to promote participant safety and satisfaction. Respond to all emergency situations and adhere to established protocol including pre- and post- incident procedures. All RecSports employees are expected to abide by the RecSports Student Staff Career Readiness Principles that clarifies shared expectations and standards in effort to best serve our patrons, develop each team member, and prepare student employees for future career endeavors. Job Position Responsibilities Officials: Learn & enforce sport rules during competition Communicate with Scorekeepers, Supervisors, and Participants as necessary to facilitate game contests in an efficient and effective manner Scorekeepers: Learn & enforce sport timing and scoring rules during competition Communicate with Officials, Supervisors, and Participants as necessary to facilitate game contests in an efficient and effective manner Officials will carry out responsibilities at the following Intramural Sports contests: Fall - 7v7 Flag Football, Kickball, Indoor Volleyball, Indoor Soccer, 3v3 Soccer Spring - 5v5 Basketball, Softball, 4v4 Flag Football, Outdoor Soccer, Dodgeball Summer - 5v5 Basketball, Indoor Soccer, 3v3 Soccer Scorekeepers will carry out responsibilities at the following Intramural Sports contests: Fall - 7v7 Flag Football Spring - 5v5 Basketball, Softball Summer - 5v5 Basketball *Candidates are hired as both positions but may select which position and which sport they prefer to work; candidates are encouraged to work both positions and multiple sports. RecSports Fall Kick-Off 2027: Tuesday, August 17th 8am – 9:30am Fall Kick-Off is our all-staff event to discuss department-wide updates, facilitate unit training sessions, as well as cultivate community and positive energy within our RecSports team. All RecSports Student Staff are expected to attend and will be paid for their training time. Expected Salary: $15.00 - $15.25 per hour Required Qualifications: Requirements/Qualifications University of Florida student Minimal experience required however a basic knowledge of sports is desired Training sessions are conducted to provide officials with officiating techniques Complete and maintain UF online certifications in GET803, OOC101, PRV802, ITT102, GET811 This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. *Federal Work Study students are encouraged to apply! Special Instructions to Applicants: For questions or additional information, please contact Danny Kandell at dkandell@ufl.edu . This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 04 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541587/recsports-student-assistant-aquatics-lifeguard": {
      "title": "RecSports Student Assistant - Aquatics Lifeguard",
      "description": "RecSports Student Assistant - Aquatics Lifeguard Apply now Job no: 541587 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Student Services Department: 04020100 - SL-RECSPTS ADMIN Classification Title: STU-AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Minimum Requirements - University of Florida student - Current American Red Cross Lifeguard/CPR/AED/First Aid Certification or willing to obtain by start date. - Successfully complete the pre-employment water test - Commit 6-10 hours/ week; (may include morning, evenings, and weekends) - Additional certifications required for merit advancement - Complete and maintain UF online certifications in GET803, OOC101, PRV802, ITT102, GET811 This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. *Federal Work Study students are encouraged to apply! Job Description: The Department of Recreational Sports is currently looking for Lifeguards to join our energetic team and move Gators toward lifelong wellbeing! The Recreational Sports Lifeguard position is open for Campus Pools. Lifeguards will be tasked with overseeing all water-based activities and ensuring the safety of our members and guests. Successful candidates will begin work at the start of Spring 2027. For questions or additional information, please contact Adam Caldwell at caldwelladam@ufl.edu . For more information about the role and onboarding process, visit RecSports Student Employment Webpage . RecSports Team Member Responsibilities Develop professional relationships with co-workers, participants, and guests. Uphold and exceed the expectations of the Cornerstones of RecSports Service: accountability, anticipating needs, attitude, and atmosphere. Demonstrate a desire to learn and apply knowledge as a RecSports ambassador. Take ownership of RecSports facilities and programs by exhibiting a responsible work ethic. Promote and maintain cleanliness and appearance within and surrounding RecSports facilities. Enforce RecSports policies and procedures to promote participant safety and satisfaction. Respond to all emergency situations and adhere to established protocol including pre- and post- incident procedures. All RecSports employees are expected to abide by the RecSports Student Staff Career Readiness Principles that clarifies shared expectations and standards in effort to best serve our patrons, develop each team member, and prepare student employees for future career endeavors. Job Position Responsibilities Perform all necessary lifeguarding, first aid, and CPR skills as certified by American Red Cross Monitor the safety of swimmers and aquatic facility users. Prevent injuries by eliminating hazardous situations and behaviors. Monitor access to the aquatics facility to ensure only valid users and their guests are admitted. Enforce rules, regulations, and policies. Perform maintenance and cleaning, as needed. Monitor water chemistry, as needed. Attend mandatory departmental Fall training and all monthly meetings/in-services. Maintain current American Red Cross Lifeguard/CPR/AED/First Aid Certification Perform all other duties as assigned by the Aquatics & Risk Management Administrative Team RecSports Fall Kick-Off 2027: Tuesday, August 17th 8am – 9:30am Fall Kick-Off is our all-staff event to discuss department-wide updates, facilitate unit training sessions, as well as cultivate community and positive energy within our RecSports team. All RecSports Student Staff are expected to attend and will be paid for their training time. Expected Salary: $15.85 per hour Required Qualifications: Requirements/Qualifications University of Florida student Current American Red Cross Lifeguard/CPR/AED/First Aid Certification or willing to obtain by start date. Successfully complete the pre-employment water test Commit 6-10 hours/ week; (may include morning, evenings, and weekends) Additional certifications required for merit advancement. Complete and maintain UF online certifications in GET803, OOC101, PRV802, ITT102, GET811) This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. *Federal Work Study students are encouraged to apply! Preferred: Preferred Requirements/Qualifications Current American Red Cross Lifeguarding (including Deep Water) CPR/AED and First Aid for Professional Rescuers certification Special Instructions to Applicants: All applicants must register for and attend one Lifeguard Try-Out to be considered for the position. This is a time-limited position. Questions: Contact Adam Caldwell at caldwelladam@ufl.edu . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 04 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 25 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/538478/ops-dental-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Dental Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Dental Assistant Apply now Job no: 538478 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Dentistry, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 34010301 - DN-CLINIC ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: OPS Dental Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma and two years of appropriate experience. Fundamentals of Dental Assisting certification, Radiology certification, and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Dentistry is accepting applications for an OPS Dental Assistant to provide dental assisting and administrative support while contributing to high-quality student dentist education and patient care. Clinical Care Groups are a critical component of the UFCD TEAM Program, and this position is Patient-Centered and Student-Friendly, supporting the UFCD mission to deliver excellence in dental education and patient care. Each Dental Assistant is assigned to a Clinical Care Group consisting of two TEAMS. The position requires strong general dentistry chairside assisting skills, proficiency with computer applications (Outlook, axiUm, Excel, Word, and Windows 7), and positive interpersonal skills. Student Support: Assist clinical staff in maintaining optimal working order of clinical equipment. Collaborate with Dental Maintenance to ensure clinics are prepared for daily student use. Conduct daily clinic surveillance to ensure compliance with infection prevention standards and promptly correct deficiencies (e.g., cleaning chairs, counters, sinks). Maintain daily student attendance records and serve as an information resource at the emergency rally point. Assist with student orientation to the clinical curriculum, including assessing infection prevention practices and general clinic safety. Provide four-handed dentistry support to students during clinic sessions. Assist dental students with proper radiographic exposure techniques as needed. Patient Care: Provide chairside four-handed and six-handed general dentistry assisting for student dentists. Maintain optimal infection control standards throughout all patient care activities. Clinic Inventory: Manage and maintain inventory of clinical supplies for the assigned Clinical Care Group (22-chair clinic). Ensure adequate stock of daily clinic supplies at all times. Additional Duties: Actively participate in daily huddles and meetings. Proctor Clinical Examinations (Mock Board Examinations) twice per year. Participate in the UFCD Quality Assurance process. Perform other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $15.00 - $16.00 per hour; commensurate with education and experience Benefits: The University of Florida offers low-cost State Health plans, a number of Dental plans to fit you and your family’s needs, and Vision. Build your retirement with the FICA Alternative Plan and a host of voluntary add-ons, such as 457 deferred compensation and 403(b) plans. Optional insurance plans such as life, disability, legal and accident insurance are also available. UF Employees are also eligible for the GatorPerks discount program , which provides big savings at various businesses and retailers! Explore UF’s benefit options here: OPS Benefits Required Qualifications: High school diploma and two years of appropriate experience. Fundamentals of Dental Assisting certification, Radiology certification, and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred: Multi-practitioner dental practice experience. General dentistry chairside assisting skills. Expanded Functions Dental Auxiliary (EFDA) Certification demonstrating the successful completion of training as specified in Chapter 64B5-16, Florida Administrative Code. Experience handling general office equipment (fax machine, computer, copier, and calculator). Experience with Windows and Microsoft Office (Word, Access, and Excel). Previous AxiUm (electronic health record) experience. Customer service skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a full time, time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/538481/dental-assistant-i-or-dental-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II",
      "description": "Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II Apply now Job no: 538481 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Dentistry, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 34010308 - DN-STUDENT CLINICAL TEAMS Classification Title: Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: Dental Assistant I - High school diploma and one year of appropriate experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Dental Assistant II - High school diploma or equivalent and three years of relevant experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Expanded Functions Dental Auxiliary (EFDA) Certification demonstrating the successful completion of training as specified in Chapter 64B5-16, Florida Administrative Code. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Dentistry is accepting applications for a Dental Assistant I / Dental Assistant II position to provide dental assisting and administrative support while contributing to high-quality student dentist education and patient care. Clinical Care Groups are a critical component of the UFCD TEAM Program, and this position is Patient-Centered and Student-Friendly, supporting the UFCD mission to deliver excellence in dental education and patient care. Each Dental Assistant is assigned to a Clinical Care Group consisting of two TEAMS. The position requires strong general dentistry chairside assisting skills, proficiency with computer applications (Outlook, axiUm, Excel, Word, and Windows 7), and positive interpersonal skills. Student Support: Assist clinical staff in maintaining optimal working order of clinical equipment. Collaborate with Dental Maintenance to ensure clinics are prepared for daily student use. Conduct daily clinic surveillance to ensure compliance with infection prevention standards and promptly correct deficiencies (e.g., cleaning chairs, counters, sinks). Maintain daily student attendance records and serve as an information resource at the emergency rally point. Assist with student orientation to the clinical curriculum, including assessing infection prevention practices and general clinic safety. Provide four-handed dentistry support to students during clinic sessions. Assist dental students with proper radiographic exposure techniques as needed. Patient Care: Provide chairside four-handed and six-handed general dentistry assisting for student dentists. Maintain optimal infection control standards throughout all patient care activities. Clinic Inventory: Manage and maintain inventory of clinical supplies for the assigned Clinical Care Group (22-chair clinic). Ensure adequate stock of daily clinic supplies at all times. Additional Duties: Actively participate in daily huddles and meetings. Proctor Clinical Examinations (Mock Board Examinations) twice per year. Participate in the UFCD Quality Assurance process. Perform other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: Dental Assistant I - $16.82 per hour Dental Assistant II - $19.23 per hour Sign on bonus available Benefits: The University of Florida offers low-cost State Health plans, a number of Dental plans to fit you and your family’s needs, and Vision. Domestic partner coverage through GatorCare is also available. Optional plans such as life, disability, legal and accident insurance are also available. Build your retirement roadmap with competitive pension plans, investment accounts and a host of voluntary add-ons, such as 457 deferred compensation and 403(b) plans. UF provides a variety of leave programs including vacation, sick leave, 11 paid holidays, personal leave days, and family medical leave. TEAMS employees accrue approximately 22 vacation days annually, 13 sick days annually, and 4 personal leave days, typically used during the holiday closing period (accruals based on full-time employment). UF also provides you the flexibility to deal with life’s challenges by offering paid family leave, eight full weeks of leave over a 24-month period. UF Employees are also eligible for the GatorPerks discount program , which provides big savings at various businesses and retailers! Explore UF’s plethora of benefit options here: TEAMS Benefits Required Qualifications: Dental Assistant I - High school diploma and one year of appropriate experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Dental Assistant II - High school diploma or equivalent and three years of relevant experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Expanded Functions Dental Auxiliary (EFDA) Certification demonstrating the successful completion of training as specified in Chapter 64B5-16, Florida Administrative Code. Preferred: Two years of Multi-practitioner Dental Practice experience. Certified Dental Assistant (Dental Assisting National Board CDA), Dental Radiology certificate/permit, completion of formal training with a dental assisting program through a community college or vocational technology center. Experience handling general office equipment (fax machine, computer, copier and calculator). Information technology skills operating a computer, and experience with Windows, and Microsoft Office (Word, Access and Excel). Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/538999/research-assistant-scientist-machine-learning-sensing-lab": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Scientist - Machine Learning & Sensing Lab",
      "description": "Research Assistant Scientist - Machine Learning & Sensing Lab Apply now Job no: 538999 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Computer Science, Engineering Department: 19050000 - EG-ELECTRICAL - COMPUTER ENG Classification Title: RES AST SCTST Classification Minimum Requirements: PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning or a closely related field. Job Description: The Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering (ECE) in the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering (HWCOE) at the University of Florida is soliciting applications for a full-time, twelve-month, time-limited, non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Research Assistant Scientist in the Machine Learning and Sensing Lab. The principal duties and responsibilities assigned to this position are to assist the Director of the Machine Learning and Sensing Lab in development of an AI research program, mentoring students and supporting additional lab management and operations tasks as needed. This position will conduct cutting-edge research focused on developing algorithms and AI approaches for a wide array of research applications and tasks. This position will facilitate the engineering and development of AI tools for use by UF faculty, staff, students, collaborators and others through funded research efforts. This position will participate and facilitate in proposal development and resource sharing. This position will work with the Director of the Machine Learning and Sensing Lab to identify and pursue a range of federal, state, local and philanthropic funding opportunities, and prepare materials required for successful applications for such opportunities. Expected Salary: Salary is commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Data Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning or a closely related field. Preferred: Prior research lab management experience; Successful research publication experience in venues for AI/Machine Learning/Computer Science/Data Science/other related fields; >5 years of python programming experience; Experience with standard AI libraries; Prior proposal development experience. Special Instructions to Applicants: The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately, with the first full committee screening occurring during the week of March 30th, and will continue to review applications until the position is filled. You must apply by submitting an application through UFCareers via https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . ( Job 538999 ) The application consists of attached PDF files of the following required documents: 1. Cover letter (summary, introduction related to hiring emphasis areas) 2. Curriculum vitae (including a 1-page CV highlights) 3. Names, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses of no less than three and up to five references. Additional documents should be uploaded as one PDF to the “other documents” selection in the application. 4. A personal research program vision statement detailing short-and long-term goals. 5. A vision statement for the Machine Learning and Sensing Lab detailing short-and long-term goals (identify any synergies with personal research program). 6. A personal teaching statement describing the applicant’s teaching experience and interests. The anticipated start date for this position is May 1, 2026. For further questions, please contact Alina Zare, azare@ufl.edu. The University of Florida (UF) is the flagship campus of the State of Florida university system and is consistently ranked among the nation’s top public universities. UF is home to HiPerGator, the fastest AI supercomputer in higher education, and the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering is undergoing a major expansion in faculty, research, and facilities with a strong focus on artificial intelligence. In Fall 2023, UF opened Malachowsky Hall for Data Science & Information Technology, a 260,000-square-foot facility that serves as the hub for AI. For more information about college initiatives, visit eng.ufl.edu Additional Requirements The selected candidate must provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. Transcripts marked “Issued to Student” will not be considered official. Degrees earned outside the United States must be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES) . Additional Information The University and College count among its greatest strengths a community of faculty, students and staff who support a culture of respect and dignity where learning and research thrive. If you require a reasonable accommodation to apply, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD) . Employment is contingent upon eligibility to work in the United States. All searches are conducted in accordance with Florida’s Sunshine Law . The University of Florida is an equal opportunity employer. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Position is re-posted, current applicants do not need to re-apply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541165/dental-assistant-i-or-dental-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II",
      "description": "Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II Apply now Job no: 541165 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Dentistry, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 34010308 - DN-STUDENT CLINICAL TEAMS Classification Title: Dental Assistant I or Dental Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: Dental Assistant I - High school diploma and one year of appropriate experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Dental Assistant II - High school diploma or equivalent and three years of relevant experience and Basic Life Support (BLS) certification. Appropriate college course work or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Expanded Functions Dental Auxiliary (EFDA) Certification demonstrating the successful completion of training as specified in Chapter 64B5-16, Florida Administrative Code. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Dentistry is accepting applications for a Dental Assistant I / Dental Assistant II position to provide dental assisting and administrative support while contributing to high-quality student dentist education and patient care. Clinical Care Groups are a critical component of the UFCD TEAM Program, and this position is Patient-Centered and Student-Friendly, supporting the UFCD mission to deliver excellence in dental education and patient care. Each Dental Assistant is assigned to a Clinical Care Group consisting of two TEAMS. The position requires strong general dentistry chairside assisting skills, proficiency with computer applications (Outlook, axiUm, Excel, Word, and Windows 7), and positive interpersonal skills. Student Support: Assist clinical staff in maintaining optimal working order of clinical equipment. Collaborate with