    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541603/roofer-entry": {
      "title": "Roofer, Entry",
      "description": "Roofer, Entry Apply now Job no: 541603 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 63570600 - FS-OPER-ROOFING Classification Title: Roofer, Entry Level Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma (or equivalent) Job Description: Support other trades and contractors in new construction, maintenance, and repairs of facilities, structures, and equipment, including roofs, parapets, and related work. Assist with install, repair, and preventatively maintain various types of roofs, including shingle, metal, and BUR systems (e.g., modified and gravel surfaced roofs). Assist with install, repair, and preventively maintain single-ply roofing systems (e.g., TPO, PVC, EPDM, and “Teflon” fabrics). Assist with resurfacing existing roofs with coating, fabric, and other materials. Assist with install, repair, and preventatively maintaining roof drain buckets, clamping rings, and flashings. Point up and caulk parapet walls and masonry joints. Install dowel pins, reset parapet wall capstones, and perform related work. Assist with fabrication and install various sheet metal accessories (e.g., gutters, downspouts, and wall flashings). Clean roofs and gutter systems. Power wash various facilities and structures. Assist with work in several trade areas Enter data (work requests and time) via the AiM system. Operate UF/state vehicles. Clean and maintain workshop and personal equipment. Perform other duties (as assigned by supervisor). - Post-offer health assessment - Criminal background check - Valid Florida driver license - Roofing Level 1 OJT Task List NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: - Schedule may vary depending on location - Total of 40 hours per week - Perform emergency work as needed - Swing shift and standby duties as required - Position considered as Essential Personnel as defined by UF Policy Expected Salary: $17.00 Hourly Required Qualifications: High school diploma (or equivalent) Preferred: EXPERIENCE: None noted KNOWLEDGE - Knowledge of safe work practices in maintenance and repair work - Knowledge of proper materials and equipment used for specific jobs - Knowledge of planning, organizing, and coordinating work assignments SKILLS - Skill in using hand tools, power tools, and equipment - Skill in repairing BUR systems (e.g., modified, gravel surfaced, and shingle roofs) - Skill in using high reach equipment - Skill in using and pressure washing equipment - Skill in preventively maintaining roofing systems - Skill in working with single ply roof systems (including (but not limited to) TPO, EPDM, and “Teflon”) ABILITIES - Ability to communicate effectively - Ability to reach above shoulder frequently - Ability to kneel - Ability to bend repeatedly - Ability to read a service request - Ability to recognize safe working practices in maintenance and construction - Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships - Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate work assignments - Ability to identify potentially dangerous materials and situations that require adhering to extensive safety precautions and employing the use of personal protective equipment Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541606/human-resources-generalist-ii": {
      "title": "Human Resources Generalist II",
      "description": "Human Resources Generalist II Apply now Job no: 541606 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources Department: 29140101 - MD-SURGERY-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: HR Generalist II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Department of Surgery is seeking highly qualified candidates to provide professional support and expertise in the implementation of a broad range of human resources functions or programs. This position will serve as a human resources business partner to the administration, faculty, and staff of the department of Surgery, which includes the Regional Programs in Daytona and Deltona. Essential functions include recruitment, onboarding, effort reporting, and training coordination. This position requires a thorough knowledge of human resources policies and procedures as well as the hospital credentialing process. Duties include, but are not limited to: Performs broad range of human resources functions including, but not limited to, recruitment and staffing, timekeeping, and promotion and tenure. Recommends policies and operating practices associated with the Surgery Department. Processes all personnel transactions in accordance with University policies and procedures. Performs complex data analysis, prepares reports and/or presentations for management. Monitors the effectiveness of human resources policies and recommends revisions or modification to meet the needs of the university. Serves as a human resources consultant to faculty and staff by providing advice and guidance related to human resources, such as, all personnel issues, including benefits eligibility, extended leave, including FMLA, policies and procedures, etc.. Coordinates and processes extended leaves of absence. Prepares leave accrual projections for those anticipating extended leaves or terminating employment, including obtaining minimal leave required to maintain benefits from Fringe Benefits on employee’s behalf. Maintains and shares as needed all human resources data related to APPs in the department, both UF and Shands employed. Information required includes credentialing, effort allocations between divisions and Shands, multiple employee ID’s and hire and termination dates. Maintains current departmental HR records. Reviews compensation data for accuracy as requested. Maintains departmental personnel files in accordance with University policy. Ensures that all employees participate in required training sessions. Prepares compliance reports. Maintains Faculty Assignment spreadsheets and documentation. Other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $65,000-$70,000/annually Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Thorough understanding of UF and College of Medicine personnel and payroll policies, procedures and requirements. • Thorough understanding of PeopleSoft’s human resource applications and rules governing each application to timely process faculty and staff recruitments, job actions, position actions, compliance reporting, national and local advertising, and effort tracking. • Strong ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing to independently generate internal and external correspondence and advertisements. • Proven track record in recruitment, particularly faculty recruitment. • Advanced computer skills in Microsoft Word and Excel to prepare spreadsheets and other documents as needed. • Strong organizational skills • Strong attention to details. • Strong ability to prioritize job assignments to complete within established time limits. • Strong customer service skills. • Strong ability to generate and analyze payroll and HR reports.Item two Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and a minimum of three professional references with contact information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 02 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541384/securityfire-alarm-sys-tech": {
      "title": "Security/Fire Alarm Sys Tech",
      "description": "Security/Fire Alarm Sys Tech Apply now Job no: 541384 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades Department: 07700200 - HO-CABLE SHOP Classification Title: Security/Fire Alarm Sys Tech Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: Maintain, inspect, and repair life safety and fire systems Install, maintain, and perform functional testing and inspections of life safety systems, including, but not limited to testing smoke detectors, pull stations, bells, fire alarm control panels, annunciation panels, water flow and tamper switches, and related equipment. Perform annual inspections; Develop schedule for inspection and coordinate with stakeholders as necessary Install, maintain, and repair ADA devices such as door openers, bed shakers, bang bars, and visual notifications Communicate with University Police Department (UFPD), who is the alarm monitoring agent Remain up to date on current federal and state fire alarm safety codes Maintain, Inspect, and repair electronic access control systems Install, test, and maintain electronic lock and security systems including but not limited to electronic door strikes, electronic door magnets, readers, push to exit buttons, and infrared motion detectors. Install, test, and maintain ADA accessible electronic door hardware Order and maintain inventory control of electronic and hardware components Repair equipment and return to active inventory Responsible for following proper procurement and purchasing procedures within university, and departmental guidelines Maintain, inspect, and repair cable, data, telephone lines, and networking systems Install, test, and maintain uninterrupted power supplies (UPS) and communication equipment. Test, repair, and replace network equipment and devices. Collaborate with divisions within University of Florida Information Technology and outside vendors to keep housing telecommunication systems and networks functional. Install, repair, test, and maintain low voltage copper communication systems, fiber optic communications systems, and television cable systems Design, install, test, and maintain community antenna televisions (CATV) and closed-circuit television (CCTV) systems, voice and data communication. Provide administrative support for area Evaluate plans, schematics, specifications, and upgrades of new and existing systems in support of projects Retrieve work orders, close out work orders, record system data testing, and record detailed notes of work completed. Assist with the preparation of annual budget for area Train and collaborate with other technicians on systems, practices, departmental and university standards Coordinate and work with vendors, contractors, and departmental stakeholders responding to fire alarms and fire alarm system associated equipment Develop reports, handle special projects, tasks, and other duties as assigned Complete underground cable locates Serve in an on-call duty rotation, providing coverage for the area responding to calls for assistance and emergency situations Expected Salary: $25 - $27 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. A valid driver’s license is required. Preferred: EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE NICET Inspection and Testing of Fire Alarm Systems Level I & II Five years of fire alarm, access control, and/or telecommunication experienceWorking knowledge of low voltage and telecommunications industry practices and procedures Working knowledge of NFPA Working knowledge of the electrical trade SKILLS Skilled in installation of electrical conduit, wire, cable, fiber optic, and electrical/electronic devices Demonstrated proficiency with computers and basic software applications Demonstrated communication skills (verbal and written) Demonstrated customer service skills Demonstrated interpersonal skills ABILITIES Ability to perform types of physical exertion necessary for task completion Demonstrated ability to handle multiple projects or tasks simultaneously Demonstrated ability to function effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions Demonstrated ability to understand, interpret, and apply rules, regulations, policies, and procedures Demonstrated ability to work as part of a team Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541540/assistant-professor-biology-department": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Biology Department",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Biology Department Apply now Job no: 541540 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science Department: 16900000 - LS-BIOLOGY Classification Title: Assistant Professor Job Description: The Department of Biology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) at the University of Florida (UF) invites applications for a nine-month, full-time (1.0 FTE), tenure-accruing Assistant Professor position in Plant Ecology, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an internationally recognized, extramurally funded research program and contribute to undergraduate teaching through local field courses and other classes within the Botany major. The candidate will also be expected to provide graduate training and mentorship in their area of expertise and participate in service activities that support the missions of the Department, College, and University. The successful candidate will join a large and diverse group of Biology faculty in CLAS and have access to the department’s newly completed greenhouse, along with HiPerGator , one of the largest university-based research computing clusters in the US, core facilities at the Interdisciplinary Center for Biotechnology Research , and a diverse array of other resources and services. UF’s local network of field stations includes 31 natural areas on campus as well as UF’s Austin-Cary Forest , the Nature Coast Biological Station , the Ordway-Swisher Biological Station , and the Whitney Laboratory for Marine Bioscience . The successful candidate will also have the opportunity to interact with faculty in other UF units including the Florida Museum of Natural History , the Institute for Food and Agricultural Sciences , the College of Medicine , and the College of Engineering , many of whom are affiliated with the Tropical Conservation and Development Program in the Center for Latin American Studies , the Center for African Studies , UF’s Biodiversity Institute , Emerging Pathogens Institute , Genetics Institute , Informatics Research Institute , Water Institute , and the Organization for Tropical Studies , of which UF is a founding and permanent member. UF is the state’s oldest, largest, and most comprehensive land, sea, and space grant university with an enrollment of over 50,000 students. It is located in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida that is within a short drive of the Atlantic and Gulf coast beaches, freshwater springs, and numerous state parks and recreation areas. The climate supports year-round outdoor activities. Alachua County schools are highly rated and offer a variety of programs including magnet schools and an International Baccalaureate program. Together UF and Gainesville host a cultural life and other amenities comparable to those of a much larger metropolitan area (see Visit Gainesville for weekly activities). Minimum Qualifications PhD in Biology, Botany, Ecology, or related field Expected Salary & Benefits: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. Benefits: This faculty position is eligible for a comprehensive benefits package that includes state medical, dental, and vision plans; life and disability coverage; multiple retirement options; and paid time away and university holidays. Learn more about UF faculty benefits here: https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits/ . Special Instructions to Applicants: Applications must be submitted online. Click on Apply Now at the top of this posting. A complete application includes: Cover Letter summarizing the applicant's suitability for the position Curriculum vitae Two page statement describing the applicant’s research accomplishments and future plans Two page statement describing the applicant’s teaching experience and future plans Names and email addresses of three colleagues that can provide a letter of reference. Letter writers will be contacted for applicants that pass the initial screening process. Review of complete applications will begin November 9, 2026, but the position will remain open until filled. Please contact the Chair of the search committee, Dr. Stuart McDaniel ( stuartmcdaniel@ufl.edu ) with any questions about the position. All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States require evaluation by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541560/ops-sustainable-field-lab-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Sustainable Field Lab Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Sustainable Field Lab Assistant Apply now Job no: 541560 Work type: Staff Part-Time Location: Dade Categories: Agricultural Sciences Department: 60790000 - AG-TREC-HOMESTEAD Classification Title: OPS Time Limited Classification Minimum Requirements: Ability to work outdoors under South Florida environmental conditions, including heat and humidity. Ability to perform physical activities associated with field and greenhouse operations. Strong communication and organizational skills. Ability and willingness to perform pesticide applications as needed; pesticide applicator certification may be provided after hiring. Valid driver’s license. Job Description: The OPS Sustainable Field Lab Assistant will support the management and operation of the UF/IFAS TREC Sustainable Field Lab, with an emphasis on sustainable vegetable and herb production, greenhouse operations, crop and cultivar selection, and field-based extension and research activities. Responsibilities will include seedling and transplant production, greenhouse maintenance, planting, irrigation, fertilization, weed and pest management, harvesting, and general field maintenance. The position will also assist with the selection and evaluation of vegetables, herbs, specialty and underutilized crops, as well as sustainable production systems including high tunnels and hydroponics. Additional responsibilities may include organizing field days and outreach activities, establishing and maintaining experiments, collecting field and plant samples, recording and entering data, and assisting with research and extension projects. Expected Salary: $15.00-$18.00 an hour commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Ability to work outdoors under South Florida environmental conditions, including heat and humidity. Ability to perform physical activities associated with field and greenhouse operations. Strong communication and organizational skills. Ability and willingness to perform pesticide applications as needed; pesticide applicator certification may be provided after hiring. Valid driver’s license. Preferred: Experience in vegetable and herb production, greenhouse management, or field research. Knowledge of sustainable agricultural practices and crop production systems. Experience with data collection, Excel, and basic computer applications. Experience with high tunnel, hydroponic, or other protected-culture systems. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541564/ast-prof": {
      "title": "AST PROF",
      "description": "AST PROF Apply now Job no: 541564 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Construction/Design/Planning, Engineering Department: 15020000 - DCP-SCHOOL OF ARCHITECTURE Classification Title: Assistant Professor Job Description: The University of Florida’s School of Architecture ( UFSoA ) in the College of Design, Construction and Planning (DCP) invites applications for one faculty position in architectural design and research at the Assistant Professor level to be based at its main campus in Gainesville, Florida. Position Summary: The School of Architecture at UF invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor . We seek an innovative designer, educator, and researcher with strong research interests who are prepared to thrive within a highly competitive R1 research university with demonstrated expertise in the areas of applied fabrication, materials research, and construction technology. This position coincides with the opening of the Ramos Collaboratory, a new 50,000 sf research lab and education building expanding the College of Design, Construction and Planning. This position supports a strategic initiative to expand the school’s capacity to address the transformative impacts of emerging technologies on architecture and the built environment. We welcome applicants whose research explores fabrication, materials research, and construction technology, including work that engages broader societal considerations such as housing, health, natural disasters, and other emerging challenges. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate design studios, as well as seminars or technical courses related to fabrication techniques, construction assemblies, and building materials. Conduct original research and creative practice that contributes to the advancement of applied fabrication, materials research, and construction technology. Engage the new design computation and fabrication facilities in the Ramos Collaboratory building set to open in Spring 2027. Engage in interdisciplinary collaboration across the university (e.g., with engineering, computer science, or art/design departments). Contribute to curriculum development and the school’s evolving digital and fabrication facilities. Participate in academic advising, service, and governance within the school and university. The University of Florida’s School of Architecture ( UFSoA ) UFSoA is known for its rigorous and interdisciplinary design studio curriculum and culture, which includes numerous international opportunities and academic concentrations. The program has approximately 425 undergraduate and 200 master's and PhD students. There are three off-campus programs: CityLab-Orlando; CityLab-Jacksonville; and the Vicenza Institute of Architecture in Vicenza, Italy. International studies play an important role in the SoA curriculum with almost 75% of the student body participating in study abroad programs in Latin America and the Caribbean, Europe, Africa, and Asia. The 32 full-time faculty of the School of Architecture produce research, creative works, and design scholarship through independent initiatives, centers, and institutes. The School of Architecture offers graduate concentrations and certificates in Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Computational Design, Public Interest Design (PID), Acoustics, Sustainable Architecture and Design, Themed Environments Integration (TEI), Healthcare Design Integration (HDI), Building Performance, and Architectural Design Pedagogy. UFSoA offers the following degree programs: Bachelor of Design in Architecture, Master of Architecture (NAAB Accredited), Master of Science in Architectural Studies, and a Doctor of Philosophy in Architecture that includes interdisciplinary coursework in design, construction, and planning. UFSoA is one of five active, interdisciplinary units in the College of Design, Construction and Planning that contribute to solving built environment challenges in Florida, across the US, and the world. The successful candidate will join a highly motivated faculty at a top-ranked public university abundant with cutting-edge research, scholarship, and teaching. This rich environment provides ample opportunity for collaboration. SoA is committed to supporting faculty through mentorship, research and travel funding, assistance with grant writing and publication, and funding for graduate assistants to support teaching and research. The College of Design, Construction and Planning (DCP) The College of Design, Construction and Planning (DCP) is one of the few colleges in the nation that houses design, construction and planning under one college. With programs in architecture, construction management, interior design, landscape architecture and urban planning, historic preservation, and sustainability and the built environment, students are exposed to an interdisciplinary reflection of the world around them. UFSoA faculty collaborate in research and teaching with faculty in each of the college’s other units, and across the university, reflecting the college’s dedication to interdisciplinary collaboration. The Bruno E. and Maritz F. Ramos Collaboratory will further unite the disciplines under one roof. This new facility includes a research hub to house all DCP research centers, a large multipurpose hall and seminar rooms for lecture series and symposiums, creative collision common spaces, and a digital modeling and fabrication space. The City of Gainesville Gainesville is a vibrant city with a low cost of living, welcoming community, diverse population, excellent public schools, Division I NCAA sports, and no state income tax. The area is known for its nature parks, bike trails, sporting events, museums, mild winters, and warm summers. Being centrally located makes Gainesville easily situated for day trips to beautiful beaches along the Atlantic Ocean and Gulf of Mexico, and to theme parks including Disney World, and other cities including Orlando, Jacksonville, and Tampa. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville - https://www.visitgainesville.com/ Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Professional or post-professional graduate degree in architecture or related fields. Preferred: Professional license and/or Ph.D. is highly desirable, as is previous design studio teaching, peer-reviewed research (peer-reviewed publications, externally funded research, and other evidence of scholarly production), and/or professional experience. The successful candidate must be able to build effective working relationships and provide support to students, faculty, and staff throughout the campus community. We are especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the excellence of the academic community. The University of Florida is an equal opportunity employer. Special Instructions to Applicants: To apply for this position, visit jobs.ufl.edu . Job number for this vacancy is 541564. Review of completed applications will begin on November 30, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. If accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Interested individuals should apply online with the following materials: 1. a letter of interest that provides professional, pedagogical, and research/creative scholarship interests and goals with specific discussion of how your work is supportive of a diverse and vibrant studio culture 2. a current curriculum vitae; 3. a portfolio demonstrating creative, scholarly, professional, teaching and/or studio instruction works 4. at least three references with contact information Inquiries may be sent to: Jeff Carney Chair, Faculty Search Committee University of Florida, School of Architecture P.O. Box 115702, Gainesville, FL 32611-5702 Tel: 510-520-4465, j.carney@ufl.edu Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541568/uf-health-physician-anesthesiologist": {
      "title": "UF Health Physician - Anesthesiologist",
      "description": "UF Health Physician - Anesthesiologist Apply now Job no: 541568 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Volusia Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29049200 - MD-ANEST-DELTONA Classification Title: UFHealth Physician Classification Minimum Requirements: Halifax Health is seeking an anesthesiologist to join our growing, physician-led, MD-only anesthesiology practice in Deltona, Florida. Our MD-only model provides an opportunity to practice alongside experienced anesthesiologists in a collaborative environment with a strong focus on high-quality patient care. Located in Central Florida along the I-4 corridor, Deltona offers an appealing combination of professional opportunity and quality of life. Deltona is approximately 25 miles from both Orlando and Daytona Beach, providing easy access to major metropolitan amenities, international travel, world-class entertainment, and some of Florida’s most popular beaches. The community itself offers a more relaxed pace of life, with numerous lakes, parks, trails, and outdoor recreational opportunities nearby. Deltona is the largest municipality in Volusia County and one of Central Florida’s growing communities. Its location makes it an ideal home base for physicians who want access to Orlando and the Atlantic coast without living in the center of a major metropolitan area. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Preferred: Board certified in Anesthesiology Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida and Federal DEA Certification. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload a curriculum vitae and three professional references. Review of applications will begin on October 1, 2026 and will continue until a sufficient applicant pool has been established. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541570/extension-online-operations-lead": {
      "title": "Extension Online Operations Lead",
      "description": "Extension Online Operations Lead Apply now Job no: 541570 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 60030000 - AG-DEAN FOR ACADEMIC PROGRAMS Classification Title: Education/Training Specialist III Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and six years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: This time-limited position is part of a team that supports faculty and staff in the UF Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences (UF/IFAS) and the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences (CALS) through the CALS Faculty Instructional Resources and Support Team (FIRST). FIRST supports faculty and staff in the development and delivery of online academic and Extension (non-credit) courses and programs. In coordination with other team members, the Education/Training Specialist III (Extension Online Operations Lead) assists in planning, implementing, and administering operational workflows of online courses and teaching support programs for UF/IFAS Extension Online Learning. Job functions include: Utilizing knowledge of best practices in online course design and teaching, coordinates day-to-day operations of online non-credit course development and delivery in UF/IFAS Extension Online Learning, including course approval, course launch, quality review and content review workflows. Manages and assigns tasks from intake requests. Coordinates and manages course development and support workflows to ensure deadlines are met for course launches and other milestones. Manages captioning and accessibility workflows and tasks. Manages technical assistance and support to learners and instructors. Supervises OPS and other technical support staff and submits support tickets when escalation is needed. Tracks LMS and registration product releases and coordinates team communication on new features and gaps. Coordinates data collection and sharing. Tracks revenue and creates reports, working with UF/IFAS Extension Business and Artificial Intelligence team to access and refine dashboards. Manages and tracks course refunds and communication with credit card office. Coordinates hiring, onboarding, and management of student workers and OPS assistants, in collaboration with other team members. Supervises student OPS and OPS assistants assigned to video captioning, accessibility, technical support, and other operational tasks, coordinating their work with other team members. In collaboration with other team members, consults with faculty to assess needs. Collaborates with instructional designers, faculty, or subject matter experts on program development and design. Monitors practices and processes to ensure continued relevance and effectiveness. Develops and documents new workflows as new processes are needed. Maintains knowledge of current practices and trends in the training/learning/development field. Participates in and provides support to on-campus teaching events and activities hosted by the CALS Dean’s Office or that are otherwise relevant to FIRST activities, and to relevant UF/IFAS Extension events and trainings. Coordinates with other UF/IFAS and UF units, departments and programs as needed. Further Information: The University of Florida Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences (UF/IFAS) is a federal-state-county partnership dedicated to developing knowledge in agriculture, human and natural resources, and the life sciences. UF/IFAS Extension partners with communities to provide quality, relevant education and research-based expertise to foster healthy people, a healthy environment, and a healthy economy. The College of Agricultural and Life Sciences (CALS) prepares the next generation of leaders to address the world's critical challenges related to agriculture, food systems, human wellbeing, natural resources and sustainable communities. UF/IFAS Extension and CALS are creating an environment that inspires learning for all and affirms community across all dimensions. We particularly welcome applicants who can contribute to such an environment. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD) or visit Accessibility at UF . Expected Salary: $69,000 - $72,000 Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in an appropriate area and six years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Education or experience in teaching or training and developing instructional materials, especially for adult learners. Project and/or program management experience. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple concurrent projects and activities and effectively prioritize and allocate time to meet deadlines and schedules. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Ability to communicate effectively and to engage with instructors and other clients in a professional, accessible, and courteous manner. Experience or familiarity with online Learning Management Systems, especially Canvas, and with educational technology and collaboration tools (e.g., Articulate Storyline, Camtasia, Playposit, Cidilabs DesignPlus for Canvas, Adobe Suite, Mediasite, Zoom, HTML, Microsoft 365/Teams). Experience providing technical support to instructors or learners. Ability to work independently and in a collaborative team to meet both individual and team goals. Ability to seek solutions proactively. Flexibility and ability to adapt in a changing environment Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, applicants must submit a cover letter, resume, and list of references. Finalists may be asked to provide sample work and/or participate in a skills-based assessment. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541572/assistant-professor-in-geological-sciences-earth-and-planetary-remote-sensing": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Geological Sciences Earth and Planetary Remote Sensing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Geological Sciences Earth and Planetary Remote Sensing Apply now Job no: 541572 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Physical/Mathematical Sciences Department: 16240000 - LS-GEOLOGY Classification Title: Assistant Professor in Geological Sciences Earth and Planetary Remote Sensing Job Description: We expect the successful candidate to establish a strong externally funded research program that includes mentoring graduate students and teaching graduate and undergraduate courses in their area of expertise and contribute courses supporting and/or developing degree programs in Geophysics, Astrobiology and Planetary Science, and the UF AI Certificate. We are particularly interested in candidates who will engage in interdisciplinary research with the Department, the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, and/or University of Florida, e.g. the Astraeus Space Institute, and with the potential to participate in current or future airborne or space missions. The Department of Geological Sciences resides in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences and Department faculty members have broad expertise in Earth and Planetary Sciences, including geophysics, paleoclimatology, volcanology, petrology, tectonics, hydrology, geomorphology, sedimentology, marine geology, biogeochemistry, astrobiology, paleontology, and geoscience education among others. Available resources include state-of-the-art departmental Research Facilities , the Nanoscale Research Center , the UF Water Institute , the HiPerGator supercomputer and the UF AI Informatics Research Institute . Additionally, the UF Astraeus Space Institute supports and connects researchers in space science across the state. Astraeus also offers access to an on-campus Missions Operations Center for supporting in-space activities and missions. Expected Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. UF offers a strong benefits package for eligible faculty appointments, including health insurance, paid leave (as applicable), and retirement options. Learn more here . Required Qualifications: PhD or equivalent or have completed the PhD requirements by August 16, 2027. Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applications must include: (1) a brief letter of application, summarizing the applicant's qualifications, interests, future research goals, and suitability for the position, (2) a complete curriculum vitae, (3) a research statement detailing current activities and future research plans, (4) a statement summarizing teaching experience and interests, and (5) a list of names and contact information of at least three references. After initial review, letters of recommendation will be requested from the references for selected applicants. Applications will be reviewed beginning November 1, 2026. Only complete applications will be reviewed on that date. The position will remain open until filled, and applications received after the initial review date will be considered at the discretion of the committee and/or hiring authority. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Courtney Sprain ( csprain@ufl.edu ). All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States require evaluation by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541579/conservation-sciforester-i": {
      "title": "Conservation Sci/Forester I",
      "description": "Conservation Sci/Forester I Apply now Job no: 541579 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Agricultural Sciences Department: 60460000 - AG-SCHL FOR, FISH, & GEOMATICS Classification Title: Conservation Sci/Forester I Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in forestry, agricultural science, rangeland management, environmental science, or a closely related field. Job Description: Assist in land management operations on Hickory Sink Forest including hardwood control, herbicide use to manage invasive species, tree planting, road work, boundary maintenance, and related. Participates in and/or plans prescribed burns. Attend to prescribed fire-related operational needs, including preparing fire breaks, participating/managing burns, and mop-up and monitoring post-burn conditions/results. Maintains equipment in ready status. Scouts, documents, and initiates control efforts for invasive species. Assists with the implementation of restoration projects. Enforces FFGS and UF policies with visitors, including natural resources protection, in a tactful manner. Assist in infrastructure and maintenance activities throughout the Hickory Sink Forest. Operates and maintains heavy equipment used in land management, including bulldozers, front-end loaders, chemical sprayers, farm tractors, mowers, trucks, trailers, ATVs, chainsaws, and similar. Maintains roads, fire breaks, property boundaries, buildings, and related. Assists with related administrative functions, including purchase requests and work order requests. Coordination with researchers and instructors on natural resource-related projects, including assisting with logistics for research studies, assisting with tours that support education efforts, and assistance with outreach/Extension programs. May engage with students on specific projects or courses, assist with special outreach projects, and irregularly assist with management of other School-managed properties. Expected Salary: $23.94/hour commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in forestry, agricultural science, rangeland management, environmental science, or a closely related field. Valid driver's license required to drive state vehicles. Preferred: Bachelor's degree in a natural resources-related field Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541582/ops-counselor": {
      "title": "OPS Counselor",
      "description": "OPS Counselor Apply now Job no: 541582 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Social/Behavioral Science, Student Services, Counseling/Community Outreach/Social Work Department: 04030100 - SL-COUNSELING & WELLNESS CTR Classification Title: OPS Counselor Classification Minimum Requirements: Professionals with one of the following credentials are qualified to provide psychosocial counseling: ■ Social worker with a master’s degree or a Ph.D. in social work from a Certified Social Work Education-accredited school of social work. ■ Registered nurse with advanced specialized counseling education and training as a clinical nurse specialist or certified psychiatric nurse. ■ Professional licensed to provide clinical, counseling, and psychotherapy services by the Florida Department of Health, Division of Medical Quality Assurance. ■ Counselor with a master’s degree in counseling. ■ Psychologist with a master’s or Ph.D. in psychology. ■ Master’s or doctoral level graduate student intern from an accredited school of social work or a psychology or counseling program, under the supervision of a licensed practitioner qualified to supervise such interns. Job Description: This is a Time-Limited OPS Counselor position, 28 hours per week, for an estimated time period of 12-16 weeks, with the potential of an extension based on program and staffing needs. Under the general direction of the Counseling and Wellness Center (CWC) Associate Director and immediate direction of the CWC Assistant Director/CART Coordinator, this position requires a variety of skills involving brief consultation & referral, brief clinical assessment, and crisis counseling, including referral to on-campus and off-campus resources, as well as lethality assessment, safety planning, case management, and consultation with parents, faculty, and staff. CART counselors spend the majority of their time conducting brief consultation & referral appointments and providing crisis counseling/consultations to students who walk in for same-day support. Crisis Counseling: Provide daytime crisis services. Consult with faculty, staff, students, and family members who are concerned about a student. Crisis counseling includes the following skills: empathic listening and validation, de-escalation, prioritization, assessment of suicide/homicide danger, safety planning, efficient intervention, consultation, and consideration of other risk factors such substance use, self-care, social support, and mental status. Crisis counseling occasionally involves interventions of last resort, such as psychiatric hospitalization. Crisis Counseling Consultation: Consult with clinical faculty, clinical director, clinic coordinator, and case managers on students with urgent/emergent/recurrent concerns. Brief Consultation & Referral: Brief Consultation & Referral (BCR) appointments are brief (20-30 minutes) assessment and referral meetings with UF students seeking counseling services. During these meetings, CART counselors briefly determine students’ appropriateness for various on-campus and community resources and make recommendations and referrals accordingly. During the BCR, CART counselors also assess for suicide/homicide danger and address other urgent concerns, such as substance use and mental status. BCRs may include safety planning and referral to on-call CART counselors for further evaluation and crisis intervention. •In collaboration with CWC case managers, maintain and monitor a clinical case management system to provide continuity of care and follow-up for clients. •Assist students with social services needs including, but not limited to, referral to community resources. •Follow up to ensure that clients are appropriately assessed, successfully referred, and compliant with treatment recommendations. •Complete records punctually according to record keeping/report writing procedures that are currently operative at the CWC and required by legal and ethical regulations. Prepare and submit all service reports, or other communications involving the clinical operations of the CWC which are intended for persons, departments, or agencies outside of the CWC for review and approval of the Director or Associate Director. Performs other related duties as assigned; such as campus outreach, single-session therapy, group therapy, etc. Attend weekly meetings and dyadic/group supervision. Maintain awareness of CWC’s relationships with other university departments, community health providers, services, hospitals, and other resources. Clinical supervision of trainees, as needed or requested. The Counseling and Wellness Center is a multi-mission agency within the Division of Student Life serving a wide variety of counseling services and programs offered to students in direct support of the academic mission of the University. There is also extensive outreach and consultation to the campus community, a national professional training program (at levels ranging from pre-practicum through residencies), and academic activities. The multi-disciplinary staff of the CWC includes approximately 45 1.0 FTE permanent Clinical faculty and professional staff, 13 TEAMS/USPS support staff, and 10 CART counselors. Additional personnel include 15 or more graduate student trainees, and approximately 10 student assistants. The Center is housed in two physical locations. The CART Team is located on the fourth floor of Peabody Hall & Counseling & Case Management Teams are located at Radio Road. We also have several embedded positions within the university. Students use the Center in increasingly large numbers, averaging over 5,800 student clients per year and approximately 44,000 annual counseling appointment hours. Outreach programs and consultations are offered to more than 29,000 contacts. The CWC provides: •Individual, couples, and group counseling for students with psychological, emotional, academic and/or relationship concerns •Crisis intervention for students experiencing a personal crisis or emergency •Psychiatric evaluation and medication consultation •Stress management and biofeedback services •Outreach, prevention, and educational programs for students, faculty, and staff •Consultation services for students, faculty, staff, families, and friends of students •Training and supervision in counseling and psychology graduate students from pre-practicum through Post-doctoral residency •Assessment and referral services •Teaching, research, and scholarship Expected Salary: $50,400 Required Qualifications: Professionals with one of the following credentials are qualified to provide psychosocial counseling: ■ Social worker with a master’s degree or a Ph.D. in social work from a Certified Social Work Education-accredited school of social work. ■ Registered nurse with advanced specialized counseling education and training as a clinical nurse specialist or certified psychiatric nurse. ■ Professional licensed to provide clinical, counseling, and psychotherapy services by the Florida Department of Health, Division of Medical Quality Assurance. ■ Counselor with a master’s degree in counseling. ■ Psychologist with a master’s or Ph.D. in psychology. ■ Master’s or doctoral level graduate student intern from an accredited school of social work or a psychology or counseling program, under the supervision of a licensed practitioner qualified to supervise such interns. Preferred: Preferred qualifications include: (1) demonstrated expertise in clinical case management, (2) administrative and computer application skills required to effectively implement and maintain clinical documentation, (3) demonstrated skill in working well under pressure to prioritize and manage multiple clinical situations and to coordinate these efforts as a part of a multidisciplinary team, (4) energy to flexibly manage the professional demands of a challenging workload while maintaining positive and healthy perspectives and relationships, (5) collaborative spirit of warmth, acceptance, respect, and trust towards colleagues, (6) self-motivated, self-directed commitment to high professional ideals, (7) excellent oral and written communication skills, and (8) experience in college mental health, including crisis assessment, brief intervention, confidentiality requirements, and referral. Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, application letters, vitas, and three letters of recommendation from professional references including email addresses for contact should be submitted. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541589/assistant-vice-president-and-university-registrar": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President and University Registrar",
      "description": "Assistant Vice President and University Registrar Apply now Job no: 541589 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Academic Advising/Support, Executive/Director/Management Department: 03030000 - EM-OFFICE OF REGISTRAR Classification Title: Ast Vice President Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and eight years of appropriate experience. Job Description: The University of Florida seeks nominations and applications for the position of Assistant Vice President and University Registrar (AVP). Reporting to the Vice President and Chief Enrollment Strategist, the AVP will serve as a senior leader within the Division of Enrollment Management and provide strategic leadership for one of higher education's most complex and influential registrar operations. This is an exceptional opportunity to join a University widely recognized for its academic excellence, research enterprise, and institutional momentum. Ranked among the nation's leading public universities, the University of Florida enrolls more than 61,000 students, employs over 6,400 faculty members, and supports more than $1 billion in annual research expenditures. The University's continued growth and national prominence create a dynamic environment for a forward-thinking leader who can help shape the systems, policies, and practices that support student success, operational excellence, and institutional effectiveness. As the University's chief steward of academic records and registration operations, the AVP will oversee a comprehensive portfolio that includes academic records administration, registration services, degree certification, academic catalog administration, course scheduling and classroom utilization, student-athlete eligibility certification, veterans educational benefits certification, student information systems, and data governance. The AVP will serve as a strategic institutional leader and trusted partner to leaders across Enrollment Management, Academic Affairs, Information Technology, Institutional Research, and Student Life, advancing the University's goals for enrollment, retention, persistence, and graduation. The AVP will join the University at an important moment. The Office of the University Registrar is poised for its next chapter of leadership and innovation, with opportunities to strengthen organizational effectiveness, deepen campus partnerships, and lead significant technology and process transformation initiatives, including the implementation of the University's new degree planning and audit platform. The role will be mission-critical to UF's ability to advance student success, improve time-to-degree, optimize classroom utilization, strengthen academic scheduling practices, and support a more coordinated strategic enrollment management model. The successful candidate will build upon a strong foundation while helping position the office to meet the evolving needs of a large, complex, and highly ambitious institution. The ideal candidate will be a strategic, collaborative, and student-centered leader with deep expertise in registrar operations. This individual will possess the ability to navigate complexity, foster cross-campus collaboration, champion innovation and continuous improvement, and strengthen a culture of accountability, trust, and service excellence. The successful leader will be energized by a fast-paced environment, adept at balancing competing priorities, and committed to advancing institutional goals through strong partnerships and effective leadership. Expected Salary: Commensurate with experience In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and six years of appropriate experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and eight years of appropriate experience. Preferred: Master's degree in Higher Education Administration, Educational Leadership, Business Administration, Public Administration, Information Systems, or a related field preferred. Progressive leadership experience in a university registrar's office, including significant experience managing complex academic records, registration, curriculum, scheduling, and student information systems functions. Demonstrated success in a leadership role within a large, complex institution. Experience contributing to institutional strategic planning, policy development, and organizational decision-making. Extensive knowledge of strategic enrollment management principles and practices, including the intersection of registration, academic policies, student success, retention, persistence, and graduation initiatives. Experience with institutional data governance, data quality management, reporting, analytics, and leveraging data to support strategic and operational decisions. Comprehensive knowledge of federal and state regulations affecting higher education, including FERPA, veterans educational benefits, accreditation requirements, and student records compliance. Experience collaborating effectively with Academic Affairs, Student Life, Information Technology, Institutional Research, faculty governance bodies, and executive leadership. Demonstrated ability to lead organizational change, manage complex projects, improve business processes, and implement innovative solutions in a dynamic environment. Strong financial and administrative management experience, including budget oversight, resource allocation, and personnel management. Proven ability to develop, mentor, and retain a high-performing workforce while fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Experience representing an institution with state, regional, or national higher education organizations and professional associations. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills, with the ability to influence and collaborate effectively across all levels of a complex organization. Commitment to service excellence and enhancing the student experience through efficient, equitable, and student-centered policies, processes, and technologies. Special Instructions to Applicants: WittKieffer is assisting the University of Florida in this search. Application materials should be submitted using WittKieffer’s candidate portal at: Assistant Vice President and University Registrar | WittKieffer . Nominations and inquiries can be directed to: Amy Crutchfield , Ashlee Musser , and Tyler Workman UF-Registrar@wittkieffer.com Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 02 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541590/research-admin-assistant": {
      "title": "Research Admin Assistant",
      "description": "Research Admin Assistant Apply now Job no: 541590 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Grant or Research Administration, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 15010000 - DCP-DEAN'S OFFICE Classification Title: Research Admin Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma and four years of relevant experience or equivalent college mcoursework in place of experience. Job Description: 25% – Pre-Award Research Administration Assist faculty, principal investigators, and research administrators with the development, review, and submission of sponsored proposals, including review of sponsor guidelines; preparation and review of budgets, budget justifications, forms, institutional documents, and other required materials; and preparation and routing of proposals through UFIRST and other applicable systems. Coordinate with faculty, staff, research administrators, and university offices to obtain required information and approvals, monitor proposal timelines, follow up on outstanding materials, and maintain appropriate proposal records and tracking information. 25% – Post-Award Research Administration Assist with the administration and fiscal monitoring of sponsored projects throughout the award lifecycle, including reviewing and reconciling expenditures, encumbrances, balances, project end dates, payroll distributions, effort, cost sharing, and other financial activity. Prepare financial information and participate in project review meetings; assist with UFIRST award setup and modifications, budget revisions, no-cost extensions, and other award actions; identify and assist with resolving discrepancies; maintain supporting documentation; and assist with award closeout and coordination with university offices. 20% – Dean’s Office Centers, Institutes, and Research Initiatives Provide pre-award and post-award research administration support for Dean’s Office-supported centers, institutes, and other assigned research initiatives. Assist leadership, faculty, and project personnel with proposal submissions, sponsored award administration, financial monitoring, research-related reporting, and data requests, and coordinate with departments and college units when sponsored activities involve multiple organizational areas. 15% – Research Administration Coverage and College Support Serve as backup to the Research Administration Manager for designated activities and provide temporary pre-award and post-award support to college units during extended staff absences, vacancies, or other significant staffing transitions. Assist with research administrator meetings, training, communications, distribution of research administration information, and maintenance of college research administration website resources. Respond to routine research administration inquiries and direct faculty and staff to appropriate resources or university offices as needed. 10% – Reporting, Systems, and Administrative Support Run and compile reports from university systems and other data sources; maintain research administration spreadsheets, tracking tools, records, and data; and assist with research-related reporting for college leadership. Support process improvements, special projects, and other research administration initiatives assigned by the Research Administration Manager. 5% Other Duties as Assigned The percentage of time allocated to each essential function represents the anticipated distribution of responsibilities and may fluctuate based on workload, sponsored project activity, staffing needs, and College priorities. Expected Salary: $21 - $23 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma and four years of relevant experience or equivalent college coursework in place of experience. Preferred: Experience supporting research administration, sponsored programs, grants, contracts, or related financial administration. Familiarity with pre-award and post-award sponsored programs administration and university administrative systems. Proficiency with Microsoft Office, particularly Excel, Word, Outlook, and Teams. Ability to review and reconcile financial information and learn and interpret sponsor guidelines, university policies, research administration procedures, and applicable requirements. Strong organizational, analytical, communication, and customer service skills; attention to detail; ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines; and ability to work independently while recognizing when consultation or escalation is appropriate. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, candidates must upload a cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541151/ops-administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "OPS Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "OPS Administrative Assistant II Apply now Job no: 541151 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 11030000 - RE-PERSONNEL SERVICES Classification Title: OPS Administrative Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Administrative and Human Resource Duties Assists in processing new hires (OPS, Volunteers, TEAMS, Student Assistant, Graduate Assistant, Fellows and foreign national) including posting positions, processing background checks, performing pre-hire experience verifications, and completing necessary new hire paperwork, ensuring new hires are processed following university, state and federal regulations. Process various job edits, reclassifications, changes in FTE, reclassifications, non-renewals, terminations/resignations and leave cash-outs. Maintain and track positions within UF | Research, ensuring position descriptions and position numbers are properly assigned and maintained. Review time and labor for an assigned portfolio of departments on a bi-weekly basis through review of timesheets, leave applications and paylists. Assist in managing and retaining leave calendar and applications, and processing various payroll-related actions as-needed. Process and update payroll distributions, ensuring information entered is accurate and has necessary backup, as needed. Assist in distributing mail and securing UF | Research’s offices, daily when assigned. Travel and Fiscal Support Serve as one of UF | Research’s point of contacts for travel processing through providing assistance in creating travel authorizations, booking travel, and initiating expense reports. Review applications for graduate student requests for travel funds and faculty requests for conference funds. This includes ensuring all eligibility criteria is met, drafting letters for the Vice President for Research’s approval, and disseminating letters to applicants. Assistance to the Director for Human Resources The Administrative Assistant II will perform a variety of duties as assigned by the Director of Human Resources according to daily needs and operation of UF | Research, Personnel Services. This includes performing errands, scheduling, reporting services/repairs, distributing mail, and performing special projects as assigned. Space Certifications Assist in coordinating space inventory interviews with department staff. Responsible for entry into UF’s Space Inventory and Allocation System, ensuring all departmental space is accurately coded and accounted for. Miscellaneous Responsible for online directory upkeep, calendar maintenance, state vehicle reservations, supply orders, GatorOne ID authorizations, creation of UFID’s and affiliations for external researchers. Other duties as assigned The Administrative Assistant will be cross-trained to assist in all areas of the office during peak workload periods. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Preferred: Bachelor’s degree; understanding of the necessity and value of accuracy and attention to detail, ability to process information with high levels of accuracy; effective communication skills; ability to manage multiple concurrent projects and make effective judgment to prioritize assignments; knowledge and ability to use office support tools, e.g., excel spreadsheets, organization charts and e-mail communication; ability to work with a variety of individuals in a constructive and collaborative manner; knowledge of office administration, ability to carry out ongoing office administration tasks effective and efficiently in support of UF Research; ability to meet or exceed employee needs and provide excellent service in a direct or indirect manner; maintain confidentiality of all information entrusted to this position; and ability to work effectively as part of a team. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, applicants must provide a cover letter, resume and list of professional references. A criminal background check is required. This is not a remote position and is located at the University of Florida's Main Campus in Gainesville, Florida. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541353/ops-staff": {
      "title": "OPS staff",
      "description": "OPS staff Apply now Job no: 541353 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 17060100 - BA-FIRE BUSINESS OFFICE Classification Title: OPS Administrative Staff Classification Minimum Requirements High school diploma or equivalent and one year of general accounts transaction experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience Job Description: We are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented individual to join the Eugene F. Brigham Finance, Insurance, and Real Estate Department. This position supports financial operations, including processing UFGO transactions, travel reimbursements, and faculty professional development expenses. The candidate will also provide backup support by learning and assisting with other fiscal functions within the team. Additionally, this role serves as the front office receptionist, handling responsibilities such as answering the main phone line, mail pick-up and distribution, managing room reservation requests, and assisting visitors, faculty, and staff. The ideal candidate will have a solid understanding of university procedures, and the ability to manage multiple tasks. Working knowledge of UF Marketplace and UF GO. This is a great opportunity for someone looking for part-time work that can complement family and personal commitments. Preferred schedule M-F, four hours a day. Expected Salary: $18.00-$20.00 an hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of general accounts transaction experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience Preferred The ideal candidate will have a solid understanding of university policies and procedures, and the ability to manage multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Working knowledge of UF Marketplace and UF GO. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must apply online at https://jobs.ufl.edu/ and upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No. Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 16 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541389/program-coordinator": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Program Coordinator Apply now Job no: 541389 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Academic Advising/Support, Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Education/Training/Instructional Design, Allied Health, Student Services Department: 33030000 - HP-OCCUPATIONAL THERAPY Classification Title: Academic Program Specialist I Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: This position provides administrative support for the implementation of the OTD program. Serves as the primary point of contact for OTD student registration, course scheduling, classroom assignments, and textbook adoptions through the University Bookstores. Monitors the submission of grades through Grade-A-Gator, the University’s official online grading system, and facilitates course evaluations. Serves as a liaison between students and the Program Director when questions arise, including scheduling appointments and directing students to appropriate resources as needed. Serves as a liaison to the departmental Fiscal Assistant regarding the purchase of equipment and supplies for OTD courses and activities and maintains related inventory. Provides administrative support for departmental student organizations as well as attends and participates in faculty meetings. Completes the Academic Activity Reporting for all faculty and provides additional faculty support as needed. Maintains systems to track recruitment and application activities and prepare related reports at the request of the Program Director. Develops and maintains enrollment reports for the OTD program and identifies and reports trends related to recruitment efforts. Tracks and maintains program inventory related to marketing and recruitment activities and coordinates orders as needed. Organizes OTD program events, including Capstone Presentation, Networking Event, Pinning and Awards Ceremony, OTD Open House, and OTD information sessions and assists with other program events as needed. Serves as the primary point of contact for all communications related to admission to the OTD program. Manages the processing of student applications during two OTD and one Bachelor of Health Science- OTD admission cycles. Utilizes admissions databases to organize and categorize applications for faculty review and prepare applicant decision letters. Coordinates the enrollment of admitted students, communicates admission decisions to applicants, monitors completion of enrollment requirements (e.g., prerequisite courses, vaccinations, HIPAA, etc.), and plans welcome sessions and program orientation. Assists prospective students with questions, forms, and other admission-related needs. Assists the Program Director in the design and implementation of admissions processes. Interprets applicable admissions regulations and policies as well as develops and implements systems to effectively manage admissions activities. Manages the application processes of the OTD program, which involves monitoring and tracking applications in SLATE (internal) and Occupational Therapy Centralized Application Service (OTCAS) (external), initiating and maintaining consistent communication with multiple parties, and ensuring timely review and decision-making. Composes and signs routine correspondence pertaining to admissions. Liaises with the University’s admissions office regarding admission-related petitions. Assists in establishing performance goals and measures to evaluate the effectiveness of OTD admissions processes and program outcomes. Coordinates multiple aspects of recruitment for the OTD program, including recruiting prospective students, facilitating campus visits, and attending select local, regional, and national events and conferences to promote and represent the program. Coordinates informational sessions and open houses and represents the program at recruitment fairs. Develops and maintains recruitment and admission content for websites, social media, and other platforms. Collaborates with the college’s marketing team to promote the OTD program. Collaborates in the development and distribution of marketing materials for the OTD program and assists with the development and distribution of marketing materials, including multimedia content for websites and social media platforms. Supports recruitment efforts by facilitating connections among current students, alumni, and prospective students. Serves as the first point of contact for prospective students, employers, and other stakeholders. Triages telephone calls, responds to program-related inquires, and assists visitors as needed. Assists clinical education staff with maintenance of clinical affiliation agreements, solicitation of clinical sites and associated documentation, and maintenance of student and clinical site contact information within the clinical education database. Maintains student and clinical education documentation in accordance with applicable legal and professional accreditation requirements. Ensures documentation related to OTD student graduation and state licensure requirements is accurate, complete, and processed in a timely manner. Facilitates correspondence with University Administrative Offices, PHHP Dean’s Office, clinical site partners, and multiple state licensure boards. Completes other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $60,000 - $65,000 annually; commensurate with education and experience. The University of Florida (UF) offers an exceptional benefits package, including health, dental and vision insurance; state retirement plans; a generous leave program; and tuition assistance. UF is a Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) eligible employer. For more information on benefits, please visit UF HR Benefits and Rewards at https://benefits.hr.ufl.edu/ . Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Master’s degree in education or a related field is strongly preferred. Excellent interpersonal skills. Ability to provide effective customer service and work collaboratively with students, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders in a fast-paced environment. Highly organized with good attention to detail. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Excellent prioritization skills including proficiency in goal setting, tracking, and follow through. Highly motivated self-starter and effective at working autonomously. Proficient in MS Suite (e.g., Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and general computer skills. Knowledge of maintaining websites (WordPress). Demonstrated team player. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. If an accommodation is needed to apply for this position, please call 352/392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800/955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the U.S. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida’s Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541541/research-development-strategist-iii": {
      "title": "Research Development Strategist III",
      "description": "Research Development Strategist III Apply now Job no: 541541 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Grant or Research Administration, Engineering Department: 19010600 - EG-RESEARCH Classification Title: Rsrch Devlopmnt Strategist III Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree and three years of experience in grant and contract administration, grant writing, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Job Description: Strategic Research Support Assist in developing a strategic plan to align collaborative initiatives with HWCOE’s research goals Support the development of large-scale interdisciplinary center and team proposals Provide guidance and support for faculty and research teams throughout the proposal development process, including concept development and sponsor alignment Help faculty identify and pursue external and internal funding opportunities by monitoring sponsor announcements, facilitating funding searches, and advising on competitive proposal strategies Serve as a strategic resource for faculty scholarship by supporting the development of research, scholarly, and creative activities that align with college priorities Collaborate with HWCOE leadership to assess research capacity, identify growth opportunities, and support initiatives that enhance the college’s research and scholarship portfolio Support HWCOE institutes and centers in planning and developing research-program activities Identify potential applicants for high-profile, limited-applications opportunities, and target those opportunities to them Engage with stakeholders to gather feedback and act as a point of contact for program-related inquiries and information Funding Opportunities Identify funding opportunities that align with the HWCOE’s research priorities and long-term research goals Stay abreast of national and international funding opportunities and priorities across the disciplines relevant to HWCOE Review and use reports to identify trends in funding opportunities and guide decision-making Provide funding-opportunity data and analyses to HWCOE leadership, department chairs, and faculty Implement tools to track and assess the success of funding pursuits Proposal Development and Grant Writing Support Provide proposal development support on multidisciplinary proposals Coordinate project activities and timelines, and offer guidance on the content, structure, and strategy of grant proposals Arrange and manage external consultants and vendor services as needed, including scopes of work and review of vendor invoices Offer guidance on the non-technical components of proposals, such as data management, broader impacts, facilities, and budget justification, to reduce the administrative burden on researchers Coordinate with UF Research Security and Export Controls on proposals expected to involve export-controlled or ITAR (International Traffic in Arms Regulations) work Training and Workshops Develop and maintain an annual plan for ongoing training initiatives Design and structure training modules to address specific research-development needs Organize and conduct specialized workshops on advanced topics related to research development, and tailor them to the evolving needs of researchers Align training programs with the evolving research landscape and HWCOE goals Collaborate with other colleges and institutions on joint outreach initiatives Organize seminars and speaker series featuring experts in relevant fields Incorporate current practices and trends into training programs Assess and improve the effectiveness of training and outreach initiatives Metrics, Analysis and Reports Develop key performance indicators for research development activity Conduct data analysis, manage databases, and generate reports on research activities, funding, and outcomes to support decision-making Track and analyze research and scholarship metrics to inform planning, reporting, and continuous improvement efforts within the college Ensure accuracy and timely delivery of reports Advise on emerging research and funding trends Site Visits Support and coordinate activities for sponsor and review-panel site visits, including developing timelines and checklists, and facilitating preparation sessions as needed Conduct training sessions for researchers and staff on best practices for these visits Engage and coordinate with principal investigators, department chairs, and other stakeholders to ensure their preparedness for the visit Coordinate with the sponsor and its program officers to address any pre-visit queries and requests, and respond to any post-visit reviewer questions Address any unexpected issues that may arise during the visit Expected Salary: Salary is commensurate based on education and experience Required Qualifications: Master's degree and three years of experience in grant and contract administration, grant writing, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Preferred: PhD degree in engineering or a related field, and experience in grant and contract administration or grant writing, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. In addition to advanced degree, ability to search out funding opportunities and apply critical thinking skills to make effective decisions; good project management and organizational skills; understanding of research funding mechanism or grant development process; analytical mindset to identify and leverage strategic opportunities; and being proficient with relevant research tools and software. Experience in research development, grant writing or related areas; experience working with interdisciplinary research teams; project management and organizational skills; and understanding of funding agencies and mechanisms in academia. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered for this position, you must upload a cover letter and resume with application. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 14 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541554/uf-health-regional-physician-general-surgery-uf-health-central-florida-lake-and-marion-counties": {
      "title": "UF Health Regional Physician (General Surgery) - UF Health Central Florida (Lake and Marion Counties)",
      "description": "UF Health Regional Physician (General Surgery) - UF Health Central Florida (Lake and Marion Counties) Apply now Job no: 541554 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Lake Categories: Allied Health, Medicine/Physicians Department: 29760900 - MD-RPN CENTRAL FLORIDA HEALTH Classification Title: UF Health Physician (General Surgery) Classification Minimum Requirements: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Job Description: UF Health Central Florida, formerly known as Central Florida Health and acquired by the University of Florida Health in January 2020, is an award-winning, locally owned and governed not-for-profit healthcare system and the largest, most comprehensive provider of health care services in the region. We care for patients in Lake, Sumter, and Marion counties through inpatient acute hospital services at UF Health Spanish Plaines/The Villages Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital, inpatient rehabilitation services at UF Health The Villages Rehabilitation Hospital, and diagnostic laboratory services at several locations. As a premier healthcare provider, UF Health Central Florida takes pride in providing progressive, innovative technology, along with building strong relationships with patients, families, physicians, and residents of the communities we serve. UF Health Medical Group in Leesburg, Florida and The Villages, Florida is seeking a full-time General Surgeon to join its General Surgery Department. Board Certified or Board Eligible. Experienced and recent graduates are welcome. This is an outstanding opportunity for any professional with a wealth of knowledge and experience in their field. To provide, establish and execute best practice strategies and quality outcomes. Manage strategic clinical relationships with regional physicians and collaborate with the VP of Strategic Service Lines for marketing and Business Development activities. Setting major goals to align with broad functional objectives for General Surgery also aids in developing patient care pathways. The aim is to build a patient-centered team of professionals in Central Florida to enhance General Surgery health, provide top-notch outcomes for interventions, and minimize costs. Expected Salary: Commensurate with experience and education. Required Qualifications: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Preferred: Specialty License or Certification; Board certified or Board Eligible in Specified Area of Medical Specialty; Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida and Federal DEA Certification. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
