    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541561/multimedia-specialist-iii": {
      "title": "Multimedia Specialist III",
      "description": "Multimedia Specialist III Apply now Job no: 541561 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 04011200 - SL-MARKETING & COMMUNICATIONS Classification Title: Multimedia Specialist III Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Appropriate vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: As the department's dedicated video professional, this role owns video storytelling for Student Life end to end from ideation through production and delivery across both short-form and long-form content. This position works in close partnership with leadership to shape strategy, and with a team of student staff to bring it to life. Lead Video Storytelling and Production Develop, direct, film and edit high-quality video projects that capture the student experience and advances the Student Life mission through projects to be featured on social, web, digital and other platforms Coordinate and execute on all stages of production including concept development, location scouting, storyboarding, scriptwriting, pre-production, filming, lighting, post-production editing and delivery Ensure projects align with divisional goals, university brand standards and ADA compliance standards Creative Strategy and Content Development Collaborate with department leadership to identify goals and coordinate with stakeholders to translate them into creative video projects Establish visual direction and assist in shaping the brand voice and storytelling tone Develop platform specific strategies (Instagram, YouTube, Threads, etc.) to maximize impact and engagement Research and apply emerging video, digital storytelling and social media trends Recommend and implement new approaches to keep Student Life content fresh and engaging Monitor peer institution and industry leaders for best practices Regularly communicate with stakeholders on the planning and execution of video requests, balancing high-volume social content needs with occasional longer-form storytelling. Digital Asset, Equipment & Risk Management Maintain a secure and organized digital asset management system Oversee equipment inventory and maintenance schedule Ensure all cameras, lighting, rigs and related gear are in working order and meet production standards Maintain safe working environments during all shoots Anticipate and mitigate risks related to multimedia production Create and provide user training for system use as needed Multimedia Leadership & Training Recruit, train, supervise and evaluate a multimedia team, including student staff Responsible for the administrative functions related to employee management (e.g. time approvals) Responsible for developing, maintaining, disseminating and enforcing policies, procedures, and guidelines for areas of responsibility Interpret and ensure compliance with departmental and university policies, guidelines and other relevant regulations Analyze, generate and review processes and procedures for areas of responsibility and make recommendations based on findings Coordinate schedules and resources for multimedia projects Manage time and resource allocation to align with divisional priorities Foster a culture of creativity, accountability and professional growth Expected Salary: $60,500 annually. In addition, the University of Florida offers a very competitive benefits package. Learn more by visiting: https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Appropriate vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. A valid Driver's License is required Preferred: Knowledge Demonstrate experience in camera operation with foundational knowledge of light, audio and composition principles Demonstrate proficiency in video editing and post-production with expert-level skill in Adobe Premiere Pro and working familiarity with After Effects, Photoshop and related Creative Cloud program Skills Expertise in multiple lighting set-ups including studio, location and event Demonstrate excellent collaboration, planning, organization and communication (verbal and written) skills Demonstrated interpersonal and professional skills Abilities Strong visual storytelling ability with proven understanding of pace, mood and narrative that captivates and creates strong emotional connections with target audiences Demonstrated ability to handle multiple projects or tasks simultaneously Ability to work as part of a team in a complex environment Demonstrated ability to produce polished, high-production-value short-from videos while shaping the content strategy that drives audience growth and engagement Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 20 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541562/research-administration-manager": {
      "title": "Research Administration Manager",
      "description": "Research Administration Manager Apply now Job no: 541562 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Grant or Research Administration Department: 16010800 - LS-CLAS RESEARCH OFFICE Classification Title: Research Administration Manager Classification Minimum Requirements Bachelor's degree and four years of experience in grant and contract administration; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Lead Post-Award Research Administration Provide strategic direction and operational oversight for post-award research administration across departments and units served by the CLAS Research Office. The manager will establish consistent workflows, internal controls, service expectations, and quality standards while monitoring portfolio activity and emerging financial or compliance risks. Responsibilities include overseeing award setup and account structures; financial monitoring and forecasting; payroll and effort; award modifications; subawards; sponsor reporting coordination; project closeout; and other post-award activities. The manager will also help resolve complex or escalated financial and administrative matters and provide direct portfolio support when needed during transitions, high-volume periods, or other critical situations. Provide Expert Guidance and Manage Risk Serve as an advanced resource to faculty, research administrators, departments, and College leadership on post-award financial and compliance requirements. The manager will provide guidance on allowability, allocability, reasonableness, award restrictions, prior approvals, cost sharing, participant support, rebudgeting, effort, payroll, subawards, award changes, and other complex post-award matters. The position will identify emerging risks, recommend corrective actions, support audits and compliance reviews, and help ensure that sponsored projects are administered in accordance with sponsor, institutional, state, and federal requirements. Lead and Develop a High-Performing Team Supervise, coach, and mentor post-award research administration staff. The manager will assign and balance work, monitor service levels, provide technical guidance, support resolution of complex issues, and create opportunities for staff development and cross-training. The manager will also lead structured onboarding and continuing education for post-award research administrators and help develop a culture of shared knowledge, accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement. The underlying position description specifically places responsibility for onboarding, continuing education, mentoring, shadowing, and skill-building with this role. Build Faculty and Campus Partnerships Develop strong relationships with Principal Investigators, departmental staff, College leadership, and central administrative offices. The manager will facilitate recurring portfolio reviews, communicate financial and compliance matters clearly, anticipate upcoming needs, and help faculty and administrators make informed decisions throughout the life of an award. The position serves as a key liaison among the CLAS Research Office, departments, DSP, Contracts & Grants, and other university partners and may communicate with sponsors and external partners as appropriate and authorized. Help Shape a Growing Research Office The CLAS Research Office values thoughtful improvement, shared knowledge, professional development, and consistent service. The Research Administration Manager will play an important role in developing the infrastructure needed to support those goals. The manager will develop and improve procedures, tools, templates, checklists, training materials, internal controls, performance measures, and other resources supporting post-award administration. The position will monitor changes in sponsor and federal requirements, identify recurring operational or compliance challenges, and work with Research Office leadership to develop practical and scalable solutions. Expected Salary: $95,000 - $105,000 annually This is a TEAMS position and is eligible for a suite of excellent benefits, retirement options, and paid leave. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four years of experience in grant and contract administration; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Successful candidates will demonstrate a combination of the following: Significant experience in sponsored research administration, with strong knowledge of post-award financial management and compliance. Demonstrated leadership experience, including supervising, developing, training, or mentoring staff. Strong analytical, organizational, problem-solving, communication, and interpersonal skills. Ability to independently interpret complex requirements, identify risk, and develop practical solutions. Experience developing or improving processes, tools, resources, or service delivery. Demonstrated commitment to professionalism, collaboration, customer service, and continuous improvement. Experience working effectively with faculty, departmental staff, institutional leadership, and central administrative offices. Proficiency with research administration, financial, reporting, and productivity systems; experience with University of Florida systems and processes is preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered for this position, please upload your cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information of three professional references. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541563/ast-prof": {
      "title": "AST PROF",
      "description": "AST PROF Apply now Job no: 541563 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 17080100 - BA-MARKETING-BUSINESS OFFICE Classification Title: Assistant Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: Ph.D. degree in Marketing, Management Sciences, Economics, Psychology and Statistics or a closely related field. Job Description: The University of Florida, in Gainesville, Florida is seeking a Assistant Professor for the Department of Marketing at the Warrington College of Business. Duties and responsibilities include teaching, research and service. Teaching duties include teaching graduate students on the Application of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to Marketing Problems. Position requires a Ph.D. degree in Marketing, Management Sciences, Economics, Psychology and Statistics or a closely related field. For more information about the position, including instructions on how to apply, please visit us on-line at UF Career website. UF is a member of the State University System of Florida and an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment based on merit. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. degree in Marketing, Management Sciences, Economics, Psychology and Statistics or a closely related field. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541565/the-agency-directorassociatein": {
      "title": "The Agency Director/Associate-IN",
      "description": "The Agency Director/Associate-IN Apply now Job no: 541565 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Executive/Director/Management Department: 23140100 - CJC-THE AGENCY-ADMIN Classification Title: ASO IN Classification Minimum Requirements: •Bachelor's degree in Media, Advertising, Public Relations, Communication(s), or related fields •10 years’ experience in communications agency operations/creative/client services •Three years in a management leadership position •Working knowledge of core communications disciplines, including media relations, content creation, social media, campaign strategy, and evaluation. •Demonstrated ability to mentor, coach, teach, or supervise early-career professionals, interns, or students. Job Description: The Opportunity The Agency, a client-serving firm based in the College of Journalism and Communications (CJC) at the University of Florida staffed by students and led by professionals, is looking for its next director. We are seeking an energetic, visionary leader who can utilize their substantial professional experience in advertising, public relations, or an integrated mix of both fields, to guide the Agency through its next phase of growth. The director will lead the administrative management team responsible for business development, operations and client services, and mentor, guide and develop the operational and student staff. They will maximize the immersive learning experience, preparing students for careers in a rapidly changing communication marketplace through hands-on, applied, and collaborative learning. The position is classified as an Associate-In faculty position within the Agency (12-month, non-tenure track) to begin in the Spring 2027 term. The director will teach 2-3 agency related courses per term, mentor and advise undergraduate students as assigned, participate in scholarly and professional organizations , participate in shared governance, and perform other duties as assigned. This is an in-person position based in Gainesville, Fla. We are particularly interested in candidates who are excellent professionals/teachers/mentors that are on their way to establishing a national/international reputation. The selected candidate will provide strategic leadership for the UF communications agency model that integrates professional practice, teaching, mentoring, and student development. In addition, the candidate will contribute to the undergraduate program by supporting curriculum development, course delivery, advising, and student success initiatives, balance the academic, operational, and professional dimensions of the agency, including curriculum alignment, financial sustainability, and experiential learning opportunities. The candidate will build and maintain relationships with clients, alumni, industry professionals, faculty, and campus partners to expand student opportunities. Mentoring students as emerging professionals through project-based work, portfolio development, client engagement, teamwork, and career preparation is a key component of this role. The candidate will collaborate with the College’s academic departments and professional graduate program, and contribute to departmental teaching, service, and program goals, along with supporting an inclusive learning environment that prepares students to work across advertising, public relations, strategic communication, and related professional fields. About UF’s College of Journalism and Communications Accredited by ACEJMC, the college has earned its reputation for excellence over the last half century on the strength of its programs, faculty, students and alumni; the stories they tell; and the difference they make around the world. Our 80 full-time faculty members and 175 part-time instructors serve in four academic departments: Advertising, Journalism, Public Relations and Media Production, Management and Technology. We enroll about 2,500 undergraduates both in-person and online. More than 800 students are earning master’s and doctoral degrees. The Agency was dedicated in 2015 as a unit within the University of Florida College of Journalism and Communications. Its purpose is to provide immersive learning experience for our students to gain experience working for real-world clients and develop the professional skills needed to navigate an agency's work environment. The founding vision of the Agency prioritized bridging the industry and the classroom, and it continues to tear down walls between the two. Today, The Agency is a Gen Z-focused strategic communications firm, where approximately 120 students work alongside professionals to create real-world campaigns. Students can work as strategists, creatives, developers, researchers, producers, and media coordinators. https://theagency.jou.ufl.edu/ The College of Journalism and Communications is committed to building a culture of belonging and engagement, preeminent scholarship, cross-disciplinary education, superior skills development, and collaboration spanning the science and practice of communication to produce significant societal impact on a local, state, and global scale. CJC is also home to several cross-disciplinary initiatives such as the Innovation News Center, The Agency, Consortium on Trust in Media and Technology, the STEM Translational Communication Center, the Center for Public Interest Communication, the Atlas Social Media Listening Lab, the Brechner Freedom of Information Project, and the Media Effects and Technology Lab, among others. About the University of Florida UF is the state’s sole member of the Association of American Universities. It is in the midst of a multi-year pre-eminence initiative that has created more than 500 new faculty positions and generated a $70 million partnership with NVIDIA to create the nation’s top research lab in artificial intelligence. The University of Florida spent a record $1.34 billion on research in fiscal year 2026. The University of Florida offers a competitive salary commensurate with similar positions and includes a full benefits package. To view the university’s Total Reward benefit package, please click here: https://benefits.hr.ufl.edu/ . The University of Florida is an equal opportunity institution dedicated to attracting, hiring, and retaining top talent by fostering environments where team members feel included, valued, and empowered to do their best work. About Gainesville, Florida As home to Florida's largest and oldest university, Gainesville ( http://cityofgainesville.org ) is one of the state's centers of education, medicine, cultural events and athletics. Gainesville and the surrounding area is home to about 250,000 people, a robust arts community, several museums, a world-class health care system anchored at UF, a downtown core known for its restaurants and brew pubs, excellent public and private schools, and abundant nature exemplified by clear, natural springs. Additionally, within 2 hours are attractions such as Disney World, University Studios, Busch Gardens, and historic St. Augustine. Explore Gainesville in 60 Seconds. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: •Bachelor's degree in Media, Advertising, Public Relations, Communication(s), or related fields •10 years’ experience in communications agency operations/creative/client services •Three years in a management leadership position •Working knowledge of core communications disciplines, including media relations, content creation, social media, campaign strategy, and evaluation. •Demonstrated ability to mentor, coach, teach, or supervise early-career professionals, interns, or students. Preferred: Master’s degree in Media, Advertising, Public Relations, Communication(s), or related fields. 15 years’ experience in communications agency operations/creative/client servicesFive years in a management leadership position Prior experience training and mentoring, client management, business development and retention, or creative work Demonstrated experience managing client relationships, campaigns, or projects from proposal through execution and evaluation. Experience managing budgets, billing processes, and/or financial records. Experience with higher education settings, including academic calendars, teaching, guest lecturing, curriculum development, student organizations, and university procurement/finance processes. Professional industry certification or organization affiliation such as American Association of Advertising Agencies (4As), Accreditation in Public Relations (APR), American Advertising Federation, American Marketing Association, Public Relations Society of America, Communications Network, etc. Experience with new business development, including client prospecting, pitching, proposal writing, and contract negotiation. Commitment to institution-building and collaborative initiatives at the college and university level. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit your applications online via https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . Applications must be submitted in a single pdf file that includes: A cover letter detailing previous professional, leadership and/or teaching experience. A current CV or résumé. Teaching portfolio, if applicable (including teaching philosophy, sample syllabi, student evaluations, etc.). Contact details, names, phone numbers, and email addresses, for three references. Any other supporting documentation that you deem relevant to the position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Note: The Search Committee may request additional materials at a later time. For additional questions or more information, please contact search committee chair Katrice Graham at kgraham@jou.ufl.edu Review of applications begins October 16 continues until the position is filled. Candidates are encouraged to apply by Oct. 16 to receive priority consideration. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http//www.naces.org/. The application packet will be submitted as one PDF file through the UF Jobs website at https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening, which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The University of Florida is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Florida’s Government-in-the-Sunshine Laws require that all documents relating to the search process, including letters of application, nomination and reference, be available for public inspection. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541566/senior-graphic-designer": {
      "title": "Senior Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Senior Graphic Designer Apply now Job no: 541566 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 23010100 - CJC-JOURN - COMMUNICA-ADMIN Classification Title: Graphic Designer II Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Bring ideas to life. Shape the brand. Make an impact. The University of Florida College of Journalism and Communications (CJC) is seeking a talented and experienced Senior Graphic Designer to help shape how one of the nation’s leading journalism and communications programs is seen and experienced. This is an exciting opportunity for a creative professional who can transform ideas, information, and complex concepts into compelling, sophisticated, and accessible visual communications. As a key member of the College’s communications and creative efforts, the Senior Graphic Designer will develop visual solutions that elevate the CJC brand and support its academic programs, research centers, departments, events, strategic initiatives, and community engagement. This full-time, in-person position offers the opportunity to work on a diverse portfolio of projects spanning print, digital, environmental, and multimedia communications. No two projects are alike—from designing a high-impact magazine or annual report to developing social media campaigns, digital advertising, event materials, presentations, signage, and graphics for multimedia productions. Create. Collaborate. Lead. The Senior Graphic Designer will take projects from concept to completion, partnering with faculty, staff, leadership, and other College stakeholders to understand communication objectives and develop creative solutions that deliver results. The ideal candidate brings a sophisticated eye for typography, composition, visual hierarchy, layout, imagery, branding, and accessible design, along with the ability to balance creativity with strategic communication goals. This position requires someone who is comfortable taking ownership of projects, managing competing priorities, solving problems independently, and delivering exceptional work under deadlines. What You’ll Do Conceptualize and create high-quality visual communications for print, including magazines, reports, brochures, booklets, program guides, advertisements, flyers, promotional materials, signage, banners, and other collateral. Design engaging digital communications for websites, social media, email, digital advertising, presentations, digital displays, and other platforms, adapting designs to meet the technical and visual requirements of each environment. Shape and strengthen the CJC visual identity, applying and advancing College brand standards to create a cohesive experience across print, digital, and environmental communications. Partner with faculty, staff, leadership, and stakeholders to understand communication goals, provide creative direction, and translate ideas and information into effective visual solutions. Manage projects from concept through final production, including establishing scope and timelines, gathering and evaluating content, coordinating revisions, preparing production-ready files, and ensuring projects are delivered accurately and on schedule. Collaborate with printers, vendors, and external partners to coordinate production and ensure high-quality final products. Champion accessible design by incorporating best practices for typography, readability, color contrast, visual hierarchy, and digital accessibility. Review and refine final products for accuracy, consistency, accessibility, brand alignment, and overall quality. Contribute graphics and visual assets for video and other multimedia productions as needed. What We’re Looking For We are looking for a designer who is both strategic and creative—someone who can take a communication challenge, identify the visual opportunity, and develop a polished solution that connects with its intended audience. The successful candidate will demonstrate: An impressive portfolio showcasing high-quality print and digital design. Strong knowledge of typography, composition, layout, visual hierarchy, branding, imagery, and production. The ability to translate complex information into clear, engaging, and visually compelling communications. Experience managing multiple projects, deadlines, revisions, and stakeholder expectations. Strong communication, collaboration, problem-solving, and project-management skills. The ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with a wide range of clients and creative partners. A commitment to quality, accuracy, accessibility, and attention to detail. Experience working within established brand standards while identifying opportunities to thoughtfully evolve a visual identity. A Creative Opportunity at a Leading Institution At the University of Florida College of Journalism and Communications, your work will help tell the story of a dynamic institution preparing the next generation of communicators and advancing research and innovation across journalism and communications. Your designs will reach students, faculty, alumni, industry leaders, prospective students, donors, partners, and communities through a wide range of platforms and experiences. If you are a designer who enjoys turning ideas into meaningful visual experiences, thrives on variety, and wants your creative work to have a visible impact, we invite you to bring your talent to CJC. Work Schedule The typical schedule for this position is Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m., with periodic adjustments to accommodate special projects, events, productions, and other College needs. About the University of Florida The University of Florida is the state’s sole member of the Association of American Universities (AAU) and is engaged in a multi-year preeminence initiative that has created more than 500 new faculty positions and generated a $70 million partnership with NVIDIA to create a leading research laboratory in artificial intelligence. The University of Florida reported a record $1.34 billion in research expenditures in fiscal year 2026. UF offers a competitive salary commensurate with similar positions and a comprehensive benefits package. To learn more about the University of Florida’s Total Rewards benefits, visit the UF Total Rewards Benefits website. The University of Florida is an equal opportunity institution dedicated to attracting, hiring, and retaining top talent by fostering environments where team members feel included, valued, and empowered to do their best work. About Gainesville, Florida As home to Florida’s largest and oldest university, Gainesville is a vibrant center for education, medicine, cultural events, and athletics. The Gainesville area is home to approximately 250,000 people and offers a thriving arts community, museums, excellent schools, world-class health care, a lively downtown, and abundant outdoor recreation, including Florida’s renowned natural springs. Gainesville combines the energy of a college town with the accessibility of a growing community. Major attractions, including Orlando’s theme parks, Tampa Bay, and historic St. Augustine, are within approximately two hours by car. Explore the City of Gainesville | Explore Gainesville in 60 Seconds Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Strong portfolio demonstrating both print and digital design, including magazines, publications, brochures, reports and other multipage materials, as well as digital communications. Advanced proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud, particularly InDesign, Illustrator and Photoshop, with strong knowledge of typography, layout, composition, visual hierarchy and information design. Experience managing and applying brand standards across multiple communication channels and projects. Experience managing design projects from concept through production, including timelines, client communication, revisions and coordination with vendors and other stakeholders. Strong understanding of ADA/WCAG accessibility principles and experience applying accessible design practices to print and digital communications. Excellent communication, organization and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects, work independently, exercise creative judgment and collaborate effectively with clients and colleagues. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please submit your applications online via https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . Three references;please include names and email addresses. Any other supporting documentation that you deem relevant to the position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-4621 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). For additional questions or more information, please contact search panel chair Jen Ford jennifer.ford@jou.ufl.edu Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http//www.naces.org/. The application packet will be submitted as one PDF file through the UF Jobs website at https://jobs.ufl.edu/. All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening, which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. University of Florida is a member of the State University System of Florida and an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment based on merit. Florida’s Government-in-the-Sunshine Laws require that all documents relating to the search process, including letters of application, nomination and reference, be available for public inspection. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541569/ast-prof": {
      "title": "AST PROF",
      "description": "AST PROF Apply now Job no: 541569 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Social/Behavioral Science Department: 26040100 - HH-SPM ADMIN-INSTRUCTION Classification Title: AST PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate in sport management or related discipline is required. Candidates should have experience in conducting high-impact research, publishing in top sport management journals, and seeking external funding to support their scholarship. They should be passionate and enthusiastic toward student learning and demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence. Job Description: The Department of Sport Management (SPM) at the University of Florida (UF) invites applications and nominations for one, full-time, 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position. This is an on-campus position (not remote). Qualifications We are seeking candidates who will pursue an innovative, rigorous research program; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; and provide department, college, and professional services. An earned doctorate in sport management or related discipline is required. Candidates should have experience in conducting high-impact research, publishing in top sport management journals, and seeking external funding to support their scholarship. They should be passionate and enthusiastic toward student learning and demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence. We seek applicants with expertise in sport-related data analytics, including business, marketing, social media, performance, and/or geospatial applications. Candidates should be prepared to conduct and teach quantitative and computational research using modern analytical methods and tools. They should be passionate and enthusiastic toward student learning and demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence. Preferred qualifications include proficiency in R and/or Python and experience with one or more of the following: statistical modeling or machine learning, data visualization, SQL and relational databases, geospatial analysis, web scraping or APIs, and reproducible research workflows. Preference will be given to applicants who have a demonstrated ability to publish in high-impact journals and successfully pursue external funding to support their scholarship. The Department of Sport Management The Department of Sport Management is committed to excellence and impact through (a) innovative, socially impactful research; (b) the preparation and training of future industry and academic professionals; (c) engaging with the community, and (d) shaping the future of sport management. The department includes 9 instructional and 8 tenured or tenure-track faculty, who are supported by award winning advisory and administrative staff. Across residential and online programs, SPM reaches more than 900 students (over 600 undergraduate majors, 350 master’s students, and 14 PhD students). The Sport Management online program was one of the first in the country and is a thriving part of the department. Our website ( https://hhp.ufl.edu/about/departments/spm/ ) expands upon our research and teaching activities. The University of Florida The University of Florida is one of the top ranked Public Universities in the United States1 and is Florida’s oldest and largest land grant university. UF is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, an organization comprising the top public and private institutions in North America. With an enrollment of over 61,000 students annually, UF is home to 16 colleges and more than 200 research, service and education centers, bureaus, and institutes. There is a vibrant culture of research, with over $1 billion in research expenditures last fiscal year. The UF campus is in Gainesville, a city of approximately 145,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 85 miles from the Georgia border, 50 miles from the gulf, and 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean. It has abundant wildlife, mature forests, prairies, lakes, and opportunities for many outdoor activities. Alachua County Public Schools is an excellent school system, with many public schools ranked highly in the state and nation. Expected Salary: Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in sport management or related discipline is required. Preferred: Preferred qualifications include proficiency in R and/or Python and experience with one or more of the following: statistical modeling or machine learning, data visualization, SQL and relational databases, geospatial analysis, web scraping or APIs, and reproducible research workflows. Preference will be given to applicants who have a demonstrated ability to publish in high-impact journals and successfully pursue external funding to support their scholarship. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Instructions Interested applicants must apply online at https://jobs.ufl.edu (reference job # 541569) and include (a) an application letter summarizing qualifications; (b) a research statement and evidence of research proficiency; (c) a teaching statement and evidence of teaching proficiency; (d) a curriculum vitae; and (e) names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of three references. The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately. To receive full consideration, complete applications must be received by October 30, 2026, however, the position will remain open until filled. Send inquiries and nominations to Dr. Yong Jae Ko, Search Committee Chair, yongko@hhp.ufl.edu. This is a 9-month, full-time, tenure-track position that begins August 15, 2027. The University of Florida is an equal opportunity employer. Selected candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluations Services (NACES) which can be found at http://www.ncas.org. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD). Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 30 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/530126/assistantassociatefull-professor-electrophysiology-cardiology": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Electrophysiology Cardiology",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Electrophysiology Cardiology Apply now Job no: 530126 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty, Non-Tenure-Track Faculty, Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29050400 - MD-CARDIOLOGY Classification Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (tenure) or Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (non-tenure) Job Description: The Department of Medicine, Division of Cardiovascular Medicine at the University of Florida is seeking an Assistant/Associate/Professor to become an active and integral member of the Division. Responsibilities will include electrophysiology cardiology services at Shands Hospital at the University of Florida. Clinical duties will include performance and teaching in electrophysiology cardiology procedures, Electrophysiology inpatient services, as well as outpatient clinic duties at the University clinics. Opportunities are also available for participation in the general cardiology consultation service as well as periodic rotation on the general cardiology teaching service. Rank and Tenure (tenure or non-tenure track) status will be commensurate with qualifications. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with education and experience. Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have a medical degree and Florida Medical License. Special Instructions to Applicants: To be considered, please submit your application online at https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/ and attach your current curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ This position has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 29 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/536116/floor-care-worker": {
      "title": "Floor Care Worker",
      "description": "Floor Care Worker Apply now Job no: 536116 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 63400300 - FS-BLDGSRVC OPERATIONS-HC Classification Title: CUSTODIAL WORKER I Classification Minimum Requirements: Completion of ninth grade. Job Description: Cleans and maintains on a daily basis all halls, offices, shops, classrooms, restrooms, conference rooms, labs, gym areas, locker rooms, elevators which includes sweeping, dusting, dust-mopping, wet mopping, spot-mopping, reconditioning of floors and spot washing and cleaning of walls, doors, and partitions. Cleans and maintains all floors and floor coverings which includes regular duties such as vacuuming, shampooing, striping, sealing and waxing. Cleans all entrances, entrances walks, steps, patios, and concourses. Spot cleans and cleans all exterior and interior glass surfaces of all assigned buildings; cleans ceiling lights and Venetian blinds. Empties and cleans all waste cans, trashcans, recycle bins, water fountains and doormats. Required to complete training prescribed by Facilities Services Training and Education Department, and the University’s Compliance Training. Required to follow and adhere to all Building Services Standard Operating Procedures, and Facilities Services Policies and Directives. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: 5:00PM to 1:30AM (Monday through Friday). Workdays and shift times may vary in response to customer needs for special event coverage and/or departmental needs. Some overtime may be required. Total hours per week is 40. Management retains the right and discretion to modify schedules, building assignments, shifts and/or days for operational purposes. Position is considered as Essential Personnel as defined by UF Policy. Expected Salary: $15.00- $16.82 Hourly based on experience and work hours. Required Qualifications: Completion of ninth grade. Preferred: EDUCATION & TRAINING: High school diploma and two (2) years of commercial custodial experience. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 29 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 13 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
