    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541169/ufhealth-physician-crsgeneral-surgery": {
      "title": "UFHealth Physician: CRS/General Surgery",
      "description": "UFHealth Physician: CRS/General Surgery Apply now Job no: 541169 Work type: Staff Part-Time Location: Volusia Categories: Allied Health, Medicine/Physicians Department: 29149520 - MD-SURG GENSURG DAYTONA Classification Title: UFHealth Physician Classification Minimum Requirements: Licensed to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes* plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Job Description: UF Health – The Power of Together! At UF Heather, together, we strive to create unstoppable momentum towards the goal of improving individual and community health through discovery, clinical and translational science and technology, exceptional education and patient-centered, innovative, high-quality health care. At the heart of our mission is to provide high-quality clinical care and to promise every patient their best experience possible. Won’t you join us? UF Health Regional Physicians is seeking to hire a Colorectal Surgeon, UF Health Regional Physician Network physician to join UF Health in Daytona Beach, FL. This is an outstanding opportunity to be part of a patient-centered, collegial group committed to delivering high-quality clinical care. The selected candidate will enjoy a market-based, competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package. About UF Health: UF Health represents the shared vision and commitment to patient care excellence of more than 22,000 employees of the University of Florida Health Science Center and UF Health Shands health care system. With campus in Gainesville and Jacksonville, UF Health includes six health colleges, nine research institutes and centers, two teaching hospitals, tow specialty hospitals and a host of physician medical practices and outpatient services throughout north central and northeast Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care; innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences; and high-impact research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical invesitigation. The UF Health Regional Physicians Network represents the extension of our spectrum of patient-care services to the regional community under the University of Florida’s College of Medicine. Expected Salary: Competitive and commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: License to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes with appropriate experience. Preferred: Certification/Licensure in the State of Florida and Federal DEA Certification Medical Degree – MD or DO Completion of accredited surgical residency Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 01 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541193/postdoctoral-research-associate-plant-immunity-and-extracellular-immune-signaling": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Plant Immunity and Extracellular Immune Signaling",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Plant Immunity and Extracellular Immune Signaling Apply now Job no: 541193 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science, Agricultural Sciences Department: 60100000 - AG-MICROBIOLOGY - CELL SCI Classification Title: Postdoc Aso Classification Minimum Requirements: The appointee shall have received the doctorate in a field appropriate to the assigned duties and responsibilities. Job Description: The Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences is creating an environment that affirms community across all dimensions. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD) or visit Accessibility at UF . A postdoctoral research associate position is available in the laboratory of Dr. Zhonglin Mou in the Department of Microbiology and Cell Science at the University of Florida. The position is supported by a newly funded three-year USDA/NIFA grant focused on understanding extracellular immune signaling in plants. The successful candidate will investigate how extracellular signaling molecules, including extracellular NAD(P) and salicylic acid (SA), are sensed at the plant cell surface and how these signals activate local and systemic immune responses. Our research has identified lectin receptor kinases as key components of extracellular NAD(P) and SA signaling pathways that contribute to systemic acquired resistance (Li et al., Extracellular salicylic acid activates immune signaling through cell-surface receptors. bioRxiv 2026). The postdoctoral researcher will use molecular, genetic, biochemical, and cell biological approaches to define receptor activation mechanisms and determine how extracellular immune signaling interfaces with intracellular SA signaling and systemic immunity. Potential research areas include receptor-ligand interactions, receptor kinase activation and phosphorylation, protein-protein interactions, calcium and other early immune signaling events, genetic analysis of immune signaling pathways, and characterization of local and systemic disease resistance. The project provides opportunities to develop new mechanistic insights into plant immune signaling and to contribute to high-impact publications. The University of Florida is a Land-Grant, Sea-Grant, and Space-Grant institution, encompassing virtually all academic and professional disciplines, with an enrollment of more than 56,000 students. UF is a member of The Association of American Universities. The Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences includes the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences , the Florida Agricultural Experiment Station , the Florida Cooperative Extension Service , the College of Veterinary Medicine , the Florida Sea Grant program, and encompasses 16 on-campus academic departments and schools, 12 Research and Educational Centers (REC) located throughout the state, 6 Research sites/demonstration units administered by RECs or academic departments, and Florida Cooperative Extension Service offices in all 67 counties (counties operate and maintain). The School of Natural Resources and Environment is an interdisciplinary unit housed in IFAS and managed by several colleges on campus. UF/IFAS employs nearly 4,500 people, which includes approximately 990 salaried faculty and 1,400 permanent support personnel located in Gainesville and throughout the state. IFAS, one of the nation’s largest agricultural and natural resources research and education organizations, is administered by a Vice President and four deans: the Dean of the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences, the Dean for Extension and Director of the Florida Cooperative Extension Service, the Dean for Research and Director of the Florida Agricultural Experiment Station, and the Dean for the College of Veterinary Medicine. UF/IFAS also engages in cooperative work with Florida A&M University in Tallahassee. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. (foreign equivalent acceptable) in plant biology, plant pathology, molecular biology, biochemistry, or a closely related field. Candidates should have strong experimental skills, a solid publication record, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Candidates must be supportive of the mission of the Land-Grant system. Candidates must also have a commitment to UF core values . Preferred: Experience in the following areas is desirable: plant molecular genetics, plant-microbe interactions, protein biochemistry, receptor kinase signaling, protein-protein interaction assays, phosphorylation analysis, and Arabidopsis research. Special Instructions to Applicants: Individuals wishing to apply should go online to Careers at UF by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date and submit: Cover letter describing research experience and interests Curriculum vitae Contact information (including email addresses) for 3 individuals willing to write letters of recommendation Selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES) . Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under Florida Sunshine and Public Record laws. The University and greater Gainesville community enjoy a variety of cultural events, restaurants, year-round outdoor recreational activities, and social opportunities. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 01 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 10 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541204/post-doc-researcher": {
      "title": "Post Doc Researcher",
      "description": "Post Doc Researcher Apply now Job no: 541204 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Grant or Research Administration, Artificial Intelligence Department: 13050000 - DW-DIGITAL WORLD Classification Title: OPS Job Description: The Postdoctoral Associate will: Design, implement, and evaluate VR/MR-based experiential learning studies, particularly in workforce training and education. Collect, process, and analyze multimodal data in VR environments (e.g., eye-tracking data and interaction/event logs) to understand and model the decision-making strategies and heuristics of expert engineers. Apply machine learning techniques to develop VR/MR workforce-training applications for assembly and manufacturing tasks informed by models of expert engineering behavior. Collaborate with multidisciplinary faculty and researchers across Human–Computer Interaction, Educational Technology, and Electrical Engineering to iteratively refine research questions, study designs, and research projects. Disseminate research findings through peer-reviewed publications and presentations at leading conferences and journals in Human–Computer Interaction and Educational Technology. Contribute to technical reports, progress reports, and other project deliverables for funding agencies. Expected Salary: $31.13 - 33.52 /hr ($65,000–$70,000 annually), negotiable based on qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Computer Science, Human–Computer Interaction, Educational Technology, or a closely related field. Evidence of success in promoting an environment that advances access, equity, and inclusion. Preferred: The successful candidate will have: Technical expertise in Artificial Intelligence. Demonstrated research experience with VR/MR Research experience in teleoperation and familiarity with semiconductor manufacturing and assembly are considered a plus. Strong quantitative, qualitative, or mixed-methods research skills. Record of publications and presentations in relevant fields. Experience with interdisciplinary collaboration. Special Instructions to Applicants: Online applications must include the following: Letter of Interest CV References. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, with the initial review beginning on October 15, 2026. Priority will be given to applicants who are available to begin working on the project in Spring 2027. Application Deadline: December 31, 2026. Inquiries may be sent to: Hyo Kang Assistant Professor hkang2@ufl.edu The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call +1 (352) 392- 2477or the Florida Relay System at +1 (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: No About COTA and the University of Florida THE COLLEGE OF THE ARTS: The College of the Arts is an engine of transformation that generates paradigmatic shifts in the arts and beyond, while nurturing adaptability, innovation, and excellence. We foster an environment where novel creative practice, leading research, and experiential learning thrive. Our students, faculty, and staff interrogate and respond to the ever-changing relationship between technology and the human spirit. We prepare future leaders in artistic professions and creative industries, while developing student capacity for interdisciplinary scholarship that serves and engages local and global communities. The College offers baccalaureate, masters, and doctoral degrees. Approximately 1,600 students are pursuing majors in degrees offered by the College of the Arts under the direction of 150 faculty members in its three accredited schools— the School of Art + Art History, the School of Music, and the School of Theatre + Dance, and in the Center for Arts in Medicine, the Digital Worlds Institute, and the Center for Arts, Migration, and Entrepreneurship. In addition, the college comprises the University Galleries, and the University level of the New World School of the Arts in Miami. The University of Florida: The University of Florida is a comprehensive learning institution built on a land grant foundation. We are The Gator Nation, a community dedicated to excellence in education and research and shaping a better future for Florida, the nation and the world. Our mission is to enable our students to lead and influence the next generation and beyond for economic, cultural and societal benefit. UF is a graduate research institution with more than 50,000 students and membership in the prestigious Association of American Universities. Gainesville, which is consistently ranked as one of the nation’s most livable cities, is located midway between the Gulf of Mexico and the Atlantic Ocean. Together, the University and the community comprise the educational, medical and cultural center of North Central Florida. Advertised: 01 Sep 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/537048/section-chief-neuroradiology": {
      "title": "Section Chief - Neuroradiology",
      "description": "Section Chief - Neuroradiology Apply now Job no: 537048 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29130400 - MD-RADIOLOGY-NEURORADIOLOGY Classification Title: Associate/Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: MD or DO degree Board-certified in Diagnostic Radiology Academic rank of Associate Professor or Professor preferred (or qualifications to support appointment at that level) Eligibility for Florida medical licensure Job Description: NEURORADIOLOGIST, SECTION CHIEF UNIVERSITY OF FLORIDA GAINESVILLE The Department of Radiology at the University of Florida is seeking applicants for a full-time faculty position at the rank of Clinical Associate Professor or Professor. This role may be offered on a tenure or non-tenure track and will be based primarily at UF Health Shands in Gainesville. Responsibilities include providing patient care—such as neuroimaging interpretation and CT- and ultrasound-guided procedures in both adult and pediatric patients—as well as teaching residents and medical students. The position also supports clinical practice at the University of Florida Children’s Hospital, which offers a comprehensive range of pediatric tertiary care services and subspecialties. Position Summary: The University of Florida Department of Radiology is recruiting an accomplished physician-leader to serve as Chief of the Neuroradiology Division. This academic leadership role offers the opportunity to guide a collaborative and expanding neuroradiology team within a top-ranked academic medical center. The Chief will provide leadership across the division’s clinical, educational, and research missions, working closely with faculty, trainees, and colleagues in neurology, neurosurgery, otolaryngology, oncology, and related disciplines. Key Responsibilities: Leadership & Administration Partner with the Chair and other department leaders on strategic initiatives and operational needs for the Department and for the Division. Lead efforts in recruitment, mentoring, and faculty development. Promote a positive culture of clinical excellence, academic achievement, and professional integrity. Oversee division scheduling, workflow optimization, and quality assurance initiatives. Ensure compliance with institutional policies and regulatory requirements. Clinical Duties Interpret a full range of diagnostic neuroradiology studies, including CT, MRI, and advanced imaging of the brain, spine, head and neck. Participate in multidisciplinary conferences (tumor boards, epilepsy, surgery planning, spine, etc.). Participation in after-hours/weekend call based on departmental structure. Education & Training Foster a vibrant teaching environment for medical students, residents, and neuroradiology fellows. Organize and participate in didactic lectures, case conferences, and hands-on training. Support curriculum development and educational innovation. Research & Scholarly Activity Encourage and participate in clinical, translational, or basic science research. Support junior faculty and trainees in academic pursuits. Facilitate collaboration with other UF Health colleges and research institutes. About the Institution: The UF College of Medicine is part of UF Health, one of the Southeast’s most comprehensive academic health centers, with major campuses in Gainesville and Jacksonville. UF Health includes a top-ranked medical school, multiple affiliated hospitals, and nationally recognized research centers. The Department of Radiology offers a collegial and collaborative environment with access to cutting-edge technology, a robust research infrastructure, and a full complement of subspecialty-trained radiologists. Benefits: Competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package Academic appointment and promotion opportunities Relocation assistance Paid CME, vacation, and retirement benefits through the State University System Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications: MD or DO degree Board-certified in Diagnostic Radiology Academic rank of Associate Professor or Professor preferred (or qualifications to support appointment at that level) Eligibility for Florida medical licensure Preferred: Preferred Qualifications: Fellowship training in Neuroradiology Subspecialty certification in Neuroradiology Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic setting Strong interpersonal and communication skills Track record of teaching excellence and mentorship Experience in clinical operations and quality improvement Active research or scholarly output Experience in AI or Informatics, optimal but not required Special Instructions to Applicants: If you are interested in a rewarding position in a friendly, state-of-the-art environment, including a new Neuro medicine tower with intra-operative MRI and the latest Siemens scanners, please apply via Careers at UF - University of Florida - Recent Jobs . Attach your C.V. and cover letter of interest. The final candidate will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed as soon as possible after the posting date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/538779/musculoskeletal-radiologist": {
      "title": "Musculoskeletal Radiologist",
      "description": "Musculoskeletal Radiologist Apply now Job no: 538779 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29130600 - MD-RADIOLOGY-ORTHOPAEDIC Classification Title: MUSCULOSKELETAL RADIOLOGIST Classification Minimum Requirements: At the time of application, candidates must: Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology Be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida prior to employment Job Description: The Department of Radiology at the University of Florida is recruiting a radiologist at the rank of Clinical Assistant, Associate, or Professor for a full-time, non-tenure track faculty position. Primary clinical responsibilities will be based at UF Health Shands Hospital in Gainesville, Florida. This position will provide comprehensive coverage in Musculoskeletal Radiology within a high-volume academic and tertiary care environment. UF Health Shands is a Level I Trauma Center and major referral center with full subspecialty representation and advanced imaging capabilities. Responsibilities include: Interpretation of musculoskeletal imaging across all modalities Performance of image-guided musculoskeletal procedures Participation in inpatient and outpatient clinical services Teaching and supervision of residents and fellows Participation in call coverage Engagement in scholarly activity, which is supported and encouraged Musculoskeletal radiologists primarily practice at a free-standing outpatient center supporting busy Orthopedic Oncology, Sports Medicine, Upper Extremity, and Joint Reconstruction programs, with frequent face-to-face collaboration with orthopedic faculty. Gainesville, with a metropolitan population of approximately 350,000, is home to one of the nation’s leading public universities and a major Division I athletic program. The area offers excellent schools, a growing technology sector, and an abundance of outdoor recreational opportunities. Gainesville is located less than 90 minutes from both the Atlantic and Gulf coasts and within two hours of Orlando, Tampa, and Jacksonville. The University of Florida is a leading academic institution and academic health center in the Southeast, offering a strong environment for clinical care, education, and research. Expected Salary: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. The University of Florida offers a comprehensive benefits package. Required Qualifications: At the time of application, candidates must: Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology Be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida prior to employment Preferred: Completion of a Musculoskeletal Radiology fellowship preferred, but not required. Special Instructions to Applicants: Qualified applicants should submit a CV and cover letter for consideration. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered official if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from institutions outside the United States must be evaluated by a credentialing service recognized by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES). The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Health Assessment Required: YES Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/538892/interventional-radiologist": {
      "title": "Interventional Radiologist",
      "description": "Interventional Radiologist Apply now Job no: 538892 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29130200 - MD-RADIOLOGY-ANGIO-INTERVENT Classification Title: Clinical Interventional Radiologist Classification Minimum Requirements: At the time of application, candidates must: 1. Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree. 2. Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology. 3. Hold or be eligible to obtain a medical license in the State of Florida. Additionally, the selected candidate must obtain IR/DR certification within one (1) year of the start date. Job Description: The Department of Radiology at the University of Florida College of Medicine is seeking a full-time Interventional Radiologist to join our clinical faculty on the non-tenure clinical track. Appointment rank will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. This position offers the opportunity to participate in a comprehensive interventional radiology practice within an academic medical center while contributing to the department’s missions in patient care and education. Responsibilities Provide comprehensive interventional radiology patient care Teach and mentor residents, fellows, and medical students Participate in scholarly activities Collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical teams Contribute to the development and adoption of emerging interventional procedures and techniques within the practice Clinical Expertise Candidates must demonstrate experience and competency in a wide range of interventional procedures, including: Y90 radioembolization (glass) DEB-TACE Uterine artery embolization (UAE) Percutaneous tumor ablations TIPS and other portal interventions Pulmonary/bronchial angiography and embolization Percutaneous transhepatic biliary drainage (PTHD) and biliary interventions Percutaneous nephrostomies Fistulagrams and declot procedures Vertebral augmentation Spine and pain interventions Sclerotherapy Trauma interventions Arterial, venous, portal, and pulmonary thrombolysis Core/basic interventional procedures The University of Florida is a leading academic institution and academic health center in the Southeast, offering a strong environment for clinical care, education, and research. Expected Salary: Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. The University of Florida offers a comprehensive benefits package. Required Qualifications: At the time of application, candidates must: 1. Hold an M.D. or D.O. degree. 2. Be Board Certified or Board Eligible in Radiology. 3. Hold or be eligible to obtain a medical license in the State of Florida. Additionally, the selected candidate must obtain IR/DR certification within one (1) year of the start date. Preferred: Preferred candidate will have completed an ACGME-accredited Vascular and Interventional Radiology Fellowship or an ACGME-accredited IR/DR Residency. Special Instructions to Applicants: Qualified applicants should submit a CV and cover letter for consideration. Final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an institution outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a credentialing service approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES): http://naces.org/ . The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
