    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541133/bank-of-america-eminent-scholar-in-finance": {
      "title": "Bank of America Eminent Scholar in Finance",
      "description": "Bank of America Eminent Scholar in Finance Apply now Job no: 541133 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 17060100 - BA-FIRE BUSINESS OFFICE Classification Title: Professor Job Description The University of Florida Warrington College of Business is seeking to hire a Full Professor of Finance to hold the Bank of America Eminent Scholar Chair. The successful candidate will be expected to enhance the research environment of the Eugene F. Brigham Finance, Insurance and Real Estate Department and the college through mentorship of doctoral students and active engagement on campus in the department’s research and intellectual life. Teaching duties will primarily be at the graduate level and come with an attractive teaching load. The position will begin in August 2027. The ideal candidate will have a record of impactful, highly cited research in top-tier finance and economics journals sustained over time. The position requires an active research agenda and recognition as a leading scholar in the field. A Ph.D. in finance or a closely related discipline is required, along with demonstrated teaching experience at the graduate level. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The University of Florida is ranked among the top public universities in the United States, and the Warrington College of Business is consistently ranked among the nation’s leading business schools. The Eugene F. Brigham Finance, Insurance and Real Estate Department includes more than 30 faculty members and has a strong research presence across corporate finance, investments, AI in finance, fintech, financial institutions, asset pricing, behavioral finance, household finance, and real estate. Faculty benefit from access to university-wide research infrastructure, including HiPerGator, UF’s advanced supercomputing cluster, and the on-campus Florida Federal Statistical Research Data Center. The department is also home to several research centers, including the FinTech Research Center and the Kelley A. Bergstrom Real Estate Center. The department serves more than 1,500 undergraduate finance majors and supports nationally recognized Master of Science in Finance (MSF) and Master of Science in Real Estate (MSRE) programs, as well as the new Master of Science in Finance and Technology (MSFT) program. The department’s rigorous Ph.D. program has a strong record of placing graduates at research universities in the United States and internationally. Expected Salary: Competitive and commensurate with experience and academic credentials. Required Qualifications: Ph.D. in finance or a closely related area and teaching experience at the graduate level. Preferred: The ideal candidate should have a record of impactful and highly cited research in top-tier finance and economics journals over a sustained period. Candidate with an active current research agenda and recognition as a top-flight scholar Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation to the University of Florida Careers website https://jobs.ufl.edu/ . Review of applications will begin immediately. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541134/astasofull-prof-in-finance": {
      "title": "AST/ASO/FULL PROF in Finance",
      "description": "AST/ASO/FULL PROF in Finance Apply now Job no: 541134 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 17060100 - BA-FIRE BUSINESS OFFICE Classification Title: Ast/Aso/Full Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: Must have a PhD in Finance or Economics or related fields (or evidence of meeting this requirement in the near future). Job Description: The Eugene F. Brigham Finance, Insurance and Real Estate Department of the Warrington College of Business invites applications for two tenure-track positions of Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance. Positions entail research and teaching requirements commensurate with a tenure track finance professor at a top-level U.S. University. Preference will be given to candidates with an established record of publications in top-tier journals, a strong ongoing research agenda, and the ability to contribute immediately to the department’s research and teaching missions. The positions begin in August 2027. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The University of Florida is ranked among the top public universities in the United States, and the Warrington College of Business is consistently ranked among the nation’s leading business schools. The Eugene F. Brigham Finance, Insurance and Real Estate Department includes more than 30 faculty members and has a strong research presence across corporate finance, investments, AI in finance, fintech, financial institutions, asset pricing, behavioral finance, household finance, and real estate. Faculty benefit from access to university-wide research infrastructure, including HiPerGator, UF’s advanced supercomputing cluster, and the on-campus Florida Federal Statistical Research Data Center. The department is also home to several research centers, including the FinTech Research Center and the Kelley A. Bergstrom Real Estate Center. The department serves more than 1,500 undergraduate finance majors and supports nationally recognized Master of Science in Finance (MSF) and Master of Science in Real Estate (MSRE) programs, as well as the new Master of Science in Finance and Technology (MSFT) program. The department’s rigorous Ph.D. program has a strong record of placing graduates at research universities in the United States and internationally. Expected Salary: Competitive and commensurate with experience and academic credentials. Required Qualifications: Must have a PhD in Finance or Economics or related fields (or evidence of meeting this requirement in the near future). Preferred: Evidence of top-tier publications. Also, a preference for senior Assistant rank professors for any Assistant-level hire. Demonstrated proficiency in academic research as evidenced by academic publications and working papers. Teaching experience at the collegiate level. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please apply at The University of Florida Careers website https/jobs.ufl.edu and provide the following: (a) cover letter with a curriculum vita, (b) three letters of recommendation, and (c) teaching evaluations (if available) or evidence of teaching excellence. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541159/clin-astasofull-prof": {
      "title": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF",
      "description": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF Apply now Job no: 541159 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Grant or Research Administration Department: 17030100 - BA-FSOA-BUSINESS OFFICE Classification Title: CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF Classification Minimum Requirements Candidates should possess an earned doctorate in Accounting or related discipline. Candidates for Associate or Full Clinical Professor should have at least 5 years of full time experience teaching accounting in a university setting and a history of publications that would meet the Fisher School’s criteria for classification as a Scholarly Academic under AACSB guidelines. Candidates for Assistant Clinical Professor should demonstrate potential for such publications. Job Description: The Fisher School of Accounting at the University of Florida seeks non-tenure track full-time Assistant, Associate, or Full Clinical Professor candidates for a position beginning Fall 2027. Primary teaching areas are financial and cost accounting at the undergraduate and master’s level, but ability to teach in a third area such as auditing, taxation, or information systems/analytics is a plus. Expected Salary: Commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Candidates should possess an earned doctorate in Accounting or related discipline. Candidates for Associate or Full Clinical Professor should have at least 5 years of full time experience teaching accounting in a university setting and a history of publications that would meet the Fisher School’s criteria for classification as a Scholarly Academic under AACSB guidelines. Candidates for Assistant Clinical Professor should demonstrate potential for such publications. Preferred Candidates should possess an earned doctorate in Accounting or related discipline. Candidates for Associate or Full Clinical Professor should have at least 5 years of full time experience teaching accounting in a university setting and a history of publications that would meet the Fisher School’s criteria for classification as a Scholarly Academic under AACSB guidelines. Candidates for Assistant Clinical Professor should demonstrate potential for such publications. Special Instructions to Applicants: Must submit online application along with CV, sample articles or book chapters, and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is an equal Opportunity Employer. The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541162/clinical-assistant-associate-professor-of-general-dentistry": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant / Associate Professor of General Dentistry",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant / Associate Professor of General Dentistry Apply now Job no: 541162 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Dentistry Department: 34170300 - DN-GENERAL DENT DIVISION Classification Title: Clinical Assistant / Associate Professor of General Dentistry Classification Minimum Requirements: The position’s requirements include a DDS, DMD or equivalent degree. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Dentistry is seeking applications for a full time clinical track faculty position in the Department of Restorative Dental Sciences, Division of General Dentistry at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank. The University of Florida College of Dentistry (UFCD) is one of the leading dental schools in the United States devoted to improving and promoting oral health throughout Florida, the nation and worldwide through excellence in teaching, research, patient care and service. Responsibilities for this position will center on learner-centered pre-doctoral level didactic, pre-clinical and clinical instruction in general dentistry, including serving as a course director, participation in intramural faculty practice, distinction in academic pursuits and service, and include opportunities for participation in the development of departmental research and/or other scholarly activities. Applicants should possess the skills and knowledge to provide clinical coverage in all aspects of general dentistry. As well as being a strong clinician, applicants should be organized, open minded, dedicated to excellence in teaching students according to the guidelines set by the department, proficient with technology and the use of electronic health records, abreast of current evidence-based dentistry and possess excellent communication skills. The position’s requirements include a DDS, DMD or equivalent degree. Teaching and private practice experience are preferred. Salary and rank are commensurate with credentials and experience. The University of Florida (UF), a member of the AAU, is the largest and most comprehensive public university in the state of Florida, with large undergraduate, graduate, and postgraduate educational programs. The UF Health Science Center and its six colleges (Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, Veterinary Medicine) are co-located on the Gainesville campus, with additional teaching, research, and patient care sites throughout Florida, and beyond. Expected Salary: Salary and rank are commensurate with credentials and experience Required Qualifications: The position’s requirements include a DDS, DMD or equivalent degree. Preferred: Teaching and private practice experience are preferred. Applicants should possess the skills and knowledge to provide clinical coverage in all aspects of general dentistry. As well as being a strong clinician, applicants should be organized, open minded, dedicated to excellence in teaching students according to the guidelines set by the department, proficient with technology and the use of electronic health records, abreast of current evidence-based dentistry and possess excellent communication skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: Initial review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until an applicant pool is identified. Applicants should attach a curriculum vitae, a cover letter describing their interest containing a statement of academic objectives, and a contact list of three references with their application for consideration. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. The University of Florida is An Equal Employment Opportunity Institution. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 352/392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800/955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. For more information about the University of Florida College of Dentistry, visit: www.dental.ufl.edu . Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541122/interventional-pulmonology-clinical-assistantassociatefull-pulmonary-critical-care-sleep": {
      "title": "Interventional Pulmonology - Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full - Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep",
      "description": "Interventional Pulmonology - Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full - Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep Apply now Job no: 541122 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Medicine/Physicians Department: 30050000 - JX-MEDICINE AT JAX Classification Title: Interventional Pulmonology - CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF - Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep Classification Minimum Requirements: Candidates should have a MD/DO, completion of an ACGME accredited fellowship in Pulmonary and Critical Care, completion of accredited lnterventional Pulmonology fellowship. Be BE/BC in Pulmonary Medicine and Critical Care Medicine. Job Description: The lnterventional Pulmonologist is a full-time faculty physician within the Division of Pulmonary, Critical Care & Sleep Medicine at the University of Florida College of Medicine Jacksonville. The position is responsible for providing specialized clinical care in lnterventional Pulmonology, participating in the education of medical students, residents, and fellows, engaging in scholarly activity, and contributing to the academic, clinical, and strategic missions of the University of Florida and UF Health Jacksonville. The faculty member will collaborate with multidisciplinary teams across the institution to provide comprehensive care for patients with complex airway, pleural, and thoracic diseases while supporting the continued growth of advanced bronchoscopy and thoracic oncology services. Appointment will be at the tenure/non-tenure accruing level of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, based on qualifications. Salary is negotiable; excellent benefits. About UF Health: UF Health is the Southeast's premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine - Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. About College of Medicine - Jacksonville (COM-J) The UF College of Medicine -Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country's leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine - Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission - to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit htt ps :// rned. jax.u fl.edu/ administ rative-aff airs/faculty-orientation-guide/. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable; excellent benefits Required Qualifications: Candidates should have a MD/DO, completion of an ACGME accredited fellowship in Pulmonary and Critical Care, completion of accredited lnterventional Pulmonology fellowship. Be BE/BC in Pulmonary Medicine and Critical Care Medicine. Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will begin to review applications as soon as an applicant pool is identified. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541129/assistant-professor-of-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Biology Apply now Job no: 541129 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 16900000 - LS-BIOLOGY Classification Title: Assistant Professor Classification Minimum Requirements: PhD in Biology, Computational Biology, Applied Mathematics or Biomathematics, or related field Job Description: Tenure-track Assistant Professor of Ecology and Evolution of Infectious Disease The Department of Biology in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) at the University of Florida invites applicants for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level focused on theoretical and quantitative approaches to the ecology and evolution of infectious disease. We are seeking an exceptional scholar to establish an externally funded research program to investigate fundamental questions on the dynamics of infectious disease and host-parasite systems using mathematical, quantitative or computational approaches. The position is aimed at deepening our theoretical and mathematical understanding of infectious disease systems, but we are open to applicants engaged in collaborative research at any level of biological organization, from cells to ecosystems, and in any system (e.g., marine, terrestrial, freshwater, human). This research program would ideally be broadly collaborative in nature, include both undergraduate and graduate students, and complement existing strengths in theoretical ecology and evolution in the department and across campus. Teaching could include contributions to the undergraduate curriculum in ecology and evolution, and specialized courses such as theoretical infectious disease biology, and the evolution of pathogens. The successful candidate would have an opportunity to interact with researchers in a wide variety of programs and units related to infectious disease at the University of Florida, including the UF Emerging Pathogens Institute, the Florida Museum of Natural History, the UF Genetics Institute, the UF Biodiversity Institute, the UF Informatics Institute, the Center for Statistics and Quantitative Infectious Diseases in the College of Medicine, the One Health Center of Excellence in the College of Public Health, the Department of Plant Pathology and other departments in the Institute for Food and Agricultural Sciences, and the Departments of Physics, Geography, and Mathematics (among others) within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. The candidate would have access to extraordinary data management and analysis resources, including one of the nation’s most powerful supercomputers. UF is the state’s oldest, largest, and most comprehensive land grant university with an enrollment of over 50,000 students. UF is located in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 50 miles from the Gulf, and 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean, and within a 2-hour drive to large metropolitan areas (Orlando, Tampa, Jacksonville). The beautiful climate and extensive nearby parks and recreational areas afford year-round outdoor activities, including hiking, biking, and nature photography. UF’s museums, and performing arts center support a range of activities and cultural events for residents to enjoy. Alachua County schools are highly rated and offer a variety of programs including magnet schools and an international baccalaureate program. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville . Expected Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. Benefits: This faculty position is eligible for a comprehensive benefits package that includes state medical, dental, and vision plans; life and disability coverage; multiple retirement options; and paid time away and university holidays. Learn more about UF faculty benefits here. Required Qualifications: PhD in Biology, Computational Biology, Applied Mathematics or Biomathematics, or related field Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applications must be submitted online. Click on Apply Now at the top of this posting. A complete application includes: Letter of application summarizing the applicant's qualifications, interests, and suitability for the position A complete curriculum vitae A statement of teaching philosophy A research statement The names and email addresses of three references must be provided. References will be asked by email to provide a letter after an initial screening process. Review of complete applications will begin on October 16, 2026, but applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the committee and/or hiring authority. The position will remain open until filled. If you have any further questions, please do not hesitate to contact the Chair of the search committee, Dr. José-Miguel Ponciano at josemi@ufl.edu . All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States require evaluation by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541141/ops-health-care-physician-generalist-obgyn": {
      "title": "OPS -Health Care Physician - Generalist -OB/GYN",
      "description": "OPS -Health Care Physician - Generalist -OB/GYN Apply now Job no: 541141 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 30070000 - JX-OB-GYN-JACKSONVILLE Classification Title: OPS -Health Care Physician - Generalist -OB/GYN Classification Minimum Requirements: MD/DO in Obstetrics and Gynecology Job Description: The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, College of Medicine - Jacksonville is seeking candidates to fill 2 OPS Health Care (Physician) positions. BE/BC is preferred. In addition, they must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License. ASSIGNMENTS include: Participation in daytime and overnight Labor and Delivery coverage which includes direct care of patients as the primary provider with supervision of and clinical teaching of a triage team that includes residents and medical students OB practices include management of low risk and high risk labor patients, caesareans, operative and spontaneous vaginal deliveries and post-operative management with direct supervision of residents GYN practices include floor and emergency department consultations, emergency surgical treatments with resident involvement Coverage of resident clinic and minor procedures possible Malpractice will be paid, however other benefits may not be available. The department is composed of 25 faculty members, and is based at the UF Health Science Center in Jacksonville, which is located on the easily accessible north part of downtown in Jacksonville, Florida. The UF Health Jacksonville hospital averages 3000-3500 deliveries a year and has a level 3 NICU staffed by UF neonatologists. The Department also employs full time faculty in Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery, Gynecologic Oncology, Maternal Fetal Medicine, and Minimally Invasive Surgery, which are available during overnight hours. About UF Health: UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. About College of Medicine – Jacksonville (COM-J): The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/. Expected Salary: $129.79 Required Qualifications: MD/DO in Obstetrics and Gynecology Preferred: BE/BC is preferred Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will begin to review applications on September 1, 2026. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 28 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541132/clin-astasofull-prof": {
      "title": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF",
      "description": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF Apply now Job no: 541132 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Education/Training/Instructional Design, Human Resources Department: 17020100 - BA-MANAGEMENT BUS OFFICE Classification Title: CLINICAL ASST/ASSO/FULL PROFESSOR Classification Minimum Requirements: Must have or anticipate receiving a doctorate degree in related fields of study before August 2027. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Final candidates will be required to provide official transcripts to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Job Description: The Management Department at the University of Florida Warrington College of Business seeks a non-tenure-track clinical professor (open rank at the assistant, associate, or full professor level) for one position in the area of organizational behavior/human resource (OB/HR) management. Responsibilities include teaching courses in leadership, creativity, and related OB/HR topics as well as producing scholarly research. The successful candidate will have a record of publishing in and teaching these topic areas or demonstrated potential to do so. This position will start in August 2027. Salary is competitive, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Responsibilities include teaching courses in leadership, creativity, and related OB/HR topics as well as producing scholarly research. The successful candidate will have a record of publishing in and teaching these topic areas or demonstrated potential to do so. Required Qualifications: Must have or anticipate receiving a doctorate degree in related fields of study before August 2027. Preferred: A dedication to teaching excellence. Evidence of an active research pipeline. A record of high-quality research. For applicants to the Associate or Full Professor position: A record of high-quality teaching in MBA courses. Evidence of leadership and service in one’s own institution and in the profession/field. Experience in working with junior faculty. Special Instructions to Applicants: INSTRUCTIONS: Submit a cover letter describing your interest in and qualifications for the position, curriculum vitae, evidence of teaching effectiveness, and a working paper. The position number is 00038001. To ensure full consideration, applications should be submitted by November 1st, 2026. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the hiring committee. Questions about the application process should be sent to Sokha Peck (Sokha.peck@warrington.ufl.edu). This position is open until filled. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 27 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541137/clinical-faculty-lecturer-clinical-assistantassociate-professor-college-of-nursing": {
      "title": "Clinical Faculty (Lecturer, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor)- College of Nursing",
      "description": "Clinical Faculty (Lecturer, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor)- College of Nursing Apply now Job no: 541137 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Allied Health, Nursing Department: 31030000 - NR-BNS-BIOBEHAVORIAL NUR SCI Classification Title: Clinical Faculty (Lecturer, Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor)- College of Nursing Classification Minimum Requirements: Clinical Lecturer • MSN from an accredited institution by date of hire. • Current RN license; Florida licensure eligible and obtained by date of hire. • Recent clinical experience in area of expertise. • Evidence of effective teaching or demonstrated potential for success as a clinical faculty member. Clinical Assistant Professor • Doctoral degree (DNP, EdD, PhD, or equivalent) from an accredited institution • Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution for applicants holding an EdD or PhD. • Current RN or APRN license; Florida licensure eligible and obtained by date of hire. • Recent clinical experience. • Evidence of effective teaching or demonstrated potential for success as a clinical faculty member. Clinical Associate Professor • Doctoral degree (DNP, EdD, PhD, or equivalent) from an accredited institution. • Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution for applicants holding an EdD or PhD. • Current RN or APRN license; Florida licensure required by date of hire. • National certification in specialty area, as applicable. • Sustained record of excellence in teaching and student mentorship. • Evidence of scholarship and professional contributions consistent with appointment at the associate professor rank. • Demonstrated service contributions at the college, university, clinical, and/or professional level. • Recent and ongoing clinical expertise in area of specialization. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Nursing seeks qualified applicants for non-tenure track clinical faculty positions at the rank of Clinical Lecturer, Clinical Assistant Professor, or Clinical Associate Professor, depending on qualifications and experience. The positions are for full-time, twelve-month, 1.0 FTE faculty. Part-time, evening and weekends, or 9-month appointments will also be considered. Priority will be given to applicants who have expertise in teaching undergraduate skills and simulation in the laboratory setting. New educators are also strongly encouraged to apply. These positions are primarily located in Gainesville, Florida . Selected positions are also available on the Jacksonville campus , depending on programmatic needs. These are not remote or online faculty positions. Key Responsibilities Teaching Facilitate laboratory and simulation in the BSN program as assigned. Collaborate with faculty teaching teams to ensure excellence in instructional delivery and student outcomes. Participate in curriculum development, evaluation, and continuous quality improvement activities. Maintain clinical expertise and appropriate professional credentials. Advise and mentor undergraduate students. Engage in continuing professional development to enhance teaching effectiveness. Scholarship For assistant/associate professor ranks, participate in scholarship related to clinical practice or nursing education. Service Provide service to the College of Nursing, University, profession, and community consistent with assigned rank. About the University of Florida The University of Florida is ranked among the nation's top public universities and is currently ranked #7 among public universities by U.S. News & World Report . UF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), one of North America's most prestigious organizations of leading research universities. With more than 50,000 students and 16 colleges, UF offers extensive opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. Major research resources include the Clinical and Translational Science Institute, UF Health Cancer Center, McKnight Brain Institute, Institute on Aging, Emerging Pathogens Institute, and Genetics Institute. UF's comprehensive AI initiative and HiPerGator supercomputing resources further support innovation in education, research, and healthcare. About the UF College of Nursing Under the leadership of Dean Shakira Henderson, the College of Nursing recently launched its strategic plan, Elevate 2029, reflecting the College's commitment to Care, Lead, and Inspire Boldly. The College offers nationally recognized educational programs including: BSN (Traditional and Accelerated) RN-to-BSN Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) PhD in Nursing Science The UF BSN program is ranked among the nation's best and is recognized as the top BSN program in Florida. As part of UF Health, the College collaborates extensively with clinical and research partners across the academic health center. Faculty have opportunities to engage with UF Health hospitals and clinics, the North Florida/South Georgia Veterans Health System, Archer Family Health Care, and numerous community partners throughout Florida. The College maintains campuses in Gainesville and Jacksonville and supports a culture of innovation, collaboration, and excellence in education, research, service, and patient care. Why Gainesville? Located in north central Florida, Gainesville offers a vibrant university community with abundant outdoor recreation, cultural events, Division I athletics, excellent healthcare, and easy access to Florida's beaches and major metropolitan areas. Join a faculty community committed to excellence in nursing education, innovative scholarship, and exceptional clinical care while preparing the next generation of nursing leaders. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Clinical Lecturer • MSN from an accredited institution by date of hire. • Current RN license; Florida licensure eligible and obtained by date of hire. • Recent clinical experience in area of expertise. • Evidence of effective teaching or demonstrated potential for success as a clinical faculty member. Clinical Assistant Professor • Doctoral degree (DNP, EdD, PhD, or equivalent) from an accredited institution • Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution for applicants holding an EdD or PhD. • Current RN or APRN license; Florida licensure eligible and obtained by date of hire. • Recent clinical experience. • Evidence of effective teaching or demonstrated potential for success as a clinical faculty member. Clinical Associate Professor • Doctoral degree (DNP, EdD, PhD, or equivalent) from an accredited institution. • Master's degree in nursing from an accredited institution for applicants holding an EdD or PhD. • Current RN or APRN license; Florida licensure required by date of hire. • National certification in specialty area, as applicable. • Sustained record of excellence in teaching and student mentorship. • Evidence of scholarship and professional contributions consistent with appointment at the associate professor rank. • Demonstrated service contributions at the college, university, clinical, and/or professional level. • Recent and ongoing clinical expertise in area of specialization. Preferred: Prior experience teaching in BSN program. Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) credential, or goal of earning CHSE credential within 2 years. Experience with simulation and clinical instruction. Experience mentoring undergraduate nursing students. Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested candidates must submit a curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation. Optional additions for an application package may include: a research statement and a teaching statement. Final candidate will be required to provide three (3) letters of recommendation and an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. This position is 'open until filled'. Review of applicant materials will begin immediately, and continue until the position has been filled. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 27 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541093/assistantassociatefull-professor-epilepsy-division": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Epilepsy Division",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Epilepsy Division Apply now Job no: 541093 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Allied Health, Medicine/Physicians Department: 29180200 - MD-NEUROLOGY-EPILEPSY Classification Title: Ast/Aso/Full Prof Classification Minimum Requirements: All candidates must have completed at least one year of post‑residency fellowship training in epilepsy and EEG. Job Description: The University of Florida Division of Epilepsy is seeking faculty candidates at all career stages (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) who have completed at least one year of epilepsy/EEG fellowship training after residency. The successful candidate will join a comprehensive epilepsy team that includes neurologists, a neuroscientist, advanced practice nurses, and a nurse navigator, with strong multidisciplinary support from neurosurgery, neuropsychology, neuropathology, and neuroradiology. Clinical and academic interests may include tertiary epilepsy care, epilepsy surgery, neurophysiology, brain imaging, or critical care EEG monitoring. The Division is part of a nationally recognized neurology department with more than 50 neurologists, a robust residency and fellowship training program, and an endowed epilepsy research center. The UF Comprehensive Epilepsy Program offers advanced services including SEEG, epilepsy surgery, and ICU EEG monitoring within a dedicated Neuromedicine Hospital. UF is ranked among the nation’s top public universities and is home to world-class research and neuroscience institutes, including the McKnight Brain Institute and Norman Fixel Institute for Neurological Diseases. The university invests more than $1 billion annually in research and fosters extensive interdisciplinary collaboration. Located in Gainesville, Florida, UF offers the advantages of a vibrant college town with excellent schools, abundant recreational opportunities, mild winters, and convenient access to beaches and major Florida cities. Expected Salary: Salary is commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: All candidates must have completed at least one year of post‑residency fellowship training in epilepsy and EEG. Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Candidates must apply online at https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/ and should include a letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, and three letters of recommendation. Letters of recommendation may be attached to the application or sent directly to Polly Glattli, glattpa@ufl.edu. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 26 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541052/clinical-assistantassociate-professor-family-medicine": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor -Family Medicine",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor -Family Medicine Apply now Job no: 541052 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Medicine/Physicians Department: 30160000 - JX-COMMUNITY MEDICINE-JAX Classification Title: Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor -Family Medicine Classification Minimum Requirements: Candidates must be MD/DO and have a Florida Medical License Job Description UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/ . Expected Salary: Negotiable based on Qualifications and Experience Required Qualifications Candidates must be MD/DO and have a Florida Medical License Preferred: Board certified or board eligible. Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will begin to review applications on November 1, 2026. Please provide letter of intent and Resume/Curriculum Vitae and contact information for three Professional References. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. This is a time-limited position. This position is open until filled. Health Assessment Required: yes Advertised: 25 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541090/open-rank-faculty-american-government-history-literature-and-law-aghll": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty - American Government, History, Literature, and Law (AGHLL)",
      "description": "Open Rank Faculty - American Government, History, Literature, and Law (AGHLL) Apply now Job no: 541090 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Humanities, Legal/Audit Services/Compliance Department: 57301000 - HS-HAMILTON SCHOOL ADMIN Classification Title: AST/ASO/FULL PROF Classification Minimum Requirements A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree. Job Description: Established in 2022, the Hamilton School is a multidisciplinary academic unit whose purpose is to support teaching and research concerning the ideas, traditions, and texts that shape Western civilization and American values and institutions. The School offers four undergraduate degrees, five undergraduate minors and two graduate degrees. The Hamilton School for Classical and Civic Education at the University of Florida invites applications for tenure-track and tenured faculty positions in American Government, History, Literature, and Law (AGHLL) to begin in August 2027. Hamilton seeks to fill several tenure-track and tenured faculty positions, starting in the 2027-28 academic year. Responsibilities include offering courses in Hamilton’s AGHLL major, as well as ordinarily contributing to one of Hamilton’s three other majors: (1) Great Books and Ideas; (2) Philosophy, Politics, Economics and Law; or (3) War, Statecraft and Strategy. Applicants are welcome from all relevant disciplines, including but not limited to political science, jurisprudence, constitutional studies, history, literature, religion and art history. The search is open with regard to period, ranging from colonial to contemporary America. The search is open rank, with scholars at the Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor level all encouraged to apply. Applicants are encouraged to visit the Hamilton School website ( Hamilton School ) to learn more about the Hamilton School for Classical and Civic Education. UF is the state’s oldest, largest, and most comprehensive land grant university with an enrollment of over 50,000 students and was ranked the Number 1 public university in the United States by Wall Street Journal in its “2024 Best Colleges in the U.S.” report. UF is located in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 50 miles from the Gulf of Mexico, and 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean, and within a 2-hour drive to large metropolitan areas (Orlando, Tampa, Jacksonville). The beautiful climate and extensive nearby parks and recreational areas afford year-round outdoor activities, including hiking, biking, and nature photography. UF’s large college sports programs, museums, and performing arts centers support a range of activities and cultural events for residents to enjoy. Alachua County schools are highly rated and offer a variety of programs including magnet schools and an international baccalaureate program. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville. The salary is competitive and commensurate with education and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. Employment Benefits include: - Health Insurance: UF participates in state- and university-sponsored benefits programs for individuals, families, and domestic partners, and offers voluntary insurance that includes vision, dental, long-term disability and more. - Retirement Options: Attractive options include Florida Retirement System Pension Plan, State University System Optional Retirement Program, Florida Retirement System Investment Plan, and Voluntary Retirement Savings Plan. - Leave: UF staff enjoy a generous paid leave plan as well as access to a sick-leave pool, maternity/paternity leave and leave payouts. Expected Salary: Commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree. Preferred Special Instructions to Applicants: A complete application must include: A Curriculum Vitae A cover letter addressing: Research agenda, Teaching interests and competencies; and Commitment to undergraduate and graduate education in the principles and institutions of American civilization. A sample writing sample from within the last three years; and A list of three academic references with contact information. Please address any inquiries to: Professor Paul C.H. Lim Associate Director for Faculty Affairs Hamilton School for Classical & Civic Education University of Florida 432 Newell Drive Gainesville, FL 32611 paul.lim@ufl.edu This position is open until filled. Review of applications will begin immediately, and continue until the position has been filled. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 25 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541097/dean-of-the-college-of-liberal-arts-and-sciences": {
      "title": "Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences",
      "description": "Dean of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences Apply now Job no: 541097 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Executive/Director/Management Department: 16010000 - LS-DEANS OFFICE Classification Title: DEAN & PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate, a distinguished record of academic, teaching, and research achievements worthy of appointment as professor with tenure in an academic department in the College, and an excellent record of academic leadership and administrative experience. Job Description: Applications will only be considered if submitted directly to Parker Executive Search Website: https://www.parkersearch.com/opportunities/dean-college-of-liberal-arts-and-sciences-uf About the Opportunity The Dean reports to the Provost and serves as the chief academic officer of the College, providing leadership, support, and advocacy for all academic departments and multi-disciplinary programs, their faculty and staff, and budgets. The Dean serves as the principal administrator for planning and leading CLAS, encouraging curricular and pedagogical innovation. The Dean of the College is assisted by a team of Associate Deans whose multifaceted portfolios include Undergraduate Curriculum and Instruction, Graduate Affairs, Faculty Affairs, Research, and Facilities and Infrastructure. CLAS is also supported by the offices of Advancement, Communications, Finance, Human Resources, Information Technology, and Research. About the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) is the foundational college for undergraduate education at the University of Florida, offering a broad education that prepares young people to be problem solvers, informed citizens, and lifelong learners. CLAS is UF’s largest college, with 12,800 students, more than 750 teaching faculty, a budget exceeding $200 million, and a sponsored research portfolio of around $40 million a year. It is also the most heterogeneous: the College’s twenty-two disciplinary departments and over forty centers, labs, and institutes catalyze research across disciplinary intersections both within the College and across the UF campus. The undergraduate population is home to the largest number of first-generation and Pell-eligible students. CLAS has an advancement team of 16 full-time professionals, including eight frontline fundraisers. In addition to fundraising and donor relations responsibilities, the Advancement team manages the College’s 11 advisory boards, including the Dean’s Leadership Council and 10 department/center boards. More than 125 volunteers are engaged with these boards and support the College in various ways. About the Opportunity The Dean reports to the Provost and serves as the chief academic officer of the College, providing leadership, support, and advocacy for all academic departments and multi-disciplinary programs, their faculty and staff, and budgets. The Dean serves as the principal administrator for planning and leading CLAS, encouraging curricular and pedagogical innovation. The Dean of the College is assisted by a team of Associate Deans whose multifaceted portfolios include Undergraduate Curriculum and Instruction, Graduate Affairs, Faculty Affairs, Research, and Facilities and Infrastructure. CLAS is also supported by the offices of Advancement, Communications, Finance, Human Resources, Information Technology, and Research. About the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) The College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) is the foundational college for undergraduate education at the University of Florida, offering a broad education that prepares young people to be problem solvers, informed citizens, and lifelong learners. CLAS is UF’s largest college, with 12,800 students, more than 750 teaching faculty, a budget exceeding $200 million, and a sponsored research portfolio of around $40 million a year. It is also the most heterogeneous: the College’s twenty-two disciplinary departments and over forty centers, labs, and institutes catalyze research across disciplinary intersections both within the College and across the UF campus. The undergraduate population is home to the largest number of first-generation and Pell-eligible students. CLAS has an advancement team of 16 full-time professionals, including eight frontline fundraisers. In addition to fundraising and donor relations responsibilities, the Advancement team manages the College’s 11 advisory boards, including the Dean’s Leadership Council and 10 department/center boards. More than 125 volunteers are engaged with these boards and support the College in various ways. About the University of Florida The University of Florida (UF) is the flagship university for the state of Florida, the nation’s third most populous state. Located in Gainesville, UF has 16 colleges, a major academic health center, championship-winning athletics, and, in keeping with its land-grant mission, one of the nation’s most comprehensive agriculture and natural resources programs. The University’s 2,000-acre campus joins a historic core with advanced research and classroom facilities and preserved natural areas, all connecting to adjacent innovation, commercial, and residential districts. UF is ranked 7th among the nation’s top public universities in the 2025 U.S. News Best Colleges rankings. Dean, College of Liberal Arts and Sciences · University of Florida 13 UF has over 60,000 students, 32,000 employees, a $10 billion annual budget, and more than 140 mission-focused units across Florida, including statewide healthcare and agricultural enterprises. It is one of only two public universities in Florida belonging to the Association of American Universities (comprising 71 leading public and private research universities in the U.S. and Canada). UF has more than 6,600 faculty members with distinguished records in teaching, research, and service, including 22 Eminent Scholar Chairs, 38 elected members of the National Academies, 20 elected members of the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, and 91 elected members of the American Association for the Advancement of Science. In 2024–25, UF research expenditures topped $1.33 billion. Total Rewards Salary is competitive and commensurate with education and experience. The University of Florida offers a generous benefits package that includes insurance such as health, life, and dental as well as vacation, sick leave and personal days. Explore UF Benefits . Expected Salary: Commensurate based on experience and education. Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate, a distinguished record of academic, teaching, and research achievements worthy of appointment as professor with tenure in an academic department in the College, and an excellent record of academic leadership and administrative experience. Preferred: The successful candidate must be an outstanding leader and fierce advocate of the College who possesses a clear commitment to both undergraduate and graduate education and research. The ideal candidate will possess a visionary approach to fundraising, a commitment to advancing research while maintaining teaching excellence, and a dedication to investing in the development and well-being of faculty, staff, and students. Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Advisory Committee invites letters of nomination and applications (letter of interest, full resume/CV, and contact information of at least five references) to be submitted to the search firm assisting the University. Review of materials will begin immediately and continue until the appointment is made. It is preferred, however, that all nominations and applications are submitted before January 8, 2027. Please submit electronic applications directly to Parker Executive Search . For additional information, please contact: Laurie Wilder, President Porsha Williams, Vice President and Managing Director, Higher Education Jacob Anderson, Senior Principal Hamilton Mason, Executive Recruiting Coordinator Parker Executive Search Five Concourse Parkway, Suite 2875 | Atlanta, GA 30328 (770) 804-1996 ext. 111 lwilder@parkersearch.com || pwilliams@parkersearch.com janderson@parkersearch.com || hmason@parkersearch.com Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 25 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541074/mgr-it": {
      "title": "MGR, IT",
      "description": "MGR, IT Apply now Job no: 541074 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Executive/Director/Management, Information Technology, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 27010719 - HA-IT MISCELLANEOUS SERVICES Classification Title: MGR, IT Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree and four years of relevant experience; or an associate’s degree and six years of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: SUPERVISION & STAFF MANAGEMENT Supervise IAM staff in course of daily business. Coordinate activities by scheduling work assignments, setting priorities, and directing the work of subordinate employees. Plan and coordinate project schedules and related activities. Participate in planning and administering department and project budgets. Resolve complex problems escalated by staff members. Resolve escalated problems referred by subordinate supervisors or staff members. ANALYSIS Identify, evaluate, support, and solve complex issues related to area of expertise. Resolve escalated problems referred by subordinate supervisors or staff members. Develop a complete understanding of customer business processes and system needs. Understand how system contributes to department’s process workflow. Identify and develop mitigations for potential system impacts across multiple systems. Identify business process impacts across departments. Participate in analyzing of current IS processes and standards. MAINTENANCE & SUPPORT Prepare long- and short-range plans for IAM strategy, including applications selection, systems development, systems maintenance, production activities, and necessary support resources. Maintain IAM day-to-day processes and systems with minimal adverse impact to customers and IS. Resolve issues timely and thoroughly. Coordinate with, and communicate to primary stakeholders. Determine root causes of issues and follows up on all matters. Seek, recommend, and implement opportunities for support process improvements. Guide customers to develop change control processes. Recommend opportunities for process improvement. TECHNICAL PERFORMANCE Supervise and provide highly complex technical design, implementation, maintenance, and system administration for IAM and in support of IT technical and applications teams. Apply technical skills needed to supervise staff assignments effectively. Remain proficient with tools and maintains knowledge of newest features. Utilize breadth of technical experience results in solutions to complex problems. Identify potential data discrepancies and their impact; recommend modifications. PROJECT & TASK MANAGEMENT Participate in departmental and enterprise project planning. Plan and coordinate project schedules and related activities involving IAM staff members. Plan, execute, and monitor projects and/or tasks according to IS standards and management expectations. Apply advanced project management concepts and established procedures across multiple departments. Build, monitor, and adjust the plan with minimal assistance. Anticipate, understand, and act to mitigate potential impacts to projects. Prioritize tasks according to departmental and strategic objectives Expected Salary: $100,000 Required Qualifications: Master's degree and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree and four years of relevant experience; or an associate’s degree and six years of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Preferred: Advanced knowledge of Entra ID (Azure AD) and Active Directory, including identity lifecycle management, authentication, authorization, and hybrid identity architectures. Strong understanding of IAM architecture principles, including the design and implementation of scalable, secure, and compliant identity solutions across complex enterprise environments. Experience with workflow design and identity automation to streamline provisioning, deprovisioning, access requests, approvals, and governance processes. Knowledge of Privileged Access Management (PAM) integrations and privileged access engineering. Strong understanding of identity governance concepts, including access certifications, separation of duties, role-based access controls, policy enforcement, and compliance requirements. Experience integrating identity platforms with enterprise applications through API integrations, web services, and modern authentication protocols. Knowledge of healthcare-specific access management requirements. Ability to evaluate, design, and support integrated identity ecosystems that leverage Entra ID, Active Directory, PAM solutions, and other enterprise technologies to enable secure and efficient access management. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please upload the following - CV or Resume, Cover Letter and List of Professional References. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539583/instructional-designer-campaign": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer Campaign",
      "description": "Instructional Designer Campaign Apply now Job no: 539583 Work type: Staff Full-Time, Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources, Campaign Department: As an Instructional Designer with the University of Florida Human Resources, you won’t just create courses; you’ll influence how a top-tier university learns, adapts, and performs. In this role, you’ll collaborate with senior leaders, subject matter experts, and HR partners to design innovative, evidence-based learning experiences that drive measurable impact across a complex, mission-driven organization. Here, instructional design is more than production, its strategy. You’ll have the autonomy to shape solutions, experiment with modern learning approaches, and apply research-backed practices to real organizational challenges. From leadership development to workforce transformation, your work will directly elevate employee performance and institutional effectiveness. At UF HR, you’ll find a rare combination of creative ownership and strategic influence, along with the opportunity to work across diverse topics, audiences, and formats. If you’re motivated by meaningful impact, continuous innovation, and the chance to shape learning at scale, this is where your work will matter most. CORE FOCUS AREAS: Leadership & professional development Organizational effectiveness & change readiness Workforce upskilling and reskilling Digital learning innovation (eLearning, microlearning, blended learning) YOU WILL: Design and develop engaging, scalable learning experiences across multiple modalities Partner with subject matter experts and stakeholders to translate business needs into learning strategies Create high-quality digital content including eLearning, instructor-led materials, job aids, and multimedia assets Apply instructional design methodologies and adult learning principles to drive measurable outcomes Evaluate program effectiveness and continuously improve based on data and feedback QUALITIES AND CORE RESPONSIBILITIES Learning Strategy & Design Conduct needs assessments to identify performance gaps and recommend learning solutions Design visually compelling, learner-centered content that enhances engagement and retention Develop end-to-end learning experiences using tools such as Articulate Storyline, Rise, and multimedia platforms Ensure alignment with organizational goals and measurable business outcomes Project & Program Management Lead & manage multiple projects simultaneously, managing timelines, stakeholders, and deliverables Support implementation of system-wide learning initiatives and programs Develop rapid, high-quality content in fast-paced environments Collaboration & Consultation Partner with leaders, HR teams, and SMEs to co-create impactful learning solutions Facilitate training sessions and workshops for faculty and staff Translate complex processes into clear, actionable learning experiences Innovation & Continuous Improvement Stay current with emerging trends in instructional design and workplace learning Engage leading technologies and approaches to enhance learning effectiveness Evaluate learning impact and refine programs to maximize ROI Phased deliverables and aggressive timelines WHY JOIN OUR TEAM? At the University of Florida, you’ll be part of a nationally recognized institution committed to excellence in education, research, and employee development. Our work has been recognized with the Florida TaxWatch Productivity Award, reflecting our strong emphasis on innovation, efficiency, and measurable impact. To learn more about our team, Click Here WHAT SETS THIS ROLE APART: Creative Ownership – Design innovative learning experiences that reach thousands Strategic Influence – Partner with leaders to shape workforce capability Modern Learning Environment – Work with cutting-edge tools and methodologies Mission-Driven Impact – Contribute to a culture of continuous learning and growth TOTAL REWARDS The University of Florida offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your well-being and long-term success, including competitive compensation, robust health and retirement programs, generous leave and holiday plans, and meaningful opportunities for professional growth and career advancement, all within a collaborative, high-performing academic community. For more information on our elevated benefits Click Here . REQUIRED EXPERIENCE Hiring for both temporary positions (not extending beyond December 2027) and regular full-time instructional design roles across multiple levels. Placements decisions will be based on candidates’ experience, education, and demonstrated impact. Instructional Designer II Master’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and four years of relevant experience. Instructional Designer III Master's degree in an appropriate area and four years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and six years of relevant experience. Demonstrated experience running complex, large‑scale programs such as GBAS, RAFT, or comparable efforts PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Proven ability to lead instructional design projects from needs analysis through implementation and evaluation Digital Portfolio with at least one Rise Course. Advanced experience designing and developing engaging, high-quality learning solutions (eLearning, instructor-led, blended, microlearning) Strong consultation skills with the ability to translate complex business needs into effective learning strategies Demonstrated project management experience, including managing multiple initiatives simultaneously Experience with rapid development tools and multimedia learning assets (e.g., Abode Creative Suite, Canva) Ability to evaluate program effectiveness and align learning solutions with organizational goals and performance outcomes Demonstrated ability to independently design and develop instructional materials across multiple modalities Experience using eLearning authoring tools such as Articulate Storyline and Rise Ability to manage multiple projects and timelines with minimal supervision Strong collaboration skills working with subject matter experts and stakeholders Experience applying instructional design methodologies and evaluating learning effectiveness NOTICE TO APPLICANTS Interest forms for opportunities will be reviewed on an ongoing basis as positions become available. Should you be considered to advance in the screening and selection process, you will be contacted by the department. Because this is a pooled recruitment, applicants may not receive immediate updates regarding their status. Hiring managers will review qualified candidates as openings arise, and selected applicants will be contacted directly for further screening, interviews, or additional documentation. We appreciate your patience throughout this process. Inclusion in the talent pool indicates that your application will remain active and eligible for consideration for up to six months from the date of submission. Applicants are encouraged to ensure that contact information remains current during this period. Advertised: 21 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/537918/assistantassociatefull-professor-sleep-medical-director": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Sleep Medical Director",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Sleep Medical Director Apply now Job no: 537918 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty, Non-Tenure-Track Faculty, Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Executive/Director/Management, Medicine/Physicians Department: 29050903 - MD-PULMONARY-OTHER Classification Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Sleep Medical Director Classification Minimum Requirements: MD or DO with Board Certification/Board Eligibility in Sleep Medicine. Candidates must be eligible for licensure in the State of Florida. Job Description: The University of Florida College of Medicine–Gainesville, is seeking applicants for a Sleep Medical Director within the Department of Medicine. This is a 1.0 FTE position reporting to the chief of the division. Responsibilities include overseeing clinical care delivered by faculty within the Sleep program, promoting investigator-initiated scholarship, and engaging in training of house staff and students. Substantial commitments of space and resources will be available for the successful candidate to expand Divisional activities. Appointment will be at the tenure or non-tenure accruing level of Assistant/Associate/Full Professor, based on qualifications. The division has a collaborative relationship with UF Health Shands Hospital and we pride ourselves in professional and cooperative interdisciplinary care. The Department of Medicine is a national leader in cancer, cardiology, gastroenterology, kidney disorders, and pulmonology. About UF Health: UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: MD or DO with Board Certification/Board Eligibility in Sleep Medicine. Candidates must be eligible for licensure in the State of Florida. Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes. Advertised: 20 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
