    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539287/data-scientist-iv": {
      "title": "Data Scientist IV",
      "description": "Data Scientist IV Apply now Job no: 539287 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Computer Science, Health Care Administration/Support, Physical/Mathematical Sciences Department: 57720000 - INSTITUTE-CHILD HEALTH POLICY Classification Title: Data Scientist IV Classification Minimum Requirements: A Bachelor's Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and seven years of experience; Master's Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and five years of experience; Doctoral Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and three years of experience. Job Description: The Institute for Child Health Policy (ICHP) at the University of Florida is seeking a Data Scientist IV to join its leadership team. This role focuses on supporting research and program evaluation for Medicaid and the Children’s Health Insurance Program (CHIP), assessing the quality of care for beneficiaries. The ideal candidate will have expertise in administrative healthcare data, Medicaid policy, and advanced analytical methods. Responsibilities include leading research projects, developing data-driven insights, collaborating with a multidisciplinary team of health policy researchers and economists, and authoring technical reports. Strong communication skills and a proven track record in data science are essential. Research Development: Leverage expertise in healthcare administrative and clinical data to support the design and execution of research studies evaluating healthcare quality, access, and outcomes for the Medicaid population. Apply advanced analytical methods and predictive analytics to address key complex policy and operational questions. Lead development of study frameworks, analytic plans, and methodological documentation. Collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams to identify critical healthcare challenges and translate research objectives into executable analytic strategies. Serve as lead or first author on technical reports, policy briefs, peer-reviewed journal articles, and other scholarly or applied publications. Produce high-quality written products suitable for internal leadership, state and federal stakeholders, and academic dissemination. Data Analytics: Apply data science methodologies using SAS, Python, R, and SQL to analyze large-scale healthcare administrative and clinical datasets. Develop, optimize, and validate analytic code and database queries to integrate multi-source data into centralized analytic environments. Ensure rigorous data transformation, quality assurance, and reproducibility of analytic workflows. Interpret findings within the context of Medicaid policy and healthcare delivery systems. Scientific Reporting and Policy Integration: Interpret and apply state and federal regulations relevant to assigned projects, identifying policy implications based on research findings and integrating recommendations into descriptive and technical reports. Demonstrate exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to independently author technical documentation, methodological appendices, analytic summaries, and executive-level briefings. Drive strategic initiatives, lead enterprise change management efforts, and foster collaborations with external stakeholders within the Medicaid agency. Team Development, Training, and Hiring: Participate in recruitment, training, supervision, and mentorship of analytic staff. Provide guidance on methodological rigor, documentation standards, reproducibility practices, and professional development. Lead or co-lead project teams, providing strategic, tactical, and operational leadership. Promote a culture of analytical excellence, scholarly contribution, and high-quality written and oral communication. Other Duties: Support drafting budgets, data use agreements, and other project-related duties as assigned. Expected Salary: $98,000 - $110,000 Required Qualifications: A Bachelor's Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and seven years of experience; Master's Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and five years of experience; Doctoral Degree in data science, statistics, bioinformatics, analytics, or similar field and three years of experience. Preferred: 5+ years of client relations activities, interpreting and synthesizing client requirements and effectively communicating complex healthcare analytic outcomes to client satisfaction. Experience in mining large payer databases with various healthcare benefit structures for Federal and State public plans. Strong supervisory experience leading project teams and/or demonstrated mentorship ability guiding new analysts. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to communicate technical outcomes with a high degree of detail and precision to technical audiences, while at the same time being able to communicate those outcomes to non-technical audiences in an approachable and understandable manner. Exceptional problem-solving abilities, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and the ability to multitask while meeting deadlines. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a time limited position. This requisition will be used to fill multiple positions and has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/539783/chemistry-postdoctoral-associate-unsupervised-and-generative-machine-learning": {
      "title": "Chemistry Post-Doctoral Associate - Unsupervised and Generative Machine Learning",
      "description": "Chemistry Post-Doctoral Associate - Unsupervised and Generative Machine Learning Apply now Job no: 539783 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Grant or Research Administration, Artificial Intelligence, Physical/Mathematical Sciences, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 16120100 - LS-CHEMISTRY-GENERAL Classification Title: Post-Doctoral Associate in unsupervised and generative ML for chemistry Classification Minimum Requirements: PhD in Chemistry or related area Strong coding (Python) and algorithm design skills Expertise on ML tools for chemistry, in particular, generative AI Experience with Python, ML, and AI for chemical applications Job Description: A Post-doctoral Associate in Theoretical Chemistry is available for work on a project in unsupervised and generative ML for chemical applications led by Dr. Ramon Miranda Quintana in the Department of Chemistry. We have a position available in our group to work on the development, implementation, and application of hyper-efficient unsupervised learning techniques to chemical problems, with emphasis on improvements to representation learning and generative methods. Must have PhD in Chemistry or related area. This position will be initially awarded for one year, and, contingent upon strong performance and conduct and availability of funds, may be renewed for up to two years. Expected Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. To see more, visit benefits.hr.ufl.edu . Required Qualifications: PhD in Chemistry or related area Strong coding (Python) and algorithm design skills Expertise on ML tools for chemistry, in particular, generative AI Experience with Python, ML, and AI for chemical applications Preferred: Familiarity with HPC systems Proven track record of research in ML/AI for chemistry Strong coding foundation (Python) Knowledge of C++ and CUDA Special Instructions to Applicants: For full consideration, applications must be submitted online. Click on Apply Now at the top of this posting. A complete application includes (1) a letter of application summarizing the applicant's qualifications, interests, and suitability for the position, (2) a complete curriculum vitae , (3) a list of at least two references. After initial review, letters of recommendation will be requested from the references for selected applicants. Applications will be reviewed beginning immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. Only complete applications will be reviewed at this time. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the committee and/or hiring authority. All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a review of criminal records, reference checks, and verification of education. The selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an educational institution outside of the United States require evaluation by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540218/custodial-worker-iii": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker III",
      "description": "Custodial Worker III Apply now Job no: 540218 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 63400300 - FS-BLDGSRVC OPERATIONS-HC Classification Title: Custodial Worker III Classification Minimum Requirements: Completion of ninth grade and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: Leadership Functions –Receive assignments from Supervisor that may include working alone or with a small group and overseeing the work of others while working alongside them. Leads a team of custodial workers; directs, leads, and/or coordinates the work of others. Assists in continuous training and daily monitoring the work of custodial employees. Orders supplies and manages equipment inventory and budget. Participates with the supervisor in discussions with employees pertaining to work performance and behavioral issues. Assists new employees with inputting time-off requests as needed. In the absence of the Custodial Supervisor, the Lead Worker supervises the work group. Manages processes and phases in AiM and assigns work orders. Work Functions –Cleans and maintains daily all halls, offices, shops, classrooms, conference rooms, labs, gym areas, locker rooms, restrooms, and elevators which includes sweeping, dusting, dust- mopping, wet-mopping, spot- mopping, operating floor care equipment such as scrubbers and burnishers, reconditioning of floors (shower scrub and topcoat) and spot washing and cleaning of walls, doors, and partitions, empty trash. Cleans and maintains all floors and floor coverings which includes regular duties such as vacuuming, burnishing, and encapsulation of carpets. Follow procedures for the use of chemical cleaners and power equipment to prevent damage to floors and fixtures. Mix water and detergents in containers to prepare cleaning solutions according to specifications. Cleans all entrances, entrances, steps, patios and concourses. Spot cleans and cleans all exterior and interior glass surfaces of all assigned buildings. Cleans ceiling lights and vents. Empties and cleans all waste cans, trashcans, recycle bins, water fountains, etc. Properly maintain battery powered equipment to include checking battery water levels monthly. Notify building managers concerning the need for major repairs or additions to building operating systems. Requires Class E Drivers’ License. Required to follow and adhere to all Building Services Standard Operating Procedures, and Facilities Services Policies and Directives. Criminal background check and Physical examination required. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: 5:00PM to 1:30AM (Monday through Friday). Workdays and shift times may vary in response to customer needs for special event coverage and/or departmental needs. Occasionally holiday and weekend work required. Total hours per week is 40. Management retains the right and discretion to modify schedules, building assignments, shifts and/or days for operational purposes. Position is considered as Essential Personnel as defined by UF Policy. Expected Salary: $16.00 to $16.80 Hourly Required Qualifications: Completion of ninth grade and two years of relevant experience. Preferred: EDUCATION & TRAINING High school diploma and two (2) years of commercial custodial experience. Knowledge of commercial cleaning procedures and techniques. Experience with Aim, Kronos, and Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Outlook, PeopleSoft). Experience managing large and multiple crews and operations Experience positively managing and motivating a diverse workforce Experience interfacing and providing customer service that aligns with Building Services’ values and vision Experience working collaboratively and cooperatively in a team environment Floor care training and experience (hard surfaces and carpets). Experience in electrical, plumbing, carpentry, and painting. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Multiple vacancies will be filled from this posting. Position has been reposted, previous applicants still umder consideration. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540241/compliance-audit-specialist-ii-physician-billing-compliance": {
      "title": "Compliance Audit Specialist II - Physician Billing Compliance",
      "description": "Compliance Audit Specialist II - Physician Billing Compliance Apply now Job no: 540241 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Health Care Administration/Support, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 29011800 - MD-PHYSICIAN BILL COMPLIANCE Classification Title: Compliance Audit Specialist II Classification Minimum Requirements: High School Diploma or equivalent and two years of appropriate experience. Appropriate college course work may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Certified Professional Coder (CPC)/ American Academy of Professional Coders or Certified Coding Specialist (CCS-P) (American Health Information Management Association) or Certified Coding Associate (CCA) (American Health Information Management Association) or Certified in Healthcare Compliance (CHC) or Certified in Healthcare Research Compliance (CHRC) or Certified in Healthcare Privacy Compliance (CHPC) or Certified Compliance & Ethics Professional (CCEP) or Certified Compliance & Ethics Professional-International (CCEP-I) is required Job Description: The Compliance Audit Specialist Conducts regulatory compliance audits of the University of Florida, College of Medicine departments, institutes and centers to ensure data integrity and compliance with federal and state regulations, reviewing medical and billing records to determine if service and documentation requirements are met. Works in collaboration with the Compliance Audit Specialist manager and Director of Physician Billing Compliance to provide input and assist in the development of any applicable training and education content. About this Role Conduct compliance audits of the University of Florida College of Medicine departments, institutes, and centers to ensure data integrity, compliance with federal and state regulations pertaining to, but not limited to provider billing services. Reviews medical and billing records to determine if service and documentation requirements are met. Clearly documents findings related to work performed. Communicate any identified patterns of error that may create institutional risk. Contributes to audit findings report and assist in the organization of documentation to support and communicate audit findings. May direct/supervise clerical search of paper or electronic health records. These findings may lead to substantive refunds to the College of Medicine, and/or disciplinary action for faculty, residents, non-physician providers and operational staff. Drafts summary reports, communications with physicians, compilation of findings, discussion of findings. Familiarizes with the structure of our clinical practice and participates in recommendations on educational and internal control policies to improve compliance plan effectiveness and operational outcomes. Assist with the development of training sessions for providers, professional fee billing staff and others on a regularly scheduled or ad hoc basis Responsible for current reading to remain appraised of coding changes, and seek institutional interpretations. Researches current federal, state and payer documentation, billing and coding rules and regulations. About the College of Medicine The University of Florida's College of Medicine is committed to advancing health through education, research, and patient care. With a focus on innovation and excellence, the college prepares future healthcare leaders through a rigorous curriculum that combines basic sciences with hands-on clinical experience. The College of Medicine emphasizes interdisciplinary collaboration and community engagement, fostering and environment where students, faculty, and staff work together to improve healthcare outcomes. The College is home to cutting-edge research initiatives and state-of-the-art facilities, providing an exceptional training ground for aspiring medical professionals. Dedicated to enhancing health care, the College of Medicine plays an impactful role in shaping the future of medicine. For more information about the College of Medicine and its programs, visit College of Medicine . We Offer Exceptional Benefits Low-cost State Health Plans : Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life and Disability Insurance Generous Retirement Options to secure your future Comprehensive Paid Time Off Packages with 10+ paid holidays, paid family, sick and vacation leave Exceptional Personal and Professional Development Opportunities : Access to UF Training & Organizational Development programs, leadership development, LinkedIn Learning, and more Tuition Assistance through the UF Employee Education Program Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer Learn more about what we have to offer here ! Expected Salary: $23.94 - $26.34 per hour; commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent and two years of appropriate experience. Appropriate college course work may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Certified Professional Coder (CPC)/ American Academy of Professional Coders or Certified Coding Specialist (CCS-P) (American Health Information Management Association) or Certified Coding Associate (CCA) (American Health Information Management Association) or Certified in Healthcare Compliance (CHC) or Certified in Healthcare Research Compliance (CHRC) or Certified in Healthcare Privacy Compliance (CHPC) or Certified Compliance & Ethics Professional (CCEP) or Certified Compliance & Ethics Professional-International (CCEP-I) is required Preferred: The ideal candidate will possess: CPC or CHC credentials highly preferred. Proficiency with medical terminology. Proficiency with procedural coding (including Level II HCPCs) and diagnosis coding. Proficiency with Evaluation and Management guidelines and CMS Teaching Physician regulations. Ability to manage and impart confidential information. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to deliver presentations. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies. Advanced working knowledge of Microsoft Word and Excel software in a Windows environment. Experience with PowerPoint and Access in a Windows environment a plus. Experience with management information systems and medical software. Ability to gather data, compile information, and prepare reports. Previous supervisory experience preferred Previous compliance auditing experience required Experience with Medicare, Medicaid, and Tricare/Champus regulations pertaining to billing and reimbursement required Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. This position is eligible for veterans' preference. To claim veterans' preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Form or equivalent certification with your application for consideration. See UF’s Veterans' Preference Page for more details. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540840/ops-motor-vehicle-operator-clinical-and-translational-science-institute-ctsi": {
      "title": "OPS Motor Vehicle Operator - Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI)",
      "description": "OPS Motor Vehicle Operator - Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI) Apply now Job no: 540840 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Transportation Services Department: 29680303 – MD-CTSI-CLINICAL RESEARCH VEHICLE Classification Title: OPS Motor Vehicle Operator Classification Minimum Requirements: Valid Florida commercial driver's license (CDL) with a clean driving record. Open availability to work weekends needed. Ability to lift and move equipment for event setup. Job Description: The Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI) is seeking candidates for OPS Motor Vehicle Operators . These positions will primarily be responsible for safely transporting the Clinical Research Vehicle (CRV) in a courteous and reliable manner. In this role, the Motor Vehicle Operators augment the CTSI Clinical Research Vehicle pool of drivers, enabling the team to effectively support a growing number of community events on weekends and holidays. We currently have two part-time openings, and both are expected to average 10 hours per week. The following outline the key duties associated with this role: Safely transport the Clinical Research Vehicle (CRV) in a courteous and reliable manner. Strictly observe Florida State traffic laws. Drive the CRV to and from the assigned event/clinic site. Park and set up vehicle at designated location. Assist in on-site preparation of the CRV prior to clinic or promotional events. Strictly observe patient confidentiality laws and regulations. Coordinate driver schedules. Maintain proper working order of the Clinical Research Vehicle (CRV). Inspect the CRV prior to departure and upon return to its storage location. Keep the CRV fueled. Identify and report any maintenance issues. Prepare the CRV for return to its permanent storage location. Expected Salary: $20.00 - $22.00 per hour; commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Valid Florida commercial driver's license (CDL) with a clean driving record. Open availability to work weekends needed. Ability to lift and move equipment for event setup. Preferred: Successful candidates must possess a Class B license. Must have open availability for weekend shifts. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered you must upload your resume and cover letter. This is a time-limited position. This requisition will be used to fill multiple positions. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 19 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541361/administrative-support-ast-i": {
      "title": "Administrative Support AST I",
      "description": "Administrative Support AST I Apply now Job no: 541361 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Transportation Services Department: 68040000 - BS-TRANSPORTATION - PARKING Classification Title: Administrative Support AST I Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Job Description: Serve as first point of contact for customers at Transportation and Parking Services (TAPS): • Engage with customers both in person and via telephone. • Interpret and explain policies and procedures to university students, staff, faculty, and visitors. • Address and facilitate customers’ parking needs. Accurately record customer and sales/payment information: • Document all transactions and prepare supporting documents for sales/payments, permit returns, charge adjustments, and revenue refunds. Assist with Student Traffic Court and the Hearing Authority: • Enter appeals related to citations. • Support the process for first and second level appeals. Assist with reviewing, researching and correcting error reports: • Identify and resolve discrepancies in error reports. Perform other administrative tasks and special projects as assigned. Work hours: Normal working hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Position may require occasional additional work hours to satisfy departmental needs for seasonal permit renewals, events and other tasks as directed. Expected Salary: $15.00 to $17.00 Hourly Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Preferred: • Detailed knowledge of T2 Systems Flex parking management software • Detailed knowledge of UF PeopleSoft and UF GO applications • Detailed knowledge of Microsoft Office applications • Two years customer service and money handling experience Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Position has been reposted, previous applicants still under consideration. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 15 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
