    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541743/marketing-and-comm-spec-ii": {
      "title": "Marketing and Comm Spec II",
      "description": "Marketing and Comm Spec II Apply now Job no: 541743 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing Department: 57301000 - HS-HAMILTON SCHOOL ADMIN Classification Title: Marketing and Comm Spec II Classification Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree and four years of relevant experience; or an Associate’s degree and six years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Content Creation & Visual Production Create high-quality visual and digital content to support the Hamilton School’s marketing and communications efforts. Capture and edit photography and video across events, classrooms, faculty talks, and student activities. Produce short-form and long-form video content for social media and web use. Design graphics, flyers, and promotional materials aligned with University of Florida branding standards. Maintain and organize a media library of photo, video, and graphic assets for ongoing use. Communications & Digital Execution Assist in executing the Hamilton School’s communications plan across digital platforms, including social media, newsletters, email campaigns, and website updates. Draft captions, format content, and support publishing across Instagram, X (Twitter), Facebook, and other platforms. Ensure consistency in messaging and branding across all materials. Support on-campus distribution of marketing materials and digital promotion of events. Event Coverage & Support Provide on-site support for Hamilton School events through photography, videography, and real-time content capture. Assist with the creation of event-related promotional materials and ensure timely content delivery for post-event communications. Media & Communications Support Provide support for media and communications efforts by assisting in the preparation of press materials, drafting content, and coordinating logistics as needed. Analytics & Reporting Support Assist in tracking and reporting on digital and social media performance. Support the collection of data related to marketing campaigns and provide insights to inform future content and engagement strategies. Established in 2022, the Hamilton School is a multidisciplinary academic unit whose purpose is to support teaching and research concerning the ideas, traditions, and texts that shape Western civilization and American values and institutions. The School offers four undergraduate degrees, five undergraduate minors and two graduate degrees. Applicants are encouraged to visit the Hamilton School website ( Hamilton School ) to learn more about the Hamilton School for Classical and Civic Education. UF is the state’s oldest, largest, and most comprehensive land grant university with an enrollment of over 50,000 students and was ranked the Number 1 public university in the United States by Wall Street Journal in its “2024 Best Colleges in the U.S.” report. UF is located in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 50 miles from the Gulf of America, and 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean, and within a 2-hour drive to large metropolitan areas (Orlando, Tampa, Jacksonville). The beautiful climate and extensive nearby parks and recreational areas afford year-round outdoor activities, including hiking, biking, and nature photography. UF’s large college sports programs, museums, and performing arts centers support a range of activities and cultural events for residents to enjoy. Alachua County schools are highly rated and offer a variety of programs including magnet schools and an international baccalaureate program. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville . Employment Benefits include: - Health Insurance: UF participates in state- and university-sponsored benefits programs for individuals, families, and domestic partners, and offers voluntary insurance that includes vision, dental, long-term disability and more. - Retirement Options: Attractive options include Florida Retirement System Pension Plan, State University System Optional Retirement Program, Florida Retirement System Investment Plan, and Voluntary Retirement Savings Plan. - Leave: UF staff enjoy a generous paid leave plan as well as access to a sick-leave pool, maternity/paternity leave and leave payouts. Expected Salary: $65,000-$70,000 Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and four years of relevant experience; or an Associate’s degree and six years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred A bachelor’s degree in public relations, marketing, communications, journalism, or related field and eight years of professional experience. Significant ability in audio/visual production and editing is desired. Experience working with multiple media and press outlets. Ability to plan, organize, and coordinate work assignments. Experience with online content platforms and/or website curation preferred. Demonstrated ability to work as part of a team toward organizational objectives. Proficiency in Microsoft Suite, Adobe products, and other professional design software, as well as Canva, HTML and CSS languages for managing and building websites. Excellent written and verbal communication. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume and a list of three references. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 09 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541785/clinical-associatefull-professor-vice-chair-of-education": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor & Vice Chair of Education",
      "description": "Clinical Associate/Full Professor & Vice Chair of Education Apply now Job no: 541785 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29160204 - MD-FAMILY MED CENTER AT MAIN Classification Title: AST/ASO PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: An M.D. or D.O. degree (or equivalent), board certification or eligibility in Family Medicine, and a current Florida medical license (or eligibility) are required. Job Description: UF Health – The Power of Together! At UF Health, together, we strive to create unstoppable momentum toward the goal of improving individual and community health through discovery, clinical and translational science and technology, exceptional education and patient-centered, innovative, high-quality health care. At the heart of our mission is to provide high-quality clinical care and to promise every patient their best experience possible. Ready to join us? The University of Florida Department of Community Health and Family Medicine (CHFM) is seeking a dynamic, forward-thinking physician leader to serve as the Vice Chair of Education at the rank of Associate or Full Professor . This full-time position offers a unique opportunity to complete our executive leadership team; work across the span of pre-medical, undergraduate medical, graduate medical, and continuing medical education; and shape the future of family medicine education. The successful candidate will balance clinical excellence with academic leadership. The expected assignment breakdown includes: Administrative Leadership (Vice Chair of Education): Overseeing the operational, strategic, and compliance aspects of the department's educational programs across the education continuum, reporting directly to the Department Chair. Faculty Development: Lead department efforts to help faculty become even more adroit educators, coaches, and mentors to learners and other members of the CHFM team. Clinical Education: Mentoring, training, and instructing medical students, family medicine residents, and fellows in clinical and classroom settings. Clinical (Direct Patient Care): Providing vital primary care services, to include continuity, acute, chronic, and urgent care, in one of our continuity clinic sites and on our inpatient ward. About UF Health: UF Health represents the shared vision and commitment to patient care excellence of more than 30,000 employees of the University of Florida Health Science Center and UF Health Shands health care system. With campuses in Gainesville and Jacksonville, UF Health includes six health colleges, nine research institutes and centers, two teaching hospitals, two specialty hospitals, and a host of physician medical practices and outpatient services throughout north central and northeast Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care; innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences; and high-impact research across the spectrum of basic, translational, and clinical investigation. The Department of Community Health and Family Medicine (CHFM) represents a core pillar of our patient-care and educational services under the University of Florida’s College of Medicine. If you require accommodation due to a disability to apply for this position, please contact the ADA Office at (352) 392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). For more information, visit the UF ADA Compliance website. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: An M.D. or D.O. degree (or equivalent), board certification or eligibility in Family Medicine, and a current Florida medical license (or eligibility) are required. Preferred: Clinical expertise Strong character, leadership, interpersonal, and communication skills Strong written communications skills Superior leadership qualities enhanced by superb judgment, problem-solving and cognitive skills are desired. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes. Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 09 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541787/technology-systems-coordinator": {
      "title": "Technology Systems Coordinator",
      "description": "Technology Systems Coordinator Apply now Job no: 541787 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Information Technology, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 73010000 - UPD-ADMINISTRATIVE DEPARTMENT Classification Title: Administrative Specialist II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Troubleshoot issues affecting software functionality and coordinate resolution with the vendor. Maintain Level 4 CJIS Security Awareness Training and perform LASO duties, including identifying users of approved hardware, software, and firmware and ensuring no unauthorized individuals or processes have access; documenting how equipment is connected to state systems; ensuring personnel security screening procedures are followed; verifying that approved security measures are in place and functioning; supporting overall policy compliance; and promptly reporting security incidents to the CJIS Systems Agency Information Security Officer. Maintain continual preparedness for CJIS audit readiness and ensure ongoing compliance with both UFIT and CJIS Security Policy requirements through continual policy reviews, user-level audits, and quarterly reviews with local agency peers. Serve as liaison with UFIT and provide advice and assistance as appropriate. Effectively document and manage multiple technology projects simultaneously to ensure effective coordination between internal and external partners and to make sure deadlines are met. Ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of Criminal Justice Information (CJI) and the compliant implementation of technology in accordance with the FBI CJIS Security Policy. Conduct continual review of technology vulnerability scans provided by UFIT and coordinate timely remediation efforts. Work with software vendors to efficiently and effectively upgrade software as recommended by the vendor. Make recommendations as appropriate to software vendors for system enhancements and follow through on development and installation. Assist with implementing procedural changes associated with software enhancements and coordinate training for affected personnel. Assist in the research, testing, and evaluation of emerging technologies and functionality that might enhance or replace existing systems, and make recommendations as appropriate. Manage and issue smartphones and smartphone applications, including device management through a mobile device management (MDM) security portal. Co-manage and coordinate personnel scheduling with two on-site UFIT Technology Support Services personnel. Ensure annual completion and documentation of role-based CJIS training for personnel with access to CJI and coordinate related compliance activities for the agency. Expected Salary: $63,600 - $70,000 annually Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Valid FL driver's license. Preferred: Experience in technical applications including electronic access control and video surveillance, police mobile data services, software systems integration, crime prevention principles, and budgeting. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 09 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
