    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541810/student-academic-assistant": {
      "title": "Student Academic Assistant",
      "description": "Student Academic Assistant Apply now Job no: 541810 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Academic Advising/Support, Dentistry Department: 34010201 - DN-EDUCATION ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Student Academic Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent Job Description: The Student Academic Assistant serves as a key team member who assistants with daily processes and requests while greeting visitors to the Office of Academic Affairs in the College of Dentistry. This position requires interaction with the public, students, faculty, and staff; must exercise good judgement, have time management skills and present a collaborative demeanor. Job Duties: Assist with administrative and daily tasks within the Office of Academic Affairs. Provide support for Simple Syllabus and ADA/Title II compliancy Greet and interact with office visitors, assisting with questions and processing student requests Expected Salary: $15.00 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent Preferred: Preferred Qualifications: Competent in Microsoft Office Suite (Primarily Word, Excel, and TEAMS) High attention to detail Good written and oral communication Good interpersonal skills Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
