    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541815/emergency-medicine-physician-clinical-assistant-or-associate-professor": {
      "title": "Emergency Medicine Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor",
      "description": "Emergency Medicine Physician - Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor Apply now Job no: 541815 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 30290000 - JX-EMERGENCY MEDICINE-JAX Classification Title: CLIN AST/ASO PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: Candidates should be MD/DO in Emergency Medicine and board certified or eligible. Job Description: The University of Florida Department of Emergency Medicine - Jacksonville is expanding! We are recruiting motivated and energetic physicians to join our faculty. Clinical opportunities include positions in general emergency medicine at our community sites. Successful candidates will receive an academic appointment at the non-tenure accruing level of Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor. About UF Health: UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. About College of Medicine – Jacksonville (COM-J): The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/ . Expected Salary: Salary and academic appointment are negotiable and the benefits are excellent. Required Qualifications: Candidates should be MD/DO in Emergency Medicine and board certified or eligible. Special Instructions to Applicants: The Search Committee will begin to review applications on a rolling basis until a competitive candidate pool is identified. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541819/palliative-care-faculty-ops-parttime": {
      "title": "Palliative Care Faculty – OPS / Part-time",
      "description": "Palliative Care Faculty – OPS / Part-time Apply now Job no: 541819 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29051800 - MD-PALLIATIVE CARE DIVISION Classification Title: OPS Faculty Classification Minimum Requirements: Applicants must be board-certified or board eligible in Palliative Care and be eligible for a Florida Medical License. M.D. degree or equivalent is required. Job Description: The University of Florida Department of Medicine is seeking a board-eligible or board-certified Palliative Care Physician to become an active and integral member of the team. This is an OPS/PRN appointment in the Department of Medicine. The successful candidates may perform inpatient attending duties, including consultations, as well as teaching and supervising medical students and residents. We enjoy a close collaborative relationship with UF Health Hospital and pride ourselves in professional and cooperative interdisciplinary care. Join an established interdisciplinary palliative care team that includes physicians, advanced practice providers, social work, and collaborating disciplines. Provide specialty palliative care inpatient consultation for medically complex adult population at UF Health Shands Hospital. Collaborate across oncology, hospital medicine, critical care, cardiology, neurology, surgery, geriatrics, and other specialties. Teach and mentor medical students, residents, fellows, and other health professional trainees. Participate in quality improvement, program development, and educational initiatives based on individual interests. Opportunities to collaborate with established investigators and participate in palliative care and serious illness research across the University of Florida. Requisite attributes include a commitment to service, a strong sense of teamwork and a desire to train tomorrow's doctors. The Gainesville area has superb weather, inexpensive living, nationally ranked schools, and multiple year-round recreational opportunities. We offer generous compensation. UF Health is one of the Southeast’s most comprehensive academic health centers and includes UF Health Shands, an 1,100-bed quaternary referral hospital, which consistently ranks among the top 50-hospitals by U.S. News & World Report in multiple specialties. In addition, the University of Florida is a top 5 public research university and includes substantial resources to support teaching, research, and collaboration, including one of only two Clinical Translational Science Institute (CTSI) hubs in the state of Florida. The CTSI features a Training and Research Academy for Clinical and Translational Science for early career faculty seeking to develop research skills and pursue careers as clinical investigators. About the area: The Gainesville, Florida region has an inexpensive cost of living, nationally ranked public middle and high schools, and superb weather with multiple year-round recreational opportunities including biking, hiking, kayaking, snorkeling, and cave diving. Pristine wilderness areas, coastal communities, famous theme parks, and other attractions are within a short driving distance. MSA Population: 330,000 Average High Temp in January: 66 F No State Income Tax Strong public and private schools 1 hour to Gulf of Mexico and Atlantic Ocean 2 hours or less to Jacksonville, Orlando and Tampa Expected Salary: $1,350 per 12-hour shift. Minimum Requirements: Applicants must be board-certified or board eligible in Palliative Care and be eligible for a Florida Medical License. M.D. degree or equivalent is required. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach curriculum vitae, cover letter, and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 08 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541822/game-room-student-assistant": {
      "title": "Game Room Student Assistant",
      "description": "Game Room Student Assistant Apply now Job no: 541822 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Student Services Department: 05010000 - RU-GAME ROOM ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: STU AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Classification Minimum Requirements: This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) or Federal Work-Study (FWS) and must maintain a 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. Job Description: Student employees within the Reitz Union must: Be a current UF degree seeking student registered at a minimum of 6 credit hours per semester Respond to and assist with emergency situations and building evacuations per department procedures or as instructed by building management staff Possess exceptional customer service while maintaining a high level of professionalism Demonstrate a desire and willingness to learn in a fast-paced team-oriented environment Establish an exemplary work ethic by being productive, self-motivated, and dependable Participate in all scheduled meetings, trainings, and evaluations Act as an ambassador for all Reitz Union areas as well as the University of Florida, providing accurate information and campus resources Position Specific Responsibilities: Be available to work afternoons, evenings, and weekends Operates the automatic scoring system for bowling lanes and registers. Including money handling, credit card transactions, and the front counter area Repairs bowling equipment, monitors Game Room for vandalism and functionality. Reports Game Room equipment failures to the Manager on duty Responsible for general maintenance and clerical duties including: picking up trash as needed, returning equipment to proper racks, cleaning counter area, restocking forms, sharpening pencils, and answering phones Communicates with managers problems that arise during shifts, equipment failures, and other issues that affect the smooth operation of the Game Room Provide shift reports of daily activities, supplies utilized, and other relative information Completes all training requirements upon being hired in a timely fashion Ability to commit to working 10 or more hours per week Ability to occasionally lift up to 50lbs Other duties as assigned Expected Salary: $15.00/HR Required Qualifications: This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) or Federal Work-Study (FWS) and must maintain a 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. Preferred: Although no experience is necessary to apply all training will be provided, we would prefer for all student employees to: Previous experience with customer service Proficient with verbal and written communication Physically able to perform minimum tasks related to maintenance and repair of bowling equipment and machinery Ability to handle credit card transactions correctly Have CPR and First Aid Certified, or willing to obtain Special Instructions to Applicants: Must submit a resume with application that includes all current student involvement, organizations, or current employment on campus. Availability Needed: Monday through Friday: 12pm to 11pm Saturday and Sunday: 8am to 8pm Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
