      "description": "Reitz Union Experience Student Assistant Apply now Job no: 541824 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Student Services Department: 05110200 - RU-UNION EXPERIENCE Classification Title: STU AST-NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Classification Minimum Requirements: This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. Job Description: Student employees for this position must: Be a current UF degree seeking student registered at a minimum of 6 credit hours per semester Respond to and assist with emergency situations and building evacuations per department procedures or as instructed by building management staff Provide exceptional customer service while maintaining a high level of professionalism Demonstrate a desire and willingness to learn in a fast-paced team-oriented environment Establish an exemplary work ethic by being proactive, self-motivated, and dependable Participate in all scheduled meetings, trainings, and evaluations Ability to work weekends, evenings, holidays, and academic breaks, as needed Act as an ambassador for all areas within the Reitz Union, as well as the University of Florida, providing accurate information and campus resources Position Specific Responsibilities: Functions as a team or independently to setup and tear down equipment, tables, or furniture needed for events and programs Acts as event staff, performing duties like event check-in, passing out promotional items, crowd management, audiovisual equipment operation, and more General cleaning and organizational duties, including picking up trash as needed, returning equipment to proper storage areas, cleaning as needed, restocking supplies, etc Communicates with managers, noting problems that arise during shifts, general success of events, or