ovide assistance to patrons as needed regarding lost and found items Provide shift reports of daily activities, supplies utilized, and other related information Assist in the completion of opening and/or closing procedures of the building Complete all training requirements upon being hired in a timely fashion Ability to commit to working 10 or more hours per week Other duties as assigned Expected Salary: $15.00/HR Required Qualifications: This position is open to all students who are eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) or Federal Work-Study (FWS) and must maintain a 2.0 grade point average. Registered students are employed on a part-time basis, up to 20 hours per week. Preferred: Previous customer service experience Proficient with verbal and written communication Attention to professionalism, dependability, and timeliness Ability to work shifts during the early morning, evenings, and weekends CPR and First Aid Certified, or willing to obtain Special Instructions to Applicants: Must submit a résumé with application that includes all current student involvement, organizations, or current employment on campus. Availability Needed: Monday through Thursday: 8am - 11pm Friday through Sunday: 8am - 8pm Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
