    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541829/ops-patient-registration": {
      "title": "OPS Patient Registration",
      "description": "OPS Patient Registration Apply now Job no: 541829 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 29350000 - MD-DERMATOLOGY Classification Title: OPS Patient Registration Classification Minimum Requirements: High School Diploma or GED. Job Description: The Department of Dermatology, Division of Dermathopathology is hiring for Patient Registration . This position is responsible for accurately registering patients, verifying insurance coverage, collecting demographic and billing information, obtaining authorizations when required, and ensuring all specimen and patient information is complete and compliant before processing. The specialist plays a vital role in supporting efficient laboratory operations, delivering exceptional customer service, and maintaining the integrity of patient records while adhering to HIPAA and regulatory requirements. Patient Registration & Demographic Management Perform accurate patient registration and update demographic information in the electronic medical record (EMR) and laboratory information system (LIS). Verify patient identity using established procedures. Review and validate physician orders, requisitions, and patient information for completeness. Ensure pathology specimens are matched accurately to patient records. Resolve registration discrepancies before specimen processing. Perform a Quality Control check of all assigned cases. Insurance Verification & Authorization Verify insurance eligibility, benefits, and coverage prior to laboratory services. Obtain and document referrals, prior authorizations, and pre-certifications as required. Maintain accurate documentation of insurance information and authorization approvals. Documentation & Compliance Maintain patient confidentiality in accordance with HIPAA and organizational policies. Scan, upload, and maintain registration documents, insurance cards, and patient forms. Ensure compliance with laboratory accreditation standards and regulatory requirements. Administrative Support Monitor registration work queues and resolve incomplete accounts. Participate in departmental meetings, training sessions, and quality improvement initiatives. Expected Salary: $16.00/hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or GED required. Preferred: Associate degree in Healthcare Administration, Business, or related field preferred. 1-2 years of patient registration, medical office, laboratory, or healthcare administrative experience preferred. Experience with pathology, dermatology, or laboratory services highly desirable. Experience verifying insurance eligibility and obtaining prior authorizations preferred. Strong understanding of medical terminology, insurance plans, and patient registration processes. Knowledge of HIPAA regulations and patient confidentiality requirements. Excellent customer service and interpersonal communication skills. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in data entry. Ability to prioritize tasks and work efficiently in a fast-paced healthcare environment. Proficiency with EMR, practice management systems, Microsoft Office, and laboratory information systems. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested applicants should upload a copy of their Resume/CV and list of professional references Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 03 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541830/ops-dermpath-accessioner": {
      "title": "OPS DermPath Accessioner",
      "description": "OPS DermPath Accessioner Apply now Job no: 541830 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29350000 - MD-DERMATOLOGY Classification Title: OPS Classification Minimum Requirements: High School Diploma or GED. Job Description: The Dermpath Accessioner is responsible for accurately receiving, identifying, and accessioning pathology specimens submitted for diagnostic testing. This position ensures specimen integrity, proper documentation, and compliance with established laboratory procedures, regulatory requirements, and quality standards. The Accessioner serves as a key support role for pathologists, histology staff, and laboratory personnel while maintaining efficient workflow and excellent customer service. Specimen Processing • Receive, verify, and accession pathology specimens. • Ensure all specimens are properly labeled and accompanied by complete requisition information. • Assign accession numbers and enter patient and specimen information into the Laboratory Information System (LIS). • Verify specimen identity and resolve discrepancies according to established procedures. • Maintain specimen tracking throughout the testing process. Data Entry and Documentation • Accurately enter patient demographics, physician information, specimen information and clinical history into the LIS. • Review requisitions for completeness and compliance with laboratory requirements. • Maintain accurate records and documentation in accordance with organizational policies and regulatory standards. • Generate reports, labels, and specimen tracking documentation as needed. Customer Service • Communicate professionally with providers, clinic staff, couriers, and laboratory personnel regarding specimen requirements and status. • Assist with resolving specimen-related inquiries and discrepancies. Additional / Miscellaneous Duties as Assigned • Assist with filing, scanning, and archiving pathology reports and records. • Support laboratory quality, performance improvement, and accreditation activities. • Cross-train in other laboratory administrative or support functions as needed. • Perform special projects and other duties as assigned by leadership. Expected Salary: $16.00/hour Required Qualifications: High School Diploma or GED. Preferred: • Previous healthcare, laboratory, pathology, or specimen-processing experience preferred. • Experience with laboratory information systems and electronic medical records preferred. • Strong attention to detail and accuracy. • Ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information. • Excellent organizational and multitasking skills. • Effective verbal and written communication skills. • Basic computer proficiency, including Microsoft Office applications. • Ability to work independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants should upload copies of their Resume/CV and list of professional references. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 03 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541832/hospital-assistant-care": {
      "title": "Hospital Assistant (CARE)",
      "description": "Hospital Assistant (CARE) Apply now Job no: 541832 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28311000 - VM-HOSPITAL Classification Title: Veterinary Assistant (CARE) Classification Minimum Requirements High school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: The AAHA accredited University of Florida Small Animal Hospital is recruiting for a Hospital Veterinary Assistant. The veterinary assistant works with veterinarians and technicians to provide support for patient care and administrative duties in the Small Animal Hospital. This position works under immediate supervision from a manager as well as supportive oversight from veterinarians and technicians. Provides basic patient care and administrative support as directed. This individual will work one-on-one with clients, patients, and hospital staff and must be able to develop friendly, professional relationships and maintain a positive attitude through all interactions. This position is responsible for the overall cleanliness of the hospital, providing support to client service representatives in both cleaning needs as well as retrieving food orders; stocking supplies and food; and maintaining laundry services throughout the Small Animal Hospital. Individuals should genuinely care about people and animals, possess excellent communication skills, strong public relations skills, initiative to problem solve, utilize active listening skills and confidence in handling customer interactions, project a professional image, and good interpersonal skills. Must be outgoing, full of enthusiasm, and a team player. This is a full-time, 40/hr per week position. The schedule is 5 days a week, including working at least one weekend day and may require holidays to be worked as well. Expected Salary: $15 Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a CARE position offering limited benefits, including health insurance and paid time off. When appropriate certifications are achieved, promotional opportunities to a level II title may be available. This position will also become eligible for transition into a TEAMS (staff) salary plan. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs , bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541833/ufhealth-physician": {
      "title": "UFHealth Physician",
      "description": "UFHealth Physician Apply now Job no: 541833 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty, Non-Tenure-Track Faculty, Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29051000 - MD-INTERNAL MEDICINE Classification Title: UFHealth Physician Classification Minimum Requirements: Valid Florida Medical License required or eligibility to obtain licensure before hire. Board certification in area of practice preferred. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of all applicable credentialing and privileging requirements within the UF Health system before the start of employment. Job Description: Provides full scope of primary care services to adult patients, including evaluation, diagnosis, treatment, coordination of care, preventive care, chronic disease management, and health maintenance. Establishes and manages a panel of primary care patients and provides ongoing, comprehensive care for acute and chronic medical conditions. Works collaboratively with members of the healthcare team, including pharmacists, advanced practice providers, nurses, care coordinators, and other clinical support staff. Reviews incoming reports, including laboratory studies, imaging, and other diagnostic tests, and follows up in a timely manner. Prescribes pharmaceuticals, other medications, and treatment regimens as appropriate to assessed medical conditions. Refers patients to specialists and other appropriate patient care services and coordinates care as needed. Participates in health promotion, disease prevention, chronic disease management, and other population health activities as appropriate to the position. May manage the daily operations of a specific medical program or patient care unit. Directs and coordinates the patient care activities of nursing and support staff as required. Follows established departmental policies, procedures, and objectives, including continuous quality improvement, patient safety, regulatory, environmental, and infection control standards. Participates in peer review, quality assurance activities, provider meetings, and other clinical and operational meetings as requested. Assists in updating clinical protocols, workflows, and principles of practice as requested. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, commensurate with education and experience. Required Qualifications: Valid Florida Medical License required or eligibility to obtain licensure before hire. Board certification in area of practice preferred. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of all applicable credentialing and privileging requirements within the UF Health system before the start of employment. Preferred: Board certified or board eligible in Internal Medicine. Clinical experience providing comprehensive primary care to adult patients. Experience managing acute and chronic medical conditions, preventive care, and health maintenance. Certification/Licensure in the state of Florida and Federal DEA Certification. Special Instructions to Applicants: Please attach curriculum vitae and three letters of recommendation. Final candidate will be required to provide official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541834/grants-accounting-manager": {
      "title": "Grants Accounting Manager",
      "description": "Grants Accounting Manager Apply now Job no: 541834 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Grant or Research Administration Department: 11110000 - RE-CG ACCOUNTING SERVICES Classification Title: Grants Accounting Manager Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree required and at least four years of experience in research administration (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Job Description: Supports Grant Accountants by providing training, mentoring and professional development opportunities. Trains team members in the use of myUFL, UFIRST, OnBase, MYinvestigator, myUFMarketplace and other university systems. Ensures team members understand and implement university directives and policies such as travel, procurement, cost transfer, effort, cost accounting, cost sharing and others as they relate to sponsored programs. Ensures team members have a fundamental understanding of and are able to implement Federal and sponsor specific rule sets and regulations. Manages daily post award activities for the assigned portfolio. This includes ensuring expenditures are appropriate; analyzing and reconciling projects through the use of reports and queries from the University financial system; preparing financial reports and invoices based on that reconciliation; managing the AR report by contacting sponsors who have failed to make payment as defined in the award document; and when appropriate, approving and processing budget transfer requests. This requires knowledge of electronic invoicing, cost sharing and all revenue related activities. Works closely with unit team members to ensure accuracy and timeliness of award set up, reporting, invoicing, collections and closeout. Monitors the timeliness and quality of award set up, reporting, invoicing, collections and closeout through review of management reports and team member’s work. Evaluates team members on the performance of these duties. Assists team members with complex items and resolution of issues as they arise. Escalates issues as appropriate. Works closely with local unit administrators, PI’s and senior leadership within Contracts & Grants to resolve issues for the assigned portfolio as appropriate. Works with the executive leadership team for Contracts & Grants Accounting to develop and implement directives & procedures as well as templates and training programs. Active participant in meetings with internal and external constituents. These include regular meetings with the Contracts and Grants leadership team that allow us to evaluate efficiencies, workload, provide training, and better assist our team members and customers. Conducts training sessions and makes presentations at outreach events or conferences as needed. Attend trainings and conferences as opportunities become available. Participates in testing and system upgrade initiatives. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required and at least four years of experience in research administration (or equivalent combination of education and experience). Preferred: Knowledge of external regulations and sponsor policies that apply to sponsored program financial management. Strong leadership skills and ability to communicate and interact with a diverse group of internal and external audiences. Ability to supervise and train employees, including organizing, prioritizing, and assigning projects. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Ability to build effective teams and work through others to accomplish outcomes. Candidates must have excellent written and oral communication skills and be customer service oriented. Proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word, and Outlook). Knowledge of electronic research administration software required. Ability to function under highly stressful circumstances. Special Instructions to Applicants: • In order to be considered, applicants must provide a cover letter, resume, and list of professional references. • Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. • This is not a remote position and is located on the University of Florida main campus in Gainesville, FL. • A criminal background check is required. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 09 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541835/administrative-spec-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Spec II",
      "description": "Administrative Spec II Apply now Job no: 541835 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 11800000 - RE-ANIMAL CARE SERVICES Classification Title: Administrative Spec II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor’s degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Serves as a customer service liaison for department’s Front Office. Processes service requests per SOP, which includes answering phones and greeting visitors. Fields questions regarding department policies and directs and educates customers. Responsible for Animal Procurement, which involves processing all orders submitted by UFresearchers and ensures that animal orders comply with research protocol limits. Processing of the division’s PCard charges, PO/Invoice payments using UF’s financial system and departments internal sub-system for expense and budget tracking. Process revenue collections/transfers for UF Research center internal billing through UF’s financial system and departments internal sub-system to maintain up-to-date accounts receivable data. Maintains and manages databases for protocol tracking, census management and facility access,which includes reviewing and giving facility access. Other duties as assigned. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and three years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: • Bachelor’s degree is preferred. • Knowledge of sponsored research administration and compliance processes. • Experience working with faculty, Deans, Directors, Department Chairs, University administration and regulators. • Knowledge of computers and relevant computer programs including Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Visio. • Ability to use and maintain databases and websites. • Ability to work independently with minimum supervision and function as a member of a team. • Ability to plan, organize, prioritize and coordinate work assignments and exercise initiative. • Ability to manage work flow and processes. • Effective verbal and written communication skills including the ability to write and edit reports, meeting minutes and other documents. • Excellent interpersonal skills and customer service orientation Special Instructions to Applicants: • In order to be considered, applicants must provide a cover letter, resume, and list of professional references. • Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. • This is not a remote position and is located on the University of Florida main campus in Gainesville, FL. • A criminal background check is required. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Administrative Spec II Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 02 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541837/assistant-professor": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor*",
      "description": "Assistant Professor* Apply now Job no: 541837 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Humanities Department: 57301000 - HS-HAMILTON SCHOOL ADMIN Classification Title: Assistant Professor* Classification Minimum Requirements Ph.D. or equivalent in Philosophy, Politics, Economics, Law, History, American Government. Job Description: The University of Florida, in Gainesville, Florida is seeking an Assistant Professor for the Department of Hamilton School for Classical and Civic Education. Duties and responsibilities include teaching, research, and service. Responsibilities involve teaching graduate and/or undergraduate level courses in Legal Reasoning: Think Like a Lawyer, Origins of the Contemporary West: I and II, Liberty and Order, Civil Discourse and the American Political Order, PPEL Perspectives and Thesis writing. Position is also responsible for publishing and/or presenting original, peer-reviewed research in the field of History and Political Thought. Required Qualifications: Position requires a Ph.D. or equivalent in Philosophy, Politics, Economics, Law, History, American Government. Special Instructions to Applicants: A complete application must include the following: a curriculum vitae a cover letter, which describes your interest in the Hamilton School’s mission a research statement a teaching statement a sample of scholarly writing within the last three years three (3) references. These references may be contacted at some point in the hiring process to provide recommendation letters. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. The University of Florida is an equal opportunity institution. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 27 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541839/clinical-postdoctoral-associate": {
      "title": "Clinical Postdoctoral Associate",
      "description": "Clinical Postdoctoral Associate Apply now Job no: 541839 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Social/Behavioral Science, Counseling/Community Outreach/Social Work Department: 04030100 - SL-COUNSELING & WELLNESS CTR Classification Title: Clinical Postdoctoral Associate Classification Minimum Requirements: A doctoral degree from an APA or CPA accredited program in counseling psychology, clinical psychology, or counseling related field License-eligible as a psychologist (or licensed as a psychologist) Completion of an APA accredited doctoral internship in health service psychology Job Description: The Counseling and Wellness Center (CWC) at the University of Florida is offering multiple Adjunct Clinical Postdoctoral Associate positions for the 2027-2028 academic year. The postdoctoral position offers advanced training in a variety of areas related to the health service field of psychology. Postdoctoral associates receive advanced training in university counseling services. The postdoctoral program currently offers generalists positions with the possibility for additional specialization in three major areas: (1) Psychological Assessment (2) Intensive Support (Suicide Prevention and Intervention) (3) Alcohol and Other Drugs Prevention and Intervention. Program development opportunities may be available, working alongside the program coordinators for these areas. The CWC training program adheres to the American Psychological Association’s profession-wide competencies along with the mental health code of ethics and state laws and rules. We believe that this training is vital to all aspects of counselor development and competence and thus, is incorporated into all areas of supervision, training seminars, evaluations, and professional activities. The training program is also committed to cultivating an atmosphere that is conducive to learning by providing clinical postdoctoral associates with an appropriate blend of support and challenge. Postdoctoral associates are treated as early career professionals and as such, are given a great deal of autonomy and responsibility. Simultaneously, postdoctoral associates will receive the professional support necessary to allow for their continued training and professional development. Postdoctoral associates will be expected to fulfill the multiple roles of a university counseling center clinician, which includes counseling services (individual, couples, and/or group counseling), assessment, crisis intervention, referral, consultation, outreach, participation in staff meetings and training seminars, and timely completion of necessary administrative functions. Other opportunities are available depending on the chosen area of specialization; postdoctoral associates work with their supervisors to tailor their specific responsibilities to further their training goals. Postdoctoral associates will receive a minimum of 2 hours of face-to-face individual supervision and 1 ½ hours of group supervision and didactic seminars weekly. In addition, they will be provided with various professional development opportunities. The 12-month 2000-hour (with 900 hours, including 500 direct service hours, in activities related to direct client contact) positions have been designed to meet the requirements for licensure in the State of Florida. Salary is $62,000 for 12 months. Additional benefits include paid time off, options for health, dental, vision, life and other insurances; flexible spending accounts; retirement savings plans; professional development time and $1200 professional development funds (amount subject to change); EPPP licensure study materials and release time. CWC Mission The mission of the Counseling and Wellness Center at the University of Florida is to support students in fostering their mental health and well-being to promote personal, educational, and career development. We achieve this through the delivery of high-quality, socially conscious services. Our primary focus is providing brief, confidential counseling to help students succeed both academically and in their interpersonal relationships. The faculty and staff of the Counseling and Wellness Center provide trauma-informed support services. We help students navigate periods of intense mental distress, offering support for complex trauma and other adversities they may face. Our goal is to minimize the use of non-consensual interventions, employing them only after procedural due process and when all other available resources have been exhausted. For more information, please visit the CWC Values webpage. The CWC provides: Individual, couples, and group counseling for students with psychological, emotional, academic and/or relationship concerns Crisis intervention for students experiencing a personal crisis or emergency Stress management and biofeedback services Outreach, prevention, and educational programs for students, faculty, and staff Consultation services for students, faculty, staff, families, and friends of students Training and supervision to counseling and psychology graduate students from pre-practicum through post-doctoral training Assessment and referral services Teaching, research, and scholarship Our staff consists of 55 clinicians in clinical psychology, counseling psychology, and counselor education. Expected Salary: $62,000 Preferred: The successful candidate will bring many of the following professional qualifications, skills, experience, and personal qualities Minimum of three years professional experience in a mental health setting with at least one year in a student counseling or student mental health setting. Administrative/Leadership experience . Ability to work in and with large complex systems . Demonstrated ability to conduct brief psychotherapy and crisis intervention. Knowledge of applicable laws and ethics pertaining to all mental health fields in Florida. Demonstrated skills in providing outreach and prevention services. Demonstrated ability to supervise trainees . Knowledge of developmental issues in u niversity populations . Knowledge of intermediate computer skills, e.g. Microsoft Suite and virtual meeting platforms. Ability to work with and learn various software programs. Special Instructions to Applicants: Persons interested in applying for this position should apply online. COMPLETE BOTH APPLICATIONS Complete APPA CAS https://appicpostdoc.liaisoncas.com/applicant -ux/#/login and follow prompts for required materials. If invited for an interview, applicants must also complete the Careers at UF application. Anyone requiring accommodations to complete an application should contact the Search Committee Chair: Felicia Brown, PhD: ffbrown@ufl.edu The University of Florida is an AA/EO employer and acts in compliance with all aspects of the ADA. Any questions or anyone requiring accommodations to complete an application should contact the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Felicia Brown ffbrown@ufl.edu . As an equal opportunity employer, we believe in fostering environments where faculty, staff and students feel respected, valued for their differences, and empowered to do their best work. We seek candidates that can demonstrate their experiences with working with students, faculty and staff from all backgrounds. Final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . Applications must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) on January 5, 2027 . Applications will be reviewed as they are received up to the deadline. Employment with the University of Florida is contingent upon the results of a criminal background check. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Jan 2027 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541820/custodial-superintendent": {
      "title": "Custodial Superintendent",
      "description": "Custodial Superintendent Apply now Job no: 541820 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades, Environmental/Occupational Safety Department: 05280000 - RU-HOUSEKEEPING Classification Title: Superintendent, Custodial Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Administrative Leadership & Operational Oversight Provide work management and administrative direction for custodial services, ensuring all facilities meet high sanitation and cleanliness standards, including offices, event spaces, and public areas Supervise and lead custodial staff, set performance expectations, and provide direction for goal achievement Recruit, hire, onboard, and train custodial staff, ensuring consistent standards for safety, cleaning quality, and customer service Develop long-range custodial service plans, including staffing levels, work priorities, and cleaning techniques Oversee budgeting, cost projections, purchasing approval, and financial controls for custodial operations Develop and implement policies and procedures, including safety and work quality standards, hazardous material handling, and sustainability initiatives Formulate service contracts and specifications for equipment, cleaning supplies, and services, ensuring compliance with university purchasing guidelines Coordinate services with other campus departments, including waste management, pest controls, and grounds services, as needed Staff Supervision & Workflow Management Plan, implement, and adjust custodial work shift schedules to ensure efficient workforce utilization Monitor daily operations and implement continuous improvements in cleaning methods, work activities, and performance standards Conduct service needs assessments, analyze results, and implement solutions for enhanced efficiency Develop and implement training programs for staff on safety, cleaning standards, customer service, and the proper use of equipment and supplies Oversee new employee orientation, ensure compliance with workplace safety standards, and maintain up to date safety data sheets (SDS) Handle employee performance evaluations, disciplinary actions, and human resource matters, ensuring alignment with university policies Occasionally will require hands-on work during short staffing, events, or emergencies Quality Assurance & Facility Inspection Establish and enforce high-quality custodial work standards for both internal staff and external vendors Conduct regular facility inspections and take corrective actions to maintain cleanliness, safety, and security Investigate and respond to service requests, complaints, and feedback from building occupants and customers to ensure prompt resolution Special projects and other duties Plan and execute special cleaning projects, collaborating with external vendors as necessary Develop and oversee facility-wide recycling programs and other sustainability initiatives Prepare and analyze management reports, incident reports, and custodial service assessments Coordinate custodial response during a shelter activation, hurricane recovery, or any emergency situation Collaborate with university departments and vendors to maintain high standards for custodial and facility services Expected Salary: $65,000 - $70,000; Commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Experience in managing and training a large team Ability to work as part of a team Proficiency in operating and using various custodial cleaning equipment Awareness of current cleaning methods, products, and materials including chemicals, and general knowledge of handling and disposing of hazardous materials Familiarity with building cleaning including but not limited to floor care, wall surfaces, windows, offices, restrooms, food areas, meeting and assembly spaces, and common areas Experience with work order, timekeeping, and purchasing systems Strong communication skills (verbal and written) Excellent customer service skills Understanding of budgeting practices Ability to determine work priorities, assign tasks, and ensure proper completion of work assignments Capability to function effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions Skill in handling multiple projects or tasks simultaneously Ability to understand, interpret, and apply rules, regulations, policies, and procedures Professional custodial certification from CMI, IEHA, FSPMA, ISSA, or APPA Familiarity with cleaning standards frameworks like APPA cleaning levels Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and list of professional references. Criminal background check is required Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 24 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 08 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
