    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540933/administrative-assistant-ii": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II Apply now Job no: 540933 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Health Care Administration/Support Department: 29091800 - MD-PEDS-NEUROLOGY Classification Title: Administrative Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience. Job Description: The Administrative Assistant II in the Division of Pediatric Neurology within the Department of Pediatrics provides administrative and operational support to divisional faculty, staff, and leadership by performing a variety of general to moderately complex administrative duties. Responsibilities include coordinating calendars and meetings, preparing correspondence and reports, maintaining records and shared resources, managing communications, supporting recruitment and onboarding activities, and serving as a resource regarding routine divisional policies, procedures, and administrative processes. This position also supports fiscal and human resources processes, provider scheduling, facilities and information technology coordination, and event planning. The role serves as a key administrative resource for the division by supporting daily operations, coordinating special projects, and ensuring efficient and effective office functions in accordance with University and departmental policies and procedures. General Administration, Office Operations & Program Support: Provides administrative support for an assigned division within the Department of Pediatrics by coordinating daily office activities and serving as a primary resource for faculty, staff, trainees, and divisional leadership regarding routine divisional policies, procedures, and administrative processes. Coordinates calendars, meetings, conference room reservations, and meeting logistics; prepares agendas, correspondence, reports, presentations, and meeting minutes; and maintains divisional contact lists, organizational charts, distribution lists, records, and shared resources. Monitors shared divisional email accounts, responds to routine and moderately complex inquiries, and ensures timely communication and appropriate routing of requests. Maintains office filing systems, administrative workflows, and confidential records in accordance with University and departmental procedures. Coordinates divisional meetings, seminars, lectureships, educational activities, guest speakers, and special events by arranging meeting logistics, preparing materials, coordinating travel and accommodations, and providing administrative support before, during, and after events. Operational, Fiscal & Human Resources Support: Provides administrative support for divisional operational activities, including recruitment and onboarding, provider scheduling, payroll, human resources, fiscal administration, purchasing, and facilities coordination. Coordinates candidate interviews, recruitment itineraries, travel arrangements, onboarding activities, workspace setup, access requests, and orientation scheduling. Assists with processing travel requests, expense reimbursements, purchasing requests, UF Marketplace requisitions, invoices, and other routine fiscal transactions while maintaining supporting documentation and monitoring office supply inventories. Orders and maintains office and operational supplies while monitoring inventory levels to ensure uninterrupted divisional operations and the efficient use of departmental resources. Assists with payroll and human resources processes, including timekeeping and leave reporting. Assists with facilities maintenance requests, information technology service requests, office moves, workstation setup, and other operational support activities to ensure efficient divisional operations. Cross-Divisional Administrative Support & Special Projects: Provides administrative support and cross-coverage for other divisions within the Department of Pediatrics as assigned by the Division Administrator. Assists with workload redistribution during staffing shortages, employee leave, vacancies, and other operational needs to ensure continuity of departmental operations. Supports departmental initiatives, coordinates special administrative projects, and performs additional duties as assigned by the Division Administrator and/or divisional leadership. Collaborates with divisional and departmental personnel to maintain efficient administrative workflows and ensure continuity of administrative services across the department. Expected Salary: $20.96 - $22.68 per hour Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Microsoft Office applications and familiarity with University of Florida administrative systems, including myUFL, UF GO, UF Marketplace, and Epic, along with strong organizational, communication, and customer service skills, are highly desirable. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This position is eligible for veteran’s preference. If you are claiming veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. This is a Time Limited Position. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541577/email-marketing-specialist-enrollment-marketing-communications": {
      "title": "Email Marketing Specialist (Enrollment Marketing & Communications)",
      "description": "Email Marketing Specialist (Enrollment Marketing & Communications) Apply now Job no: 541577 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing Department: 03010300 - EM-ADMIN PUBLICATIONS-COMMUNIC Classification Title: Communications Specialist Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The University of Florida is looking for an Email Marketing Specialist to support strategic enrollment marketing and communication initiatives that engage prospective students throughout their recruitment journey. In this role, you will execute multi-channel communication campaigns through CRM platforms, develop audience segmentation strategies, manage email marketing automation, and collaborate with Enrollment Management partners to increase awareness, engagement, and enrollment at the University of Florida. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Enrollment Communications & Email Marketing Collaborate with the Enrollment Marketing and Communication team to execute the annual enrollment communication plan through CRM platforms in alignment with divisional priorities and strategic objectives. Manage email communication campaigns from planning through deployment, including audience segmentation, personalization, testing, scheduling, automation, quality assurance, and optimization. Develop targeted and personalized communication experiences based on prospective student characteristics, behaviors, interests, and stages of the recruitment and enrollment journey. Create and maintain communication templates, campaign assets, and related resources within CRM platforms while ensuring alignment with University of Florida brand, accessibility, and communication standards. Apply email marketing and digital communication best practices to strengthen engagement and support divisional recruitment and enrollment objectives. CRM & Marketing Automation Develop and maintain an in-depth working knowledge of enrollment and prospective student data across undergraduate, graduate, certificate, and professional student populations. Create, manage, and maintain target audience reports, communication lists, filters, and segmentation criteria within CRM platforms to support targeted and broadcast communications. Utilize enrollment and prospect data to develop accurate audience selections and support personalized communication strategies. Analyze communication and audience data to identify opportunities to improve campaign targeting, personalization, engagement, and overall effectiveness. Maintain strong collaborative relationships with stakeholders throughout Enrollment Management and serve as a resource for communication-related CRM processes and best practices. Other Duties Performs other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Stay current on emerging trends, technologies, and best practices in email marketing, CRM strategy, marketing automation, digital communications, and enrollment marketing. Analyze existing communication processes, workflows, and content to identify opportunities for increased efficiency, accuracy, automation, and consistency. Expected Salary: $55,000 annually In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Two years of professional experience in email marketing, digital marketing, CRM communications, marketing automation, enrollment communications, or a related field is preferred. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated problem-solving skills, with the ability to be resourceful, proactive, and seek assistance as needed. Experience with CRMs such as Salesforce, Slate, HubSpot etc. Google Analytics and Google Ads experience. Familiarity with WCAG 2.1. Knowledge of email compliance regulations. Familiarity with email marketing and marketing automation technology. Excellent attention to detail, accuracy and time management skills. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with others, adapting approach to suit the needs of various audiences. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541580/gator-welcome-guide-2027-admissions": {
      "title": "Gator Welcome Guide - 2027 (Admissions)",
      "description": "Gator Welcome Guide - 2027 (Admissions) Apply now Job no: 541580 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 03020000 - EM-OFFICE OF ADMISSIONS Classification Title: STU AST - NON-CLERICAL & ADMIN Classification Minimum Requirements: Must be a current UF student who can commit to this role from January 11, 2027 through April 30, 2027, as well as commit to working either Summer A or Summer B. Job Description: The University of Florida’s Office of Admissions is seeking enthusiastic and motivated students to join our team as Gator Welcome Guides! This is a unique opportunity to represent UF, connect with prospective and admitted students and their families, and help create memorable campus visit experiences through tours, outreach, and visitor engagement. Why Join Our Team? As a Gator Welcome Guide, you will be at the forefront of showcasing UF to prospective and admitted students and their families. Through engaging storytelling, personalized interactions, and exceptional customer service, you will help deliver a best-in-class campus visit experience, both in-person and virtually, while highlighting the opportunities, traditions, and community that make UF special. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Campus Tours & Guest Engagement Lead prospective and admitted students and families on in-person and virtual campus tours, providing insights into both UF’s physical campus and its academic and student life offerings. Utilize storytelling techniques to create a memorable, engaging experience that highlights what makes UF special. Conduct indoor tours during inclement weather and adapt to different audience needs. Campus Experience & Tour Guide Team Support Serve as a representative at large visit and virtual events, providing tours, greeting guests, assisting with check-in, and offering directional guidance. This may include select weekends, evenings, and break periods. Support the daily operations of the Welcome Center or Criser Hall (Admissions Lobby) front desk, delivering excellent customer service. Assist with event logistics, including assembling materials, setting up event spaces, coordinating signage, and ensuring smooth transitions between activities. Answer phone calls and respond to inquiries from prospective students and families. Assist with other responsibilities as needed. Expected Salary: $15.50/hour Required Qualifications: Must be a current UF student who can commit to this role from January 11, 2027 through April 30, 2027, as well as commit to working either Summer A or Summer B. Preferred: Previous experience as a tour guide, student ambassador, or customer-facing role. Strong communication and storytelling skills, with the ability to engage and connect with various audiences. Friendly, professional, and reliable, with a passion for UF and a commitment to delivering an exceptional visitor experience. Willingness to support expanded tour availability, including select Saturdays and Sundays, home game Fridays, and UF academic breaks, to meet high visitor demand. Ability to work through Fall 2027. Special Instructions to Applicants: This position will report to the UF Welcome Center or Criser Hall, but will involve extensive walking across various locations on campus. Applicants must upload a resume to be considered for the position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Students seeking FWS employment should print/screenshot a copy of the Financial Aid Award Page, which contains the Federal Work Study award as proof of FWS eligibility. To locate your Financial Aid Award Page, go to https://one.uf.edu/financialaid/aidyear Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541711/ast-dirunv-housing-res-life": {
      "title": "Ast Dir,Unv Housing Res Life",
      "description": "Ast Dir,Unv Housing Res Life Apply now Job no: 541711 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Executive/Director/Management Department: 07700100 - HO-HOUSING OFFICE Classification Title: Ast Dir,Unv Housing Res Life Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience or a bachelor’s degree in appropriate areas of specialization and four years of experience. Job Description: Leadership of residential programs and student development Provide oversight and direction for a comprehensive residential program that promotes student learning, retention, and academic success. Oversee community programming and development in residential spaces ensuring strategic alignment with academic calendar, departmental and divisional goals Lead the development and evaluation of a practical and theory-based student development program and residential curriculum, living learning communities, and co-curricular initiatives aligned with departmental and divisional goals Establish policies and procedures that guide residential operations, including health and safety, facility management, and emergency response. Lead execution of residential policies, procedures, and protocols including but not limited opening/closing, reassignments, damage assessments, and health and safety inspections Collaborate with internal units to ensure residential facilities are safe, secure, and well-maintained; conduct regular building inspections Analyze assessment data and benchmark trends to inform program and policy improvements Provide oversight to advisors of department sponsored student organizations (e.g. Area Governments) including but not limited to governance, programming, and financial management Provide administrative follow-up to students, families or faculty members, addressing concerns and needs Responsible for emergency response safeguarding residents, employees, facilities, and assets in the event of emergencies or disasters aligning with departmental and University policies and procedures and divisional emergency management Serve as a Campus Security Authority Oversight of Housing Community Standards and Student Conduct & Conflict Resolution Processes Adjudicate individual student cases via administrative hearings and administrative reviews or refer to other conflict resolution processes as appropriate. Lead efforts to monitor and manage investigations, charging, caseloads, prioritization, and completion of resolutions and provide reports to departmental leadership on a regular basis. Provide leadership for Housing community standards, student conduct code, and student honor code through all resolution process types. Responsible for records maintenance to ensure compliance with institutional policies, local/state/federal law, and reporting requirements; provides responsive information related to Florida Open Records requests. Monitor case tracking and monitoring to ensure efficient, accurate, and effective case processes. Play a key role in advancing staff training related to resolution processes, community standards, conflict coaching, and mediation. Make recommendations for ongoing improvement of processes, programs, and services offered through the resolution processes. Recommend improvements to policies, regulations, and procedures related to the community standards and conduct process in consultation with the appropriate campus partners (e.g. Housing & Residence Life, General Counsel). Staff leadership and administrative management Supervise professional and student staff including recruitment, training, performance evaluation, and professional development Provide leadership in establishing goals, work priorities, and outcomes Manage administrative functions including HR compliance, payroll approval, and performance review processes. Oversee budgets for area and allocate resources to support program priorities. Lead the development, implementation, dissemination, and enforcement of departmental policies, procedures, and guidelines to ensure consistency, and compliance within areas of responsibility. Ensure effective use of information systems (e.g. Maxient, Housing Management Software) and corresponding data utilized in area operations and departmental processes Serve in after hours on-call rotation to respond to emergencies for area of responsibility Coordinate on-call schedules for area providing leadership during response and follow-up Develop reports, handle special projects, and perform other duties as assigned Serve on departmental, Division of Student Life or University of Florida committees or program support as needed Assist in unit or departmental strategic planning and reporting Operates state vehicles Expected Salary: $65,000 annually. In addition, the University of Florida offers a very competitive benefit package. Learn more by visiting: https://hr.ufl.edu/benefits/ Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience or a bachelor’s degree in appropriate areas of specialization and four years of experience. • Valid drivers license Preferred: EXPERIENCE Obtained master’s degree in in higher education, counseling, leadership or similar field Experience with full-time staff supervision Understanding of student development (e.g. theory, application to residential communities) Experience with organizational conduct processes, including investigations Experience with developing learning outcomes and assessment tools Demonstrated experience with crisis management Familiarity with relevant state and federal laws/regulations that impact student conduct policies and processes Experience working with budgets and other business-related functions SKILLS Demonstrated proficiency with computers and software applications (e.g. Microsoft Office Suite, Maxient, StarRez) Demonstrated planning, time management, and organizational skills Demonstrated communication skills (verbal and written) Demonstrated interpersonal skills ABILITIES Ability to lead a team and work cooperatively with team members Proven ability to address nuanced problems with sensitivity and discretion Demonstrated ability to function effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions Demonstrated ability to handle multiple projects or tasks simultaneously Demonstrated ability to understand, interpret, and apply rules, regulations, policies, and procedures Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and professional references Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 15 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
