    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541786/student-research-assistant-federal-work-study": {
      "title": "Student Research Assistant (Federal Work Study)",
      "description": "Student Research Assistant (Federal Work Study) Apply now Job no: 541786 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science, Dentistry Department: 34030000 - DN-ORAL BIOLOGY Classification Title: Student Research Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma (or equivalent) and at least one semester of college completed. Job Description: The principal duties and responsibilities assigned to this position are to support microbiological research by performing routine laboratory preparation and maintenance tasks. Responsibilities include preparing culture media, common laboratory solutions, and glassware and plasticware; managing biological waste; maintaining lab cleanliness; and tracking laboratory inventories. 10 hours per week. Expected Salary: $15.00 per hour Required Qualifications: Student must be participating in Federal Work Study Program, have high school diploma (or equivalent) and at least one semester of college completed. Preferred: Basic lab skills are a plus, but not required. Special Instructions to Applicants: Students seeking FWS employment should print/screenshot a copy of their Financial Aid Award Page, which contains the Federal Work Study award as proof of FWS edibility. To locate your Financial Aid Award Page, go to https://one.uf.edu/fincialaid/aidyear This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 06 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
