    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541807/federal-work-study-student-assistant-division-of-pathology": {
      "title": "Federal Work Study - Student Assistant (Division of Pathology)",
      "description": "Federal Work Study - Student Assistant (Division of Pathology) Apply now Job no: 541807 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Dentistry Department: 34160200 - DN-ORAL PATHOLOGY Classification Title: Federal Work Study - Student Assistant (Division of Pathology) Classification Minimum Requirements: Must have Federal Work Study Award Job Description: The Department of Oral and Maxillofacial Diagnostic Sciences, Division of Pathology is seeking a Federal Work Study Student. This position provides support to the Lab. Responsibilities include: Filing and organizing slides and wax blocks by accession number and year and according to established laboratory procedures. Providing backup support to full-time laboratory staff during absences or as needed, including opening and sorting daily packages. Replenishing laboratory supplies and maintaining adequate stock levels. Performing other related duties and special assignments as needed. Expected Salary: $15.00 per hour Required Qualifications: Must have Federal Work Study Award Preferred: Preferred Qualifications include: Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to follow established procedures for filing, labeling, and organizing laboratory materials High attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage large volumes of detailed information. Ability to work independently, take initiative, and multitask effectively. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume and Federal Work Study Award. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 23 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
