    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541714/professional-development-facilitator-12month": {
      "title": "Professional Development Facilitator (12-Month)",
      "description": "Professional Development Facilitator (12-Month) Apply now Job no: 541714 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Pasco Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Early childhood education/Childcare Department: 18010100 - ED-DN OFFICE-GENERAL Classification Title: Instructional Designer II Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and four years of relevant experience. Job Description: Coordinate, develop, and deliver professional learning across the CS Everyone Center Design, coordinate, facilitate, and evaluate professional learning experiences for K-12 educators and educational leaders focused on CS, AI literacy, instructional technology, and comprehensive educational practices. Deliver engaging professional learning through face-to-face workshops, virtual sessions, cohort-based programs, and Professional Learning Communities (PLCs). Translate complex and rapidly evolving topics in AI, CS, and educational technology into practical learning experiences that educators can apply in their schools and classrooms. Collaborate across CS Everyone Center projects to identify common professional learning needs, coordinate offerings, and develop coherent experiences across grant funded initiatives. Support the development and refinement of professional learning materials, resources, and tools aligned with CS Everyone goals, current CS and AI standards, accessibility principles, and comprehensive instructional practices. Promote and expand participation in professional learning opportunities Partner with school districts and educational organizations to understand local needs and support effective implementation of CS and AI initiatives. Develop and maintain professional relationships with educators, district leaders, community organizations, higher education partners, and other stakeholders. Contribute to outreach and recruitment efforts that expand participation in CS Everyone professional learning opportunities, particularly among districts and communities that may have limited access to CS and AI learning opportunities. Work closely with project managers and other Center staff to coordinate timelines, deliverables, communications, and evaluation activities. Monitor emerging developments in AI, CS education, and instructional technology and help the Center respond to evolving educator and district needs. Perform related duties as required or deemed appropriate to the accomplishment of the responsibilities and functions related to this position. Ability and willingness to travel regularly throughout Florida, including to rural and underserved communities, is required. Expected Salary: $70,000-75,000 Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and four years of relevant experience. Preferred: Substantial experience providing professional development or instructional coaching to K-12 educators Demonstrated experience in K-12 computer science, artificial intelligence, instructional technology, or related educational technology Experience translating technology or emerging educational practices into practical professional learning for educators Demonstrated ability to facilitate engaging learning experiences for broad audiences, both in person and virtually Strong presentation, written communication, relationship-building, and collaboration skills Experience working across schools, districts, organizations, or other complex educational environments Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain partnerships with educators and educational stakeholders Experience leading or supporting district-wide implementation of instructional technology, computer science, or AI initiatives Experience with AI literacy, generative AI, or AI integration in K-12 education Experience with Universal Design for Learning (UDL), accessibility, and comprehensive instructional practices Experience supporting educators serving learners with disabilities Experience with grant-funded educational initiatives Experience presenting at state, regional, or national educational conferences Experience developing or facilitating Professional Learning Communities or other cohort based professional learning Experience with project management software such as Asana, Microsoft Loop, or similar platforms Advanced degree in education, instructional design, computer science, educational technology, or related field Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload: A current resume or curriculum vitae (CV) A cover letter detailing your relevant experience with K-12 professional learning, CS/AI education, and instructional technology Names and contact information for three professional references Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541722/ops-research-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Research Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Research Assistant Apply now Job no: 541722 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science, Grant or Research Administration, Agricultural Sciences Department: 60210000 - AG-SOIL AND WATER SCIENCE Classification Title: OPS Research Assistant Classification Minimum Requirements: This OPS Research Assistant Position is time-limited with the possibility for extension depending on the availability of funding in the Department of Soil, Water, and Ecosystem Sciences. Activities will provide support to ongoing projects in marine microbial ecology under the guidance of Dr. Julie Meyer. Work will take place in a laboratory setting Monday-Friday, typically 9:00 am to 5:00 pm (up to 29 hours per week). Extended hours may be requested during busy times of the year. Job Description: -Conducts laboratory experiments using established methods and procedures. These may include DNA extractions, polymerase chain reaction, maintenance of microbiological cultures, and data analysis. -Assist or independently prepare professional progress reports documenting results of experiments for reporting to sponsoring agencies. -Maintain detailed written and digital records of laboratory methods and results. -Maintain updated inventories of consumable supplies and biological samples. Manage chemical and biological waste generation and removal for the lab. -Train graduate and undergraduate researchers in the laboratory research methods and lab safety. The duties of this position will be conducted indoors at the Cancer and Genetics Research Complex and will include biological laboratory benchwork, general lab cleaning duties, and record-keeping with lab computers. Expected Salary: $20 per hour Required Qualifications: THIS POSITION IS RESPONSIBLE FOR MEETING THE REQUIREMENTS OF THE RULES OF UNIVERSITY OF FLORIDA, 6C1-3.022 FINANCE AND ADMINISTRATION; PAYMENT TO VENDORS; PAYMENT PROCESSING GUIDELINES, AS AMENDED, REGARDING THE APPROVAL AND/OR PROCESSING OF VENDORS’ INVOICES AND/OR DISTRIBUTION OF WARRANTS TO VENDORS. Preferred: Bachelor’s degree in microbiology and experience in molecular biology. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 11 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541779/ops-research-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Research Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Research Assistant Apply now Job no: 541779 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Grant or Research Administration, Agricultural Sciences Department: 60370000 - AG-CENTER-AQUA - INVAS PLNTS Classification Title: OPS - Time Limited Classification Minimum Requirements: Pursuing a degree in biology, environmental science, or a related field is preferred. Interest in invasive species ecology, aquatic ecosystems, plant management and/or plant biology. Ability to follow detailed instructions, maintain accurate records, and work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate with colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated reliability and enthusiasm for scientific research. Willingness to work occasional weekends or evenings as needed for fieldwork or special projects. Job Description: Help set up laboratory experiments and fieldwork to study invasive aquatic plant species. Assist with the collection and processing of research data using established protocols and techniques. Perform routine laboratory tasks, including sample preparation, equipment maintenance, and inventory management. Help maintain laboratory cleanliness and organization to ensure a safe and efficient work environment. Collaborate with research team members to plan, execute experiments, and troubleshoot issues. Adhere to safety protocols and regulations while working with hazardous materials and equipment. Expected Salary: $15.00v/hour Required Qualifications: This is an hourly OPS position, with flexible scheduling based on project needs and candidate availability. This is a part-time position. Work will involve exposure to outdoor weather conditions and physical exertion during fieldwork activities. The majority of your time will be spent doing mesocosm work outdoors at our facility in Gainesville, Florida. Laboratory work will also occur inside the facility. Balance between indoor and outdoor activities will be determined based on weather conditions and project needs. Preferred: Pursuing a degree in biology, environmental science, or a related field is preferred. Interest in invasive species ecology, aquatic ecosystems, plant management and/or plant biology. Ability to follow detailed instructions, maintain accurate records, and work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Strong communication skills and the ability to collaborate with colleagues from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated reliability and enthusiasm for scientific research. Willingness to work occasional weekends or evenings as needed for fieldwork or special projects. Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested candidates should submit a resume and contact information for two professional references. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. This job is located off campus out Millhopper Road, so applicants must have their own transportation. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 03 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541782/postdoctoral-researchersmeg-and-multimodal-neuroimaging-in-dementia-and-epilepsy": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researchers–MEG and Multimodal Neuroimaging in Dementia and Epilepsy",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researchers–MEG and Multimodal Neuroimaging in Dementia and Epilepsy Apply now Job no: 541782 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science, Grant or Research Administration Department: 29180200 - MD-NEUROLOGY-EPILEPSY Classification Title: Postdoctoral Associate Classification Minimum Requirements: PhD in Biomedical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Neuroscience, Computer Science, Psychology, or closely related field Demonstrated MEG analysis experience (FieldTrip/Brainstorm/MNE-Python or similar) Job Description: The Magnetoencephalography (MEG) Lab at the University of Florida (UF) is seeking two highly motivated postdoctoral researchers to join our interdisciplinary research team. The positions are supported by NIH and other funded projects investigating clinically important questions in epilepsy and Alzheimer’s disease and related dementias (AD/ADRD). The two postdoctoral researchers will focus on complementary areas: Multimodal Language Mapping in Epilepsy This position will focus on improving prediction of language outcomes following epilepsy surgery through integration of noninvasive neuroimaging, including MEG, fMRI, and diffusion MRI (DWI/DTI), with invasive language-mapping approaches such as electrical stimulation mapping (ESM). The project provides opportunities to develop and validate computational approaches for multimodal brain mapping and clinically relevant prediction of surgical outcomes in patients with epilepsy and brain tumors. Multimodal Neuroimaging and Biomarkers in AD/ADRD This position will focus on integrating MEG with multimodal neuroimaging, including structural MRI, fMRI, diffusion MRI, and PET, to advance biomarker discovery and mechanistic understanding of neural dysfunction in Alzheimer’s disease, Lewy body disease, and related dementias. Opportunities include advanced signal processing, brain connectivity and network analyses, multimodal data integration, and machine-learning/AI approaches. Both postdoctoral researchers will have opportunities to lead analyses, develop new computational and neuroimaging methods, collaborate with multidisciplinary clinical and research teams, contribute to grant applications, and develop independent research directions aligned with their career goals. Research Environment and Career Development The positions offer substantial opportunities for scientific and professional development, including individualized mentorship in grant writing, development of independent research projects, and career-focused funding applications such as NIH K awards. Postdoctoral researchers will also be supported in presenting their work at major national and international scientific conferences. The UF MEG Laboratory research environment provides access to state-of-the-art neuroimaging and computational infrastructure, including a whole-head MEG system, two 3T MRI scanners, PET/CT imaging, clinical and research neurophysiology/neuroimaging resources, and extensive patient populations and clinical collaborations. Researchers also have access to UF HiPerGator, one of the largest university high-performance computing environments in the United States, with large-scale CPU and GPU resources for advanced neuroimaging, machine-learning, and AI workflows. These are full-time, funded postdoctoral appointments with multi-year support. About the City of Gainesville Home to the University of Florida, one of the nation's top public universities, Gainesville offers vibrant academic and healthcare communities alongside an affordable cost of living, no state income tax, and mild winters. Enjoy the outdoors with over 30 miles of bike trails, freshwater springs, and numerous water activities, plus easy access to beaches and world-class theme parks. Gainesville combines historic charm with modern amenities, including a great school system, a lively downtown, and thriving farmers' markets and craft breweries. Discover professional growth and quality of life in Gainesville—where community, innovation, and work-life balance meet! For more information, check out: The Guide to Greater Gainesville and Explore Gainesville in 60 seconds Expected Salary: $60,000 - $80,000 annually Required Qualifications: PhD in Biomedical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Neuroscience, Computer Science, Psychology, or closely related field Demonstrated MEG analysis experience (FieldTrip/Brainstorm/MNE-Python or similar) Preferred: The ideal candidate will possess: Experience in MEG and/or other neuroimaging modalities such as fMRI, diffusion MRI, or PET Strong backgrounds in signal processing, computational neuroscience, neuroimaging, or machine learning/AI Experience with one or more neuroimaging and analysis platforms, such as FieldTrip, Brainstorm, MNE-Python, FreeSurfer, FSL, or SPM, and proficiency in MATLAB and/or Python Special Instructions to Applicants: Interested candidates should email: A current CV A brief statement of research interests, including which of the two research areas is of greatest interest, to Dr. Abbas Babajani, Director of the UF MEG Lab, at babajani.a@ufl.edu . References will be requested from selected candidates at a later stage. Review of applications will begin immediately. The start date is flexible. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition will be used to fill multiple positions. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 21 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541790/cardiologist-noninvasive-clinical-assistant-associate-full-professor": {
      "title": "Cardiologist Noninvasive - Clinical Assistant, Associate, Full Professor",
      "description": "Cardiologist Noninvasive - Clinical Assistant, Associate, Full Professor Apply now Job no: 541790 Work type: Multi-Track Faculty Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 30050000 - JX-MEDICINE AT JAX Classification Title: CLIN AST/ ASO/FULL PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: Must be MD/DO and be BC/BE in Cardiology Job Description: The Cardiovascular Center at the University of Florida College of Medicine-Jacksonville seeks a full-time Cardiologist for the Noninvasive Laboratory. This is at the tenure, non-tenure accruing level of Clinical Assistant Associate or Full Professor and is Board Certified and Board Eligible in Cardiology with high interest and expertise in non-invasive imaging. The Cardiovascular Center is a state-of-the-art facility servicing North Florida and South Georgia. Our rapidly expanding Cardiovascular Program is focused on teaching and education, clinical care and research. About UF Health: UF Health is the Southeast’s premier academic health center and an integral part of the University of Florida. Our mission is to promote health through outstanding and high-quality patient care, innovative and rigorous education in the health professions and biomedical sciences, and research across the spectrum of basic, translational and clinical investigation. UF Health encompasses the Gainesville-based University of Florida colleges of Dentistry, Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health and Health Professions, and Veterinary Medicine; the UF Health Shands family of hospitals in Gainesville; UF Health Jacksonville medical center; UF Health North; an academic campus in Jacksonville that is home to the UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville and includes degree programs offered by the colleges of Nursing and Pharmacy; UF Health St. Johns in St. Augustine; UF Health Neighborhood Hospital in Ocala; and our campus in Central Florida, which includes UF Health Spanish Plaines Hospital and UF Health Leesburg Hospital. It also includes primary care and specialty practices throughout Central, North Central and northern Florida and Southeast Georgia. The UF Health network of hospitals and physician practices manages more than 3 million inpatient and outpatient visits each year, and serves patients from all 67 Florida counties, from across the nation and from dozens of countries around the world. About College of Medicine – Jacksonville (COM-J): The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville is the largest of the three colleges at the Health Science Center Jacksonville. The college's 16 clinical science departments house more than 500 faculty members, 1,560 staff and 450 residents and fellows, as well as medical students from UF and around the country. We offer an incredible breadth of clinical training programs and proud to train many of best primary care providers and specialists throughout the region, the state and the country. Research, discovery and innovation are critical aspects of our clinical campus and we have some of the country’s leading researchers at our locations searching for and finding new treatments and clinical options. The UF College of Medicine – Jacksonville faculty, administrators, residents, fellows, students and staff work as a team in pursuit of our common mission — to heal, to comfort, to educate and to discover through quality health care, elimination of health disparities, medical education, innovation and research. To learn more about our college, leadership, mission, faculty resources, and the city of Jacksonville visit https://med.jax.ufl.edu/administrative-affairs/faculty-orientation-guide/ Expected Salary: Commensurate with experience. Required Qualifications: Must be MD/DO and be BC/BE in Cardiology Preferred Qualifications: Board Certified/ Board Eligible in Cardiology with high interest and expertise in non-invasive imaging Special Instructions to Applicants: This position is open until filled. The Search Committee will begin to review applications as soon as an applicant pool is identified. Please provide letter of intent and Curriculum Vitae. The final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541791/ops-corn-breeding": {
      "title": "OPS- Corn Breeding",
      "description": "OPS- Corn Breeding Apply now Job no: 541791 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Palm Beach Categories: Agricultural Sciences Department: 60740000 - AG-EREC-BELLE GLADE Classification Title: OPS- Time Limited Classification Minimum Requirements: Valid Florida Driver's License Job Description: Assist with greenhouse and field preparation, maintenance, planting, and general crop care Safely handle agricultural tools, equipment, and materials Maintain clean and organized work areas Assist with crop tagging, labeling, sample collection, harvesting, and record keeping Perform controlled hand pollination of corn plants in field and greenhouse environments Identify corn plants and reproductive stages ready for pollination Collect and apply pollen according to established procedures Follow procedures to prevent unwanted cross-pollination or contamination Carefully handle pollen, bags, labels, and other pollination materials Accurately record pollination crosses, plant information, dates, and other required data Assist with other agricultural duties as assigned throughout the growing season Expected Salary: $15-$17/hr, based on experience Required Qualifications: Previous agricultural, farm, greenhouse, or crop-production experience preferred; willing to train the right candidate Able to perform physical work for extended periods, including standing, walking, bending, kneeling, reaching, and working with plants Able to lift and carry materials, tools, and equipment as required Comfortable working outdoors in hot, humid, dusty, or changing weather conditions Comfortable working in greenhouses where temperatures and humidity may be high Good hand coordination and attention to detail Able to follow detailed instructions, safety procedures, and established agricultural practices Reliable, punctual, responsible, and able to work effectively with others Willing to work flexible hours based on crop conditions, weather, and pollination schedules Preferred: Previous experience with corn pollination, plant breeding, or agricultural research Experience working with corn tassels, silks, pollen, or controlled crosses Greenhouse or research-farm experience Basic knowledge of crop production and plant care Valid driver's license, required for the position Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 01 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541792/assistant-professor-of-construction-management": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management Apply now Job no: 541792 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Construction/Design/Planning, Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 15030000 - DCP-RINKER SCH OF CONSTR MGMT Classification Title: AST PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate in construction management, building construction, civil engineering, architecture, or closely related fields. Doctoral candidates who have successfully passed their qualifying examinations and are expected to complete their degree before the start of the Fall 2027 semester are also encouraged to apply. Appointment will be contingent upon completion of the doctoral degree prior to the start date. Job Description: Position Description The M.E. Rinker, Sr. School of Construction Management at the University of Florida invites applications for a tenure-track appointment to the faculty at the Assistant Professor rank. We seek motivated scholars whose research focuses on the core areas of construction management, including but not limited to construction project management, project delivery methods (such as Design-Build, IPD, CMAR, etc.), design development drawings / graphical communications, cost estimating and control, project planning and scheduling, construction means, methods and operations, and productivity and performance improvement. We expect that candidates will engage in both fundamental and applied research to advance the practice of construction management. The successful candidate will also demonstrate excellence at teaching courses within core competency areas, including construction drawing, estimating, project planning, productivity improvement, and contracts, as well as have the ability and vision to develop and deliver graduate courses in their area of expertise. It is preferred that candidates demonstrate professional experience in construction or a construction-related profession, and a working knowledge of the United States construction industry. The successful candidate should demonstrate the potential to attract nationally competitive research grants, engage in multi-disciplinary research, and be motivated to collaborate with other faculty across the College of Design, Construction and Planning and within other colleges at the University of Florida. The successful faculty candidate will be expected to develop funded research programs, publish in peer-reviewed journals, supervise graduate student research, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and provide service to the University, the community, and the profession. M.E. Rinker, Sr. School of Construction Management Established in 1935, Rinker School is the oldest continuing building construction program in the country. The Rinker School has more than 8,000 graduates, over 320 upper-division undergraduate students, around 75 Master’s students, and nearly 50 Ph.D. students. The Rinker School has 29 full-time faculty members and 11 support staff. Our vibrant faculty are nationally and internationally recognized, consistently attracting a significant amount of research funding every year. The University of Florida UF, founded in 1853, is one of the state's oldest academic institutions and among the nation's most academically diverse public universities. It is ranked 7th among U.S. public universities and belongs to the prestigious Association of American Universities (AAU). UF is one of the largest institutions of higher learning in the country with more than 100 undergraduate majors offered in 16 colleges and enrolls more than 61,000 students. The College of Design, Construction and Planning Established in 1925, the College of Design, Construction, and Planning (DCP) is a preeminent college in the university. DCP’s vision is to be recognized globally as a preeminent College for teaching, research, creative scholarship, and outreach in the built and natural environments. The mission of the College is to improve the quality of the built and natural environments through offering exceptional educational and professional programs and research/scholarship initiatives that address the planning, design, construction, and preservation of the built and natural environments. Expected Salary: The salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience, and the compensation includes a full benefits package. Employment Benefits include: Health Insurance: UF participates in state- and university-sponsored benefits programs for individuals, families, and domestic partners, and offers voluntary insurance that includes vision, dental, long-term disability and more. Retirement Options: Attractive options include Florida Retirement System Pension Plan, State University System Optional Retirement Program, Florida Retirement System Investment Plan, and Voluntary Retirement Savings Plan. Leave: UF staff enjoy a generous paid leave plan as well as access to a sick-leave pool, parental leave, and leave payouts. To learn more about benefits visit: UF Benefits Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in construction management, building construction, civil engineering, architecture, or closely related fields. Doctoral candidates who have successfully passed their qualifying examinations and are expected to complete their degree before the start of the Fall 2027 semester are also encouraged to apply. Appointment will be contingent upon completion of the doctoral degree prior to the start date. Preferred: Project management and/or field supervisory experience in the construction industry in the United States. University-level teaching experience in the core construction management competency areas. Special Instructions to Applicants: To ensure full consideration, the required documents should be submitted by Dec 1, 2026, when the Search Committee begins reviewing applications and will continue until the position are filled. A completed application should include: 1. A 1-2 page cover letter. 2. A curriculum vitae. 3. A statement describing research interests, accomplishments, and future research plans (1-2 pages). 4. A statement describing experiences in, and approaches to, teaching and mentoring students (1-2 pages). (Additional Evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as course evaluations, is recommended where available.) 5. Names and contact information for a minimum of three references. For additional information, contact Idris Jeelani Ph.D., Search Committee Chair (idris.jeelani@ufl.edu). Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541797/chair-professor-mechanical-aerospace-engineering": {
      "title": "CHAIR & PROFESSOR, Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "CHAIR & PROFESSOR, Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering Apply now Job no: 541797 Work type: Faculty Admin Title Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Engineering Department: 19020000 - EG-MECHANICAL - AEROSPACE ENG Classification Title: CHAIR & PROFESSOR Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate in mechanical or aerospace engineering, or a closely related field. A distinguished record of scholarship, education, mentoring, and professional contribution that merits appointment as a tenured full professor at the University of Florida. Evidence of successful leadership in a research-intensive university or comparably complex organization, including building collaborative, high-performing organizational cultures and developing faculty, staff, and emerging leaders. Demonstrated ability to develop and articulate a compelling strategic vision to advance the reputation and ranking of the department by translating that vision into clear priorities, strategic investments and measurable outcomes. Demonstrated ability to develop and expand sponsored research programs, including fostering collaborative research and advancing high-impact programs. Excellent communication, judgment, integrity, and relationship-building skills; ability to communicate and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to student success and to a scholarly and working environment where people with varied backgrounds and perspectives can contribute and thrive. Experience with external engagement and development, such as industry partnerships, alumni outreach, and fundraising. Job Description: The Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering at the University of Florida invites nominations and applications for the position of Professor and Department Chair of the Department of Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering (MAE). Reporting to the Dean of the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering, the Chair will provide strategic, intellectual, and administrative leadership for an internationally visible research and education enterprise. The successful candidate will be an accomplished scholar and an effective organizational leader with a strong record of externally funded research who can substantially improve the department’s recognition and ranking, develop a clear vision for international impact and connect the department’s strengths to consequential opportunities for Florida and the world. The selected leader will join the Dean’s leadership team and will be expected to advance both the department and the college, contribute to university priorities, and engage constructively with the state, nation, and profession. The Department of Mechanical & Aerospace Engineering (MAE) is the largest degree-granting unit at UF. The Department has nearly 60 faculty members, 500 graduate students and 3,100 undergraduates. In 2025, annual research expenditures reached $28M with 15 active grants over $1 million. Among public universities, Aerospace Engineering is currently ranked No. 16 and Mechanical Engineering is currently ranked No. 21 in the 2026 U.S. News & World Report rankings. Traditional strengths in solid mechanics, design, thermal fluid systems, dynamics and controls are leveraged in interdisciplinary and cutting-edge efforts in autonomous systems, multiphase turbulent systems, novel energy systems, bioengineering, advanced manufacturing, computational science, and space systems. MAE is home to nearly 20 student societies and provides exceptional dedicated facilities and financial support for our student-led design/build/compete organizations that routinely capture top placement at national and international competitions. In addition to overseeing the operational management of the Department, responsibilities of the Chair include: Creating a compelling vision for the advancement of the department that fosters cutting edge research within a collaborative and multidisciplinary environment and connects existing strengths to consequential opportunities. Recruiting faculty and facilitating both the professional and scholarly growth of the faculty, particularly the junior faculty. Ensuring a premier educational experience that fosters success of all trainees (undergraduate, graduate, postdoctoral and researchers). Elevating the awareness of the department’s impact and enhancing the working partnerships with leaders of UF, government agencies, and industry. Increasing sponsored research, private and external funding opportunities for the department. Cultivating corporate, governmental, alumni and other private donations. Ensuring an exceptional culture of collaboration, respect and continuous improvement for faculty, staff and students. The Chair will have the opportunity to build upon MAE's substantial research and educational strengths, shape its future strategic directions, and work closely with college leadership to advance ambitious initiatives in faculty excellence, research, and education. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in mechanical or aerospace engineering, or a closely related field. A distinguished record of scholarship, education, mentoring, and professional contribution that merits appointment as a tenured full professor at the University of Florida. Evidence of successful leadership in a research-intensive university or comparably complex organization, including building collaborative, high-performing organizational cultures and developing faculty, staff, and emerging leaders. Demonstrated ability to develop and articulate a compelling strategic vision to advance the reputation and ranking of the department by translating that vision into clear priorities, strategic investments and measurable outcomes. Demonstrated ability to develop and expand sponsored research programs, including fostering collaborative research and advancing high-impact programs. Excellent communication, judgment, integrity, and relationship-building skills; ability to communicate and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to student success and to a scholarly and working environment where people with varied backgrounds and perspectives can contribute and thrive. Experience with external engagement and development, such as industry partnerships, alumni outreach, and fundraising. Preferred: Experience recruiting, mentoring, evaluating, and retaining faculty and staff across career stages and appointment types. Experience developing multidisciplinary initiatives, major collaborative proposals, centers, institutes, or other large-scale research activities. Experience building productive industry partnerships, including sponsored research, consortia, or public-private collaborations. Experience using industry engagement to strengthen education, experiential learning, workforce preparation, and research opportunities. The ability to identify emerging funding opportunities and organize faculty and external partners around them. Experience working with College and University leadership and across academic units. Experience in advancement, philanthropy, alumni engagement, or development of external resources. Professional leadership and service in mechanical or aerospace engineering, or a related discipline. Special Instructions to Applicants: The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue to receive applications until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted through UFCareers at: https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/listing/ (Search Job 541797 ). Complete applications must include the following files in PDF format: (1) A cover letter describing the candidate's interest in the position, relevant academic leadership experience, and scholarly background; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) the names, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses of five professional references; ( Additional required documents should be uploaded as one PDF to the “other documents” section in the application .);(4) a leadership vision statement of no more than 3 pages detailing your leadership approach, a preliminary vision for the department, and two or three strategic priorities the candidate would explore with the community. Competitive candidates are expected to clearly complement the overall mission of the department and the college. The anticipated start date for this position is August 16, 2027. Priority consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026 . Please direct questions about the position to Senior Associate Dean John M. Shea, Faculty Search Chair, email: jmshea@ufl.edu or Professor “Bala” Balachandar, Faculty Search Co-Chair, email: bala1s@ufl.edu. About the University of Florida and the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering The University of Florida is the flagship institution of the State University System of Florida, a member of the Association of American Universities, and consistently ranked among the nation’s leading public universities. UF is currently ranked as one of the top 10 best public universities, 8th according to the 2026 U.S. News & World Report of Best Colleges and is recognized by Forbes as one of 10 public “New Ivies” for producing exceptional graduates. With 16 colleges, more than 150 research centers and institutes, and over 60,000 undergraduate and graduate students, UF is one of the largest universities in the nation. UF offers broad opportunities for interdisciplinary work across engineering, medicine, agriculture, the sciences, and other fields. In FY2026, University of Florida research spending reached a record $1.34 billion. UF is also home to HiPerGator, the fastest AI supercomputer in higher education. The Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering has over 400 faculty members and combines disciplinary depth with cross-cutting institutes, centers, shared facilities, industry partnerships, and a statewide mission. For more information about college initiatives, visit eng.ufl.edu Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541799/advanced-practice-registered-nurse-cpt-daytona": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Registered Nurse- CPT- Daytona",
      "description": "Advanced Practice Registered Nurse- CPT- Daytona Apply now Job no: 541799 Work type: Staff Part-Time Location: Volusia Categories: Nursing Department: 30090000 - JX-PEDIATRICS-JACKSONVILLE Classification Title: Advanced Practice Registered Nurse- CPT- Daytona Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree with a major in nursing or another health-related area. Licensed as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in accordance with Chapter 464, Florida Statutes. Job Description: As part of the Pediatric Child Protection Team, the Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) is responsible for assisting licensed physicians in providing services for victims of child abuse and neglect. Performs medical/forensic examinations and participates as part of the multidisciplinary team, sharing, interpreting and documenting medical data. This position is located in Daytona Florida and covers Flagler, Putnam, St. Johns and Volusia counties. Reviews daily abuse reports to the Florida Hotline to determine the mandatory referrals for the Department of Children and Families to consult with CPT, per state statute. Determines situations requiring a medical examination or further testing/ hospital services/record reviews and in conjunction with supervisors and medical director. Provides diagnostic evaluations and medical consultations regarding abused and neglected children under the direction of the Medical Director. Takes patient histories, conducts physical examinations, and records the data in the patient’s record; writes progress notes and narrative discharge summaries; prepares patient workups and summaries noting pertinent positive and negative findings. Prepares medical reports. Works in conjunction with CPT satellite offices (via Telemedicine) as the medical provider on record. Assists with providing services to children within their residential county vs. traveling to Daytona if it is determined to be the appropriate medical service for the child. Consults with Case Coordinators, Program Coordinators and participates in Case Reviews and Team Staffings. Refers children exhibiting abnormal findings for additional physician evaluation. Provides physician and pharmacist referrals to patients in need of further medical care and services. Provides depositions and court testimony as required. Maintains inventory and ordering of medical supplies, assisting with recertification of clinic licensing and applications for medical supplies. Contributes to the development, implementation, and expansion of programs and initiatives, Participates in meetings, functions, events, and committees, as well as in a team of interdisciplinary health care providers. Under the direction of the Chief for the Division of Child Protection and Forensic Pediatrics, mentors professionals rotating through the Division, participating in elective rotations to include students, residents, fellows, and newly hired CPT personnel. Assists with and Presents trainings in the community (Family Integrity Program, Department of Children and Families, law enforcement, schools, & community organizations), with professional staff (nursing students, residents, medical students, visiting physicians & guests), and with new organizational personnel. Assists with the annual Conference on Child Maltreatment. Participates on the CPT Statewide quality assurance team: Participates with Medical Record Review, Video Conferencing and training for 1 to 2 CPT Site Visits to Teams outside of Daytona as a medical reviewer. Follow up is required with training & recommendations to establish consistency across Florida in conducting and recording medical information in the CPT electronic medical record. Completes research and publications as directed by the Chief of the Division of Child Protection and Forensic Pediatrics. Maintains knowledge base in the field of child abuse and neglect utilizing current literature, research, and directives from the Medical Director and Division Chief. Expected Salary: $92,000-$100,000 based on .80 FTE Required Qualifications: Master's degree with a major in nursing or another health-related area. Licensed as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse in accordance with Chapter 464, Florida Statutes. Licensure in state of Florida to practice professional nursing and certification as an advanced registered nurse practitioner or specialized pediatrics of family medicine. Children’s Medical Services (CMS) approved physician extender (as defined in the CMS Provider Handbook – Licensed Non-Physician Healthcare Professionals. This position requires a Level II background check. Preferred: Experience in pediatrics, sexual and physical abuse Special Instructions to Applicants: This is a time-limited position. Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. Background Check is Required. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References. University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville: Visit this link to watch the video. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. This position requires a Level II background check. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541801/small-animal-surgery-veterinary-assistant": {
      "title": "Small Animal Surgery Veterinary Assistant",
      "description": "Small Animal Surgery Veterinary Assistant Apply now Job no: 541801 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28311100 - VM-SURGERY Classification Title: Veterinary Assistant (CARE) Classification Minimum Requirements High school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: The Small Animal Surgery Veterinary Assistant at the University of Florida works with veterinarians and veterinary technicians to provide basic patient care and husbandry for patients being seen for orthopedic and soft tissue surgical issues. A typical day includes assisting with examinations, monitoring sedated patients, transporting animals to other areas of the hospital, coordinating with the patient care team to efficiently handle cases, stocking, cleaning, organizing, and assisting with client communication as needed. The ideal candidate has experience with veterinary patient care and is proactive and excited to learn. An individual in this position must possess excellent communication skills and be proactive in determining the needs of the service. They should enjoy learning new things and can quickly adapt to a changing environment. They should possess a good base knowledge of veterinary medicine and maintain a positive attitude in their daily work. They must be able to communicate effectively, demonstrating critical thinking and professionalism. Expected Salary: $15 - 16 /hr Preferred Certified Veterinary Assistant Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a CARE position offering limited benefits, including health insurance and paid time off. When appropriate certifications are achieved, promotional opportunities to a level II title may be available. This position will also become eligible for transition into a TEAMS (staff) salary plan. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, pull, push, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 29 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541803/ops-finance-support": {
      "title": "OPS Finance Support",
      "description": "OPS Finance Support Apply now Job no: 541803 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 63300500 - FS-FIN BUSINESS OFC Classification Title: OPS Student Assistant – Data Analyst- Accounting and Finance Support Classification Minimum Requirements: • Currently enrolled as a student at the University of Florida. • Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word, and Outlook. • Strong analytical, organizational, and attention-to-detail skills. • Ability to work independently and handle confidential information. • Availability to work up to 20 hours per week during business hours (Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM). Job Description: • Maintain and update databases, spreadsheets, and financial and operational records. • Assist with developing, enhancing, and maintaining Power BI dashboards and reports. • Organize, validate, and analyze data to support financial reporting needs. • Assist with maintaining and improving Accounts Payable (AP) and Accounts Receivable (AR) reports. • Monitor and triage the AP mailbox, including organizing and routing invoices. • Perform data entry and attach supporting documents in UF MarketPlace. • Provide additional administrative and reporting support to the Finance team as needed. Expected Salary: $15.00 per hour. Required Qualifications: • Currently enrolled as a student at the University of Florida. • Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, Word, and Outlook. • Strong analytical, organizational, and attention-to-detail skills. • Ability to work independently and handle confidential information. • Availability to work up to 20 hours per week during business hours (Monday–Friday, 8:00 AM–4:30 PM). Preferred: • Pursuing a degree in Computer Science, Data Science, Information Systems, Business Analytics, or a related field. • Experience with database management, data analysis, and reporting. • Knowledge of Power BI and dashboard development. • Advanced SQL and Excel skills, including formulas and pivot tables. • Familiarity with UF systems, including myUFL and UF MarketPlace, is a plus. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No. Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541805/student-account-specialist-i": {
      "title": "Student Account Specialist I",
      "description": "Student Account Specialist I- Apply now Job no: 541805 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 64801000 - FA-UNIVERSITY BURSAR-ADMIN Classification Title: Student Account Specialist I Classification Minimum Requirements: A bachelor's degree, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: This position within the University Bursar’s Office, is part of the Third Party Contracts team. The Third Party Contracts team coordinates and processes student and sponsor contracts/transactions, including Florida Prepaid and Veteran benefits to student accounts. This position assists with the day to day operations of the Third Party Contracts Team, including coordinating documentation requirements from students and sponsors, applying contracts to the student and sponsor accounts, invoicing sponsors, applying payments from sponsors and refunding overpayments. The incumbent in the position will deliver excellent customer service to students and ensure the timely resolution of issues. Expected Salary: $21.50 per hour Preferred: Ability to plan, organize and coordinate files, records, and work assignments. Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with others Ability to work independently and as a team. Ability to utilize problem-solving techniques. Experience in Microsoft Office, including Excel and Word. Ability to determine work priorities, assign work and ensure proper completion of work assignments. Ability to analyze and interpret accounting data Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541808/chair-professor-electrical-computer-engineering": {
      "title": "CHAIR & PROFESSOR, Electrical & Computer Engineering",
      "description": "CHAIR & PROFESSOR, Electrical & Computer Engineering Apply now Job no: 541808 Work type: Faculty Admin Title Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design, Computer Science, Engineering Department: 19050000 - EG-ELECTRICAL - COMPUTER ENG Classification Title: CHAIR & PROFESSOR Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate in electrical engineering, computer engineering, or a closely related field. A distinguished record of scholarly research, education, mentoring, and professional contribution that merits appointment as a tenured full professor at the University of Florida. Evidence of successful leadership in a research-intensive university or comparably complex organization, including building collaborative, high-performing organizational cultures and developing faculty, staff, and emerging leaders. Demonstrated ability to develop and articulate a compelling strategic vision to advance the reputation and ranking of the department by translating that vision into clear priorities, strategic investments and measurable outcomes. Is skilled in the development and expansion of sponsored research programs, including fostering collaborative research and advancing high-impact programs. Excellent communication, judgment, integrity, and relationship-building skills; ability to communicate and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to student success and to a scholarly and working environment where people with varied backgrounds and perspectives can contribute and thrive. Job Description: The Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering at the University of Florida invites nominations and applications for Department Chair of the Electrical & Computer Engineering Department. Reporting to the Dean of the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering, the Chair will provide strategic, intellectual, and administrative leadership for an internationally visible research and education enterprise. The successful candidate will be an accomplished scholar and an effective organizational leader with a strong record of externally funded research who can substantially improve the department’s recognition and ranking, develop a clear vision for international impact and connect the department’s strengths to consequential opportunities for Florida and the world. The selected leader will join the Dean’s leadership team and will be expected to advance both the department and the college, contribute to university priorities, and engage constructively with the state, nation, and profession. HWCOE Electrical and Computer Engineering at Glance More than 1,600 enrolled students and 54 tenure-track faculty members. $34 million in research expenditures in FY2025, with ten institutes or centers led or co-led by ECE faculty. 28 Fellows of the IEEE, AAAS and ACM and 28 Endowed Faculty positions The graduate program is ranked No. 20 among public universities in the 2026 U.S. News rankings. The department’s broad portfolio reaches from artificial intelligence and machine learning, communications, computing, cybersecurity, robotics, hardware security, microelectronics, semiconductor manufacturing, advanced packaging, metrology, to power electronics and connected systems. Leadership charge Strategic and intellectual leadership. Co-create a departmental direction with measurable goals for scholarship, research, education, talent, infrastructure, reputation, entrepreneurship and impact. Balance foundational fields with emerging opportunities in AI, semiconductors, cybersecurity, communications, computing, sensing, autonomy, quantum engineering, and connected systems, and has a high personal research reputation Faculty and staff success. Recruit, mentor, retain, evaluate, and recognize excellent faculty and staff. Build leadership capacity, support early- and mid-career development, and sustain a culture of openness, rigor, intellectual curiosity, and constructive accountability. Research and innovation. Grow high-impact research and sponsored activity; enable large interdisciplinary teams; improve proposal and project support; connect faculty to the institutes and centers; and advance technology transfer, standards, intellectual property, startups, and industry collaboration; raise the department’s external research profile by connecting to major funding agencies. Education and student success. Lead continuous improvement of undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs, including accreditation, curriculum development, laboratory and design experiences, advising, doctoral mentoring, enrollment strategy, student well-being, completion, and career outcomes. External partnerships and advancement. Strengthen relationships with alumni, donors, semiconductor and electronics firms, computing and communications companies, national-security partners, government agencies, professional societies, and Florida’s growing technology ecosystem, and enhance department fundraising capabilities Expected Salary: Commensurate with Education and Experience Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in electrical engineering, computer engineering, or a closely related field. A distinguished record of scholarly research, education, mentoring, and professional contribution that merits appointment as a tenured full professor at the University of Florida. Evidence of successful leadership in a research-intensive university or comparably complex organization, including building collaborative, high-performing organizational cultures and developing faculty, staff, and emerging leaders. Demonstrated ability to develop and articulate a compelling strategic vision to advance the reputation and ranking of the department by translating that vision into clear priorities, strategic investments and measurable outcomes. Is skilled in the development and expansion of sponsored research programs, including fostering collaborative research and advancing high-impact programs. Excellent communication, judgment, integrity, and relationship-building skills; ability to communicate and work effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to student success and to a scholarly and working environment where people with varied backgrounds and perspectives can contribute and thrive. Preferred: Experience recruiting, mentoring, evaluating, and retaining faculty and staff across career stages and appointment types. Experience developing multidisciplinary initiatives, major collaborative proposals, centers, institutes, or other large-scale research activities. Experience building productive industry partnerships, including sponsored research, consortia, or public-private collaborations. Experience using industry engagement to strengthen education, experiential learning, workforce preparation, and research opportunities. The ability to identify emerging funding opportunities and organize faculty and external partners around them. Experience working with College and University leadership and across academic units. Experience in advancement, philanthropy, alumni engagement, or development of external resources. Professional leadership and service in electrical or computer engineering, or a related discipline. Special Instructions to Applicants: The search committee will begin reviewing applications immediately and will continue to receive applications until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted through UFCareers at: https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/listing/ ( Search Job 541808 ). Complete applications must include the following files in PDF format: (1) A cover letter describing the candidate's interest in the position, relevant academic leadership experience, and scholarly background; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) the names, addresses, phone numbers, and email addresses of five professional references; ( Additional required documents should be uploaded as one PDF to the “other documents” section in the application .);(4) a leadership vision statement of no more than 3 pages detailing your leadership approach, a preliminary vision for the department, and two or three strategic priorities the candidate would explore with the community. Competitive candidates are expected to clearly complement the overall mission of the department and the college. The anticipated start date for this position is August 16, 2027. Priority consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026 . Please direct questions about the position to Senior Associate Dean John M. Shea, Faculty Search Chair, email: jmshea@ufl.edu or Professor YK Yoon, Faculty Search Co-Chair, email: ykyoon@ece.ufl.edu About the University of Florida and the Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering The University of Florida is the flagship institution of the State University System of Florida, a member of the Association of American Universities, and consistently ranked among the nation’s leading public universities. UF is currently ranked as one of the top 10 best public universities, 8th according to the 2026 U.S. News & World Report of Best Colleges and is recognized by Forbes as one of 10 public “New Ivies” for producing exceptional graduates. With 16 colleges, more than 150 research centers and institutes, and over 60,000 undergraduate and graduate students, UF is one of the largest universities in the nation. UF offers broad opportunities for interdisciplinary work across engineering, medicine, agriculture, the sciences, and other fields. In FY2026, University of Florida research spending reached a record $1.34 billion. UF is also home to HiPerGator, the fastest AI supercomputer in higher education. The Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering has over 400 faculty members and combines disciplinary depth with cross-cutting institutes, centers, shared facilities, industry partnerships, and a statewide mission. For more information about college initiatives, visit eng.ufl.edu Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 22 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540620/large-animal-veterinary-treatment-technician-i-and-ii-care": {
      "title": "Large Animal Veterinary Treatment Technician I and II (CARE)",
      "description": "Large Animal Veterinary Treatment Technician I and II (CARE) Apply now Job no: 540620 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Veteran's Preference Eligible, Veterinary Medicine/Animal Care Department: 28321000 - VM-HOSPITAL Classification Title: Large Animal Veterinary Treatment Technician I and II Classification Minimum Requirements: Technician I - High school diploma or equivalent and two years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses or one year of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses in a veterinary academic teaching hospital. Technician II - High school diploma or equivalent; four years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses or two years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses in a veterinary academic teaching hospital; and certification or licensure as a Veterinary Technician. Job Description: At the University of Florida, we place a high value on the role our nurses play in helping clinicians train the next generation of veterinary students. As a member of our nursing staff, you will play an instrumental role in instructing veterinary students in technical skills and performing medical treatments and procedures as directed by our veterinarians. In addition to providing exceptional facilities for providing patient care. As an academic teaching hospital, we are fortunate to have access to the latest innovations in veterinary healthcare. Individuals should genuinely care about people and animals, be outgoing, enthusiastic and a team player. This is a CARE full-time benefited position that includes PTO and retirement, retention bonus eligibility and opportunity for Vet Tech School tuition assistance and paid CE. We also offer excellent health insurance with HMO and PPO options. Additionally, there are generous shift differentials in addition to base rate of pay. Typically schedules consist of working five 8-hour shifts or four 10-hour shifts per work week. We are currently hiring for individuals to work Evening Shift. Assigned days may vary Sunday through Saturday, weekends and holidays included. However, reassignment to a different primary shift (Day shift, Evening Shift or Night Shift), rotating shifts, split shifts, extended shifts and paid “on-call duty” may be required and assigned depending on hospital needs. This individual is considered essential personnel which may include reporting to work during Main Campus closures. Expected Salary: $18-25/hr based on experience, certification & shift Required Qualifications Technician I - High school diploma or equivalent and two years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses or one year of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses in a veterinary academic teaching hospital. Technician II - High school diploma or equivalent; four years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses or two years of experience loading, unloading, restraining, handling and treating horses in a veterinary academic teaching hospital; and certification or licensure as a Veterinary Technician. Preferred: Previous experience as a veterinary technician in a large animal practice. Certification or licensure as a veterinary technician is preferred, but not required. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a CARE position offering limited benefits, including health insurance and paid time off. When appropriate certifications are achieved, promotional opportunities to a level II title may be available. This position will also become eligible for transition into a TEAMS (staff) salary plan. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Health Assessment Required: Yes; Must be able to lift a minimum of 40 lbs, bend, kneel, push, pull, twist and stand for an extended period of time. Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540756/academic-program-specialist-i-medical-education": {
      "title": "Academic Program Specialist I - Medical Education",
      "description": "Academic Program Specialist I - Medical Education Apply now Job no: 540756 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 29010805 - MD-MEDICAL EDUCATION Classification Title: Academic Program Specialist I Job Description: The Academic Program Specialist I position supports the vision and strategy of assigned academic programs by coordinating and managing courses, implementing program policies and procedures, providing advanced academic and administrative support, and partnering with faculty, students, and stakeholders to ensure high‑quality program delivery. The role oversees program processes, contributes to continuous improvement, and supervises and trains Academic Assistant IIIs while supporting curriculum processes, documentation standards, and policy implementation across assigned programs. About this role: Academic and Program Administration Responsibilities: Manage effective delivery of assigned courses by coordinating schedules, instructional activities, assessments, and course materials while maintaining accurate, up-to-date content in the learning management system and related academic resources. Liaise with faculty, students, and internal/external stakeholders to facilitate course implementation, resolve complex issues, and ensure smooth program operations. Develop, implement, and maintain program processes, guidance documentation, policies, and communication procedures to strengthen compliance, consistency, and quality improvement. Monitor program activities for alignment with academic policies, objectives, and administrative requirements, identifying areas needing adjustment or clariﬁcation. Coordinate course and program evaluation activities by collecting, organizing, reviewing, and distributing data and feedback to faculty and program leadership. Provide high-level support to course directors, faculty, and leadership. Student Support and Educational Services: Guide students regarding course expectations, requirements, and academic processes. Track completion of course activities, requirements, and evaluations, and ﬁnalize grades. Maintain records in compliance with FERPA, HIPAA, and institutional guidelines. Collaboration and Stakeholder Engagement Activities: Communicate regularly with faculty, staff, and partners to support program operations. Coordinate logistics for academic activities, meetings, and events involving internal and external partners. Support course operations by coordinating communications, documentation, and processes related to faculty or preceptor participation, in collaboration with program leadership. Curriculum and Instructional Support: Support the development, editing, and periodic updating of program documents, syllabi, templates, and academic or administrative resources. Assist faculty with curriculum‑related tasks, content preparation, or instructional coordination as needed. Contribute to curriculum planning and improvement efforts by providing feedback, supporting instructional design needs, and helping ensure alignment between course activities and program objectives. Support small‑group instructional activities and simulations by coordinating facilitator logistics, maintaining group rosters, preparing materials, and ensuring alignment with curriculum objectives. Supervision and Training: Supervise and train an Academic Assistant III, providing guidance, task oversight, and ongoing skill development to support team performance and program needs. Instruct other Academic Assistant IIIs within the division as needed regarding tasks and/or skills speciﬁc to their area of expertise. About the College of Medicine: The University of Florida's College of Medicine is committed to advancing health through education, research, and patient care. With a focus on innovation and excellence, the college prepares future healthcare leaders through a rigorous curriculum that combines basic sciences with hands-on clinical experience. The College of Medicine emphasizes interdisciplinary collaboration and community engagement, fostering and environment where students, faculty, and staff work together to improve healthcare outcomes. The College is home to cutting-edge research initiatives and state-of-the-art facilities, providing an exceptional training ground for aspiring medical professionals. Dedicated to enhancing health care, the College of Medicine plays an impactful role in shaping the future of medicine. For more information about the College of Medicine and its programs, visit College of Medicine . We Offer Exceptional Benefits Low-cost State Health Plans: Medical, Dental, and Vision Insurance Life and Disability Insurance Generous Retirement Options to secure your future Comprehensive Paid Time Off Packages with 10+ paid holidays, paid family, sick and vacation leave Exceptional Personal and Professional Development Opportunities: Access to UF Training & Organizational Development programs, leadership development, LinkedIn Learning, and more Tuition Assistance through the UF Employee Education Program Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer Learn more about what we have to offer here ! Expected Salary: $50,000 - $52,000 Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree and two years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will possess: Master’s degree in education, academic administration, health sciences, or a related ﬁeld. Experience in higher education administration, academic program coordination, or student services. Background managing contracts/affiliation agreements. Experience preparing academic documents or guiding faculty and students. Experience supporting course management, curriculum processes, or evaluation/reporting activities. Proﬁciency with Microsoft Office Suite and experience using academic systems such as Canvas, PeopleSoft, Workday, or similar tools. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple complex academic priorities in fast‑paced, deadline‑driven environments, using strong problem‑solving and critical‑thinking skills to identify issues, evaluate options, and recommend data‑informed solutions within established academic policies. Experience in making independent procedural decisions and escalating higher‑level matters appropriately, with proven ﬂexibility and adaptability in responding to shifting program needs, unexpected issues, and rapid curricular changes. Commitment to continuous learning, quickly mastering new systems and processes, applying new knowledge to improve operations, and effectively using and supporting others in advanced academic technologies and office tools. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applications are still under consideration and need not apply. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541705/clinical-research-analyst-i": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Analyst I",
      "description": "Clinical Research Analyst I Apply now Job no: 541705 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Grant or Research Administration, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 30010100 - JX-DEAN-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Clinical Research Analyst I Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Clinical Research Office (CRO) in the Office of Research Affairs (ORA), Dean’s Administration, College of Medicine–Jacksonville, is seeking a Clinical Research Analyst I to support clinical trial operations and protocol management within the University of Florida’s Clinical Trials Management System (CTMS). This position assists with the development, review, and maintenance of clinical research protocols and related documentation to ensure compliance with institutional policies, sponsor requirements, and applicable regulatory standards. The analyst will support the implementation and management of research workflows within the CTMS while providing quality review and operational support for research projects conducted across the College of Medicine–Jacksonville. This role works collaboratively with investigators, research coordinators, administrators, and institutional stakeholders to facilitate accurate protocol setup, billing compliance reviews, and research calendar and budget development. The Clinical Research Analyst I provides technical support and guidance to study teams regarding the use of the CTMS and institutional processes, assists with coverage analysis activities, and supports workflow management to ensure timely and accurate completion of assigned tasks. The position contributes to maintaining data integrity, operational efficiency, and regulatory compliance for the clinical research portfolio within the CRO. Assist with protocol coverage analyses within the Clinical Trials Management System (CTMS). Support the completion and review of Medicare Coverage Analyses (MCAs) in collaboration with team members. Review vendor-provided MCAs and assist with validation and completion to ensure alignment with institutional coverage analysis standards. Manage coverage analysis requests in a timely and professional manner. Intake and Research Compliance Assessments, Complete project intake submission assessments for new clinical research studies. Assist with research billing compliance reviews, and ensure required documentation is complete and accurate. Review study-related documents to verify adherence to institutional guidelines and regulatory requirements. Prepare Financial Language Assessments (FLAs) for informed consent forms when applicable. Manage assigned protocol portfolio within the CTMS and maintain accurate protocol records. Build and maintain billing grids and manage Office of Clinical Research workflows within the CTMS. Serve as a resource for study teams navigating the CTMS and assist with troubleshooting or record corrections. Monitor workflow timelines and ensure tasks are completed in accordance with established procedures. Build sponsor-paid protocol calendars and budgets within the CTMS application. Coordinate with study teams, fiscal teams, and coverage analysis staff to ensure accuracy and completeness. Submit and respond to vendor queries and perform quality assurance review of calendars and budgets developed through the vendor system. Make edits and updates as necessary throughout the calendar and budget development process. Serve as a liaison between investigators, study teams, administrators, and institutional offices. Provide technical assistance and guidance to departmental staff and research personnel on sponsor policies and institutional requirements. Assist with identifying system issues and communicating defects or workflow concerns to CTMS management or vendor representatives. Participate in testing and validation of the CTMS during system upgrades and implementation of new functionality. Expected Salary: $53,000-$60,000 Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: The ideal candidate will possess: One year of experience in clinical research administration and/or financial management in an academic/medical setting. Familiarity with the OnCore CTMS by Advarra or similar clinical trial management software Ability to balance customer service and research compliance. Ability to organize and work effectively, prioritize, be flexible, and stay on task in a high-paced, high-volume professional environment. Skilled in problem-solving techniques, critical thinking, and creativity Strong time management, organizational, documentation, attention to detail, and task follow-up skills. Experience using Microsoft Office Applications. Special Instructions to Applicants: This is a time-limited position. Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. Background Check is Required. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References. University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville: Visit this link to watch the video. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541710/clinical-research-coordinator-ii": {
      "title": "Clinical Research Coordinator II",
      "description": "Clinical Research Coordinator II Apply now Job no: 541710 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Grant or Research Administration, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 30010100 - JX-DEAN-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Clinical Research Coordinator II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The Clinical Research Office (CRO) in the Office of Research Affairs (ORA), Dean’s administration, College of Medicine-Jacksonville is looking for a Clinical Research Coordinator II to assist coordinating, engaging and performing research and regulatory functions for clinical research studies. The CRC II will screen and consent patients in different clinics and will conduct research visits as required by the research protocols. He/she will perform functions necessary for successful completion of all protocols including but not limited to required visits/procedures such as vital signs, phlebotomy, diagnostic tests, dispensing of investigational product, scheduling, drug accountability/reconciliation and organizational tasks, where appropriate and as delegated by the investigator, in accordance with protocol/sponsor requirements. This position will work on clinical research studies across many different disciplines, interacting with numerous research teams from the inception of a clinical trial though the close out. Work independently and proactively to coordinate all necessary activities required to set up and monitor a study, completing accurate study status reports and maintaining study documentation. Submission of protocol, consent documents for IRB approval and assist in preparing regulatory submissions as requested Work at UF research locations prescreening, consenting and enrolling participants in research studies. Conduct study visits and follow ups including functions necessary for successful completion of all protocol required visits/procedures such as vital signs, phlebotomy, diagnostic tests, dispensing of investigational product, scheduling, drug accountability/reconciliation and organizational tasks as needed. Help Investigators with proposal development, progress reports, budget creation, regulatory paperwork and study files. Expected Salary: $55,000-$65,000 Preferred: Experience in phlebotomy and clinical research. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to prioritize and effectively communicate verbally and in writing. Coordinates multiple tasks and work independently and productively in a fast paced, deadline-oriented environment. Masters degree or an allied health professional degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Proficiency in data management and superior organization skills. Integrity, careful attention to detail; ability to maintain confidentiality, demonstrate professionalism and respect for subjects’ rights and individual needs; willing to learn and maintain skills in accordance with HIPAA regulations and Good Clinical Practice guidelines. Special Instructions to Applicants: This is a time-limited position. Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. Background Check is Required. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References. University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville: Visit this link to watch the video. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541745/administrative-assistant-ii-uf-department-of-health-education-and-behavior": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II - UF Department of Health Education and Behavior",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II - UF Department of Health Education and Behavior Apply now Job no: 541745 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible Department: 26050100 - HH-HEB-ADMINISTRATION Classification Title: Administrative Assistant II Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: This position supports the faculty, students and staff in the operation of all purchasing and travel transactions in the UF Department of Health Education and Behavior; serves as liaison with vendors, guests and the UF Disbursements, Procurement and Travel offices; assists with processing property and assets for the department and consults with the Department Chair and Office Manager regarding policies and procedures for p-cards, purchasing, travel and other department operations; assists with events and other administrative functions that support the department’s daily operations. This position requires understanding of the complexity of UF foundation, state-appropriated, auxiliary, and research funding and exercising judgment in interpreting and executing relevant state and university policies and procedures to ensure responsible fiscal practices and an organized, cooperative work environment. This position reports to the department Office Manager (Administrative Specialist II). Purchasing Administers all purchasing for the department. This includes assembling and maintaining auditable fiscal back-up and documents, reconciling p-cards within the university’s required timeframe, working directly with new vendors on completing necessary forms for inclusion in UF’s vendor file, initiating purchase orders, collecting packing slips, reviewing invoices for accuracy and obtaining budget approval from the office manager prior to processing payments. Acts as liaison for the department in purchasing transactions with the university and outside vendors. Collects data in order to plan for upcoming budgetary needs. Provides and interprets state contracts and use of state-certified minority businesses for controlled purchases and keeps abreast of UF Procurement rules and regulations. Reviews invoices for accuracy and ensures corrective action is taken in a timely manner. Initiates office supply orders and purchases for department meetings and events. Initiates work order requests for equipment and space service and repair. Posts p-card voucher numbers into accounting spreadsheets. Assists college grant administrators with processing payments and ensuring charges are allowable. Travel Coordinates the processing of all travel authorizations and expense reimbursements for the department. Maintains auditable back-up documentation, enters travel authorizations for foreign and domestic travel into PeopleSoft prior to departure to secure approvals; enters all expense reimbursement requests in a timely manner and verifies that all reimbursements are processed accurately. This requires the incumbent to be knowledgeable and current in UF’s travel policies and procedures. Educates travelers prior to departure and assists with travel arrangements (e.g., for job candidates). Administrative Office Support and Events Assists with administrative functions that support the department’s daily operations including but not limited to: providing front office coverage, greeting internal and external visitors, students, vendors, etc., answering/routing phone calls, responding to inquiries, taking messages, receiving and distributing packages and mail, running on- and off- campus errands, maintaining office supply inventory, assists with the planning, coordination, and execution of departmental meetings, seminars, and events conducted on a weekly, monthly, and annual basis including the Coffee & Conversation series, Brown Bag Seminars, HEB Spring Awards Ceremony, DK Stanley Day, and other department-sponsored programs and activities. Clerical/secretarial functions (copying, faxing, scanning) for the purpose of supporting office operations. Monthly Reconciliation, Deposits, and Journal Entries Enters payroll, expenditure, budget transfer, and revenue actuals into HEB Ledger files. Assists the Office Manager with monthly reconciliations and correctional expense transfer entries. Processes Deposits and Journal Entries: ONL, E2E and E2Rs as directed by the Office Manager. Property/Asset Management and Records Retention Assists the Office Manager with tracking, processing, distributing and surveying property and assets. Maintains an accurate accounting of the department’s software inventory. Serves as the department’s records retention coordinator. Works with UF Records Management to establish retention schedules for academic, personnel, and fiscal records. Submits requests for destruction. Retains and destroys administrative records, pursuant to Florida Administrative Code and as coordinated with other administrative staff. Maintains work/task-related files so that required information can be retrieved by incumbent and other administrative staff. Other Completes other duties as assigned by the Office Manager and/or Department Chair. Will attend all on campus meetings as needed and will keep abreast of all required trainings. Work Schedule Monday – Friday from 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Overtime may be required during peak fiscal periods, such as the end of the fiscal year, or when the department is hosting a large event during non-business hours. Expected Salary: $24.90 - $26.34/hr, commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: •High school diploma or equivalent and four years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: • UF fiscal experience; Knowledgeable of University policies and procedures for procurement, accounts payables, and travel • Excellent time management skills in order to manage a wide variety of tasks that comprise the average workday, skills in effectively communicating with a diverse group of people • Ability to work independently and in a group setting, problem solving, able to take complex and unrelated information and organize it into workable terms • Deadline-oriented with excellent organizational skills Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered for this position, you must upload your cover letter, resume, and contact information for three (3) professional references. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541751/clin-astasofull-prof": {
      "title": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF",
      "description": "CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROF Apply now Job no: 541751 Work type: Non-Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Medicine/Physicians Department: 29080100 - MD-PATHOLOGY-GENERAL Classification Title: CLIN AST/ASO/FULL PROFESSOR Classification Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have an M.D. or D.O. degree, board certification in Anatomic Pathology or AP/CP, and possess or be eligible for a Florida Medical license. Subspecialty fellowship training or extensive experience in hematopathology is also required. Job Description: The Department of Pathology, Immunology and Laboratory Medicine at the University of Florida College of Medicine, Gainesville, FL, invites applications for an academic hematopathologist. Primary responsibilities will involve service and clinical teaching in hematopathology and flow cytometry. Practice in other pathology areas of interest can be supported. The successful applicant will contribute to medical student, resident and fellowship training in accredited programs within Pathology. Scholarly study and investigation in the applicant's area of interest is expected. The UFHealth System presents a rich diversity of inpatient and outpatient clinical material. Expected Salary: Salary is Commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Applicants must have an M.D. or D.O. degree, board certification in Anatomic Pathology or AP/CP, and possess or be eligible for a Florida Medical license. Subspecialty fellowship training or extensive experience in hematopathology is also required. Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Applicants should apply online@jobs.uf.edu, and include a curriculum vitae, a letter outlining interests, and three letters of reference. The letters may also be sent directly to Dr. Robert Seifert ( rseifert@ufl.edu ), Search Committee Chair, Department of Pathology, Immunology and Laboratory Medicine, University of Florida College of Medicine, and copy Stacey Oliver (oliversl@ufl.edu). Final candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered \"official\" if a designation of \"Issued to Student\" is visible. Degrees earned from an institution outside the U.S. must be evaluated by a credentialing service approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES): http://naces.org/ . The Search Committee will accept applications until the position is filled. Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis by the committee. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541754/admissions-officer-i-applicant-services": {
      "title": "Admissions Officer I (Applicant Services)",
      "description": "Admissions Officer I (Applicant Services) Apply now Job no: 541754 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 03020000 - EM-OFFICE OF ADMISSIONS Classification Title: Admissions Officer I Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The University of Florida is looking for an Admissions Officer I to support the processing and management of undergraduate, graduate, professional, certificate, online, and distance education applications within the Office of Admissions. In this role, you will review applications and supporting credentials, determine residency classifications for tuition purposes, troubleshoot admissions data across multiple systems, and serve as a primary point of contact for applicants and academic departments. Key responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Application Processing & Review Review and process undergraduate, graduate, professional, certificate, online, and distance education applications. Evaluate applications and supporting credentials to ensure completeness and accuracy. Determine residency classifications for tuition purposes in accordance with state regulations. Maintain knowledge of admission requirements, degree programs, majors, and applicant types. Review and process departmental requests related to application updates. Exercise independent judgment to prepare applications for admission decisions. Assist in cross-training admissions staff on application processing procedures. Applicant Support Serve as a primary point of contact for applicants, academic departments, and campus partners. Respond to inquiries via phone, email, Salesforce, and other communication channels. Advise applicants regarding admission requirements and outstanding application materials. Support OneStop staff with escalated admissions-related inquiries. Participate in call campaigns, Q&A sessions, and other student engagement initiatives. Provide high-quality customer service through extensive inbound and outbound communications. Data Management Manage admissions and application data within Slate and Campus Solutions. Troubleshoot data discrepancies and resolve admissions record issues across systems. Monitor and support data integration processes between Slate and the student information system. Process Salesforce cases and departmental requests related to admissions records. Create and maintain organization records and corresponding school data. Ensure institutional information remains accurate, current, and synchronized across systems. Other Duties Finalize admitted student applications in preparation for registration. Review credentials, manage admissions holds, and evaluate requests for hold deferrals. Collaborate with departments and Enrollment Management partners to support operational goals. Participate in committees, cross-functional teams, and divisional initiatives. Assist with development of reference materials, training resources, and process documentation. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Expected Salary: $43,888 annually In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer For more information on benefits, please visit UFHR Benefits and Rewards (ufl.edu) Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Strong analytical skills with the ability to compile, organize, review, and interpret complex information while maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Strong organizational skills with the ability to prioritize, coordinate, and complete multiple work assignments and training activities in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with various audiences. Demonstrated ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with colleagues, applicants, and stakeholders. Experience providing exceptional customer service in a high-volume, service-oriented environment. Experience working with student information systems, CRM platforms, or related database applications; experience with Slate and/or PeopleSoft Campus Solutions preferred. Special Instructions to Applicants: Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541761/health-support-technician-i-peds-id": {
      "title": "Health Support Technician I- Peds ID",
      "description": "Health Support Technician I- Peds ID Apply now Job no: 541761 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Jacksonville Campus Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Counseling/Community Outreach/Social Work, Health Care Administration/Support Department: 30090000 - JX-PEDIATRICS-JACKSONVILLE Classification Title: Health Support Technician I- Peds ID Classification Minimum Requirements: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Job Description: The Tester works in a team setting to provide HIV testing and available for outreach prevention services in the community. The Tester will assist in program planning and implementation including Community Advisory Board (CAB) and support groups. Locates meeting places for testing by visiting churches, community agencies, and other organizations. Expected Salary: $18-$21/hr Required Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalent and one year of relevant experience. Appropriate college coursework or vocational/technical training may substitute at an equivalent rate for the required experience. Valid Florida drivers’ license required. Training certificate in HIV 101 preferred, and 500/501, certified HIV Tester required within first 90 days of employment.. Preferred: At least 1-2 years’ experience with HIV population preferred, either via work environment or participation in volunteer activities. Basic computer proficiency. Firsthand knowledge of living with HIV/AIDS. Certified HIV Tester- completed 500/501 courses. Special Instructions to Applicants: This is a time-limited position. Time limited positions are based on circumstances, such as funding sources, which control the length of time for which the position is available. Background Check is Required. To be considered you must upload your Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and contact information for 3 References. University of Florida College of Medicine – Jacksonville: Visit this link to watch the video. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Work Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org/ . The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under the Florida Sunshine and Public Records laws. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call (352) 392-2HRS or the Florida Relay System at (800) 955-8771 (TDD). Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. Searches are conducted in accordance with Florida's Sunshine Law. Health Assessment Required: yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 03 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541769/postdoctoral-associate-pasture-mealybug-management-in-sugarcane": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate - Pasture Mealybug Management in Sugarcane",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate - Pasture Mealybug Management in Sugarcane Apply now Job no: 541769 Work type: Post Doc Associate Location: Palm Beach Categories: Biology/Life Science, Agricultural Sciences Department: 60740000 - AG-EREC-BELLE GLADE Classification Title: Postdoc Aso Classification Minimum Requirements: The appointee shall have received the doctorate in a field appropriate to the assigned duties and responsibilities. Job Description: The Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences is creating an environment that affirms community across all dimensions. If an accommodation due to a disability is needed to apply for this position, please call 352-392-2477 or the Florida Relay System at 800-955-8771 (TDD) or visit Accessibility at UF . The University of Florida's Everglades Research and Education Center (EREC) in Belle Glade, Florida, invites applications for a USDA-funded Postdoctoral Research Associate position focused on the integrated pest management of sugarcane insects. The successful candidate will lead research investigating management tactics for the invasive pasture mealybug, Heliococcus novovillei , a newly established pest threatening Florida sugarcane. Research activities will include both field experiments and greenhouse bioassays. The successful candidate will lead three primary objectives: Determine relationships among pasture mealybug density, leaf yellowing, and sugar yields Evaluate the efficacy of chemical control strategies for pasture mealybug management Screen commercially relevant sugarcane cultivars for resistance or tolerance to pasture mealybug. The postdoctoral researcher will be expected to work independently while collaborating with faculty, staff, graduate students, industry stakeholders, and Extension personnel. Responsibilities include designing and conducting experiments, collecting and analyzing data, publishing results in peer-reviewed journals, presenting findings at scientific and stakeholder meetings, and supervising technical personnel. The position provides extensive opportunities to collaborate with Florida sugarcane growers, industry representatives, and Extension personnel to develop practical management solutions. This is a full-time, two-year position funded through external grants. Continued employment beyond the initial appointment may be possible contingent upon performance and funding availability. The anticipated start date is January 1, 2027, although an earlier start date may be accommodated. The University of Florida is a Land-Grant, Sea-Grant, and Space-Grant institution, encompassing virtually all academic and professional disciplines, with an enrollment of more than 56,000 students. UF is a member of The Association of American Universities. The Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences includes the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences , the Florida Agricultural Experiment Station , the Florida Cooperative Extension Service , the College of Veterinary Medicine , the Florida Sea Grant program, and encompasses 16 on-campus academic departments and schools, 12 Research and Educational Centers (REC) located throughout the state, 6 Research sites/demonstration units administered by RECs or academic departments, and Florida Cooperative Extension Service offices in all 67 counties (counties operate and maintain). The School of Natural Resources and Environment is an interdisciplinary unit housed in IFAS and managed by several colleges on campus. UF/IFAS employs nearly 4,500 people, which includes approximately 990 salaried faculty and 1,400 permanent support personnel located in Gainesville and throughout the state. IFAS, one of the nation’s largest agricultural and natural resources research and education organizations, is administered by a Vice President and four deans: the Dean of the College of Agricultural and Life Sciences, the Dean for Extension and Director of the Florida Cooperative Extension Service, the Dean for Research and Director of the Florida Agricultural Experiment Station, and the Dean for the College of Veterinary Medicine. UF/IFAS also engages in cooperative work with Florida A&M University in Tallahassee. Expected Salary: Commensurate with Experience and Education Required Qualifications: Ph.D. (foreign equivalent acceptable) in Entomology, Crop Protection, Agronomy, Plant Science, or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated experience in experimental design, statistical analysis, and scientific writing. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary research team. Valid driver's license. Candidates must be supportive of the mission of the Land-Grant system. Candidates must also have a commitment to UF core values. Preferred: Integrated pest management field studies. Insecticide efficacy studies. Plant-insect interactions. Field and greenhouse research methodologies. Supervision of research staff and students. Applicants should be willing and able to perform field work under South Florida environmental conditions. Special Instructions to Applicants: Individuals wishing to apply should go online to Careers at UF by 11:55 PM (ET) of the closing date and submit: Cover letter describing research experience and career goals Curriculum vitae Contact information (including email addresses) for 3 professional references Selected candidate will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned from an education institution outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by National Association of Credential Evaluation Services (NACES) . Hiring is contingent upon eligibility to work in the US. The University of Florida is a public institution and subject to all requirements under Florida Sunshine and Public Record laws. The University and greater Gainesville community enjoy a variety of cultural events, restaurants, year-round outdoor recreational activities, and social opportunities. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 02 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541770/accountant-ii": {
      "title": "Accountant II",
      "description": "Accountant II Apply now Job no: 541770 Work type: Staff Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 57201000 - FSG-MANAGEMENT Classification Title: Accountant II Classification Minimum Requirements Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: The Accountant II will provide fiscal and grant management oversight for the Return Em Right Program, funded by the NOAA Restoration Center, to promote sustainable reef-fish angling. The position will reside within Florida Sea Grant and perform standard accounting duties, which include audit, reconciliation, budget creation, and financial reporting. This will also include grant-related functions, including developing and generating accounting reports that document funding status and expenditures to support program functions, including personnel, contracting consultants, programming activities, and sub-awardees. Other responsibilities include advising on program compliance with fiscal and grant requirements. This is not an entry-level position. Working knowledge of UF fiscal and grants management systems and operations is required. This is a .50 FTE position. Program & Grant Administration (40%): Oversee administrative operations of the Return Em Right. These operations include monitoring award spending and performing routine grant functions, including investigating and analyzing billing or other accounting errors and collaborating with relevant departments to correct them. Financial Ledger & Contract Reporting (25%): Maintains general or subsidiary account ledgers and administers the disbursement and monitoring of funds to sub-awardees and contractors, including purchasing of merchandise and processing grant modifications and new awards. Compliance, Audit & Reporting (15%): Conduct internal audits of program expenditures and generate monthly spending and grant status reports, including recommending policies and procedures. Strategic Budget Collaboration (10%): Collaborate with leadership in planning, coordinating, and implementing the budget. HR & Personnel Operations (5%): Provide direction as needed with the hiring and matriculation of staff and support human resources (HR) functions in collaboration with Florida Sea Grant HR and fiscal operations staff, including effort reporting and salary determination. Other 5% Expected Salary: $31,320 - $41,760 annually Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. A valid driver's license is required. Preferred Master’s degree in an appropriate discipline (finance, accounting, mathematics). Extensive knowledge of UF accounting, fiscal, and grants management systems and aptitude for learning new systems (Workflow). Strong ability to communicate complex fiscal and grants management processes and accounting outputs to project investigators and the funding agency. MUST be current UF employee. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must be a current UF employee and will need to upload your cover letter, resume and list of references. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 11 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541773/ops-agricultural-assistant": {
      "title": "OPS Agricultural Assistant",
      "description": "OPS Agricultural Assistant Apply now Job no: 541773 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Alachua Categories: Agriculture Operations Department: 60092000 - AG-DAIRY RESEARCH UNIT Classification Title: OPS Classification Minimum Requirements: None Job Description: The Department of Animal Sciences Dairy Research Unit is seeking an OPS Agricultural Assistant. This position is involved in various aspects of the dairy operations but will primarily focus on assisting with milking, cleaning, livestock handling and health and reproductive observations of animals at the facility. This position will cover the night shift milking at the dairy which begins at 5:00 pm and ends at 1:30 AM with a 00:30 h shift interval. The position may at times require flexible hours. The individual must have the capacity to assist all employees in a consistent professional manner. Duties and responsibilities include but are not limited to: MILKING OPERATIONS Bring cows from pen to milking parlor according to farm procedure. Check pens and start the milking system, milk cooling, refrigeration, washing and feed system. Attached machines after appropriate udder hygiene. Remove cups from cows following the standard operating procedures (SOP). Prepare and apply teat disinfectant for use according to SOP. Oversee the movement of cows from the dairy. Identify cows with clinical mastitis, teat damage, lameness, and other illnesses. Follow protocols for the treatment and recording of the condition. At the completion of milking, follow the procedures for plant cleaning and the shutdown process. Prepare the dairy in readiness for the next milking according to the set guidelines. Identify and correct problems in the machine function and operation as they arise. Identify and correct unsafe and unacceptable milking practices. DAIRY OPERATIONS Assures cows have adequate clean drinking water and feed available. Assures clean stalls with adequate bedding. Cleans barns and flush lanes assigned by farm supervisor. Assists with maintaining grounds, equipment and facilities. REPLACEMENTS Assist with care for newborn calves, including occasional feeding of calves, providing clean bedding, clean water, and supportive care. Normal Work Schedule: Tuesday through Saturday 5:00PM-1:30AM Expected Salary: $17 - $19 per hour Required Qualifications: None Preferred: Demonstrated effective communication and collaborations skills. Strong work ethic. Dairy animal care experience. Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This is a time-limited position. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541777/assistant-director-marketingdepartment-of-neurosurgerypreston-a-wells-jr-center": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Marketing-Department of Neurosurgery-Preston A Wells Jr Center",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Marketing-Department of Neurosurgery-Preston A Wells Jr Center Apply now Job no: 541777 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Executive/Director/Management Department: 29190000 - MD-NEUROLOGICAL SURGERY Classification Title: Assistant Director, Marketing Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience or a bachelor's degree in appropriate areas of specialization and four years of relevant experience. Job Description: Marketing Strategy and Implementation Under the direction of the UF Health AVP for Marketing and the Wells Brain Tumor Center Co-Directors to support the Preston A. Wells Jr. Center for Brain Tumor Therapy to address marketing and growth needs, with particular focus on: Directing consumer-oriented marketing campaigns for the Preston A. Wells Center for Brain Tumor Therapy. Leading efforts to ensure alignment of activities with overall Department of Neurosurgery and UF Health marketing efforts to ensure consistency in messaging, brand, and quality and avoiding unnecessary redundancy. Leading the planning and execution of community outreach and education activities related to brain tumor education and maximizing participation with Wellness University, community walks/runs and other activities as needed. Coordinating the development and optimization of web content to elevate and enhance visibility on search engines and across the web. Implements provider-focused marketing initiatives in support of reputation and referral growth, including: Generating new faculty bios for educational and research related promotions, conference participation and regional and national reputation activities. Developing newsletters and broadcast emails. Directing the creation and distribution of podcasts, videos and other multimedia content Creating content to promote clinical trial participation, research advances and specialty care advances Leads the development, implementation and evaluation of marketing and communications initiatives with input from Communications and Marketing leaders, Center leadership, faculty and staff. Drives, in collaboration with UF Health Marketing & Communications leadership and with the Wells Brain Tumor Center co-directors, the process to develop and direct a comprehensive marketing strategy for the Preston A. Wells Center that aligns with organizational strategic priorities Meets with departmental and service leaders to determine marketing needs and priorities. Collaborates with marketing and communications leadership to set marketing goals, develop and support the implementation of marketing strategies and establish growth goals to drive market share. Prepares and presents annual strategy and tactical plans to departmental and administrative leaders on fiscal year goals, strategies, objectives and tactics. Guides communications plans in support of residency, research and CME efforts. Leads a coordinated approach to marketing and advertising efforts; collaborates as necessary with UF Health colleagues to implement approved projects. Champions regular community education opportunities to cultivate potential patients and promote awareness of departmental services. Oversees establishment and integrity of the brand; assures consistent usage for UF Health and the University of Florida, where applicable, in alignment with established brand standards. Publishing and Health/Science Communications Writes, edits and/or proofreads all promotional projects, such as advertisements, newsletters, brochures, collateral material, video or television scripts or web content. Oversee the development of core narratives and storytelling strategies that elevate the center’s emphasis on academic excellence, research impact, clinical innovation and community engagement. Engages UF Health creative services colleagues or external vendors to develop design for each project and coordinate production. Works with photographers, videographers, freelancers, illustrators and social media managers as necessary to develop high-quality content for the Wells Brain Tumor Center. Responsible for ensuring a proactive editorial calendar for the creation and posting of engaging social media content across departmental and organizational social media channels. Provides content for use across pertinent UF Health and UF web pages and social accounts. Responsible for consistent application of university and UF Health brand standards. Works with UF College of Medicine, UF Health Cancer Institute, McKnight Brain Institute, UF Clinical and Translational Science Institute, and UF Health Marketing & Communications leads to highlight and disseminate institutional, regional, and national awareness of innovative discoveries and achievements of the faculty, trainees, and staff at the Preston A. Wells, Jr. Center for Brain Tumor Therapy at UF Health. Marketing Planning & Reporting Prioritizes marketing and communications investments and develops and presents annual marketing plans and budgets. Works with marketing and communications leaders to establish resourcing for proposed projects and initiatives. Regularly reports on progress. Responsible for monthly reporting on the status of projects for marketing and departmental leadership. Responsible for developing and presenting KPI performance and return on investment reports to leaders across systems. Public Relations Supports media relations efforts by coordinating with communications colleagues to assist in proactively generating news coverage and responding to media inquiries. Other Meets regularly with key chairs, chiefs, directors and faculty. Attends key planning and BTC leadership meetings. Attend regularly scheduled UF Health Marketing Team meetings. Attends UF Health Marketing & Communications divisional meetings. Uses the project management system to track and manage all marketing projects.[JB5.1] Serves as an essential employee during times the Command Center is activated. Expected Salary: commensurate with experience Required Qualifications: Master's degree in appropriate area of specialization and two years of appropriate experience or a bachelor's degree in appropriate areas of specialization and four years of relevant experience. Preferred: Marketing or Communications degree strongly preferred. Proficiency in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Canva, web content management systems such as WordPress, and social media business management systems. Proficiency in Associated Press style required. Demonstrated outstanding ability to work under pressure in a fast-paced office with frequent interruptions, changing priorities and short deadlines. Ability to plan, organize and coordinate work assignments. Proven experience developing and executing integrated communications plans and multichannel campaigns aligned with organizational priorities. Strong analytical skills, including experience using communications metrics, digital analytics and engagement data to inform strategy and decisions. Ability to establish and maintain effective, collaborative working relationships with others as part of a team. Ability to function under stressful circumstances, always maintaining respectful and supportive interactions. Superior verbal, writing and presentation skills. Ability to plan, organize and coordinate work assignments. Ability to work independently and receive feedback on work. Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, please complete an application and include a cover letter, resume and the names and email addresses of three to five references. The University of Florida is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 03 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541778/ops-studio-technician": {
      "title": "OPS Studio Technician",
      "description": "OPS Studio Technician Apply now Job no: 541778 Work type: Temp Part-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support, Information Technology Department: 14200500 - IT-AT CITT Classification Title: OPS - Time Limited Classification Minimum Requirements: Must be at least 18 years of age UF Student Assistant This position is open to all students eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. OPS Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: UF Information Technology (UFIT) is currently seeking an entry-level part-time Studio Technician to join UFIT’s Center for Instructional Technology and Training (CITT), a unit within UFIT. UF Information Technology (UFIT) enables teaching, learning, research, and service on campus and across the region with state-of-the-art enterprise IT systems, including SEC and SUS universities, and the opportunity to teach using HiPerGator. We are seeking a creative, detail-oriented, and technically skilled Part-Time Studio Technician to support daily operations within our on-campus video production studios. This position plays a key role in producing high-quality instructional, promotional, and administrative video content for the university community. Studio operating hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM. The ideal candidate is comfortable working directly with faculty, staff, and university leadership and possesses hands-on experience in studio and field video production. Candidates should demonstrate strong technical knowledge of filming, editing, lighting, audio, and live production workflows while maintaining a high level of professionalism and customer service. Key Responsibilities Set up, operate, and maintain professional studio production equipment and recording spaces Operate live production systems such as teleprompters, live switchers, video capture devices, digital cinema cameras, and studio lighting systems Guide and coach clients throughout recording sessions by providing clear direction, presentation support, and constructive feedback Capture and organize detailed production and editing notes for post-production workflows Maintain organized file structures and media management systems to support efficient editing and archival processes Edit video projects in a timely manner while maintaining high production quality and consistency Ensure strong attention to detail in video composition, lighting, audio capture, graphics, and final delivery Utilize project management and collaboration platforms such as Trello, Notion, or Monday to monitor project timelines and deliverables Edit using nonlinear editing software including Adobe Premiere Pro, Final Cut Pro, or similar platforms Create and incorporate motion graphics, visual assets, and AI-assisted production elements using tools such as Adobe After Effects, Photoshop, Illustrator, and InDesign About UF Information Technology Led by Senior Vice President and CIO Elias Eldayrie, the nine departments comprising UFIT are: Academic Technology; AI² Center; Applications, Development, and Integrations; Business Center; Customer Experience and Resource Planning; Data Platform and Analytics; Information Security Office; Infrastructure and Communication Technology; and Research Computing. UF Information Technology (UFIT) enables teaching, learning, research, and service on campus and across the region with state-of-the-art enterprise IT systems, including SEC and SUS universities, and the opportunity to teach using HiPerGator. For more information about UFIT and its goals and governance, visit https://it.ufl.edu/about-ufit/strategic-plan/ . About the University of Florida One of America’s all-around best universities, the University of Florida drives future-making education, eye-opening discoveries, life-saving health care, and community-building collaboration for our state, our nation, and our world. UF is in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 50 miles from Florida’s West Coast, 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean, and within a 2-hour drive to large metropolitan areas (Orlando, Tampa, Jacksonville). The beautiful climate and extensive nearby parks and recreational areas afford year-round outdoor activities, including hiking, biking, and nature photography. UF’s large college sports programs, museums, and performing arts center support various activities and cultural events for residents to enjoy. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville. Expected Salary: $16.00 per hour Required Qualifications: Must be at least 18 years of age UF Student Assistant This position is open to all students eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. OPS Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Preferred: The ideal candidate will possess the following education, experience, and skills: Experience working in professional, educational, broadcast, or corporate production environments Strong communication and interpersonal skills with a client-focused approach Knowledge of current video production trends, AI-assisted workflows, and multimedia technologies Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while meeting deadlines Familiarity with studio lighting, audio recording, and live streaming workflows Special Instructions to Applicants: Work visa sponsorship is not available for this position This is not a remote work position and is located in Gainesville, FL. A Level 1 Criminal Background Screening is required. Applicants are required to submit the following with their application: Cover Letter Resume List of professional references with contact information (Minimum of 3 with one from a previous or current supervisor) The application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (E.T.) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541780/biological-scientist-iidepartment-of-neurosurgery-preston-a-wells-jr-center-for-brain-tumor-therapy": {
      "title": "Biological Scientist II-Department of Neurosurgery- Preston A. Wells Jr. Center for Brain Tumor Therapy",
      "description": "Biological Scientist II-Department of Neurosurgery- Preston A. Wells Jr. Center for Brain Tumor Therapy Apply now Job no: 541780 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Biology/Life Science Department: 29190000 - MD-NEUROLOGICAL SURGERY Classification Title: Biological Scientist II Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in biology or a related field and three years of experience or Master's degree in biology or a related field with one year of relevant experience. Job Description: The Biological Scientist II will mainly focus on performing experiments that aid in the development of immunotherapeutic platforms. Additionally will be responsible for general laboratory management duties, monitoring and caring for laboratory animals, and conducting experimental work in within the Preston A. Wells Jr Center for Brain Tumor Therapy within the Department of Neurosurgery. Duties include: Under minimal supervision, perform experimental work, including: animal surgeries and treatments, isolation and generation of immune cells, flow cytometry, RNA seq analysis, cell culture and engineering. Includes analyzing data and reporting data. Generation of antigen-specific RNA. Adjust/modify experimental designs as necessary based on experimental data analysis. Assist with report writing and developing presentations. Participates in laboratory management, including: maintaining lab equipment, keeping inventory updated, purchasing lab and office supplies, maintaining laboratory safety programs, training of personnel in laboratory safety techniques, keep laboratory records, preparing reagents, maintaining clean work areas, and managing chemical and biological waste. Participate in writing and editing SOPs (standard operating procedures) for the laboratory. Helps with IACUC modifications. Participates in general upkeep and maintenance of the UF Brain Tumor Immunotherapy Program. Animal work, including: monitoring and care, surgical support (intracranial and subcutaneous tumor implantation in mice), post-surgical monitoring and care, health evaluation and surveillance, giving injections (intravenous, subcutaneous, intraperitoneal, etc), removing sutures, maintaining procedures and protocols, collecting biological samples (blood, tissues, etc.), and maintaining laboratory records. Expected Salary: $61,350-$69,700 Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in biology or a related field and three years of experience or Master's degree in biology or a related field with one year of relevant experience. Preferred: Experience in fluorescent imaging, flow cytometry, and animal methods. Special Instructions to Applicants: For consideration, please complete an application and include a cover letter, resume and the names and email addresses of three to five references. The University of Florida is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541781/biological-scientist-iv": {
      "title": "Biological Scientist IV",
      "description": "Biological Scientist IV Apply now Job no: 541781 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Health Care Administration/Support, Biology/Life Science Department: 29740000 - MD-UF DIABETES INSTITUTE Classification Title: Biological Scientist IV Classification Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree in biology or a related field and thirteen years of experience or Master's degree in biology or a related field with eleven years of experience. Doctoral degree in biology or related field with eight years of experience. Job Description: The University of Florida’s Diabetes Institute (UFDI) is seeking a candidate to provide critical support for tissue sample processing and subsequent data generation to support several type 1 diabetes research efforts. The applicant will use expertise with molecular and single cell biology to carry out research in human tissue samples and support ongoing studies in the laboratory in the areas of type 1 diabetes genetics, human immune development, and adaptive immunity. Specific duties include oversight of spatial transcriptomics operations, processing and preparation of human tissue samples for performance of assays, and management of sample processing workflows for next generation sequencing, flow cytometry, and/or image data collected via immunofluorescence. Duties include: Direct, manage, and execute research studies for the UF Diabetes Institute Spatial transcriptomics and multi-omics research group. This includes the direct supervision of other scientists, post-docs, grad students, and undergrads on all facets of these studies. Primary directives include developing new methods for spatial biology research in type 1 diabetes, monitoring and operating specialized multi-omic imaging platform equipment, and creating and executing computational approaches for data analysis and visualization. Coordinate scientific services in relation to spatial transcriptomics, scRNAseq, and high-parameter imaging platforms for the entire UFDI and collaborating members of the College of Medicine. This includes the development and oversight of all laboratory SOPs and ensuring proper processing of cell and tissue samples for the multi-omics core of the UFDI. Lead data manager and data analysis pipeline developer for the UFDI multi-omics core. Responsible for managing UF Hipergator resources and for developing the UFDI codebook in relation to all multi-omics activities and appropriately sharing these resources on GitHub or other applicable platforms. Manuscript development and writing. Generate timely reports for all study activities to the PI and UFDI leadership, including progress reports for the NIH, FDOH, and other funding authorities. Participate in grant writing for new funding opportunities, present research findings at institutional, governmental, and international scientific meetings, and prepare and submit manuscripts for publication in scientific journals. Maintain accurate laboratory records. Perform and supervise lab maintenance and upkeep to abide by EH&S and other regulatory requirements in the handling of chemical and biohazardous materials. Stay current with advancements in the fields of histology, imaging, and image processing as they relate to lab goals from journal articles, networking, seminar and conference attendance. Other duties as assigned by the project manager and principal investigator Expected Salary: $83,700 - $92,200; commensurate with education and experience Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in biology or a related field and thirteen years of experience or Master's degree in biology or a related field with eleven years of experience. Doctoral degree in biology or related field with eight years of experience. Preferred: Experience designing and troubleshooting fluorophore-antibody-filterset combinations with microscope parameters for interpretable signal to noise image acquisition Experience with tissue-clearing approaches; 3D image acquisition and analysis Knowledge of coding environments, cloning repositories, command-line/terminal execution, Linux OS, building code from source Knowledge and education covering the major systems in human physiology and pathophysiology Consistent history of productivity evidenced by contributions to publications, grants, abstracts, and presentations Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. This is a time-limited position. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: Yes Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541783/web-mobile-application-developer-internship": {
      "title": "Web & Mobile Application Developer Internship",
      "description": "Web & Mobile Application Developer Internship Apply now Job no: 541783 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Information Technology Department: 14800000 - IT-APPS DEVELOP & INTEGRATION Classification Title: OPS Intern or Student Intern Classification Minimum Requirements: MUST BE AT LEAST 18 YEARS OF AGE UF Student Assistant This position is open to all students eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. OPS Intern Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Job Description: UF Information Technology (UFIT) is currently seeking a talented and highly motivated, part-time Web & Mobile Application Developer Intern to join Applications, Development, & Integrations (ADI), a unit within UFIT for the spring semester. This semester-long, paid internship is designed to provide students currently enrolled in college an opportunity to learn practical skills and gain experience to propel them into a successful career in Information Technology. Employment with UFIT provides an excellent opportunity to work with other dedicated employees focused on understanding and interpreting the technological needs of the University of Florida’s innovative and inspirational community. This position is primarily focused on contributing to accessibility improvements for our digital solutions including the one.uf site and the UF mobile app. The incumbent will work collaboratively with the UX & Portal Solutions team, consisting of experienced developers and UX designers. Some key responsibilities and characteristics of this position are: Learn the technology stacks that the one.uf site and the UF mobile app use Learn about web and mobile app accessibility guidelines Work on accessibility improvements for the one.uf site and the UF mobile app Learn how the agile development process works in a professional environment About UF Information Technology Led by Senior Vice President and CIO Elias Eldayrie, the nine departments comprising UFIT are: Academic Technology; AI² Center; Applications, Development, and Integrations; Business Center; Customer Experience and Resource Planning; Data Platform and Analytics; Information Security Office; Infrastructure and Communication Technology; and Research Computing. UF Information Technology (UFIT) enables teaching, learning, research, and service on campus and across the region with state-of-the-art enterprise IT systems, including SEC and SUS universities, and the opportunity to teach using HiPerGator. For more information about UFIT and its goals and governance, visit https://it.ufl.edu/about-ufit/strategic-plan/ . About the University of Florida One of America’s all-around best universities, the University of Florida drives future-making education, eye-opening discoveries, life-saving health care, and community-building collaboration for our state, our nation, and our world. UF is in Gainesville, a city of approximately 150,000 residents in North-Central Florida, 50 miles from Florida’s West Coast, 67 miles from the Atlantic Ocean, and within a 2-hour drive to large metropolitan areas (Orlando, Tampa, Jacksonville). The beautiful climate and extensive nearby parks and recreational areas afford year-round outdoor activities, including hiking, biking, and nature photography. UF’s large college sports programs, museums, and performing arts center support various activities and cultural events for residents to enjoy. Learn more about what Gainesville has to offer at Visit Gainesville Expected Salary: $20.00 per Hour Required Qualifications: MUST BE AT LEAST 18 YEARS OF AGE UF Student Assistant This position is open to all students eligible to work on campus and will be employed through student Other Personnel Services (OPS) and must maintain a minimum 2.0 grade point average. OPS Intern Must have a high school diploma or equivalent. Preferred: The ideal candidate will possess the following education, experience, and skills: Some prior or current coursework and/or experience related to application or web development; personal project work will also be considered Willingness to receive direction and feedback from a mentoring developer Works well in a team environment, comfortable working independently at times, and has a willingness to ask for help when needed A desire to work on project focused on improving the user experience for UF students on one.uf and the UF mobile app Special Instructions to Applicants: A Level 2 Criminal Background Screening is required. Work visa sponsorship is not available for this position This is not a remote work position and is located in Gainesville, FL. Applicants are required to submit with their application: Cover Letter Resume or CV Professional References (Minimum of 3) Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 21 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 30 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
