    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540953/immigration-specialist-i-f1-advisordesignated-school-official-dso": {
      "title": "Immigration Specialist I (F-1 Advisor/Designated School Official (DSO)",
      "description": "Immigration Specialist I (F-1 Advisor/Designated School Official (DSO) Apply now Job no: 540953 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Human Resources, Veteran's Preference Eligible, Legal/Audit Services/Compliance Department: 20010000 - IP-INTERNATIONAL CENTER-GEN Classification Title: Immigration Specialist I (F-1 Advisor/Designated School Official (DSO) Classification Minimum Requirements: Must meet federal eligibility requirements to serve as a Designated School Official (DSO): https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/schools/get-started/designated-school-official Job Description: Form I-20 Processing, Student Advising & Compliance Serve as a primary processor of initial and transfer-in Forms I-20 for F-1 international students at the University of Florida. Review financial documentation to determine eligibility and issue accurate Forms I-20 through SEVIS. Maintain complete, audit-ready immigration records and ensure compliance with federal regulations established by ICE, DHS, and SEVP. Serve as a Designated School Official (DSO) and F-1 International Student Adviser for an assigned caseload and backing-up as needed on other caseloads. Advise students on maintaining F-1 status, including enrollment requirements, reduced course loads, program extensions, training and employment eligibility, travel, and related regulatory matters. Apply federal regulations and institutional policies to support student success while mitigating institutional risk. Maintain secure and compliant immigration records in accordance with federal and university policies. Government & Institutional Liaison; SEVIS Reporting Act as liaison with federal agencies including ICE, DHS, SEVP, CBP, and USCIS. Ensure timely and accurate SEVIS reporting of enrollment, employment, program changes, and status updates. Maintain compliance with federal reporting deadlines and audit standards. Data & Team Support Assist with SEVIS alerts, compliance monitoring, and institutional reporting. Collaborate with colleagues to resolve complex cases, improve processes, and provide cross-coverage during peak periods. Departmental Consultation Provide immigration guidance to academic departments and campus partners regarding F-1 training & employment eligibility, enrollment impacts, and immigration implications of academic actions. Communicate regulatory updates and institutional procedures. Outreach Support development and delivery of workshops, orientation programming, and educational materials related to F-1 regulations. Campus Involvement Represent International Student Services through active participation in campus engagement initiatives. Co-present at new student orientations, departmental meetings, and informational workshops to provide guidance on immigration processes and compliance requirements. Participate in tabling events and partner-sponsored activities across campus to promote services, foster collaboration, and support the university’s international student community. Other Duties as Assigned Provide operational support to ensure continuity of services, including backup phone and front desk coverage as needed. Perform additional duties to support office operations and team objectives. Eligibility Must meet federal eligibility requirements to serve as a Designated School Official (DSO): https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/schools/get-started/designated-school-official Expected Salary: $20.00-$22.00/hour Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and one year of relevant experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: EDUCATION & TRAINING - Bachelor's or Master's degree - Federal Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA) training EXPERIENCE - Experience with immigration regulations - Experience with UF rules and regulations KNOWLEDGE: - F-1 Visa Status Regulations as governed by ICE, DHS, SEVP, USCIS. SKILLS - Detail-Oriented, Effective Communicator, Culturally Sensitive, Empathetic, Resourceful, Organized, Technologically Proficient, Adaptable, Reliable Special Instructions to Applicants: Time Limited & DSO Eligibility Must meet federal eligibility requirements to serve as a Designated School Official (DSO): https://studyinthestates.dhs.gov/schools/get-started/designated-school-official In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This position is eligible for Veteran’s preference. If you are claiming Veteran’s preference, please upload a copy of your DD 214 Member Copy 4 with your application for consideration. See our Veteran's Preference Page for more specific information. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 13 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 05 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
