    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540668/accounting-specialist": {
      "title": "Accounting Specialist",
      "description": "Accounting Specialist Apply now Job no: 540668 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Business/Accounting/Finance, Facilities Operations/Skilled Trades Department: 63300500 - FS-FIN BUSINESS OFC Classification Title: Accounting Specialist Classification Minimum Requirements: A bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and one year of appropriate experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: Billing Operations – Process monthly billing for Work Request and Utility services. Ensure completion of all billing tasks and monthly reconciliations. Update, maintain, and analyze Facilities Services billing data, invoices, and exception reports. Research billing trends and ensure compliance with Facilities Services billing procedures and policies. Design and maintain invoice templates using Crystal Reports. Customer Account Management – Manage and analyze customer purchase orders and chartfield information. Review and update customer data, including billing contacts, service types, asset information, invoice addresses, and financial details. Communicate with customers to resolve billing issues; follow up on outstanding items and escalate when necessary. Maintain an organized and responsive Billing Office email inbox. Data Analysis and Quality Control – Collect, analyze, and summarize data to support management reporting and process improvements. Review quality control issues to minimize billing errors and prevent unbilled charges. Process billing adjustments and coordinate corrections with relevant departments. Identify trends and contribute to developing solutions for recurring issues. Process Improvement and Documentation – Support implementation of billing process enhancements and workflow improvements. Provide input and recommendations for ongoing process improvements. Maintain accurate and current Billing Office documentation, including procedures and guidelines. Support and Collaboration – Provide administrative and billing support to internal departments and team members as needed. Support Accounts Payable (AP) with invoice processing on an as-needed basis. Respond to inquiries and support cross-functional efforts that impact billing accuracy and efficiency. NORMAL WORK SCHEDULE: The typical work schedule is Monday – Friday 8:00AM – 5:00PM. Position is considered as Essential Personnel as defined by UF Policy. Expected Salary: $53,000 - $57,000 Annually based on experience. Required Qualifications: A bachelor's degree in an appropriate area of specialization and one year of appropriate experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: - Experience with Microsoft Office Suite, especially Excel, Outlook, Word, and Access. - Familiarity with billing systems, financial reconciliation, and invoice processing. - Experience using Crystal Reports or similar reporting tools. - Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. - Effective written and verbal communication skills for interacting with internal departments and customers. - Strong customer service and problem-solving skills related to billing and account management. - Ability to analyze financial data, identify discrepancies, and support process improvements. - Ability to learn new systems quickly and work independently with minimal su Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Multiple vacancies will be filled from this posting. Position has been reposted, previous applicants are still being considered. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 04 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541485/graphic-designer-ii-enrollment-marketing-communications": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer II (Enrollment Marketing & Communications)",
      "description": "Graphic Designer II (Enrollment Marketing & Communications) Apply now Job no: 541485 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Communications/Public Relations/Marketing, Office/Administrative/Fiscal Support Department: 03010300 - EM-ADMIN PUBLICATIONS-COMMUNIC Classification Title: Graphic Designer II Classification Minimum Requirements: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Job Description: The University of Florida is seeking a talented Graphic Designer to support the Division of Enrollment Management’s marketing and communications efforts by creating engaging, high-quality visual content across a variety of platforms. In this role, you will create print and digital materials, develop accessible digital content, manage multiple creative projects, and collaborate with internal clients and vendors to deliver effective communications that align with UF brand standards. Key responsibilities include: Print Graphic Design Create high-quality visual designs using typography, illustrations, photography, logos, and other visual elements Collaborate with Enrollment Management Marketing and Communications team to conceptualize and develop creative projects Design print-ready materials including booklets, brochures, mailers, postcards, posters, flyers, promotional items, and signage Apply University of Florida and Division of Enrollment Management brand standards across all projects Develop reusable templates and advise internal clients on design strategies, principles, and best practices Digital Graphic Design Create engaging and ADA-compliant visual designs for the division’s electronic communications Design optimized digital posts including but not limited to website and microsite wireframes/mockups Assist Slate email communications, social media graphics, PowerPoint presentations, and other digital materials Create digital and paid advertising assets optimized for their intended platforms and audiences Task Management Collaborate on multiple design projects of varying scope and complexity while meeting established deadlines. Coordinate with campus partners and other stakeholders to support successful project development and production Distribute production files, review proofs, and oversee final quality control to ensure completed projects meet established design, branding, and production standards Additional Responsibilities Collaborate with division staff and stakeholders to support marketing and communication initiatives Provide creative support for Division of Enrollment Management projects and priorities Perform other job-related duties as assigned to support the responsibilities and functions of the division Expected Salary: $55,000 annually In addition, UF offers the following exceptional benefits: Health, Dental, and Vision Insurance State Retirement Plans Paid Time Off (approximately 22 days of vacation leave, 13 days of sick leave, and 11 paid holidays annually) Tuition Assistance (UF Employee Education Program) Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Eligible Employer Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred: Proficiency in Adobe Creative Cloud software, including InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator, XD, and Acrobat Proficiency in packaging print files using Adobe InDesign Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Word and PowerPoint Experience with wireframing and web design mockups using Adobe XD, Sketch, or Figma Understanding of web standards, ADA accessibility guidelines, and responsive design Strong individual contributor who effectively supports team and organizational goals Self-starter with the ability to multitask in a fast-paced environment Detail-oriented and highly organized Ability to manage multiple duties, assignments, and priorities Ability to work effectively in a collaborative, team-oriented environment Knowledge of HTML coding Illustration skills Special Instructions to Applicants: Work visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Applicants must upload the following documents to be considered for the position: Cover Letter Resume List of References Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 11 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541747/assistant-professor-of-educational-leadership-and-policy": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy Apply now Job no: 541747 Work type: Tenure-Track Faculty Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Education/Training/Instructional Design Department: 18070000 - ED-SHDOSE-SCHL OF HUM DEV&ORG Classification Title: AST PROF Classification Minimum Requirements: An earned doctorate in education, public policy, economics, sociology, or a closely related field awarded by the time of hire Job Description: The University of Florida invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Educational Leadership and Policy in the School of Human Development and Organizational Studies in Education in the College of Education. The Educational Leadership and Policy program is committed to furthering research that improves educational outcomes through innovative policy and dynamic leadership. The Educational Leadership and Policy program includes PhD, EdD, EdS, and MEd degree programs as well as a graduate concentration in education policy. Through this search, we seek a colleague who will contribute to the goals of the program area through exemplary research, teaching, mentoring, and service. The successful candidate will demonstrate an emerging research agenda related to education policy and leadership that demonstrates the potential to successfully compete for external funding. The ideal candidate will have evidence of excellent research skills, a focused research agenda, and a demonstrated commitment to meeting the needs of all learners and communities. We are open to scholarship in a broad range of topics in educational policy and leadership, especially candidates whose research utilizes or focuses on school and district leadership, school choice, educational governance, or artificial intelligence in education. We are open to candidates that apply a variety of research methodologies (e.g., qualitative, quantitative, mixed methods). Relevant experience in P-12 schools is also desirable. The University of Florida’s Educational Leadership and Policy program is nationally ranked and includes one of the top ranked online master’s in educational leadership degrees. The successful candidate will join a dynamic faculty whose research and teaching are nationally renowned. The candidate will have opportunities to contribute to teaching and advising in our PhD program, online EdD program, and both on-campus and online master’s programs and will have opportunities to affiliate with campus partners including UF’s Education Policy Research Center ( www.ufedpolicy.org ) and the Early Childhood Policy Centers Collaborative. More information on UF’s Educational Leadership and Policy program can be found at: https://education.ufl.edu/educational-leadership/ This 9-month tenure-accruing faculty appointment will begin August 2027. Salary is negotiable, competitive, and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Expected Salary: Salary is negotiable, competitive, and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Required Qualifications: An earned doctorate in education, public policy, economics, sociology, or a closely related field awarded by the time of hire Evidence of commitment to collaboration with faculty, students, and school-based personnel A record of publication or evidence of potential for successful publication in leading education, policy, and educational leadership journals Demonstration of promise to successfully acquire external funding for research Preferred: Experience in P-12 school settings (or equivalent) A strong record of or potential for successful teaching and advising in-person and/or online Teaching, research, and/or service experiences with students from a wide range of backgrounds Ability to contribute to the national visibility of the Educational Leadership and Policy program Special Instructions to Applicants: Application Procedures: Applicant should upload all materials to the University of Florida’s employment website https://jobs.ufl.edu. If technical assistance is needed, please contact Human resources at (352) 392-2477. Complete applications include: (1) a letter of application addressing required and desired qualifications, (2) curriculum vitae or résumé, (3) contact information for three references, who after further review will be asked to send a letter of recommendation through the online application system. Applicants should reference requisition 541747 , position number 00044043 . Inquiries about the position can be addressed to Dr. Chris Redding, Search Committee Chair ( c.redding@coe.ufl.edu ). Review of candidates will begin November 21, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, application materials should be submitted by November 20 th , 2026. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the committee and hiring authority. The selection process will be conducted in accordance with the provisions of Florida’s “Government in the Sunshine” and Public Records laws. Search Committee meetings and interviews are open to the public and all applications, resumes, and other documents related to the search will be available for public inspection. Final candidates will be required to provide an official transcript to the hiring department upon hire. A transcript will not be considered “official” if a designation of “Issued to Student” is visible. Degrees earned outside of the United States are required to be evaluated by a professional credentialing service provider approved by the National Association of Credentialing Evaluation Services (NACES), which can be found at http://www.naces.org. ABOUT THE COLLEGE: Founded in 1906, the College of Education at the University of Florida has a long history of mission-driven excellence, working to advance research, prepare the next generation of educators and solve society’s most pressing challenges. The college is No. 2 in the nation among all Graduate Education Schools, according to U.S. News & World Report. In Online Graduate Education, the college has ranked No. 1 or No. 2 for the last 11 years. Among specialty rankings, both the Counseling (No. 2) and Special Education (No. 5) programs have maintained top-five designations for the past four years. In total, the college ranks top 20 in six program areas including Elementary Teacher Education (No. 12), Curriculum and Instruction (No. 17), Educational Administration (No. 19) and Higher Education (No. 19). Novel interdisciplinary research and public scholarship—in collaboration with other UF colleges, school districts, communities and education partners across the nation—are yielding powerful real-world results in teaching and learning. Last year, faculty researchers tallied more than $133.4 million in research expenditures supporting studies and projects addressing education's most challenging issues. To sustain the college's innovative edge and societal benefit, heightened emphasis on AI and emerging technologies, student experience and interdisciplinary research will effectively prepare tomorrow's leaders in all education disciplines. With both on-campus and online options, the college offers a variety of bachelor's and advanced degree programs and concentration areas within nine academic specialties. The college's educator preparation programs have been accredited by CAEP and NCATE since 1954. Follow us: @UF_COE (X), @uf_coe (Instagram), @university-of-florida-college-of-education (LinkedIn), and @UF.COE (Facebook) ABOUT THE UNIVERSITY: The University of Florida, founded in 1853, is a public land-grant, sea-grant and space-grant research university and one of the most academically diverse universities in the nation. U.S. News & World Report ranks UF No. 7 among public universities. National rankings such as No. 1 for Online Bachelor’s by U.S. News and No. 1 by the Wall Street Journal are a result of UF's commitment to provide the highest-quality education at the best value. UF is a Carnegie R1 institution, home to 16 colleges and more than 200 research, service and education centers, bureaus and institutes. The university boasts more than 6,100 faculty members, 63,000 students and 525,000 living alumni. Faculty scholars last year generated more than $1.25 billion in research awards. UF recently expanded its $70 million AI partnership with NVIDIA, adding an additional $24 million investment to make AI accessible to students and faculty across campus and the state. The Florida Legislature designated UF as a \"preeminent'' state university in 2013. ABOUT THE AREA: UF is situated in Gainesville, a vibrant college town in North Central Florida that blends big-city cultural and athletic offerings with small-town friendliness and charm, along with excellent schools. Gainesville, located about halfway between the Atlantic Ocean and Gulf of America, is recognized as one of the nation’s best college towns and is easily accessible to three major metropolitan areas (Jacksonville, Orlando and Tampa). The National Arbor Day Foundation has recognized Gainesville as a \"Tree City USA\" every year since 1982. Livability ranked Gainesville as one of the Best Places to Live in the U.S. Add the allure of Florida's famous sunshine, tropical breezes, and abundant wilderness, springs, rivers and seashores nearby, and it is little wonder that top-caliber faculty and students find our university to be the perfect balance of premier academics and a fulfilling lifestyle . Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Open until filled Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541850/marketing-and-social-media-coordinator-career-ambassador": {
      "title": "Marketing and Social Media Coordinator (Career Ambassador)",
      "description": "Marketing and Social Media Coordinator (Career Ambassador) Apply now Job no: 541850 Work type: Student Ast Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Student Services Department: 04040000 - SL-CAREER CONNECTIONS CENTER Classification Title: Student Assistant for Marketing & Social Media Classification Minimum Requirements: Portfolio submission is required Demonstrate previous design experience utilizing Adobe Creative Cloud and Canva design software Demonstrate previous experience writing social media copy Make a two-semester commitment to the position Maintain a 2.0 grade point average Job Description: Position Specific Responsibilities: Provide creative solutions to produce professional and innovative designs for all areas of Career and Integrative Partnership Portfolio to be utilized on web graphics, social media pages, and promotional materials. Portfolio areas include: Career Connections Center Brown Center for Leadership and Service Machen Florida Opportunity First-Generation Student Success Center Assist with the planning and development of marketing campaigns Proof all designs for spelling, grammar and design consistency Prepare designs for social media use Create social media copy to promote events Maintain social media items on the marketing team’s shared project board Independently track current CIP events to create weekly event posts and maintain calendar pages Complete all training requirements upon being hired in a timely fashion Ability to commit to working 15-20 hours per week Other duties as assigned Additional Responsibilities: Deliver exceptional customer service to the following areas: phone, front desks, drop-in sessions, appointments, and referring students, staff, faculty and employers to appropriate services Review resumes, cover letters, CVs, LinkedIn profiles and personal statements Coach students in interview strategies, professional dress and conducting mock interviews Convey constructive and empowering feedback to inspire students' professional growth Provide one-on-one assistance and career information to students and alumni Facilitate career development outreach presentations to classrooms and student organizations, topics ranging from resume development to career design Perform administrative duties including logging student information and developing resources Expected Salary: 15.00 Required Qualifications: Portfolio submission is required Demonstrate previous design experience utilizing Adobe Creative Cloud and Canva design software Demonstrate previous experience writing social media copy Make a two-semester commitment to the position Maintain a 2.0 grade point average Preferred: Special Instructions to Applicants: Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 28 Oct 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 11 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
