    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/541062/ops-school-bus-driver": {
      "title": "OPS School Bus Driver",
      "description": "OPS School Bus Driver Apply now Job no: 541062 Work type: Temp Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Transportation Services Department: 18180300 - ED-STUDENT SERVICES Classification Title: OPS HOURLY NON-SECRETARY CLERK Classification Minimum Requirements: A valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) is required. Passenger (P) and School Bus (S) endorsements are required. Must have a clean and satisfactory driving record. Must demonstrate a strong commitment to student safety and responsible driving. Must be dependable, punctual, and professional. Must be willing and available to work a variable schedule, including nights and weekends as needed. Level 2 DCF Background check required. Job Description: School Bus Driver, transporting K-12 students on field trips and to athletic events. Out of town travel as well as evening and occasional overnight trips required. Section 234.091 - General Qualifications - Each school bus driver shall be of good moral character, of good vision and hearing, able-bodied, free from communicable disease, mentally alert, and sufficiently strong physically to handle the bus with ease and to make emergency repairs, and s/he shall possess such other qualifications as are prescribed by the State Board, and s/he shall hold a valid Commercial Driver's License (CDL) with a passenger endorsement. Prior to transporting students on a school bus, each driver shall meet the following requirements: Hold a Florida Commercial Drivers' License and Endorsements as appropriate and required by law. Demonstrate the ability to prepare required written reports. Be physically capable of operating the vehicle as determined by an annual physical examination. Demonstrate physical and mental capabilities required to carry out all assigned responsibilities as a school bus driver. The bus driver's license shall be either posted in a conspicuous place inside the bus or be carried on the driver's person while the bus is in operation. Expected Salary: $25-30/hour based on experience Required Qualifications: A valid Commercial Driver’s License (CDL) is required. Passenger (P) and School Bus (S) endorsements are required. Up-to-date CDL physical or ability to obtain at hire Must have a clean and satisfactory driving record. Must demonstrate a strong commitment to student safety and responsible driving. Must be dependable, punctual, and professional. Must be willing and available to work a variable schedule, including nights and weekends as needed. Level 2 DCF Background check required Preferred: Previous experience transporting students or driving a school bus is preferred. The ideal candidate is someone who enjoys working with students, takes pride in providing safe and dependable transportation, and appreciates the flexibility of a part-time schedule. Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. No phone calls, please. This is a time-limited position. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No, although, a CDL Physical is required. Advertised: 21 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 27 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://explore.jobs.ufl.edu/en-us/job/540970/career-coach-environment-design-manufacturing-and-agriculture": {
      "title": "Career Coach -Environment, Design, Manufacturing and Agriculture",
      "description": "Career Coach -Environment, Design, Manufacturing and Agriculture Apply now Job no: 540970 Work type: Staff Full-Time Location: Main Campus (Gainesville, FL) Categories: Academic Advising/Support, Student Services Department: 04040000 - SL-CAREER CONNECTIONS CENTER Classification Title: Career Coach Classification Minimum Requirements: Master's degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Job Description: Serves as a career coach by delivering individual and group career planning services to UF students within a specific career cluster. Supports career clusters by facilitating individual career planning appointments, drop-in services, and small group coaching to UF undergraduate and graduate students based on industry-specific knowledge. Facilitates customized career education workshops, for-credit course material, and large group programs to UF undergraduate and graduate students for career clusters. Implements elements of the Career Action Plan and career development theory to all workshops and programs. Provides direct service or coaching through center-wide series and cohort programs focused on the professionalization of students. Customizes existing C3 marketing materials and resources for specific career cluster populations. Facilitates external career development programming and outreach to student organizations, campus partners, and faculty to promote career services and the Career Connections Center. Coordinates day-to-day outreach administration and handles logistical functions to support career education programming including scheduling, reserving space, ordering supplies, communicating with attendees and other activities. Engages with employers to facilitate their participation in industry education activities such as C3 workshops, outreaches, events and conferences. Works with team Managers to develop programs to connect students with industry. Maintains relationships with industry partners to increase employment connections for UF candidates while helping students prepare for successful applications or interviews in these opportunities. Aids in maintaining quantitative and qualitative records for various types of interactions for assessment and reporting purposes to demonstrate impact. Responsible for tracking and reporting on student engagement. Maintains up-to-date knowledge of career development trends. Expected Salary: $52,000.00 Required Qualifications: Master's degree in an appropriate area; or a bachelor's degree in an appropriate area and two years of relevant experience. Certified Career Services Practitioner (CCSP) within first year of employment. Preferred: EDUCATION & TRAINING: Bachelor’s degree in marketing, social sciences, education, student personnel, or human resources (HR) EXPERIENCE - Two (2) years of experience (minimum) in career development, education, career coaching, HR, stakeholder engagement, marketing. - Experience working with a range of different perspectives, viewpoints, and experiences. - Experience with presenting and facilitating large groups. KNOWLEDGE: Knowledge of career development, employment trends, student development, career services, career coaching, and outreach strategies SKILLS - Skilled in computer applications - Facilitative skills - Interpersonal skills - Good presentations skills, listening skills, helping skills, relationship management, and program development ABILITIES: Ability to work independently and contribute to a team PHYSICAL QUALIFICATIONS: None noted OTHER QUALIFICATIONS: None noted Special Instructions to Applicants: In order to be considered, you must upload your cover letter and resume. Application must be submitted by 11:55 p.m. (ET) of the posting end date. This requisition has been reposted. Previous applicants are still under consideration and need not reapply. Health Assessment Required: No Advertised: 14 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 10 Nov 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    }
  },
